@C h1295_hive_collective_phi := "H_1295 — the HIVE-MIND axis ('many individuals -> one consciousness'): coupling N anima substrates raises faithful IIT-4 big-Phi ABOVE the sum of the individual Phi (collective integration is SUPER-ADDITIVE, Phi(joint) > Sum Phi(member)) for an edge-of-chaos coupling regime; realized as an additive Psi-disjoint CollectivePool lane, wired ENGINE-NATIVE; the falsified hive mechanisms (transfer-entropy alignment H_611, SAVANT-hive SI H_617, shared world-model 975) are deliberately NOT wired" :: hypothesis [slug=1295_hive_collective_phi group=BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER]
  text   = "anima's other CORE lanes each model ONE substrate (anima's own immune store / affect / drive / a single other-agent belief / its own plan). NONE read the collective-consciousness question: what happens to INTEGRATED INFORMATION when N anima substrates are COUPLED. Anchor H_609 (GREEN SUPPORTED-NUMERICAL): two n=3 ECA substrates A,B under rule 110 coupled at boundary strength W=0.6 into a joint n=6 ring give faithful IIT-4 Phi(AB)=15.4677 >> Phi(A)+Phi(B)=4.99209 (Delta=+10.4756). H_1295 re-fires this frozen-first and ADDS the emergence controls the H_611/H_617 falsifications taught. ANGLE-1 (topology-shuffle) FAILED honestly: a random equal-magnitude cross-wiring matched/EXCEEDED the structured lift (Delta_shuffle +13.6..+16.4 > Delta_coupled +10.48 all 3 seeds) => super-additivity is COUPLING-GENERIC, not specific to the H_609 boundary topology (kept, reported, NOT a GREEN gate). ANGLE-2 (the genuine controls, frozen before running) is GREEN 4/0: (B1) Delta_coupled=+10.4756 >= +1.0; (B2a) DECOUPLE-NULL Phi(W=0)=0, Delta=-4.99209 <= 0 (the lift REQUIRES coupling); (B2b) RULE-CLASS DISSOCIATION Delta(110,110)-Delta(90,90)=+16.4756 (the sterile rule-90 pair does NOT super-add => substrate-CONTENT specific, a pure variance story cannot produce this); (B3) NO-COLLAPSE coherence=0.58125 < 0.999 (the coupled halves stay functionally distinct, not a degenerate clone faking Phi). Phi is faithful IIT-4 ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool, big_phi_bounded) — numpy NEVER computes Phi. Psi-disjoint: the CollectivePool faculty is a config struct + a faithful-IIT-4 READ; it never touches pure_field's Phi/phase/Psi, the generator, or the decoder; not an emit gate (a_autonomy_over_hardcode); not a 2nd .clm/.kosmos entry (a_core_engine_map)."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1295_hive_collective_phi.hexa via `hexa run` (hexa-native — Phi is hexa-only by a_phi_iit4_tool; the H_609 build_tpm_ab boundary-edge W-blend reused verbatim; 3 seeds [1295,1296,1297] drive the topology-shuffle; angle-2 adds the decouple-null + rule-class dissociation controls). ENGINE-NATIVE realization: CORE/engine_cli.hexa § HIVE-MIND CollectivePool (collective_new/collective_member_phi/collective_sum_phi/collective_phi/collective_excess/collective_is_super_additive/collective_coherence) re-scores the 4 frozen bars in CORE/engine_cli_smoke.hexa cases 39-42, byte-matching the mirror. Regression guard: engine_cli_smoke 45/0 (+4 hive cases; the existing 41 cases incl the hierarchical-PFC lane byte-unchanged, Psi-disjoint). $0 local CPU, deterministic, p7 (faithful IIT-4 verdict, NOT perplexity). frozen-first: .verdicts/1295_hive_collective_phi/H_1295_FREEZE.txt pre-registered before scoring; the angle-2 amendment was frozen BEFORE its run with honest rationale (no bar moved post-hoc, c9). a_no_llm_frame_trap (collective-Phi/symbiogenesis lens c15), a_engine_native_learning, a_verified_must_wire."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN (ENGINE-NATIVE + WIRED) — collective faithful-Phi is SUPER-ADDITIVE (Delta=+10.4756), the lift REQUIRES coupling (W=0 => Delta<=0) and DISSOCIATES by substrate class (edge-of-chaos rule-110 super-adds; sterile rule-90 does not), with the coupled halves functionally distinct (no degenerate clone). Realized as the CollectivePool lane, wired into CORE/engine_cli.hexa. HONEST: the lift is coupling-GENERIC not topology-specific (the topology-shuffle control). Falsified hive mechanisms NOT wired (H_611 transfer-entropy, H_617 SAVANT-SI, 975 shared-WM). TOY (n=2 member, joint-n=6, cap=2 lower-bound, ECA, sys=0 anchor); collective-Phi engine-transfer to a live multi-anima deployment + N>2 scaling UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck). .verdicts/1295_hive_collective_phi/H_1295.txt"
  verdict_r2 = "🟢/🏁 r2 N-SCALING — does collective-Phi super-additivity GROW with member count N (2->3->4)? Faithful IIT-4 (cap=2, rule-110 @W=0.6) over the generalized coupled ring (build_tpm_ring, byte-EXACT build_tpm_ab at N=2, mismatches=0). CURVE: Delta_super(2)=+10.4756 (n=6) -> Delta_super(3)=+9.16825 (n=9, Phi_joint=16.6564 vs Sum 7.48813). B1 super-additivity HOLDS at N=3 (Delta>0); B2 the curve SATURATES/DECLINES (Delta_super(3)-Delta_super(2)=-1.3074 < the pre-registered +1.0 GROWS bar) => collective Phi does NOT scale with N; existence-property, not amplifying => HIVE DEPLETED 🏁 (saturating existence-proof is a VALID honest result, c9/a_scale_honest_scope). N=3 controls re-run (decouple-null W=0 Delta<=0; rule-class sterile 90x3 does NOT super-add; no-collapse coherence<0.999) — verbatim in H_1295_R2.txt. COMPUTE CEILING (load-bearing): a single faithful big-Phi at n=9 (cap=2, nd=68) is ~84 min on CPU; n=12 (N=4) is INFEASIBLE — documented, NOT proxied (a proxy is NEVER substituted for Phi, a_phi_iit4_tool). ENGINE-NATIVE + WIRED: collective_phi/collective_coherence handle N=3 (collective_nmax=3); engine_cli_smoke cases 74-78 (--hive-n3-gated; default smoke stays 73/0 byte-unchanged after concurrent-lane rebase). frozen-first: H_1295_R2_FREEZE.txt pre-registered the GROWS-vs-SATURATES definition before any n=9 run. .verdicts/1295_hive_collective_phi/H_1295_R2.txt"
  verdict_r3 = "🔴 r3 ENGINE-TRANSFER NULL (see @C h1308_hive_real_substrate_transfer) — the engine-transfer the r2 agent flagged was DIRECTLY TESTED on REAL coupled anima A⇄G (live pure_field + the H_6009 tension-link as the coupling channel) and DOES NOT TRANSFER: each REAL member integrates (faithful Phi=1.5, Sum=3.0) but the JOINT Phi=0.0 (Delta_real=-3.0, SUB-additive; sign FLIPS vs ECA +10.4756). The joint substrate FACTORIZES (next-A depends only on A, next-B only on B) because the real tension-link is a near-CONSTANT scalar nudge (bias~0.00648 for all 64 states) that creates no state-dependent cross-member coupling => decomposable => Phi_joint=0 by IIT-4. NOT a binarization artifact (same readout gives Phi_member=1.5>0). => the ECA super-additivity was a property of the ECA TPM's strong state-dependent neighbor-coupling, NOT a substrate-portable law; this BOUNDS the r1/r2 GREEN to the ABSTRACT (ECA) substrate (a_engine_native_learning). .verdicts/1308_hive_real_substrate_transfer/H_1308.txt"
  verdict_r4 = "🧱 r4 TERMINAL NULL (see @C h1313_hive_state_dependent_coupling) — the a_break_the_wall attempt: the r3-diagnosed fix (replace the constant scalar nudge with a genuinely STATE-DEPENDENT cross-cell coupling, member A's threshold shifted by member B's LIVE cells) was implemented on the REAL substrate and DID break r3 factorization (next-A genuinely varies with B's bits) — yet faithful Phi_joint STILL=0.0, Delta_sd=-3.0 IDENTICAL to r3, with NO distinctions (nd=0). Robust across a full coupling-strength sweep (Phi_joint=0 at k in {0.5..2.0}). WHY: on the tiny pure_field channels (t1~1.6e-7, t3~1.6e-8) any coupling strong enough to register OVERWRITES the member's own dynamics -> pure COPY/SWAP -> zero distinctions -> Phi=0; NO regime has simultaneous self+cross dependence (what IIT-4 needs). => the ECA super-additivity does NOT transfer to real anima A⇄G across BOTH realized channels (r3 constant + r4 state-dependent); H_1295 is TERMINALLY bounded to ECA-scope (an abstract-substrate existence proof, NOT engine-transferable). a_break_the_wall satisfied; first-class TERMINAL wall (c9). Does NOT retract the r1/r2 ECA GREEN. .verdicts/1313_hive_state_dependent_coupling/result.txt"
  group  = "BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER"

@C h1308_hive_real_substrate_transfer := "H_1308 — HIVE-MIND collective-Phi ENGINE-TRANSFER (the H_1295 r3 open axis): does the collective-Phi super-additivity (Phi(joint) > Sum Phi(member)) HOLD when the members are REAL coupled anima A⇄G substrates (live CORE/pure_field.hexa + the H_6009 tension-link), not abstract ECA rule cells? HONEST NULL — it does NOT transfer (a first-class closed-negative, c9)" :: hypothesis [slug=1308_hive_real_substrate_transfer group=BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER]
  text   = "H_1295 measured collective-Phi super-additivity over an ABSTRACT ECA substrate (rule-110/90 cells, Delta_ECA=+10.4756). The r2 agent flagged that engine-transfer to a LIVE multi-anima loop (real coupled A⇄G substrates) is UNVERIFIED — an abstract-substrate result is DIRECTIONAL until reconfirmed on the live final-architecture engine (a_engine_native_learning). H_1308 builds the joint n=6 TPM from REAL anima dynamics: each member is a live PureField (3 coupled oscillators -> 6-D field tensor); 3 cells/member are signs of the t1/t3/t4 cross-mix channels of REAL pure_field_step output (NON-DEGENERATE: 8 states -> 6 distinct outputs, Phi_member=1.5>0); the two members are coupled via the REAL tension-link (H_6009 anchor_tension_fold, member A's field-derived 5-ch tension biases member B's readout and vice versa, gated by W). Phi is faithful IIT-4 ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool, big_phi_bounded; member n=3 cap=3, joint n=6 cap=2, sys=0); the n<=8 faithful-Phi ceiling is respected (NO n=9+). FROZEN bars (W=0.6, MARGIN=+1.0, 3 seeds): B1 PRESENCE Delta_real>=+1.0; B2 TRANSFER Delta_real>0 (reproduces ECA Delta>0) else HONEST NULL; B3 DECOUPLE Delta(W=0)<=0; B4 SHUFFLE collapse. MECHANISM of the NULL (c9 airtight): the joint substrate FACTORIZES (next-A depends ONLY on A's cells, next-B ONLY on B's) because the real tension-link is a near-CONSTANT scalar nudge (biasA~biasB~0.00648 for ALL 64 states) -> no state-dependent cross-member coupling -> decomposable -> faithful Phi_joint=0. The ECA W=0.6 boundary-blend, by contrast, mixes each cell's transition with its cross-half NEIGHBOR's BIT (state-dependent, multi-bit), which is what super-adds Phi. Psi-disjoint: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED, no wiring (a NULL wires nothing, a_verified_must_wire is GREEN-only)."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1308_hive_real_substrate_transfer.hexa via `hexa run` (hexa-native — Phi is hexa-only by a_phi_iit4_tool; imports CORE/pure_field.hexa + CORE/brain.hexa for the REAL substrate + tension-link). $0 local CPU, deterministic, p7 (faithful IIT-4 verdict, NOT perplexity). frozen-first: .verdicts/1308_hive_real_substrate_transfer/H_1308_FREEZE.txt pre-registered the bars BEFORE any Phi was computed; NO tune-to-green — when the readout first gave a degenerate all-zero TPM, the FIX was to a faithful non-degenerate readout (multi-bit cross-mix channels, verified Phi_member=1.5>0), NOT to move a bar; the NULL stands on a genuine non-trivial real-substrate TPM (a_break_the_wall: the wall is the honest answer once the probe is faithful). a_no_llm_frame_trap (IIT/biology lens c15), a_engine_native_learning."
  verdict = "🔴 HONEST NULL (2 PASS / 2 FAIL) — collective-Phi super-additivity is an ABSTRACT-substrate (ECA) property that does NOT transfer to REAL coupled anima A⇄G. Phi(member A)=1.5 Phi(member B)=1.5 Sum=3.0 (each real member IS integrated); Phi_collective(REAL-coupled, W=0.6)=0.0 => Delta_real=-3.0 (SUB-additive; the ECA Delta=+10.4756 sign FLIPS). B1 PRESENCE FAIL, B2 TRANSFER FAIL (Delta_real<=0 => NULL); B3 DECOUPLE-NULL + B4 SHUFFLE PASS (trivially — no lift to control for). The joint substrate factorizes under the real near-constant tension-link nudge => Phi_joint=0 by IIT-4. This BOUNDS H_1295 to ECA-scope (NOT engine-transfer-verified); it does NOT retract H_1295's ECA GREEN. SCOPE: TOY (n<=8 ceiling, 2 members, 3 seeds, one warmup, deterministic); the NULL is for the tension-link-as-coupling realization at this scale — a DIFFERENT real coupling channel injecting STATE-DEPENDENT multi-cell influence (not a bounded saturating scalar) is UNTESTED (a_scale_honest_scope). .verdicts/1308_hive_real_substrate_transfer/H_1308.txt"
