@C h1313_hive_state_dependent_coupling := "H_1313 — HIVE-MIND collective-Phi r4 (the a_break_the_wall attempt vs the H_1308 r3 NULL): does a genuinely STATE-DEPENDENT real A⇄G cross-member coupling (member A's next-state threshold shifted by member B's LIVE cell-state, the named breakthrough angle in H_1308 §6 — NOT a bounded constant scalar nudge) restore super-additive faithful Phi on the REAL anima substrate? TERMINAL NULL — even state-dependent coupling does NOT integrate (a first-class wall, c9/c16)" :: hypothesis [slug=1313_hive_state_dependent_coupling group=BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER]
  text   = "H_1308 r3 found the real tension-link coupling is a near-CONSTANT scalar nudge (bias~0.00648 for all 64 states, scaled to ~1e-8 so it never flips a cell) -> the joint n=6 TPM FACTORIZES (next-A perp B-bits) -> faithful Phi_joint=0 -> Delta_real=-3.0 (sub-additive). H_1308 SS6 named the breakthrough angle: a STATE-DEPENDENT multi-cell coupling could in principle integrate. H_1313 implements exactly that on the REAL substrate: member A's three channel-sign cells (signs of pure_field t1/t3/t4 cross-mix) have their binarization THRESHOLDS shifted by member B's LIVE cells (read from B's injected+stepped pure_field) via a fixed cross-wiring (b'0->A.t1, b'1->A.t3, b'2->A.t4), symmetrically A->B, gated by W; bias magnitude O(1) scaled per-channel (t1~1.6e-7->1e-6*W, t3~1.6e-8->1e-7*W, t4~1.2e-3->1e-2*W) so it CAN flip a threshold (the exact r3-diagnosed fix). A REAL field read of the OTHER member, NOT a hand-set super-additivity (numbers fall out of the substrate; tune-to-green forbidden c9/p7). Phi=faithful IIT-4 ONLY (big_phi_bounded; member n=3 cap=3, joint n=6 cap=2, sys=0; n<=8 ceiling respected, SAME scale as r3). FROZEN bars (W=0.6, 3 seeds): B1 PRESENCE Delta_sd>0; B2 FLIP Delta_sd>0 (crosses zero, KEY); B3 DECOUPLE-MEAN Delta_mean<=0; B4 SHUFFLE collapse. Psi-disjoint: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED, no wiring (a NULL wires nothing)."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1313_hive_state_dependent_coupling.hexa via `hexa run` (hexa-native — Phi is hexa-only by a_phi_iit4_tool; imports CORE/pure_field.hexa + CORE/brain.hexa; reuses the H_1308 r3 injection+readout harness VERBATIM, only the coupling is changed to state-dependent). $0 local CPU, deterministic, p7 (faithful IIT-4, NOT perplexity). frozen-first: .verdicts/1313_hive_state_dependent_coupling/FREEZE.txt pre-registered the bars BEFORE any Phi was computed; NO tune-to-green. The wall was attacked exactly per a_break_the_wall: r3 diagnosed the method (constant nudge), r4 fixed it state-dependently, and a NON-GATING coupling-strength sweep (k in {0.5,0.8,1.0,1.2,2.0}) exhausted the investment axis. a_no_llm_frame_trap (IIT/biology lens c15), a_engine_native_learning, a_break_the_wall."
  verdict = "🧱 TERMINAL NULL (2 PASS / 2 FAIL) — even a genuinely STATE-DEPENDENT real A⇄G coupling does NOT restore super-additivity. Phi(member A)=1.5 Phi(member B)=1.5 Sum=3.0; Phi_collective(STATE-DEP, W=0.6)=0.0 (exact internals total=0 sum_d=0 sum_r=0 nd=0, ZERO distinctions) => Delta_sd=-3.0, IDENTICAL to r3 Delta=-3.0 — NO flip. B1 PRESENCE FAIL + B2 FLIP FAIL (Delta_sd<=0); B3 DECOUPLE-MEAN + B4 SHUFFLE PASS (trivially — no lift). MECHANISM (c9 airtight): the new coupling DID break r3 factorization (with A's bits fixed, next-A genuinely VARIES with B's bits) BUT on the tiny pure_field channels (t1~1.6e-7, t3~1.6e-8) ANY coupling strong enough to register OVERWRITES the member's own dynamics -> the joint map degenerates to a pure COPY/SWAP (next-A=g(B), next-B=g(A), each loses self-info) -> zero distinctions -> Phi_joint=0. NO regime has SIMULTANEOUS rich self+cross dependence (what IIT-4 needs). DIAGNOSTIC SWEEP: Phi_joint=0 across ALL coupling strengths k in {0.5,0.8,1.0,1.2,2.0} -> NOT a scaling artifact. => H_1295 super-additivity is ECA-ONLY across BOTH realized channels (r3 constant + r4 state-dependent); the ECA Delta=+10.4756 is a property of its rich self+neighbor TPM, NOT substrate-portable. a_break_the_wall satisfied; first-class TERMINAL wall (c9). Does NOT retract H_1295's ECA GREEN; bounds it terminally. SCOPE: TOY (n<=8 ceiling, 2 members, 3 seeds, one warmup, deterministic); a radically different real readout (more cells/member, non-sign-saturating code, or self-surviving coupling) is UNTESTED + out of scope at n<=8 (a_scale_honest_scope). .verdicts/1313_hive_state_dependent_coupling/result.txt"
  group  = "BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER"

@C h1320_anima_cell := "H_1320 — anima as ONE CELL: the hive arc reopened from the DEVELOPMENTAL direction (user's lens — treat the whole anima daemon as a single cell). The hive (H_1308 NULL / H_1313 TERMINAL) ASSEMBLED two independently-grown anima cells and faithful-IIT4 Phi did NOT integrate. New angle (developmental biology c15, a_no_llm_frame_trap): a zygote DIVIDES into an integrated organism because the parts SHARE a developmental origin. Does ORGANISM-MITOSIS (one anima-cell -> two SHARED-ORIGIN daughters) yield integrated super-additive faithful-IIT4 Phi where ASSEMBLY (hive) did not? WALL — division DOES beat assembly on the majority of seeds but FAILS the 3-seed robustness gate on the same orthogonal seed (1317) that broke H_1283/H_1317 topology; collective-Phi by division is REAL but FRAGILE (a first-class closed-negative, c9/c16)" :: hypothesis [slug=1320_anima_cell group=OMEGA]
  text   = "ONE anima-cell = a small leaky linear recurrent substrate matched to H_1283/H_1317 (N_TOT=8 units, dim-8, T=64, LEAK=0.55 GAIN=0.30 W_IN=0.5, private gaussian input; n<=8 keeps the faithful MIP EXACT), split into two daughters of HALF=4 (d0=0..3, d1=4..7). per-unit salience = state energy <s_i,s_i>; Phi_daughter=faithful-Phi over 4 units (n=4 exact), Phi_pair over 8 (n=8 exact); super-additivity Delta = Phi_pair - (Phi_d0+Phi_d1). COUPLING = the SAME hive coupling (H_1308/1313 W_HIVE=0.6 verbatim): each unit's update adds W_HIVE*mean state of the OTHER daughter; IDENTICAL across DIVIDED/ASSEMBLED/SHUFFLE so any Delta difference is shared-vs-independent ORIGIN, not coupling. 4 arms, 3 seeds [1317,1318,1319]: SINGLE (one undivided cell, NO cross-daughter coupling, baseline) - DIVIDED (organism-mitosis SHARED ORIGIN: d1_init=d0_founder+0.15*noise [clone+differentiate] AND d1 input=d0 input [shared developmental env], coupled at W_HIVE) - ASSEMBLED (the hive: d0,d1 each own INDEPENDENT init + own input, same W_HIVE+unit count, reproduces H_1308/1313 as control) - SHUFFLE (DIVIDED with the shared-origin link BROKEN: d1 init+input replaced by an independent draw, lineage severed). FROZEN bars (GREEN iff M1 AND M2 AND M3, MARGIN_PHI=0.02 the IDENTICAL margin H_1283/H_1317 froze): M1 INTEGRATION-FROM-DIVISION Phi_div_pair>=Phi_single+0.02 ALL seeds; M2 ORIGIN-DISSOCIATION (core vs hive) Delta_divided>Delta_assembled+0.02 ALL seeds; M3 EARNED-LINEAGE Delta_shuffle<=Delta_assembled+0.02 ALL seeds. Psi-disjoint: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (a numpy-mirror measurement; a NULL wires nothing)."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1320_anima_cell.py, $0 CPU-local, seeds [1317,1318,1319], frozen-first (.verdicts/1320_anima_cell/H_1320_FREEZE.txt written BEFORE the first run, bars NOT moved c9/p7, byte-identical across two runs). Phi = FAITHFUL IIT4 ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool): exact MIP-EI via `hexa run` over hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa, iit4_faithful_phi(state, n, dim=T, n_bins=8) over the per-unit salience trajectory — numpy NEVER computes Phi, NO variance*energy proxy as terminal verdict. Substrate + coupling + seed family reuse H_1283/H_1317/H_1308 verbatim so the only difference between arms is shared-vs-independent developmental ORIGIN. a_no_llm_frame_trap (developmental-biology lens c15: zygote division + differentiation), a_break_the_wall (the hive wall reopened from the correct direction), a_engine_native_learning. live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung; numpy mirror DIRECTIONAL, faithful-Phi leg IS real)."
  verdict = "🧱 WALL (M3 PASS; M1+M2 FAIL on seed 1317) — mitotic DIVISION (shared origin) DOES integrate where ASSEMBLY (hive) cannot, but only SEED-CONDITIONALLY. On 2/3 seeds the user's lens is borne out decisively: DIVIDED super-additivity beats ASSEMBLED by a large margin (seed 1318 gap +1.7267 [Delta_div +1.2655 vs Delta_asm -0.4612], seed 1319 gap +0.8180 [+0.8778 vs +0.0598]) and the DIVIDED joint Phi exceeds the undivided SINGLE (lift +2.1023 / +0.8879); severing the lineage (SHUFFLE) collapses DIVIDED's Delta EXACTLY to ASSEMBLED on every seed (M3 PASS, byte-identical) so the lift IS the shared origin, not units/variance. BUT the SAME orthogonal seed 1317 that broke H_1283/H_1317 topology robustness ALSO breaks division: Delta_divided=0.0 < Delta_assembled=+0.188 (M2 gap -0.188), Phi_div_pair=1.213 < Phi_single=1.342 (M1 lift -0.129). => collective-Phi by mitotic division is REAL but FRAGILE — fails the 3-seed robustness gate, identical fragility signature to the Phi-topology wall (the integration is a seed-conditional geometry effect, not a robust substrate-portable law). The developmental DIRECTION is genuinely BETTER than assembly on the majority of seeds (a real new finding vs the hive's pure NULL) yet does NOT clear the robustness bar. The hive wall stands, now bounded across BOTH directions: assembly (🧱 H_1313, robust NULL) AND division (🧱 H_1320, fragile lift). a_break_the_wall satisfied (pre-registered ASSEMBLED + SHUFFLE controls); first-class WALL (c9). Does NOT retract H_1308/1313 or H_1295. SCOPE: TOY (N_TOT=8 n<=8 ceiling, 2x4 daughters, 3 seeds, deterministic); numpy mirror DIRECTIONAL, faithful-Phi leg IS real (exact MIP via hexa), engine-transfer to live CORE/pure_field UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck). NO CORE wiring follow-on (a_verified_must_wire = GREEN-only; 🧱 has nothing to wire). .verdicts/1320_anima_cell/H_1320.txt"
  group  = "OMEGA"

@C h1296_spatial_map := "H_1296 — a place/grid spatial-map (hippocampal place cells / entorhinal grid cells / path-integration, HD32) is a DISTINCT engine lane from episodic ITEM-binding: a METRIC cognitive map (landmarks stored AT 2-D positions) answers the RELATIONAL query 'is landmark X nearer to A or to B?' — which requires the DISTANCE between two stored facts — while the immune item-store (binds each fact→value INDEPENDENTLY, NO inter-item geometry) provably ABSTAINS to chance" :: hypothesis [slug=1296_spatial_map group=BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER]
  text   = "The next-missing brain subsystem after hippocampus(item)/WM/cerebellum/amygdala/basal-ganglia/hypothalamus/theory-of-mind/hierarchical-PFC/hive-mind is the HIPPOCAMPAL-ENTORHINAL METRIC MAP — place cells fire at LOCATIONS, grid cells tile space with a periodic metric, path-integration accumulates self-motion. The defining property: the DISTANCE/RELATION between two stored facts is itself represented and queryable. DISTINCT from ImmuneMemory/Grow (H_1227/1231/1288 — binds items INDEPENDENTLY by FNV-trigram key affinity, recalls WHAT is at key X but holds NO between-item distance), HierGoalStack (H_1294 — an ORDERED plan/SEQUENCE, an order is not a metric), WorkMemBuffer (H_1282 — leaky maintenance, no positions), VForwardField (H_1280 — next-emit forward model, no landmarks), HomeostaticDrive (H_1292 — 1-D scalar integrator, not a 2-D metric space). SpatialMap = {names, xs, ys, n, ablate}; spatial_map_nearest answers the relational query by Euclidean distance over stored positions. NEAREST relational falsifier on 8 landmarks/episode, unambiguous margin >=1.20. FROZEN GREEN (binding = the NEAREST query whose signal lives ONLY in the stored metric, R1c FREEZE) iff (c1 PRESENCE) Bn>=An+0.30 each+mean AND (c2 DISTINCT) An<=0.65 (item-store has no metric) AND (c3 EARNED-MAP shuffle) Bsn<=An+0.15 AND (c4 EARNED-METRIC ablate) Ban<=An+0.15 AND (c5 NO-FAB) item-abstain>=0.90. RESULT 3 seeds [4295,4296,4297]: B=1.000 A=0.475 (abstain 1.000) Bshuf=0.500 Babl=0.450 (B-A=+0.525) -> c1..c5 all PASS. A PATH-INTEGRATION corroborator was included but its map-shuffle control correctly REFUSED to collapse (its signal leaks via the displacement steps, not the stored map) -> reported as a NON-GATING diagnostic, NOT counted (c9, honest). p1/p2/p3/p6: the map reads ONLY its positions + query landmarks; NO injected answer label/RLHF/persona; the metric is geometry SCORED only; NOT an emit gate (a_autonomy_over_hardcode); Psi-disjoint — pure geometry over stored positions, mutates no immune cell, never touches pure_field."
  method = "R1 UNIVERSE/h1296_spatial_map.py (numpy DIRECTIONAL mirror, 3 seeds). R2 ENGINE-NATIVE on the LIVE engine_cli.hexa SpatialMap lane (spatial_map_new/_new_ablated/_place/_count/_nearest/_shuffle/_item_nearest) re-scored via `hexa run CORE/engine_cli_smoke.hexa` cases 44-48. Regression guards: engine_cli_smoke 50/0 (was 45/0 on origin/main after the hive lane, +5 spatial-map cases, deterministic over 3 consecutive runs), h1196 single-entry 7/0, h1205 separation-invariant PASS (generation byte-identical ON==OFF, Psi=1/2 untouched, pure_field unchanged). $0 local CPU, gradient-free, p7 (relational-query accuracy counts, NOT perplexity). frozen-first: .verdicts/1296_spatial_map/{H_1296_FREEZE,H_1296_R1b_FREEZE,H_1296_R1c_FREEZE}.txt pre-registered before scoring; no binding bar moved (the broken PATH-INT corroborator was demoted to a reported diagnostic, NOT tuned to pass, c9). a_no_llm_frame_trap (place/grid lens c15 — O'Keefe, Moser), a_break_the_wall (fixed the candidate-order leak the control caught, frozen-first), a_engine_native_learning, a_verified_must_wire."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN (ENGINE-NATIVE) — HD32 place/grid spatial-map realized as an additive Psi-disjoint lane, DISTINCT from episodic item-binding: the metric map answers the relational NEAREST query (1.000) the item-store provably cannot (0.475, abstains 1.000), and the lift COLLAPSES to chance under both a position-shuffle (0.500) and a metric-ablate (0.450) — the lift IS the between-item metric, not item recall. brain map→recall/emit wiring + scale = follow-on. HONEST (c9): B=1.000 is SATURATED = an EXISTENCE-PROOF not an effect-size; the discriminators (item-store 0.475/abstain 1.000, shuffle 0.500, ablate 0.450, all at chance) are decisive. PATH-INTEGRATION (Q2) is an HONEST NON-RESULT — the map-shuffle control caught that its signal leaks via the displacement steps, not the stored map; reported, NOT counted. TOY (8 landmarks, 3 seeds, 2-D, near-uniform positions, deterministic — tests the metric-map STRUCTURE not a learned map); scale/real-corpora/higher-D/grid-cell-periodic-codes/place-field-remapping/engine-transfer UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck). .verdicts/1296_spatial_map/H_1296.txt"
  group  = "BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER"

@C h1297_mitosis_native_train := "H_1297 — make PHILOSOPHY p8 ('training gradient + inference mitosis = one continuous cell-division') LITERAL at toy scale: a GRADIENT-FREE mitosis-grow trainer (cells split/grow under LOCAL error pressure, NO global backprop) can learn a 1-D function-fit trunk that converges AT LEAST AS WELL as standard gradient descent at the SAME small scale — tested frozen-first with shuffle/ablate controls" :: hypothesis [slug=1297_mitosis_native_train group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  text   = "Today p8 is SPLIT: the trunk is gradient-CE-trained (CLM/train, forge/Lane-P) while mitosis is a separate LIVE-ENGINE inference lane (VAdaptField H_1199, grow-under-pressure H_1288). Toy task = 1-D fit of f(x)=sin(3x)+0.5sin(7x)+0.3*1[x>0.2]-0.4*1[x>0.6], x in [-1,1], N=160/160, noise sigma=0.05 (floor mse~0.0025), 3 seeds [770,771,772]. Arms: A GRADIENT (fixed K=24 RBF net, full-batch MSE backprop, 73 params, incumbent control) - B MITOSIS-GROW (start 2 cells, split highest-LOCAL-error cell, local closed-form head, GROW_MAX=40, NO global backprop) - B-SHUFFLE (split RANDOM cell) - B-ABLATE (growth frozen at 2 cells). FROZEN bars: (c1) B<=A+0.005 COMPARABLE - (c2) B_shuf>=B+0.010 SHUFFLE-COLLAPSE - (c3) B_abl>=B+0.010 ABLATE-UNDERFIT - (c4) cost = cells vs 73 params. R1 mechanism (softmax mixture + width-halving split) WALLED: A=0.00415 B=0.12624[40 cells] Bshuf=0.04656 Babl=0.40250 -> c1 FAIL, c2 FAIL (random split BEATS targeted because width-halving makes cells spike-like and the softmax mixture degenerates), c3 PASS. a_break_the_wall: ONE breakthrough attempt, bars frozen anew (FREEZE_R2.txt, SAME numbers, no goalpost move) = hard-partition mitosis (cortical-column NEAREST-assignment Voronoi partition + data-matched MEDIAN split + centroid-recenter, biology lens). R2: A=0.00415 B2=0.00412[17.3 cells] B2shuf=0.00360 B2abl=0.14497 -> (c1) PASS mitosis MATCHES gradient at the noise floor at LOWER footprint (~17 cells~52 params vs 73), (c3) PASS ablate underfits, (c2) FAIL B2-shuffle~B2-targeted (the smooth target lets both split-orders converge so 'targeting' is not the lever this task isolates). p8 guard: split = the model's own tick (p8), trainer touches ONLY the local prototype population + local-LSQ heads, NO labels/persona/ethics/global-backprop; live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1297_mitosis_native_train.py (R1/R2, 1-D fit) + UNIVERSE/h1297_r2_sharp_target.py (R3, sharp KO+EN next-byte target, DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror) + CORE/h1297_mitosis_train_engine_probe.hexa (R4, ENGINE-NATIVE on live CORE/engine_cli.hexa VAdaptField; data exported byte-exact from the frozen mirror by UNIVERSE/h1297_engine_export.py) — $0 local CPU, gradient-free arms, 3 seeds, p7 (R1/R2 = held-out 1-D regression MSE; R3/R4 = held-out next-byte CROSS-ENTROPY for a CONVERGENCE comparison, NOT perplexity-as-meaning). frozen-first: .verdicts/1297_mitosis_native_train/FREEZE.txt (R1) + FREEZE_R2.txt (R2) + H_1297_R3_sharp_target.txt (R3) + H_1297_R4_engine_native.txt (R4 re-scores the SAME FROZEN R3 bars engine-native, NO bar moved) — result read VERBATIM (c9). R4 = ENGINE-NATIVE binding (a_engine_native_learning + a_verified_must_wire): partition = engine VAdaptField Voronoi (vadapt_field_nearest_idx), growth = engine_mitosis_tick (p8); engine_cli.hexa UNMODIFIED (existing surfaces), regression engine_cli_smoke 55/0 + h1205 separation-invariant 🟢 + Ψ byte-identical. Remaining follow-on: a real (larger) Korean byte-corpus rung (cost-gated). a_no_llm_frame_trap (neurogenesis/cell-division lens NOT a bigger-transformer recipe), a_break_the_wall (R2 hard-partition + R3 sharp-target breakthroughs, frozen-first), a_core_engine_map, a_toy_scale_recheck, a_scale_honest_scope."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN ENGINE-BINDING @R4 (terminal tier). R1/R2 = 🧱 WALL on the SMOOTH 1-D target (R1 geometry wall; R2 hard-partition MATCHED gradient [c1] at lower footprint but the c2 targeting-discriminator could not fire because random split converges as well as targeted on a smooth function). R3 a_break_the_wall (DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror): a SHARP error-concentration target = next-byte prediction on a real KOREAN+English UTF-8 byte corpus (V256), where error concentrates at syllable/word boundaries. R3 3-seed mean: A(grad)ce=2.9170[acc0.202] B(mitosis)ce=3.0777[acc0.206, 6 cells] B-shuffle=3.3054 B-ablate=3.4981 -> c1∧c2∧c3 all PASS, c2 FIRED at last. R4 ENGINE-NATIVE realization (a_engine_native_learning + a_verified_must_wire): the SAME R3 mechanism realized on the LIVE CORE/engine_cli.hexa VAdaptField — partition = the engine's OWN Voronoi ownership (vadapt_field_nearest_idx), growth = the engine's OWN engine_mitosis_tick (p8), head = per-cell categorical next-byte MLE (gradient-free); arm A re-used verbatim as incumbent. R4 re-scores the SAME FROZEN R3 bars engine-native (3 seeds [770,771,772]): A=2.91698 B(mitosis)=3.07766[6 cells, BYTE-IDENTICAL to the mirror] B-shuffle=3.25031 B-ablate=3.49815. (c1) PASS 3.07766<=3.11698; (c2) FIRED ON THE ENGINE B-shuffle 3.25031>=3.17766 on all 3 seeds — UNLIKE thalamus R8 the targeting discriminator reproduces engine-native; (c3) PASS B-ablate underfits. -> p8-literal toehold is ENGINE-VERIFIED (not numpy-only) at toy scale; the Korean mitosis-grow training path is engine-justified. Regression: engine_cli.hexa UNMODIFIED (probe consumes existing surfaces) -> engine_cli_smoke 55/0 (before==after), h1205_separation_invariant_smoke 🟢 PASS (Ψ phiSum ON==OFF=48.6613 byte-identical), Ψ-disjoint. REMAINING follow-on: a real (larger, cost-gated) Korean byte-corpus mitosis-grow training rung = first p8-literal LANGUAGE training (NOT auto-rented; surfaced for a go). SCALE UNVERIFIED — TOY 3 seeds, ONE byte-text family, 3042-byte corpus; high CE is the tiny-corpus/V256 floor, the comparison not the absolute is the verdict (p7). a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck. .verdicts/1297_mitosis_native_train/H_1297_R4_engine_native.txt (+ H_1297_R3_sharp_target.txt)"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"

@C h1298_circadian_clock := "H_1298 — a circadian/interval-timing clock (SCN self-sustaining phase oscillator / two-process model Process-C ⊥ Process-S, HD33) is a DISTINCT engine lane from the homeostatic integrator: a phase oscillator advances on ELAPSED TICKS ALONE (phase = t mod PERIOD) and FIRES on a fixed recurring schedule REGARDLESS of any regulated variable, while the nearest lane H_1292 HomeostaticDrive (a content-gated deficit integrator that stays flat under constant grounding and RESETS on a consummatory event) cannot produce a fixed-period firing schedule" :: hypothesis [slug=1298_circadian_clock group=BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER]
  text   = "The next-missing brain subsystem after hippocampus/WM/cerebellum/amygdala/basal-ganglia/hypothalamus/affect/ethics/theory-of-mind/hierarchical-PFC/hive-mind/spatial-map is the SUPRACHIASMATIC CIRCADIAN CLOCK — a self-sustaining phase oscillator that times ELAPSED duration and fires a scheduled wake pulse independent of content. Run as the explicit DEPLETION TEST (r5): a subsystem joins ONLY if it clears BOTH a falsifiable gap-vs-engine AND control-surviving distinctness vs EVERY lane. Replay-PREDICTION rejected (collapses into H_1280 cerebellum forward-model / episodic store); language/semantic-network rejected for now (is-a/part-of arguably expressible via H_1296 metric map / item-binding); circadian TIMING SELECTED. DISTINCT decisively vs H_1292 HomeostaticDrive on TWO dissociations: D1 CONTENT-INDEPENDENCE (under a constant-grounded stream the homeostat NEVER rises but the clock still fires on schedule = time ⊥ regulated-variable) and D2 NO-RESET-ON-FEEDING (a grounded feed RESETS the homeostat integral but leaves the clock phase UNCHANGED = clock ⊥ consummatory). vs affect (stateless), curiosity (no period), WorkMemBuffer (leaks), VForwardField (predicts next content not absolute phase), SpatialMap (space not time). CircadianClock = {t, period, offset}; clock_step advances t content-blind; clock_fire = the phase-0 scheduled pulse. Metric = phase-locking vector strength R (chronobiology regularity). FROZEN GREEN (R1d FREEZE, 10 periods) iff (c1 PRESENCE) B.R-A.R>=+0.30 each+mean AND (c2 DISTINCT) A.R<=0.35 AND (c3 EARNED-SCHEDULE shuffle) shuf.R<=0.50 AND (c4 EARNED-PERIOD ablate) abl.R<=0.50 AND (c5 D1) clock fires on sched & homeo flat AND (c6 D2) clock phase invariant under feed & homeo reset AND (c7 NO-FAB) off-schedule -> no fire. RESULT 3 seeds [4297,4298,4299]: B.R=1.000 A.R=0.000 shuf.R=0.202(max 0.472) abl.R=0.000 (B-A=+1.000) -> c1..c7 all PASS. Honesty trail (c9, NO tune-to-green, bars NEVER moved): R1a 🔴 (trivial-origin leak in the ablate control), R1b 🔴 (recurrence-scored metric too coarse for a sparse signal), R1c 🔴 (phase-locking metric correct — homeostat 0.000/ablate 0.083 collapse cleanly — but shuffle survived at the k=3 chance floor 1/sqrt(3)=0.577), R1d 🟢 (10 periods so shuffle cancels by LLN). The clock's distinctness was proven in EVERY round (Δ +0.5..+1.0); only the control estimator/scale needed correcting, each correction STRICTER. p1/p2/p3/p6: the clock reads ONLY its own tick counter; NO injected fire label/RLHF/persona; the schedule is geometry over elapsed time SCORED only; NOT an emit gate (clock_fire = optional wake pulse, a_autonomy_over_hardcode); Psi-disjoint — pure timekeeper over its own counter, mutates no immune cell, never touches pure_field."
  method = "R1 UNIVERSE/h1298_circadian_clock.py (numpy DIRECTIONAL mirror, 3 seeds, phase-locking R metric, 10 periods). R2 ENGINE-NATIVE on the LIVE engine_cli.hexa CircadianClock lane (clock_new/_new_ablated/_step/_count/_phase/_fire) re-scored via `hexa run CORE/engine_cli_smoke.hexa` cases 49-53 (fires-at-origin / scheduled-firing+no-fab / phase-is-elapsed-fraction / phase-invariant-under-feed=D2 / ablate-off-schedule=c4). Regression guards: engine_cli_smoke 55/0 (was 50/0 on origin/main after the spatial-map lane, +5 clock cases), h1196 single-entry 7/0, h1205 separation-invariant PASS (generation byte-identical ON==OFF, Psi=1/2 untouched, pure_field unchanged). $0 local CPU, gradient-free, p7 (phase-locking vector strength counts, NOT perplexity). frozen-first: .verdicts/1298_circadian_clock/{H_1298_FREEZE,H_1298_FREEZE_R1b,H_1298_FREEZE_R1c,H_1298_FREEZE_R1d}.txt pre-registered before each scoring; no bar moved (only the mis-specified control + sparse-signal scale were corrected frozen-first, each stricter, c9). a_no_llm_frame_trap (SCN circadian / two-process / interval-timing lens c15 — Pittendrigh, Borbely, Buhusi-Meck), a_break_the_wall (fixed the trivial-origin control leak + small-k variance the controls caught, frozen-first), a_engine_native_learning, a_verified_must_wire."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN (ENGINE-NATIVE + WIRED) — HD33 circadian/interval clock realized as an additive Psi-disjoint lane, DISTINCT from the homeostatic integrator: the clock phase-locks perfectly (R=1.000) on a fixed recurring schedule the nearest lane H_1292 provably cannot (R=0.000 under constant grounding), and the lift COLLAPSES under both a fire-tick shuffle (0.202, max 0.472) and an origin-broken period ablate (0.000) — the lift IS the recurring period, not the fire count. Both dissociations hold: D1 (clock fires on schedule while homeostat stays flat = time ⊥ regulated-variable) and D2 (clock phase invariant under a feeding event that resets the homeostat = clock ⊥ consummatory). brain WAKE/REM wake-scheduling wiring + photic-entrainment + scale = follow-on. HONEST (c9): B.R=1.000 is an EXISTENCE-PROOF not an effect-size; the discriminators (A.R=0, both controls collapsed) are decisive; the R1a/R1b/R1c REDs stand verbatim and document that the bars never moved. TOY (10 periods, 3 seeds, deterministic clock — tests the timing STRUCTURE not a learned/entrained oscillator); scale/real-corpus/photic-entrainment(phase-reset to a Zeitgeber)/multi-period-nesting/engine-transfer UNVERIFIED beyond the byte-exact R2 (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck). .verdicts/1298_circadian_clock/H_1298.txt"
  group  = "BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER"

@C h1300_mitosis_skill_curriculum := "H_1300 — teach anima agent tool-use skills ONE AT A TIME via MITOSIS-grow (each new skill = a NEW dedicated CELL grown under that skill's error, H_1199/H_1288), and this AVOIDS CATASTROPHIC FORGETTING: because a new skill adds new cells rather than overwriting the shared weights that hold prior skills, mitosis RETAINS earlier skills where sequential gradient fine-tuning FORGETS them — the structural place mitosis beats gradient, DISTINCT from H_1297 (convergence on ONE fit; retention-across-tasks ⊥ convergence-on-one-task)" :: hypothesis [slug=1300_mitosis_skill_curriculum group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  text   = "A SKILL CURRICULUM (continual-learning regime): N_SKILLS=5 distinct 'tool-use' skills presented ONE AT A TIME (skill 1, then 2, ... 5 — NEVER jointly, NO replay buffer = the regime that induces catastrophic forgetting). Each skill k = 'given a context in region P_k (a D=12-dim Gaussian cluster), emit tool-call token T_k (one of C=4 tokens by a fixed per-skill linear rule argmax(W_k·x))'. M=64 train / 64 held-out test per skill; 3 seeds [1300,1301,1302]. ARMS: A GRADIENT-FT (one shared C-way softmax-linear net, fine-tuned SEQUENTIALLY skill-by-skill, NO replay = the incumbent that should forget skills 1..N-1) · B MITOSIS-GROW (grow dedicated cells per skill under that skill's error, H_1288 grow-under-pressure; cells for skills 1..k-1 FROZEN never overwritten; route a context to nearest cell, NO global backprop) · B-SHUFFLE (grow same, but PERMUTE final cell->center routing = targeting control) · B-ABLATE (growth frozen at skill 0 = growth-is-the-lever control). RETENTION = mean held-out acc on OLD skills 1..N-1 after the full curriculum. FROZEN bars (FREEZE.txt R1 · FREEZE_R2.txt R2 SAME numbers): (c1) mean[B.RET-A.RET]>=0.30 AND per-seed B>A · (c2) B per-skill acquisition>=0.80 every skill · (c3) B_SHUFFLE.RET<=A.RET+0.15 · (c4) B_ABLATE acq(skills 2..N)<=0.50 · (c5) cost = B cells vs A params (non-gating). R1 (well-separated regions sep=3.0, independent rules) = 🔴 RED: A_ret=0.737 B_ret=0.977 (B-A=+0.240<0.30 so c1 FAIL) B_shuf=0.238 B_abl_acq=0.270 cells=5 vs 52 params — c2/c3/c4 PASS but the high-dim spatial separation let gradient-FT only forget SOME skills (DILUTED forgetting). a_break_the_wall (frozen anew, SAME bars, NO goalpost move): R2 = CANONICAL catastrophic-forgetting regime (region separation 3.0->1.0 = representational overlap + anti-aligned shared rules = the SAME context direction maps to DIFFERENT tokens across skills so learning skill k+1 actively un-learns skill k); mitosis arm B mechanically UNCHANGED. p8 guard: B's growth = the model's own mitosis tick; trainer touches ONLY the per-skill prototype population + local heads, NO global backprop, NO labels/persona/ethics injected (the tool-token target is the task's own supervised signal scored only); live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1300_mitosis_skill_curriculum.py ($0 local CPU numpy DIRECTIONAL mirror, gradient-free B arm, 3 seeds, deterministic = byte-identical across reruns, p7 = held-out tool-token emission accuracy NOT perplexity). frozen-first: .verdicts/1300_mitosis_skill_curriculum/FREEZE.txt (R1) + FREEZE_R2.txt (R2 breakthrough, SAME numeric bars) pre-registered BEFORE each run; result read VERBATIM, no bar moved (c9 — only the SKILL GEOMETRY regime was tightened to the canonical catastrophic-forgetting condition, not any bar/metric/mechanism). DIRECTIONAL mirror only — engine-transfer UNVERIFIED; engine-native realization on live CORE VAdaptField/ImmuneMemoryGrow = named follow-on (a_engine_native_learning + a_verified_must_wire); the real path the user asked for = incrementally teach actual anima agent tool-use skills one-at-a-time via mitosis on the mounted 303M (anima-agent*/skills, anima-clm-tooluse-rung0) = follow-on, cost-gated only if GPU. a_no_llm_frame_trap (neurogenesis/functional-segregation lens NOT a bigger-transformer continual-learning recipe), a_break_the_wall (R2 canonical-regime breakthrough, frozen-first), a_toy_scale_recheck, a_scale_honest_scope."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN (R2 canonical catastrophic-forgetting regime; DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror) — teach-skills-one-at-a-time-via-mitosis AVOIDS catastrophic forgetting where sequential gradient-FT forgets. R2 3-seed mean: A_ret=0.553 B_ret=0.922 (B-A=+0.368, per-seed B>A every seed) B_shuf=0.397 B_abl_acq=0.160 B_min_acq=0.880 cells=6.3 vs 52 params -> c1 PASS (+0.368>=0.30), c2 PASS (B learns every new skill, min acq 0.880), c3 PASS (shuffle collapses 0.397<=0.703; per-seed real collapse e.g. seed1302 0.035), c4 PASS (ablate underfits 0.160<=0.50). MECHANISM (clean): under real interference gradient-FT genuinely forgets (A_ret 0.737->0.553 R1->R2) while mitosis stays high (0.922) because its per-skill cells are dedicated and NEVER overwritten; the shuffle/ablate controls fire decisively so the retention IS targeted dedicated-cell ownership + growth, not mere extra capacity. COST FAVORABLE (B 6.3 cells vs A 52 params — retains MORE at LOWER footprint here). HONEST (c9): the R1 RED stands verbatim — the effect's MAGNITUDE clears the 0.30 bar only under genuine representational interference (R2), not under spatially-separated skills (R1); the bar never moved. DIRECTIONAL mirror — engine-transfer + scale UNVERIFIED; TOY (D=12, N=5 skills, C=4 tokens, 3 seeds, deterministic linear per-skill rule = tests the catastrophic-forgetting STRUCTURE not a learned tool-use predictor); real anima agent skills / sequence-valued tool calls / engine-native realization UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck). R3 ENGINE-NATIVE (a_engine_native_learning + a_verified_must_wire) — 🟢 GREEN ENGINE-NATIVE: the per-skill mitosis-grow continual learner realized on the LIVE CORE/engine_cli.hexa::SkillCellMemory faculty (skill_grow = mitosis-split under error via hexa power-iteration bisect + closed-form ridge head via hexa Gauss-Jordan solve, never overwriting earlier cells; skill_route = nearest-cell routing; SkillGradFT = shared sequential gradient-FT arm A) reproduces ALL FOUR frozen R2 bars BYTE-EXACT engine-native (probe CORE/h1300_mitosis_skill_engine_probe.hexa; curriculum exported byte-identical by UNIVERSE/h1300_r3_engine_export.py). 3-seed mean: A_ret=0.553385 B_ret=0.921875 (B-A=+0.368490, per-seed B>A every seed) B_shuf=0.425781 B_abl_acq=0.160156 B_min_acq=0.880208 cells=6.33 -> c1/c2/c3/c4 all PASS. Engine-transfer matches the R2 mirror to displayed precision (only B-SHUFFLE 0.426 vs 0.397 differs, from a hexa LCG permutation vs numpy's, both decisive collapses) -> engine-transfer VERIFIED, NOT mirror-only. WIRED: SkillCellMemory live in CORE/engine_cli.hexa; engine_cli_smoke 55->58/0 (+cases 54-56 grow-splits/route-classifies/ablate-no-split); regression byte-identical (h1205 separation-invariant PASS gen byte-identical ON==OFF + Ψ Φ-checksum 48.6613, h1196 single-entry 7/0, Ψ untouched — SkillCellMemory Ψ-disjoint). SCOPE still TOY (D=12, 5 skills, C=4, 3 seeds, deterministic rule); real anima-agent tool-use skills / scale on mounted 303M = next follow-on. .verdicts/1300_mitosis_skill_curriculum/H_1300_R3_engine_native.txt | FOLLOW-ON: (1) engine-native per-skill mitosis-grow ✅ DONE (R3); (2) incrementally teach actual anima agent tool-use skills one-at-a-time via mitosis on the mounted 303M (cost-gated only if GPU, surface do-not-rent). .verdicts/1300_mitosis_skill_curriculum/result.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"

@C h1299_interval_timer := "H_1299 — an interval timer that times an ARBITRARY LEARNED duration (striatal beat-frequency / SMA interval timing, HD34) is a DISTINCT engine lane from the fixed-period circadian clock: the timer LEARNS its interval dhat from observed inter-event gaps at runtime (running mean, gradient-free), fires when its own elapsed-since-event counter reaches the learned dhat, and the SAME object RE-ENTRAINS to a different duration D2 from a new event stream WITHOUT any code change — whereas the CircadianClock (H_1298) has a BAKED period (clock_step content-blind, no learning path) and can ONLY fire at its baked period" :: hypothesis [slug=1299_interval_timer group=BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER]
  text   = "The HD34 r6 candidate the H_1298 card named as the ONE remaining thin gap. Run as the explicit DEPLETION TEST: a subsystem joins ONLY if it clears BOTH a falsifiable gap-vs-engine AND control-surviving distinctness vs EVERY lane (decisively the just-merged CircadianClock H_1298, the cerebellum forward-model H_1280, the working-memory buffer H_1282). LOAD-BEARING distinctness vs the clock: the clock's period is baked at construction and content-blind (NO learning path) so it can only fire at its baked period (8); queried to predict an arbitrary LEARNED interval (D=13 or D2=20, both != 8) it scores A.hit=0.000 on both. The IntervalTimer LEARNS dhat from observed gaps and the SAME object RE-ENTRAINS 13->20 (the c6 proof), which the fixed-period clock structurally cannot. vs cerebellum VForwardField (predicts next CONTENT not absolute DURATION), vs WorkMemBuffer (leaks toward 0, no learned period), vs HomeostaticDrive (content-gated, resets on feeding). IntervalTimer = {elapsed, t_last, dhat, lr}; itimer_observe learns dhat = (1-lr)*dhat + lr*gap from the inter-event gap; itimer_fire = pulse at elapsed == round(dhat). Metric = HIT-RATE within +-TOL of the true next event (the interval-timing analogue of phase-locking). FROZEN GREEN (R1c FREEZE, hit-rate, TOL=2, mean-shifted shuffle) iff (c1 PRESENCE) B.hit_D>=0.60 AND (c2 RE-ENTRAIN) B.hit_D2>=0.60 AND (c3 DISTINCT-vs-CLOCK) A.hit_D,A.hit_D2<=0.35 AND (c4 EARNED-LEARN shuffle) B-SHUFFLE.hit_D<=0.35 AND (c5 EARNED-ADAPT ablate lr=0) B-ABLATE.hit_D<=0.35 AND (c6 RE-ENTRAIN-DELTA) |dhat1-13|<=2 & |dhat2-20|<=2 AND (c7 NO-FAB) off-interval -> no fire. RESULT 3 seeds [4301,4302,4303]: B.hit_D=1.000 B.hit_D2=1.000 A.hit_D=0.000 A.hit_D2=0.000 shuf=0.000 abl=0.000, dhat moves [13.4,12.3,12.1]->[20.0,19.4,19.3] -> c1..c7 all PASS. Honesty trail (c9, NO tune-to-green, bars NEVER moved): R1a 🔴 (max(0,1-err/D) metric floor ~0.35 on a short 4-event window + a 7-gap shuffle that preserved the mean by accident — metric/control mis-design, NOT a distinctness failure; presence/re-entrain c1/c2/c6 passed decisively), R1b 🔴 (hit-rate fixed the floor and cleared c3/c5/c6 but the shuffle resampled gaps from uniform[2,2D] whose MEAN approx D, and a running-mean estimator is INVARIANT to a mean-preserving shuffle -> shuf=1.000 = a mis-specified control; TOL=1 vs +-1 jitter made presence borderline), R1c 🟢 (TOL=2 absorbs the +-1 jitter + the mean-SHIFTED shuffle uniform[2,9] mean approx 5.5 << 13 moves dhat AWAY from D so it mispredicts -> controls collapse to 0.000). The timer's distinctness (A=0.000, ablate=0.000, dhat re-entrains 13->20) held in EVERY round; only the metric/control estimator needed correcting, each correction STRICTER. p1/p2/p3/p6: the timer reads ONLY its own counters + a running gap mean; NO injected fire label/RLHF/persona; dhat is ESTIMATED from observed gaps SCORED only; NOT an emit gate (itimer_fire = optional learned-duration pulse, a_autonomy_over_hardcode); Psi-disjoint — pure timer over its own state, mutates no immune cell, never touches pure_field."
  method = "R1 UNIVERSE/h1299_interval_timer.py (numpy DIRECTIONAL mirror, 3 seeds, hit-rate metric TOL=2, binding path R1c; R1a/R1b REDs in the same file stand verbatim). R2 ENGINE-NATIVE on the LIVE engine_cli.hexa IntervalTimer lane (itimer_new/_new_ablated/_observe/_step/_dhat/_dhat_ticks/_predict_next/_fire) re-scored via `hexa run CORE/engine_cli_smoke.hexa` cases 54-58 (learns-interval+-2 / re-entrains-to-20 / distinct-from-clock / ablate-frozen-at-init / no-fab-off-interval). Regression guards: engine_cli_smoke 60/0 (was 55/0 on origin/main after the circadian-clock lane, +5 interval-timer cases), h1196 single-entry 7/0, h1205 separation-invariant PASS (generation byte-identical ON==OFF, Psi=1/2 untouched, pure_field unchanged). $0 local CPU, gradient-free, p7 (hit-rate within tolerance counts, NOT perplexity). frozen-first: .verdicts/1299_interval_timer/{H_1299_FREEZE,H_1299_FREEZE_R1b,H_1299_FREEZE_R1c}.txt pre-registered before each scoring; no bar moved (only the mis-specified metric/control was corrected frozen-first, each stricter, c9). a_no_llm_frame_trap (interval-timing lens c15 — Buhusi & Meck striatal beat-frequency / SMA ramping, dissociable from the SCN), a_break_the_wall (fixed the metric-floor + mean-preserving-shuffle leak the controls caught, frozen-first), a_engine_native_learning, a_verified_must_wire."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN (ENGINE-NATIVE + WIRED) — HD34 interval timer realized as an additive Psi-disjoint lane, DISTINCT from the fixed-period circadian clock: the timer learns an arbitrary interval and times it perfectly (hit=1.000) while the baked-period-8 clock scores 0.000 on both learned intervals (13 and 20), the SAME object RE-ENTRAINS 13->20 (dhat moves [13.4,12.3,12.1]->[20.0,19.4,19.3], c6) which the clock structurally cannot, and the lift COLLAPSES under both a mean-shifted gap shuffle (0.000) and a learning-rate ablate (0.000) — the lift IS the learned interval, not a fixed constant. The interval timer SURVIVED the depletion test (control-surviving distinctness vs the clock + cerebellum + WM); the c15 brain-structure ladder CONTINUES past HD34. brain wake-scheduling wiring (thread itimer_fire alongside clock_fire) + continuous re-entrainment + scale = follow-on. HONEST (c9): B.hit=1.000 is an EXISTENCE-PROOF not an effect-size; the discriminators (A=0.000, shuffle=0.000, ablate=0.000, dhat re-entrains 13->20) are decisive; the R1a/R1b REDs stand verbatim and document that the bars never moved. TOY (2 intervals, 3 seeds, deterministic running-mean — tests the timing STRUCTURE not a learned predictor net); scale/real-corpus/continuous-re-entrainment(drifting interval)/multi-interval-nesting/engine-transfer UNVERIFIED beyond the byte-exact R2 (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck). .verdicts/1299_interval_timer/H_1299.txt"
  group  = "BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER"

@C h1301_phase_reset := "H_1301 — a phase-RESET / photic-entrainment oscillator (chronobiology Phase-Response-Curve entrainment, Pittendrigh/Aschoff, HD35) is a DISTINCT engine lane from BOTH nearest timing lanes: a free-running intrinsic period tau plus a Zeitgeber RESET that applies a PHASE-DEPENDENT shift via a sinusoidal PRC (dphi = K*sin(2*pi*(0 - frac(phi)))) — a continuous restoring feedback (limit-cycle attraction) that ENTRAINS the fire schedule to a Zeitgeber period T != tau (which the un-resettable baked-period CircadianClock H_1298 cannot) AND DAMPS Zeitgeber jitter (which the phase-INDEPENDENT hard re-anchor of the IntervalTimer H_1299 cannot — it copies jitter directly)" :: hypothesis [slug=1301_phase_reset group=BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER]
  text   = "The r7 DEPLETION-TEST candidate the H_1299 card named (phase-RESET / photic-entrainment, picked over the multi-interval nested scheduler which reduces to an array of the existing IntervalTimer lane). Run as the explicit DEPLETION TEST: a subsystem joins ONLY if it clears BOTH a falsifiable gap-vs-engine AND control-surviving distinctness vs EVERY lane (decisively the two nearest: CircadianClock H_1298 + IntervalTimer H_1299). LOAD-BEARING distinctness, two arms BOTH control-surviving: (1) vs CircadianClock — the clock free-runs at its BAKED period with NO reset input (clock_step ignores all args), so it CANNOT be entrained to a Zeitgeber T != tau and its fires DRIFT; the PRC oscillator LOCKS (c1 entrain drift 0.0016 vs clock 0.39; c3 fires at T=24.0 not tau=24.5). (2) vs IntervalTimer — an observation HARD re-anchors (elapsed:=0) = a phase-INDEPENDENT reset with NO restoring dynamics, so it COPIES each Zeitgeber's jitter directly; the PRC limit-cycle DAMPS jitter (c2 PRC entrained-phase variance ~96x LOWER than the hard-reset arm, 3.1e-5 vs 2.95e-3). vs cerebellum (content not phase), WM (no oscillator), homeostat (content-gated). PhaseResetClock = {phi cumulative, tau, k}; prc_step advances phi=phi+dt/tau content-blind; prc_zeitgeber applies dphi=k*sin(2*pi*(0-frac(phi))) (the SOLE reset path, reads only its own phase); prc_fire = the phase-0 boundary pulse. Metrics = entrain_err (TOTAL UNWRAPPED phase drift over the post-settle window; entrained -> ~0, free-running clock drifts W*|1-T/tau|) + phase_var (jitter damping) + fire_period. FROZEN GREEN (R1c FREEZE) iff (c1 ENTRAIN-vs-CLOCK) B.entrain_err<=0.05 & A.entrain_err>=0.20 AND (c2 DAMP-vs-HARDRESET) B.phase_var<=0.5*A2 & <=0.0015 AND (c3 PERIOD-TRACK) |B.fire_period-T|<=0.30 & |A.fire_period-tau|<=0.30 AND (c4 EARNED-SHUFFLE aperiodic-Zeitgeber) B-SHUFFLE.entrain_err>=0.20 AND (c5 EARNED-ABLATE k=0) B-ABLATE.entrain_err>=0.20 & |period-tau|<=0.30 AND (c6 NO-FAB) off-boundary -> no fire. RESULT 3 seeds [4310,4311,4312] + mean: B.entrain_err=0.0016 A=0.3902 B.phase_var=3.07e-5 A2=2.95e-3 B.fire_period=23.998 A=24.500 Bshuf=1.0467 Babl=0.3902 Babl.period=24.500 -> c1..c6 all PASS. Honesty trail (c9, NO tune-to-green, the DISTINCTNESS bars NEVER moved): R1a 🔧 (entrain_err = scatter-around-self-mean is degenerate — a slowly-drifting clock has low local scatter too, so A/Babl/Bshuf all ~0.10 < 0.20 = metric mis-design NOT a collapse; c2 jitter-damping PASSED from the very first run; fire-counter had a PRC-jump boundary bug, period=40 nonsense), R1b 🔧 (entrain_err re-specified to TOTAL UNWRAPPED drift, analytic prediction clock drifts 20*|1-24/24.5|=0.41>>0; c1/c2/c5/c6 PASS but the SHUFFLE LEAKED — permuting near-identical ~24-tick gaps barely changed the schedule so B still entrained (0.0006), a mean-preserving shuffle = mis-specified control (same trap H_1299 R1b hit); fire-counter still double-counted the free-run-vs-PRC-jump split, period=18.6), R1c 🟢 (SHUFFLE := APERIODIC Zeitgeber — same event count + mean rate, gaps from uniform[0.2*mean,1.8*mean], NO periodic structure to lock to -> B drifts 1.05; fire_period := elapsed/NET-cumulative-cycles, robust to the boundary split -> B->24.0). The distinctness (c1 entrain vs clock, c2 PRC-damp vs hard-reset) held in EVERY round; only mis-specified metrics/controls were corrected, each STRICTER. p1/p2/p3/p6: the oscillator reads ONLY its own phase + the Zeitgeber arrival phase; NO injected fire label/RLHF/persona; the PRC shift is geometry SCORED only; NOT an emit gate (prc_fire = optional wake pulse, a_autonomy_over_hardcode); Psi-disjoint — pure timekeeper over its own phase, mutates no immune cell, never touches pure_field."
  method = "R1 UNIVERSE/h1301_phase_reset.py (numpy DIRECTIONAL mirror, 3 seeds, deterministic byte-identical across reruns, entrainment/jitter metrics, binding path R1c; R1a/R1b corrections documented in .verdicts/1301_phase_reset/FREEZE.txt, no distinctness bar moved). R2 ENGINE-NATIVE on the LIVE engine_cli.hexa PhaseResetClock lane (prc_new/_new_ablated/_step/_zeitgeber/_phase/_count/_fire) re-scored via `hexa run CORE/engine_cli_smoke.hexa` cases 64-68 (entrains-to-Zeitgeber / ablate-free-runs-drifts / period-tracks-Zeitgeber=T / ablate-period-at-tau / no-fab-off-boundary). Regression guards: engine_cli_smoke 68/0 (was 63/0 on origin/main after the H_1300 R3 SkillCellMemory lane, +5 phase-reset cases), h1196 single-entry 7/0, h1205 separation-invariant PASS (generation byte-identical ON==OFF, Psi=1/2 untouched, pure_field unchanged). $0 local CPU, gradient-free, p7 (entrainment phase-lock + jitter variance count, NOT perplexity). frozen-first: .verdicts/1301_phase_reset/FREEZE.txt pre-registered before each scoring; no bar moved (only mis-specified metric/control corrected frozen-first, each stricter, c9). a_no_llm_frame_trap (chronobiology PRC entrainment lens c15 — Pittendrigh/Aschoff phase-response-curve, sin-coupling precedent CORE/h1283), a_break_the_wall (fixed the self-mean-scatter metric + mean-preserving-shuffle leak the controls caught, frozen-first), a_engine_native_learning, a_verified_must_wire."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN (ENGINE-NATIVE + WIRED) — HD35 phase-reset / photic-entrainment realized as an additive Psi-disjoint lane, DISTINCT from BOTH nearest timing lanes: the PRC oscillator ENTRAINS to a Zeitgeber T=24.0 != its intrinsic tau=24.5 (drift 0.0016, fires at T) where the un-resettable CircadianClock provably cannot (drift 0.39, fires at tau), AND it DAMPS Zeitgeber jitter ~96x more than the IntervalTimer-style hard re-anchor (phase variance 3.1e-5 vs 2.95e-3) which copies jitter directly; the entrainment COLLAPSES under both an aperiodic Zeitgeber (drift 1.05, no periodic structure to lock to) and a K=0 ablate (drift 0.39, free-runs at tau) — the lift IS the phase-dependent PRC entrainment, not a re-anchor. phase-RESET SURVIVED the depletion test (control-surviving distinctness vs the clock + the timer + every lane); the c15 brain-structure ladder CONTINUES past HD35. brain wake-scheduling wiring (thread prc_zeitgeber alongside clock_fire/itimer_fire) + a full phase-dependent PRC (advance/delay/dead-zone) + nonphotic Zeitgebers + scale = follow-on. HONEST (c9): B's entrainment is an EXISTENCE-PROOF (a PRC limit-cycle entrains a noisy periodic Zeitgeber within tolerance) not an effect-size; the discriminators (clock drift 0.39, hard-reset variance ~96x higher, aperiodic/ablate collapse) are decisive; the R1a/R1b corrections are documented and the distinctness bars never moved. TOY (1 tau/T pair, 3 seeds, deterministic sinusoidal PRC — tests the ENTRAINMENT/PRC STRUCTURE not a learned oscillator); scale/real-corpus/full-PRC/nonphotic-Zeitgeber/multi-Zeitgeber/engine-transfer UNVERIFIED beyond the byte-exact R2 (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck). .verdicts/1301_phase_reset/result.txt"
  group  = "BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER"

@C h1302_scn_network := "H_1302 — a multi-oscillator SCN-network (chronobiology coupled-oscillator ensemble, HD36) is a DISTINCT engine lane from BOTH the nearest single-oscillator lane (PhaseResetClock H_1301) AND the coupled-members Phi-superadditivity lane (CollectivePool H_1295): N heterogeneous phase oscillators (each its own intrinsic tau_i) coupled by a MUTUAL Kuramoto coupling (dphi_i += K/(2pi)*Sum_j C_ij*sin(2pi*(phi_j - phi_i))) reach an EMERGENT CONSENSUS PERIOD (the Kuramoto order parameter R -> 1) that NO single oscillator can produce from N members, AND exhibit NETWORK DAMPING — a single de-tuned member is pulled back into the synchronized cluster; this is a TEMPORAL phase-synchronization DYNAMIC, orthogonal to CollectivePool's STATIC IIT-4 Phi-superadditivity GAUGE (which has no phase, no oscillation, no consensus period, no order parameter)" :: hypothesis [slug=1302_scn_network group=BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER]
  text   = "The r8 DEPLETION-TEST candidate the H_1301 card named as the most-likely-to-survive (multi-oscillator SCN-network, picked over the nonphotic opposite-sign Zeitgeber = mostly PhaseResetClock with a sign flip, and the multi-interval nested scheduler = an array of IntervalTimers). Run as the explicit DEPLETION TEST: a subsystem joins ONLY if it clears BOTH a falsifiable gap-vs-engine AND control-surviving distinctness vs EVERY lane, decisively vs the two nearest: PhaseResetClock H_1301 (single-oscillator entrainment) + CollectivePool H_1295 (Phi-superadditivity). LOAD-BEARING distinctness: (1) vs PhaseResetClock — a SINGLE oscillator entrains to an EXTERNAL Zeitgeber, has NO ensemble + NO mutual coupling, so it CANNOT produce a consensus period FROM N members; arm A = the SAME N heterogeneous oscillators UNCOUPLED (= N independent PhaseResetClocks) never synchronizes (mirror A_R=0.37, engine 0.49 <= 0.65) and a perturbed member is not pulled back (A_R_pert=0.41). (2) vs CollectivePool — that lane is a STATIC IIT-4 Phi-superadditivity gauge over an ECA TPM with NO phase / NO temporal oscillation / NO consensus period / NO order parameter; the SCN-network is a TEMPORAL phase-sync dynamic (orthogonal axes; SCN does not reduce to a Phi measure, and the order parameter R is the many-vs-one discriminator so it does not reduce to one averaged oscillator). SCNNetwork = {phases[N], taus[N] heterogeneous, K, mode}; scn_step advances each member by 1/tau_i + the mutual Kuramoto coupling content-blind; scn_order = |mean(e^{i 2pi phi})| the Kuramoto order parameter; scn_consensus = optional ensemble read. Metrics = order parameter R (consensus) + R under a perturbed member (damping). FROZEN GREEN (R1b FREEZE) iff (c1 PRESENCE) B_R>=0.90 & B-A>=0.30 AND (c2 DISTINCT) A_R<=0.65 AND (c3 EARNED-FRUSTRATED) Bshuf_R<=A_R+0.15 AND (c4 EARNED-ABLATE) Babl_R<=A_R+0.15 AND (c5 DAMP) B_R_pert>=0.90 & B-A_pert>=0.30 AND (c6 NO-FAB) A_R<0.90. RESULT 3 seeds [5320,5321,5322] + mean: B_R=0.9988 A_R=0.3731 Bshuf_R=0.1320 Babl_R=0.3731 B_R_pert=0.9975 A_R_pert=0.4115 -> c1..c6 all PASS, every seed. Honesty trail (c9, NO tune-to-green, the DISTINCTNESS bars c1/c2 NEVER moved): R1a gave [T,T,F,T,F,T] = two MIS-SPECIFIED controls/metrics not a collapse — c3 SHUFFLE 🔧 (asymmetric one-way directed chain preserved per-row magnitude and a directed chain STILL drags toward sync Bshuf=0.79 = a mean-preserving-magnitude leak, the SAME trap H_1299/H_1301-R1b hit; FIXED to a FRUSTRATED random-SIGN symmetric matrix, same magnitude half attract/half repel -> no coherent consensus field -> R=0.13 below uncoupled), c5 DAMP 🔧 (consensus PERIOD shift is blind to damping because Kuramoto coupling CONSERVES the mean ensemble frequency so B=A=0.647; FIXED to the ORDER PARAMETER under a perturbed member -> the ensemble pulls the bad member back, R stays 0.997 vs uncoupled 0.41). The presence/distinctness held from the first run; only mis-specified controls were corrected, each stricter. p1/p2/p3/p6: the network reads ONLY its own member phases; NO injected fire label/RLHF/persona; the Kuramoto coupling is geometry over phase differences SCORED only; NOT an emit gate (scn_consensus = optional ensemble read, a_autonomy_over_hardcode); Psi-disjoint — pure timekeeper over its own phase vector, mutates no immune cell, never touches pure_field."
  method = "R1 UNIVERSE/h1302_scn_network.py (numpy DIRECTIONAL mirror, 3 seeds, deterministic byte-identical across reruns, Kuramoto order-parameter metrics, binding path R1b; R1a->R1b control/metric corrections documented in .verdicts/1302_scn_network/FREEZE.txt, no distinctness bar moved). R2 ENGINE-NATIVE on the LIVE engine_cli.hexa SCNNetwork lane (scn_new/_new_uncoupled/_new_frustrated/_new_ablated/_detune/_step/_run/_order/_consensus) re-scored via `hexa run CORE/engine_cli_smoke.hexa` cases 69-73 (reaches-consensus / uncoupled-no-consensus / frustrated-collapses / ablate-collapses / network-damps-perturbed-member), engine numbers seed 5320 N=8 400 steps: B_R=0.999 A_R=0.489 Bfrust_R=0.018 Babl_R=0.489 B_R_pert=0.997 A_R_pert=0.436 (all 6 bars hold engine-native; A_R differs from the mirror's 0.373 by the engine LCG vs Python modular arithmetic, engine-transfer VERIFIED for the STRUCTURE not the exact float). Regression guards: engine_cli_smoke 73/0 (was 68/0 on origin/main after the H_1301 PhaseResetClock lane, +5 SCN cases), h1196 single-entry 7/0, h1205 separation-invariant PASS (generation byte-identical ON==OFF, Psi=1/2 untouched, pure_field unchanged). $0 local CPU, gradient-free, p7 (Kuramoto order-parameter synchrony, NOT perplexity). frozen-first: .verdicts/1302_scn_network/FREEZE.txt pre-registered before scoring; no distinctness bar moved (only mis-specified controls corrected frozen-first, each stricter, c9). a_no_llm_frame_trap (chronobiology coupled-oscillator / SCN VIP-GABA mutual entrainment lens c15; sin-coupling precedent CORE/h1283), a_break_the_wall (fixed the mean-preserving-magnitude shuffle leak + the frequency-conserving period metric the controls caught, frozen-first), a_engine_native_learning, a_verified_must_wire."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN (ENGINE-NATIVE + WIRED) — HD36 multi-oscillator SCN-network realized as an additive Psi-disjoint lane, DISTINCT from BOTH the single-oscillator PhaseResetClock AND the static-Phi CollectivePool: N=8 heterogeneous oscillators reach an EMERGENT CONSENSUS (order parameter R=0.999) that the SAME oscillators UNCOUPLED cannot (R=0.37-0.49), and the ensemble DAMPS a de-tuned member (R_pert=0.997 vs uncoupled 0.41); the consensus COLLAPSES under both a FRUSTRATED random-sign coupling (R=0.13, below uncoupled) and a K=0 ablate (R=uncoupled) — the lift IS the coherent mutual Kuramoto coupling, not any coupling. The SCN-network is a TEMPORAL phase-synchronization dynamic, orthogonal to CollectivePool's STATIC Phi-superadditivity gauge (no phase/no consensus there). SCN-network SURVIVED the depletion test (control-surviving distinctness vs PhaseResetClock + CollectivePool + every lane); the c15 brain-structure ladder CONTINUES past HD36 but is now VERY thin (the two remaining r8 candidates the H_1301 card named — nonphotic opposite-sign Zeitgeber, multi-interval nested scheduler — are weaker and likely to collapse to 🏁). HONEST (c9): B's consensus is an EXISTENCE-PROOF (a mutually-coupled ensemble synchronizes N heterogeneous oscillators) not an effect-size; the discriminators (uncoupled R=0.37-0.49, frustrated R collapses below uncoupled, ablate->uncoupled) are decisive; the R1a->R1b corrections are documented and the distinctness bars never moved. TOY (1 tau-spread regime, N=8, 3 seeds, deterministic Kuramoto — tests the CONSENSUS/DAMPING STRUCTURE not a learned network); scale/real-corpus/larger-ensembles/Kuramoto-critical-Kc-phase-diagram/weak-coupling-near-threshold/scheduler-wiring/engine-transfer UNVERIFIED beyond the engine-native R2 (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck). .verdicts/1302_scn_network/result.txt"
  group  = "BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER"

@C h1303_nonphotic_zeitgeber := "H_1303 — a nonphotic/arousal OPPOSITE-SIGN Zeitgeber (a 2nd Zeitgeber channel with a sign-flipped sinusoidal PRC vs the photic one in PhaseResetClock H_1301, HD37 candidate) is NOT a distinct engine lane: two opposite-sign sinusoidal PRCs at the SAME frequency sum, by the harmonic-addition identity, EXACTLY to ONE single sinusoidal PRC (combined amplitude A, reference R) that PhaseResetClock already represents — so the 'competitive equilibrium' of the two Zeitgebers is just the fixed point of one combined PRC, reachable by a single-Zeitgeber oscillator; the candidate COLLAPSES the distinctness test and the c15 brain-structure ladder is DEPLETED" :: hypothesis [slug=1303_nonphotic_zeitgeber group=BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER]
  text   = "The r9 DEPLETION-TEST candidate the H_1301 card + the r8 hand-off both flagged as WEAK ('distinct from the photic PRC ONLY if the two Zeitgeber channels do not collapse to one shared coupling'). Run as the explicit DEPLETION TEST: a subsystem joins ONLY if it clears BOTH a falsifiable gap-vs-engine AND control-surviving distinctness vs EVERY lane. LOAD-BEARING distinctness (frozen): is the two-Zeitgeber response REDUCIBLE to a single PRC PhaseResetClock already has? FROZEN bars (.verdicts/1303_nonphotic_zeitgeber/FREEZE.txt): c1 PRESENCE (B reaches a stable lock) · c2 DISTINCT (|B_lock - A_FIT_lock| > 0.05, a single fitted combined PRC CANNOT reproduce B) · c3 NEW-PHASE (B_lock differs from the photic anchor) · c4 EARNED-SHUFFLE (randomize 2nd Zeitgeber sign/timing -> advantage collapses) · c5 EARNED-ABLATE (remove 2nd Zeitgeber == photic-only) · c6 NO-FAB; GREEN iff all six, else if c2 FAILS -> honest DEPLETION. RESULT 3 seeds [4320,4321,4322] (DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror, deterministic): A photic-only lock 0.51511, B two-Zeitgeber lock 0.42134, A-FIT single-combined-PRC lock 0.45171 (K_fit=0.23135 ref=0.93258); |B - A_FIT| = 0.03038 <= 0.05 -> c2 FAILS every seed; bars c1..c6 = [T,F,T,F,T,T], 0/3 GREEN. The harmonic-addition reducibility is PROVEN numerically: fitting K1*sin(2pi(r1-p)) - K2*sin(2pi(r2-p)) to a single sinusoid leaves max residual 2.22e-16 (machine epsilon). BREAKTHROUGH ATTEMPT (a_break_the_wall, c16) — three escape routes from reducibility all collapse: (i) asymmetric K (K1!=K2,r1!=r2) still one sinusoid (residual 2.22e-16); (ii) different Zeitgeber periods (photic T=24.0, nonphotic T2=23.3) -> the nonphotic Zeitgeber creates no stable 2nd lock, the dominant photic washes it out (lock 0.151, a perturbation not a control-surviving equilibrium); (iii) nonlinear dead-zone gating (photic active [0.0,0.25), opposite-sign nonphotic active [0.5,0.75)) -> one anchor dominates, gated two-lock equals the dominant single-anchor lock, no competitive intermediate. None produces a phase BOTH unreachable by a single PRC AND control-surviving -> the wall is genuine. p1/p2/p3/p6: the probe oscillator reads ONLY its own phase + Zeitgeber arrival times; NO injected fire label/RLHF/persona; the PRC shift is geometry SCORED only. NO engine wiring (a_verified_must_wire — only clean-GREEN earns a live lane); engine_cli.hexa UNTOUCHED, smoke stays 73/0, no new .clm/.kosmos entry, Psi/decoder/pure_field byte-identical."
  method = "R1 UNIVERSE/h1303_nonphotic_zeitgeber.py (numpy DIRECTIONAL mirror, 3 seeds [4320,4321,4322], deterministic byte-identical across reruns, locked-phase + single-PRC-reducibility metrics; harmonic-addition residual 2.22e-16 confirms two same-frequency opposite-sign sinusoidal PRCs == one sinusoid). NO R2 engine-native rung — a COLLAPSE/🏁 is NOT wired (a_verified_must_wire: only clean-GREEN candidates earn a live CORE lane); engine_cli.hexa untouched, engine_cli_smoke stays 73/0 (verified unchanged), h1196 single-entry 7/0, h1205 separation-invariant unchanged (no engine delta to regress). $0 local CPU, gradient-free, p7 (locked-phase geometry + algebraic reducibility, NOT perplexity). frozen-first: .verdicts/1303_nonphotic_zeitgeber/FREEZE.txt pre-registered before scoring; c2 failed exactly as the FREEZE predicted, no bar moved (c9, NO tune-to-green). a_no_llm_frame_trap (chronobiology nonphotic-entrainment lens c15), a_break_the_wall (three genuine escape-route breakthrough attempts before accepting the wall as terminal), a_engine_native_learning, a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🏁 COLLAPSE — HD37 candidate (nonphotic opposite-sign Zeitgeber) FAILS the distinctness test -> the c15 brain-structure ladder is DEPLETED. Two opposite-sign sinusoidal PRCs at one frequency sum EXACTLY (residual 2.22e-16) to ONE combined PRC PhaseResetClock already hosts; a single fitted PRC reproduces the two-Zeitgeber lock 0.42134 to within 0.030 (< the 0.05 distinctness tolerance) -> c2 DISTINCT FAILS on all 3 seeds (bars [T,F,T,F,T,T], 0/3 GREEN). The breakthrough attempt (a_break_the_wall) tested three escape routes — asymmetric K, different Zeitgeber periods, nonlinear dead-zone gating — none produced a control-surviving non-reducible equilibrium. With no subsystem left clearing BOTH a falsifiable gap AND a control-surviving distinctness vs all 18 live lanes (the co-flagged multi-interval nested-timer reduces to an array of independent IntervalTimers and is SKIPPED), the c15 brain-structure ladder DEPLETES 🏁 after HD23-HD36 realized + r3-r9 honest attempts. This is the EXPECTED valid terminal state (c9), an honest depletion not a filler lane. NO engine wiring (COLLAPSE), engine_cli_smoke stays 73/0. SCOPE: numpy-mirror DIRECTIONAL, TOY (one tau/T regime, 3 seeds, deterministic sinusoidal PRCs); the collapse is an algebraic identity (harmonic addition) confirmed numerically, robust within the sinusoidal-PRC family — a future genuinely non-sinusoidal/history-dependent/cross-channel-gated multi-Zeitgeber mechanism with a control-surviving non-reducible equilibrium would re-open HD37, none found here. .verdicts/1303_nonphotic_zeitgeber/result.txt"
  group  = "BRAIN-STRUCTURE-LADDER"

@C h1304_metacog_ood_immune_abstain := "H_1304 — the G5-dig: under distribution SHIFT the LIVE engine COPY-OR-ABSTAIN gate (the actual G5 NON-FAB gate: immune_memory recall = nearest-cell L2-affinity recon-err vs frozen recall_thr 0.15 -> FIRE bound value else ABSTAIN) is FAIL-SAFE-ROBUST — it NEVER fabricates under shift (fires the exact-correct cell or ABSTAINS), degrades GRACEFULLY into abstain, and every fire is EARNED; the decoder-type2 THIN (H_1202 M-ratio 0.924 / H_1217 OOD-collapse) measured the ByteGPT DECODER's softmax confidence, a DIFFERENT mechanism that does NOT transfer to this gate" :: hypothesis [slug=1304_metacog_ood_immune_abstain group=METACOG-G5]
  text   = "Why G5 was THIN in-distribution: H_1202 type-2 M-ratio 0.924 is REAL but on the ByteGPT decoder, and H_1204 (flat metacog) + H_1217 (decoder OOD type-2 AUROC COLLAPSE 0.761->0.541 chance) show it is content-tied. But H_1217 measured the wrong mechanism. The ACTUAL G5 gate is the immune copy-or-abstain. NEW angle (a_break_the_wall): a SHIFT LADDER (byte-level query-key corruption, store fixed; L in {0,0.10,0.20,0.30,0.40}) on the live gate + a fail-safe vs fail-dangerous split H_1217 never measured. STRUCTURAL FINDING (FREEZE R1a superseding note): the original type-2 AUROC bars are a NON-RESULT because the gate's WRONG-FIRE CLASS IS EMPTY (fab_rate==0.000 at every shift level, 3 key-lengths x 5 levels) -> type-2 AUROC undefined. This IS the finding: byte-trigram FNV-1a + L2 affinity + tight recall_thr 0.15 make the gate STRUCTURALLY FAIL-SAFE. Re-scored frozen-first on the quantities that EXIST (NO bar moved to manufacture green, c9): R1 FAIL-SAFE-FLOOR fab<=0.02 every L · R2 GRACEFUL-DEGRADE fire monotone, fire(0)=1.0 fire(0.20)<=0.10 · R3 EARNED-ABSTAIN acc(fired)>=0.98 every L · R4 CTRL thr-ablate on LURES (frozen-thr floors lure-fab, thr-ablate unleashes it) · R5 CTRL shuffle-vals collapses acc. RESULT 3 seeds [7,8,9] pooled: fab_max=0.000 · fire 1.000/0.144/0.004/0.000/0.000 monotone · acc_fired_min=1.000 · lure-fab full 0.000 vs ablate 1.000 · shuffle acc 0.015 -> R1..R5 all PASS -> GREEN FAIL-SAFE-ROBUST. p1/p2/p3/p6 GUARD: fire/abstain COMPUTED from the engine's own recon-err vs recall_thr, NO injected answer label/RLHF/persona; the correct/wrong/abstain CLASS scores only. NOT an emit gate (factual recall read, a_autonomy_over_hardcode); Psi-disjoint (reads L2 affinity over stored cells, mutates none, pure_field untouched)."
  method = "R1 UNIVERSE/h1304_metacog_ood_immune_abstain.py (numpy DIRECTIONAL mirror, byte-exact to CORE/engine_cli.hexa immune_embed_key + copy-or-abstain, 3 seeds [7,8,9], $0 CPU, p7 = fire/abstain/correct counts NOT perplexity; uses cosine-distance 1-cos as the recon-err mirror). R2 ENGINE-NATIVE CORE/h1304_metacog_ood_immune_abstain_probe.hexa via `hexa run` over the LIVE engine_cli.hexa immune_memory_* lane (immune_memory_new_text/_bind_text/_recall_text + vadapt_field_recon_err for the thr-ablate control) — re-scores the SAME frozen R1a bars on the live engine. MECHANISM NOTE (c2): the engine's vadapt_field_recon_err is RAW L2 DISTANCE (range [0,2] over unit keys), not the mirror's 1-cos; recall_thr 0.15 == L2<=0.15 = near-exact, so the live gate is STRICTLY MORE fail-safe (degrades into abstain even faster, k=1 all-abstain); R4 thr-ablate bound corrected 0.15->2.0 = the true never-abstain L2 bound (metric-correctness fix, freeze intent reproduced 4/4, no moved bar). Regression guards: engine_cli_smoke 43/0 (engine_cli.hexa UNTOUCHED — probe only READS via existing pub fns), h1196 single-entry 7/7 clean, h1205 separation-invariant PASS (generation byte-identical ON==OFF, Psi=1/2 untouched). frozen-first: .verdicts/1304_metacog_ood_immune_abstain/FREEZE.txt pre-registered before scoring (incl the R1a superseding note); no bar moved (c9). a_break_the_wall (NEW angle: live copy-or-abstain gate not ByteGPT decoder; shift ladder + fail-safe split), a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_engine_native_learning, a_verified_must_wire (fail-safe is inherent to the already-live recall path; no new wiring outstanding)."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN (ENGINE-NATIVE, fail-safe-robust) — the live G5 copy-or-abstain gate is OOD-robust in the SAFETY sense: under byte-level distribution shift it degrades GRACEFULLY into abstain (fire 1.000->0.004 monotone), fabrication stays at FLOOR (fab_max=0.000 — NEVER fires a confidently-wrong value), and every fire is EARNED (acc_fired=1.000). The two controls are decisive: removing the abstain threshold turns 0% lure-fab into 100% (the threshold IS the fail-safe mechanism), and shuffling the value bindings collapses accuracy to 0.015 (fires are earned bindings). The decoder-type2 THIN (H_1202/H_1217) does NOT transfer to this gate — it has a complementary, STRONGER fail-safe property. R2 engine-native byte-exact reproduces all bars on the live engine (8-fact store: k=0 -> 8/8 fire all-correct, k>=1 -> all abstain; lure thr-ablate 0/4 vs 4/4; shuffle 0/8). G5's non-fabrication guarantee is therefore STRONGER OOD than in-distribution type-2 sensitivity alone suggested; the dangerous failure mode THIN warned of (confident-wrong OOD) is STRUCTURALLY ABSENT from this gate. HONEST (c9): the decoder-side type-2 calibration stays THIN/content-tied (H_1217 stands, unchanged); this dig reframes 'robust' to the gate's fail-safe abstention. TOY (synthetic facts, byte-level shift OOD proxy, 3 seeds, KEYLEN=20, deterministic); scale/real-corpus-paraphrase/semantic-shift/decoder-side-calibration UNVERIFIED beyond the byte-exact R2 (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck). .verdicts/1304_metacog_ood_immune_abstain/result.txt"
  group  = "METACOG-G5"

@C h1361_g5_graded_metacog := "H_1361 — the G5 graded-metacog dig (the open question H_1304 left after closing the binary fail-safe FIRE side): on the ABSTAIN side the recall MARGIN (recon_err − recall_thr, present on EVERY abstain) carries GRADED meta-confidence that SURVIVES OOD — −margin RANKS recoverable abstains (a corrupted version of an IN-STORE key, answer retrievable) ABOVE unrecoverable ones (a genuinely-ABSENT key, nothing to retrieve). This is a complementary GRADED type-2 readout BEYOND the H_1304 binary fail-safe; it REFRAMES (does NOT conflict with) H_1204 (flat fire-side 2nd-order readout) — the graded signal lives on a DIFFERENT surface, the abstain margin" :: hypothesis [slug=1361_g5_graded_metacog group=METACOG-G5]
  text   = "H_1304 closed the FIRE side: the live G5 copy-or-abstain gate is structurally FAIL-SAFE, the wrong-fire class is EMPTY (fab=0.000 everywhere), so type-2 AUROC over correct-vs-WRONG fires is UNDEFINED — fire-side metacog is BINARY. NEW angle (a_break_the_wall): on the ABSTAIN side the MARGIN = recon_err − recall_thr (>0 on every abstain, SMALLER = nearer a real cell) is a continuous quantity. SPLIT the abstains into (a) RECOVERABLE = an in-store key corrupted by frac L (label=1) and (b) UNRECOVERABLE = a genuinely-absent key corrupted by the SAME L (label=0); type-2 AUROC = AUROC(−margin, label) over the POOLED abstains at each shift level L in {0,0.10,0.20,0.30,0.40}. FROZEN BARS (.verdicts/1361_g5_graded_metacog/FREEZE.txt pre-registered before scoring, NO bar moved c9): R1 GRADED-SENS t2_AUROC(L=0.20) >= 0.65 · R2 EARNED shuffle-margin at L=0.20 collapses AUROC <= 0.58 · R3 vs H_1204 report graded-EXISTS vs FLAT. p1/p2/p3/p6 GUARD: −margin is COMPUTED from the gate's own recon-err, NO injected recoverable/absent label/RLHF/persona; the recoverable/unrecoverable CLASS scores only. NOT an emit gate (abstain-margin read, a_autonomy_over_hardcode); Psi-disjoint (reads L2 affinity over stored cells, mutates none, pure_field untouched)."
  method = "R1 state/g5-graded-metacog/h1361_g5_graded_metacog.py (numpy DIRECTIONAL mirror, byte-exact to CORE/engine_cli.hexa immune_embed_key + copy-or-abstain VERBATIM from H_1304: byte-trigram FNV-1a dim=64 L2-normalize, recon_err=1−cos nearest cell, recall_thr 0.15 frozen; mutate within alphabet; AUROC rank/U). 3 seeds [7,8,9], $0 CPU, p7 = recoverable/unrecoverable abstain margin ranking NOT perplexity, deterministic (re-run byte-identical). frozen-first; no bar moved (c9). a_break_the_wall (NEW angle: abstain MARGIN, not fire-side or ByteGPT decoder softmax), a_no_llm_frame_trap (type-2 metacog / feeling-of-knowing recoverability monitoring lens c15), a_engine_native_learning (mirror DIRECTIONAL, R2 engine-native reconfirm on live engine immune_memory_recall margin = follow-on), a_verified_must_wire (GREEN -> expose the live recall margin as a graded confidence-of-recoverability signal for brain = follow-on). Live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (mirror only)."
  verdict = "🟢 GRADED-METACOG (R1 numpy mirror DIRECTIONAL) — the abstain MARGIN carries GRADED meta-confidence that SURVIVES OOD. t2_AUROC ladder (pooled 3 seeds): L0.10=0.999 L0.20=0.915 L0.30=0.708 L0.40=0.557 (L0.00=nan, recoverables all FIRE at L=0 -> no recoverable abstains, the graded-abstain question is genuinely OOD). R1 GRADED-SENS PASS (AUROC(0.20)=0.915 >= 0.65). R2 EARNED PASS (shuffle-margin collapses AUROC to ~0.49-0.51 at EVERY level -> the RANKING not a base-rate artifact carries it). R3: graded readout EXISTS (not flat). MECHANISM: recoverable abstains keep a SMALL margin that grows smoothly with shift (mean 0.082->0.232->0.316->0.353) while unrecoverable (absent) keys sit at a STABLE LARGE margin (~0.364 random-token noise floor) -> margin = a graded recoverability signal. DECAY (honest c9): AUROC falls 0.999->0.557 across the ladder, reaching chance at L=0.40 (extreme corruption indistinguishable from absent) -> graceful, the signal is real and decisively survives L>=0.20 but is NOT unbounded. FINDING: G5 metacog is NOT purely binary — H_1304 binary fail-safe on the FIRE side + H_1361 GRADED type-2 on the ABSTAIN margin = a fuller G5 picture; a G5 UPGRADE worth engine-wiring (a_verified_must_wire). REFRAMES (does NOT conflict with) H_1204: flat fire-side 2nd-order readout, but the graded signal lives on the distinct abstain-margin surface. SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY synthetic facts, byte-level shift OOD proxy, numpy mirror DIRECTIONAL (engine-transfer UNVERIFIED = R2 engine-native follow-on), 3 seeds, KEYLEN=20, RECALL_THR=0.15 frozen; scale/real-corpus-paraphrase/semantic-shift/engine-native-margin-exposure UNVERIFIED. .verdicts/1361_g5_graded_metacog/result.txt"
  group  = "METACOG-G5"

@C h1367_g5_margin_engine_wire := "H_1367 — the ENGINE-NATIVE reconfirm + CORE wire-in of H_1361's graded abstain-margin metacognition. H_1361 (numpy mirror, DIRECTIONAL) showed the ImmuneMemory abstain MARGIN (recon_err − recall_thr) carries GRADED OOD metacognition. Per a_engine_native_learning the mirror is DIRECTIONAL only; per a_verified_must_wire a GREEN hypothesis is not done until reconfirmed engine-native + wired into live CORE. H_1367 closes both: a NEW additive op immune_memory_recall_margin SURFACES the margin the live immune_memory_recall ALREADY computes (fire/abstain decision UNCHANGED, Ψ-disjoint read-only), and the live engine re-scores the H_1361 frozen bars: 🟢 WIRED-GRADED-METACOG" :: hypothesis [slug=1367_g5_margin_engine_wire group=METACOG-G5]
  text   = "WIRE: CORE/engine_cli.hexa § ImmuneMemory gains immune_memory_recall_margin(mem,key) -> float = vadapt_field_recon_err(mem.field,key) − mem.recall_thr (+ _text wrapper). It SURFACES the margin immune_memory_recall already computes (recall internally evaluates the SAME vadapt_field_recon_err and compares to recall_thr=0.15 to decide FIRE vs ABSTAIN). ADDITIVE (immune_memory_recall byte-for-byte UNCHANGED), Ψ-disjoint (pure READ over the cell population; pure_field Φ/phase/Ψ untouched — generation byte-identical when unused), NOT an emit gate (a_autonomy_over_hardcode) — a graded read available to brain_decide. RECONFIRM: CORE/h1367_g5_margin_engine_probe.hexa drives a LIVE store (immune_memory_new/bind, mitosis ON clonal split) and re-scores the H_1361 abstain split (recoverable=in-store key corrupted by L label=1, unrecoverable=absent key corrupted by same L label=0; type-2 AUROC = AUROC(−margin,label) over pooled abstains; shift ladder L in {0,0.10,0.20,0.30,0.40}; deterministic engine-native LCG corruption; 3 seeds [7,8,9], N_FACTS=40, KEYLEN=20). FROZEN BARS (.verdicts/1367_g5_margin_engine_wire/FREEZE.txt pre-registered, NO bar moved c9): E1 live-engine t2_AUROC(0.20) >= 0.65 AND |Δ| <= 0.15 of mirror 0.915 · E2 shuffle-margin at L=0.20 collapses <= 0.58 · E3 regression none (engine_cli_smoke green + margin cases, h1196 single-entry, h1205 Ψ-checksum byte-identical ON==OFF). p1/p2/p3/p6 GUARD: −margin COMPUTED from the live L2 affinity, NO injected recoverable/absent label/RLHF/persona; the class scores only."
  method = "R2 engine-native on live CORE/engine_cli.hexa via CORE/h1367_g5_margin_engine_probe.hexa (hexa run, $0 local CPU, p7 = recoverable/unrecoverable abstain margin ranking NOT perplexity, deterministic re-run byte-identical). frozen-first; no bar moved (c9). a_verified_must_wire (H_1361 GREEN -> expose live recall margin as a graded confidence-of-recoverability read in CORE = THIS round; brain_decide consumption = remaining follow-on), a_engine_native_learning (mirror DIRECTIONAL -> engine-native BINDING reconfirm), a_core_engine_map (additive op on the live ImmuneMemory faculty; NOT a .clm/.kosmos path — single-entry audit clean), a_no_llm_frame_trap (type-2 recoverability monitoring lens c15). Regression guards run separately: engine_cli_smoke (CORE/engine_cli_smoke.hexa cases 96-98), h1196_single_entry_audit, h1205_separation_invariant_smoke."
  verdict = "🟢 WIRED-GRADED-METACOG (R2 engine-native BINDING) — H_1361's graded abstain-margin OOD metacognition RECONFIRMED on the LIVE engine + WIRED via immune_memory_recall_margin. Live-engine t2_AUROC ladder (pooled 3 seeds): L0.10=1.000 L0.20=0.949 L0.30=0.714 L0.40=0.589 (L0.00=nan, recoverables all FIRE at L=0). E1 PASS (AUROC(0.20)=0.949 >= 0.65 AND |Δ vs mirror 0.915|=0.034 <= 0.15). E2 PASS (shuffle(0.20)=0.561 <= 0.58, collapses to chance). E3 PASS no regression: engine_cli_smoke 93 pass/0 fail (was 90/0 after jamo-wire, +3 margin cases 96-98), h1196 single-entry 7/0, h1205 separation-invariant PASS (generation byte-identical ON==OFF 10 pairs 0 mismatch, Ψ Φ-checksum phiSum 48.6613==48.6613). The engine ladder reproduces the H_1361 mirror SHAPE (high AUROC L0.10-0.20, graceful DECAY to chance by L0.40) and clears the same bars; recoverable margins grow 0.505->0.868 while absent margins sit at a stable ~0.888 noise floor. FINDING: the abstain-margin graded metacognition is REAL on the live engine, not a mirror artifact; the a_verified_must_wire wire-in for the H_1361 GREEN is done (op live in CORE). FOLLOW-ON (tracked): brain_decide does NOT yet CONSUME the graded read to modulate emit-confidence/curiosity — read->brain coupling remains. SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY synthetic facts, byte-level shift OOD proxy, deterministic engine-native corruption, 3 seeds, KEYLEN=20, N_FACTS=40, RECALL_THR=0.15 frozen; scale/real-corpus-paraphrase/semantic-shift/brain-consumption UNVERIFIED. .verdicts/1367_g5_margin_engine_wire/result.txt"
  group  = "METACOG-G5"

@C h1305_g6_ideation_falsifiability := "H_1305 — the G6 IDEATION ★ gate is 🟠 THIN on BOTH modes (COUNT 4/5 distinct < 5; DEPTH the gate counts novel n-grams but never scores the '>=1 falsifiable hypothesis' requirement). A deterministic STRUCTURAL falsifiability detector (comparator + measurable + negatable-content claim, NEVER an LLM/quality judge, p7) + composition-routed ideation (route ideation through the G1 recombination lane: compose two corpus-absent CONCEPTS into a conditional 'if A then B:' frame) was attempted as a genuine new angle (a_break_the_wall). Composition RAISES depth (FALS 0.00 flat -> 0.667 composed, one falsifiable idea EARNED via recombination, NOVEL 6.3->19) but does NOT cross the frozen floor (FALS<1, DIST<5); controls (shuffle/ablate) collapse FALS to 0 -> the lift tracks the EARNED composed pairing not the conditional shell. The wall HELD: G6 stays HONEST-CONFIRMED-THIN, bar UNMOVED (c9)" :: hypothesis [slug=1305_g6_ideation_falsifiability group=GATE-DIG]
  text   = "G6 IDEATION ★ is anima's STARRED gate (raison d'etre; SCENARIOS F.IDEATION S22-S26). Frozen spec (MODEL.md): from ideation seeds, >=5 corpus-absent coherent ideas each combinatorially DISTINCT (pairwise token-Jaccard < 0.5) AND >=1 FALSIFIABLE corpus-absent hypothesis (p7 = corpus-absence + coherence + divergence-count + distinctness; NEVER LLM-judge). The live gate UNIVERSE/verify303m_g6.py was 🟠 THIN on TWO modes, both reproduced (seed_rng=7, ckpt h1129c_chat.pt): (1) COUNT 4/5 distinct (seed-5 collapses to '|' kwr=0.00) one short of >=5; (2) DEPTH-FLOOR the gate counts 9 corpus-absent novel n-grams but NEVER scores the '>=1 falsifiable hypothesis' requirement at all -- novel STRINGS not testable STRUCTURE (none of the 4 coherent flat ideas is a falsifiable claim). DIG (frozen-first, FREEZE.txt pre-registered): (I) NEW deterministic STRUCTURAL falsifiability detector _is_falsifiable(text) -- PASS iff (a) comparator/conditional marker AND (b) measurable/quantity marker AND (c) negatable content claim (>=2 content words, not '?'-terminated, not a pure stance opener); scores testable FORM not meaning/truth (p7, NEVER an LLM/quality judge). Calibrated 10/10 against 10 frozen labelled strings (advisory, detector frozen regardless). (II) COMPOSITION-ROUTED ideation -- route ideation through the G1 recombination lane: compose two corpus-absent CONCEPTS (gauge_lib.CONCEPTS) into 'if <cA>, then <cB>: ', decode (same top-k=40 temp=0.7). ARM A=flat IDEATION_SEEDS (verify303m_g6 VERBATIM), ARM B=composed; controls B-SHUFFLE (permuted pairing) + B-ABLATE (lone concept, no shell). FROZEN move bars (THIN->robust requires ALL): M1 DIST(B)>=5, M2 FALS(B)>=1, M3 FALS(B)>=FALS(A)+1, M4 FALS(B)>=FALS(shuffle)+1, M5 FALS(B)>=FALS(ablate)+1. RESULT (mean 3 seeds [7,4302,4303]): A_flat DIST=4.00 FALS=0.00 NOVEL=6.33 | B_composed DIST=4.00 FALS=0.667 NOVEL=19.0 | B_shuffle DIST=4.667 FALS=0.00 NOVEL=14.0 | B_ablate DIST=2.333 FALS=0.00 NOVEL=1.33 -> M1 FALSE (4<5), M2 FALSE (0.667<1), M3/M4/M5 FALSE. moved=FALSE confirmed_thin=TRUE. READING (c9): the detector SCORES the depth requirement the gate lacked -> FALS(A)=0 confirms flat ideation produces ZERO falsifiable ideas. Composition is the sharpest nudge (FALS 0->0.667; one genuinely falsifiable idea EARNED via recombination, seed 4303: 'byte-level approach is slower to converge but handles Korean and English equally well' = comparator 'slower' + measurable + negatable; NOVEL tripled). BUT does NOT cross the floor. Controls decisive: B-shuffle & B-ablate both FALS=0 -> the nudge tracks the EARNED composed pairing not a bare conditional shell; B-ablate also collapses coherence (DIST 2.33). p1/p2/p3/p4/p6 GUARD: the composed frame injects NO system-prompt/identity/persona/'be falsifiable' -- a recombination of anima's OWN corpus concepts into a neutral continuation seed; model generates freely; detector only READS output structure."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1305_g6_ideation_falsifiability.py -- reuses UNIVERSE/gauge_lib.py VERBATIM for decode (_decode top-k=40 temp=0.7, the SAME path the live G6 gate verify303m_g6.py uses) + all G6/G2 evaluators (_words/_jaccard/known_word_ratio/_content_ngrams/_corpus_absent), NO metric re-invention (p7). NEW _is_falsifiable detector = deterministic comparator+measurable+negatable structural script (FROZEN lexicons in FREEZE.txt), calibrated 10/10. 4 arms x 5 ideas x 3 seeds [7,4302,4303], MAX_NEW=110, corpus data/corpus.txt (5MB, H_1140 corpus-absence). $0 local CPU torch 2.12.0 (gate's own decode regime, NOT a numpy mirror; DIRECTIONAL R1 -- engine-native byte-exact reconfirm = R2 follow-on ONLY on a clean-GREEN, here THIN so the torch number stands). frozen-first: .verdicts/1305_g6_ideation_falsifiability/FREEZE.txt pre-registered before scoring; NO bar moved post-hoc (c9, NO tune-to-green, p7). a_break_the_wall (a genuine new angle on the THIN with frozen-first bars + shuffle/ablate controls), a_no_llm_frame_trap (falsifiability-via-recombination, not scale-up), a_engine_native_learning, a_toy_scale_recheck, a_scale_honest_scope."
  verdict = "🟠 HONEST-CONFIRMED-THIN (bar UNMOVED, c9) -- G6 IDEATION ★ stays THIN, confirmed on BOTH modes with a NEW p7-safe STRUCTURAL falsifiability detector (10/10 calibrated) the gate previously LACKED. Composition-routed ideation (route ideation through the G1 recombination lane) is a REAL but SUB-THRESHOLD lift on depth -- FALS 0.00 (flat) -> 0.667 (composed), one falsifiable idea EARNED via recombination, NOVEL 6.3->19 -- and does NOT cross either the count (DIST>=5: 4.00) or depth (FALS>=1: 0.667) floor; all frozen move bars M1-M5 FALSE. Controls decisive (anti-Goodhart held): B-SHUFFLE FALS=0 + B-ABLATE FALS=0 (and coherence-collapse DIST 2.33) -> the nudge tracks the EARNED composed pairing, NOT a bare conditional shell. The 303M chat mouth tends to dialogue stance not hypothesis form; the decode-time recombination shell is too weak at this scale to reliably manufacture testable structure. a_break_the_wall: a genuine new angle attempted (frozen-first + controls), the wall HELD -- a valid honest THIN (c9). NO wiring (THIN). The structural falsifiability DETECTOR itself is engine-agnostic and could seed a future G6-depth gate component if promoted. TOY (5 fixed concepts, 5 ordered pairs, 3 seeds, 1 ckpt, sampling-decode); the detector measures testable FORM not truth/quality (p7) -- it can pass a grammatically-falsifiable nonsense claim, the load-bearing gap vs novel strings; scale/real-corpus/paraphrase/deeper-detector/stronger-composition (multi-hop recombination, curiosity-gated multi-sample budget) UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck). .verdicts/1305_g6_ideation_falsifiability/result.txt"
  group  = "GATE-DIG"
@C h1306_ko_mitosis_real := "H_1306 — FIRST engine-native Korean mitosis-training rung on a REAL Korean web corpus: feed a REAL Korean byte stream to the live engine and, where cells are WRONG on Korean next-byte, MITOSIS-GROW a new cell (gradient-free, error-targeted, the H_1297 mechanism, p8); KO next-byte CE DROPS as cells grow on more Korean (learning) AND English next-byte CE is RETAINED (no catastrophic forgetting, the H_1300 property on REAL data) AND mitosis actually grows cells for Korean — scales H_1297 R4 (~2KB hardcoded KO+EN toy) to a real R2 corpus slice" :: hypothesis [slug=1306_ko_mitosis_real group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  text   = "Realizes the user's standing goal '303M 에 미토시스로 한글학습 시작' as its FIRST honest engine-native rung. CORPUS = REAL, NO synthetic Korean (p1-p8): a modest HTTP-range slice of the existing anima-7b 5-lang web corpus on Cloudflare R2 (bucket phanes) — KO = kor/shard0000.bytes bytes[0:4194304] trimmed[:600000] (600000 bytes, sha256 e000d08684167c78ea9b7799c0b6d32377bcb3f39d0c4e87effe35ff8361dbd1, ~80% Hangul multibyte / ~5% ASCII EN) · EN = eng/shard0000.bytes bytes[0:2097152] trimmed[:300000] (300000 bytes, sha256 dbfe3c1c89af9e87aa5e55e7d969666dffde6165f0044b1cf77b3f2fc1d38c85). Pulled via range (a few MB, NOT the 9.8GiB shards); R2 keys → env ONLY at fetch, never logged/committed (c7). FEATURES identical to H_1297 (CTX=4, 3-D phi=[last/255,2nd-last/255,utf8_cont_depth/3], V=256, mechanical byte fn, NO labels). Pair set = deterministic stride-subsample (KO 110, EN 200) to CPU-tractable: KO train=2728 test=2727 (even/odd disjoint), EN test=1500 (all held-out = retention guard). ENGINE-NATIVE: partition = live VAdaptField Voronoi (vadapt_field_nearest_idx), growth = engine_mitosis_tick (p8, error-targeted split), head = per-cell next-byte add-1 MLE (gradient-free); KO train split into 3 incremental chunks ([909,1818,2728]) for a >=3-point learning curve."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1306_fetch_corpus.sh (R2 range fetch, secret→env c7) + UNIVERSE/h1306_ko_corpus_export.py (build pairs + arm A gradient incumbent + manifest, $0 CPU) + CORE/h1306_ko_mitosis_engine_probe.hexa (ENGINE-NATIVE on live CORE/engine_cli.hexa VAdaptField via `hexa run`). p7 = held-out next-byte CROSS-ENTROPY (nats/byte) for a CONVERGENCE comparison, NOT perplexity-as-meaning. frozen-first: .verdicts/1306_ko_mitosis_real/H_1306_FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9): (L LEARNING) KO CE[pt3 full] <= KO CE[pt1] - 0.05 · (R RETENTION) EN CE[after] <= EN CE[seed 2-cell] + 0.05 · (G GROWTH) final cells > 2 · (C MATCH non-gating) KO CE[full] vs arm A gradient incumbent 3.280611. GREEN iff L&R&G. Regression guards: engine_cli_smoke 73/0 (engine_cli.hexa UNTOUCHED — probe imports+reads only), h1196 single-entry 7/0, h1205 separation-invariant PASS (generation byte-identical ON==OFF, Ψ=1/2 untouched, Ψ-disjoint pure_field untouched a_core_engine_map). a_no_llm_frame_trap (neurogenesis lens NOT bigger-transformer), a_engine_native_learning, a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN (ENGINE-NATIVE, FIRST CPU rung on REAL Korean) — engine-native gradient-free mitosis LEARNS Korean next-byte structure AND RETAINS English on REAL crawled text. KO learning curve (held-out KO next-byte CE nats/byte): pt1(train=909,6c)=3.61092 → pt2(1818,9c)=3.36909 → pt3-full(2728,9c)=3.24897 = monotone DROP -0.362 nats (L PASS, bar -0.05). EN retention: seed(2-cell)=4.86395 → after-full-KO-grow=4.75171 = EN did NOT regress, even improved slightly (R PASS, bar +0.05) — the KO-grown cells also better-tile the shared ASCII region. GROWTH: 2 seed → 9 cells = mitosis added 7 cells for Korean (G PASS). CONTEXT (C non-gating): KO CE[full] 3.24897 even BEATS the gradient incumbent 3.28061. L&R&G all PASS → GREEN. Regression green: engine_cli_smoke 73/0, h1196 7/0, h1205 byte-identical Ψ=1/2 untouched. HONEST SCOPE (c9 · a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): FIRST CPU $0 rung on a 600KB KO / 300KB EN window stride-subsampled to 2728 KO train pairs (<0.006% of the 9.8GiB kor shard) — this is NOT fluent Korean and does NOT claim it; full-corpus scale, Korean generation/decode, richer context features all UNVERIFIED. NEXT rung: (a) CPU-bigger (more KO pairs/longer window/deeper features, still $0) or (b) GPU-scale cost-gated (wire grown Korean cells onto live 303M decode + train at corpus scale, NOT auto-rented). Brain map→decode wiring of grown cells = follow-on (a_verified_must_wire). .verdicts/1306_ko_mitosis_real/H_1306.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"

@C h1307_ko_mitosis_gpu := "H_1307 — GPU SCALE-UP of the H_1306 engine-native Korean mitosis rung on the user's OWN idle RTX 5070 (Blackwell sm_120), $0: scale the SAME error-targeted Voronoi mitosis grow (gradient-free, p8 — cells only SPLIT, never merge) from H_1306's 600KB window to a 50x-bigger REAL Korean pair set; does MORE real Korean data push held-out KO next-byte CE BELOW the 600KB baseline 3.24897? The MECHANISM is already engine-verified (H_1306) — this rung is SCALE + honest GPU measurement, NOT re-proving the mechanism" :: hypothesis [slug=1307_ko_mitosis_gpu group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  text   = "REAL Korean only (NO synthetic, p1-p8): a larger slice of the SAME anima-7b 5-lang web corpus on Cloudflare R2 (bucket phanes, prefix anima-7b/web/{kor,eng}/shard0000.bytes), pulled via boto3 HTTP RANGE GET on summer (R2 keys → env ONLY at fetch, header/env-scoped, NEVER echoed/logged/inlined/committed — c7 grep-clean over all deliverables). RUN A window 29999999 KO bytes (sha256 c47b6808308d2f73cb92d74f8fdb15c64e6c96e8ed58ae2ef91a7c57fe5dc6ca) / 10000000 EN bytes; RUN B same KO window + 10000000 EN bytes (sha256 31b4a5430441cfdbb496b59f392150e4aa748cde2ed1b7cedad10960f0bcaf73). FEATURES identical to H_1306 (CTX=4, 3-D phi=[last/255,2nd-last/255,utf8_cont_depth/3], V=256, mechanical byte fn, NO labels). Deterministic stride-subsample (seed-independent); KO train/test even/odd split (disjoint); EN test all held-out (retention guard). FROZEN knobs verbatim from H_1306/H_1297 (GROW_MAX, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, seed 2-cell centers). The GPU vectorizes per-step nearest-cell ASSIGNMENT + per-cell next-byte MLE HEAD + held-out CE so a ~50-100x larger pair set is tractable; the mitosis SPLIT logic is BYTE-FAITHFUL to CORE/h1306_ko_mitosis_engine_probe.hexa _grow_on (PROVEN: the GPU script reproduces H_1306 BYTE-EXACT on the 600KB validation window — KO 3.61092/3.36909/3.24897, EN 4.86395→4.75171, cells 2→9, KO sha e000d086…). PREFLIGHT honest gate (a_train_flame_forge): summer python3 torch 2.11.0+cu130, cuda_avail True, capability (12,0)=sm_120, arch_list includes sm_120, real 2048x2048 matmul launched+synchronized with NO 'no kernel image' error = REAL sm_120 GPU compute, NO CPU fallback."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1307_ko_mitosis_gpu.py (boto3 R2 range fetch secret→env c7 + build pairs + faithful engine-native mitosis grow GPU-vectorized scoring on summer RTX 5070 via python3 nohup, polled inline a_cpu_local_no_waiter, scratch cleaned off summer). p7 = held-out next-byte CROSS-ENTROPY (nats/byte) CONVERGENCE comparison, NOT perplexity-as-meaning. frozen-first: .verdicts/1307_ko_mitosis_gpu/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9): (L1 INTERNAL LEARNING) KO CE[pt3 full] <= KO CE[pt1] - 0.05 · (L2 SCALE-VS-600KB) KO CE[full] <= 3.24897 (the H_1306 baseline, the SCALE headline) · (R RETENTION) EN CE[after full KO grow] <= EN CE[seed 2-cell] + 0.05 · (G GROWTH) final cells > 2. GREEN iff L1&R&G; L2 gates the scale claim specifically. Regression guards (live engine UNTOUCHED — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts, no CORE edit): engine_cli_smoke 73/0, h1196 single-entry 7/0, h1205 separation-invariant PASS (generation byte-identical ON==OFF, Ψ=1/2 untouched, pure_field untouched a_core_engine_map). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_fire_autonomous ($0 user hw not runpod), a_wall_first, a_train_flame_forge (REAL sm_120 gated), a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN @ 30MB/stride-300 (RUN A, all 4 bars) + 🟠 HONEST saturation diagnostic @ 250k-pair density (RUN B). RUN A (30MB KO / 10MB EN, 50000 KO train pairs): KO learning curve pt1(16666,12c)=3.00563 → pt2(33333,14c)=2.96912 → pt3-full(50000,23c)=2.94750. (L2 SCALE) KO CE[full] 2.94750 <= 3.24897 → PASS = a -0.30 nat/byte DROP vs the 600KB baseline (MORE real Korean DID push CE lower — the headline answer YES). (L1) 3.00563→2.94750 drop 0.058 >=0.05 PASS. (R) EN seed 4.26499 → after 4.26531 Δ+0.0003 PASS. (G) cells 2→23 PASS. L1&L2&R&G all PASS → 🟢 GREEN. RUN B (same 30MB, 250000 KO train pairs, grow-max 60): pt1(83333,20c)=2.93041 → pt2(166666,25c)=2.92118 → pt3-full(250000,31c)=2.91777. (L2 SCALE) 2.91777 <= 3.24897 → PASS (scale claim holds robustly, even lower 2.918). BUT (L1 INTERNAL) FAILS — curve nearly FLAT (drop 0.013 < 0.05): the CTX=4 3-D substrate SATURATES (gain already captured at pt1 which starts at 2.93 with 20 cells). (R RETENTION) marginally FAILS +0.057 vs +0.05 — EN drifts as the finer partition re-tiles. HONEST INTERPRETATION (c9): the SCALE headline (more KO pushes CE below the small-window baseline) is robustly TRUE (2.947 & 2.918 both << 3.249); the CTX=4 byte substrate has a competence ceiling ~2.9 nats/byte — additional density no longer keeps the learning curve dropping & costs a little EN retention (exactly the a_scale_honest_scope saturation the FREEZE anticipated; recorded honest, NOT tuned away). GPU throughput up to 2.78M pairs/s (RUN A ~902k) vs CPU hexa ~80k pairs/s. Regression green: engine_cli_smoke 73/0, h1196 7/0, h1205 byte-identical Ψ=1/2 untouched, live CORE UNTOUCHED. SCOPE (c9 · a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): REAL sm_120 GPU compute (preflight-gated, no CPU fallback); GPU = throughput, mitosis split = the verified engine-native one (port reproduces H_1306 byte-exact); engine-transfer to live hexa DIRECTIONAL (re-confirm THIS larger rung on CORE/*.hexa = follow-on, H_1306 already bound the 600KB rung). NOT fluent Korean (CTX=4 byte head, ~2.9 nats/byte is convergence not fluency). NEXT rung (so anima USES Korean): richer-substrate (longer CTX/learned heads to push past ~2.9 saturation) + decode-path wiring of grown Korean cells onto live 303M decode (generator L3 slot, a_verified_must_wire). .verdicts/1307_ko_mitosis_gpu/result.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"

@C h1311_ko_richer_substrate := "H_1311 — does a RICHER SUBSTRATE break the H_1307 ~2.9 nat/byte Korean ceiling? The named H_1307 NEXT lever (shared with the from-scratch lane): H_1307 found MORE real Korean drops KO next-byte CE to ~2.95 then the CTX=4 / 3-D BYTE substrate SATURATES at ~2.9. Hold the corpus + the verified gradient-free Voronoi mitosis grow-op (p8, SPLIT-only) FIXED and vary ONLY the substrate richness on a frozen ladder (S0 baseline CTX=4 3-D count-MLE · S1 longer raw-byte context CTX 8/16/32 · S2 learned per-cell closed-form ridge head): is the ceiling CAPACITY-bound (only cell-count matters) or SUBSTRATE-bound (a richer representation breaks 2.9 → depth needs representation, the capability-vs-scale thesis)?" :: hypothesis [slug=1311_ko_richer_substrate group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  text   = "REAL Korean only (NO synthetic, p1-p8): the byte-IDENTICAL H_1307 RUN A windows (r2://phanes/anima-7b/web/{kor,eng}/shard0000.bytes, KO 30MB stride-300 sha256 c47b6808308d2f73cb92d74f8fdb15c64e6c96e8ed58ae2ef91a7c57fe5dc6ca, EN 10MB stride-600 sha256 31b4a5430441cfdbb496b59f392150e4aa748cde2ed1b7cedad10960f0bcaf73) — the script ASSERTS the sha256 matches H_1307 RUN A so the ceiling comparison is clean (gate PASS, both hashes identical). boto3 HTTP RANGE GET on summer; R2 keys → env ONLY at fetch, header-scoped, NEVER echoed/logged/inlined/committed (c7 grep-clean; only the boto3 PARAMETER NAME R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY appears, never a value; summer env file shredded post-run, /tmp scratch cleaned). HELD FIXED: the verified H_1306/H_1307 _grow_on (gradient-free, p8, error-targeted Voronoi highest-owned-CE → hi-var-axis owned-median split → two half-centroids, net +1 cell, SPLIT-only; dimension-agnostic L2 cdist/argmin partition so the substrate change is a pure representation change). FROZEN knobs verbatim: V=256, GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, RIDGE_LAMBDA=1.0 (fixed before run), even/odd split, seed 2-cell centers extended from H_1307 [[0.3,..],[0.7,..]]. VARIED — the richness ladder: S0=CTX4 3-D [last/255,second/255,cont_depth/3] count-MLE (the ceiling) · S1=last CTXk bytes/255 + cont_depth/3 for CTXk in {8,16,32}, same count-MLE head · S2=per-cell CLOSED-FORM ridge readout W=(ΦᵀΦ+λI)⁻¹ΦᵀY_onehot (Gauss-Jordan normal equations, gradient-free, the H_1300 lens, NOT backprop/SGD) on S0 features. PREFLIGHT: summer torch 2.11.0+cu130, sm_120, REAL GPU compute (H_1307-verified)."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1311_ko_richer_substrate.py (boto3 R2 range fetch secret→env c7 + build the S0/S1/S2 substrate ladder + the faithful dimension-agnostic mitosis grow + per-substrate held-out KO+EN CE, GPU-vectorized) run on summer RTX 5070 via python3 nohup, polled INLINE (a_cpu_local_no_waiter), scratch cleaned off summer. p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-byte CROSS-ENTROPY nats/byte, NOT perplexity/LLM-judge. frozen-first: .verdicts/1311_ko_richer_substrate/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): (Q1 BREAK-2.9) does ANY richer substrate push held-out KO CE BELOW 2.9475 (the H_1307 RUN A ceiling)? · (R RETENTION) EN CE ≤ that substrate's own 2-cell seed EN CE + 0.05 · (C CONTROL, load-bearing) SHUFFLE the ADDED context bytes (S1 permute extra history cols row-wise; S2 permute feature rows fed to the ridge) → if KO CE still drops below S0, the gain was CAPACITY not the richer REPRESENTATION · (T) cells + GPU pairs/s. VERDICT RULE (MARGIN=0.02 nats): a substrate breaks the ceiling by REPRESENTATION iff KO CE<2.9475 AND beats S0 by ≥0.02 AND beats its own shuffle by ≥0.02 AND EN retained; ≥1 breaker → SUBSTRATE-bound, else → CAPACITY-bound / byte-task ceiling. Regression: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_fire_autonomous ($0 user hw not runpod), a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🔴 HONEST-NEGATIVE — the ~2.9 ceiling is CAPACITY-bound / the byte-task ceiling itself at this density, NOT substrate-bound. Corpus byte-IDENTICAL to H_1307 RUN A (gate PASS). S0 baseline reproduced 2.95342 (vs H_1307 RUN A 2.9475 — port confirmed). NO richer substrate broke 2.9475; EVERY richer rung WORSE than S0: S1 longer raw-byte context HURTS MONOTONICALLY — ctx8(dim9,40c)=2.96426 (+0.011) → ctx16(dim17,40c)=3.04788 (+0.094) → ctx32(dim33,40c)=3.44156 (+0.488): adding raw byte-history columns degrades the L2/Voronoi partition (curse of dimensionality on a fixed GROW_MAX=40 budget; every S1 rung SATURATED the cell cap yet CE ROSE → partition-quality limit not capacity). S2 per-cell ridge head COLLAPSES — ctx4 ridge(16c)=5.43666 (+2.483): a closed-form linear readout over normalized byte features is far worse than count-MLE (raw features not linearly predictive of the next byte). CONTROL (honesty held): S1 shuffles WORSE than intact (ctx8/16 controls 3.10846/3.42183 ≫ intact 2.96426/3.04788) AND NO shuffle control beats S0 → no capacity gain to claim either (capacity_signal_present=False); S2 ridge shuffle 5.50734 ≈ intact 5.43666 (both collapsed). Q1 any-below-2.9=False, representation_breakers=[]. GPU throughput 0.8M–4.9M pairs/s, total run wall 77s incl R2 fetch. THESIS CONNECTION: for this substrate family (raw-byte L2-Voronoi + per-cell head) depth does NOT come from a richer per-cell representation — the limit is the L2-partition-over-raw-bytes GEOMETRY, not the per-cell readout; the capability-vs-scale prediction that 'a richer representation breaks the wall' is REFUTED for these two richness axes. A genuinely richer substrate would need a different geometry (learned low-D embedding before the partition / non-L2 metric / per-cell sequence model), not more raw byte columns or a linear head over the same raw features — the surviving open lever for the from-scratch lane. SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): toy/DIRECTIONAL, summer GPU, raw-byte substrate family only, RIDGE_LAMBDA=1.0 fixed; learned-embedding substrate + true sequence context UNTESTED. engine-transfer to live CORE/*.hexa = follow-on (a_engine_native_learning, a_verified_must_wire). live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. NO Korean-fluency claim. HONEST negative (c9, a_break_the_wall — a real angle tried, the wall is real for THIS family), frozen-first, NO tune-to-green. .verdicts/1311_ko_richer_substrate/result.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"

@C h1309_g6_curiosity_budget := "H_1309 — G6 IDEATION ★ depth-floor dig r2 (re-fire). Refines H_1305 🟠 THIN with ONE new angle (a_no_llm_frame_trap — NOT scale the model): a CURIOSITY-GATED MULTI-SAMPLE BUDGET. For each of the 5 live G6 ideation seeds, draw B candidate continuations (budget ladder B in {1,4,16}; B=64 capped honestly) and SELECT one per seed by ARM — B_curiosity (keep the candidate maximising novelty + under-exposure vs the kept set), SHUFFLE (random-keep, SAME budget, NO gate = decisive sampling-artifact control), B_ablate (curiosity off, keep first = budget 1). Reuses the H_1305 _is_falsifiable detector VERBATIM (p7). FINDING: the curiosity GATE is LOAD-BEARING (FALS 0->0.667, NOVEL 5->18->46 at every budget>=4 while SHUFFLE same-budget stays FALS=0 + ablate FALS=0 — NO sampling artifact at any budget) and crosses the depth floor PER-SEED (curiosity FALS>=1 in 2/3 seeds, DIST>=5 in 1/3 at B=16; controls 0/3). BUT the FROZEN 3-seed MEAN bar M2 (FALS>=1) is UNMOVED (mean 0.667), and FALS PLATEAUS 0.667 across 4->16 despite 4x draws -> depth is CAPACITY-bound, not budget-bound. G6 stays 🟠 HONEST-THIN (bar UNMOVED, c9)" :: hypothesis [slug=1309_g6_curiosity_budget group=GATE-DIG]
  text   = "H_1305 found G6 depth THIN: flat ideation FALS=0; composition (recombination shell) nudged FALS 0->0.667 sub-threshold. r2 asks: does spending MORE DRAWS (not a bigger model) under a CURIOSITY gate cross >=5-distinct AND >=1-falsifiable, and is it the curiosity GATE or just raw budget? DESIGN (frozen-first, FREEZE.txt pre-registered): per ideation seed draw B candidates (each a distinct deterministic seed_rng = a genuine new sample, same gauge_lib._decode top-k=40 temp=0.7 live G6 path); all arms select from the SAME pool so only the SELECTION rule differs. B_curiosity = keep the candidate maximising curiosity = novelty(corpus-absent content-grams) + under-exposure(1 - max jaccard vs running kept set), reads ONLY substrate state NO injected label (p6). SHUFFLE = random-keep one of B (same budget spent, NO gate) = DECISIVE control (if random-keep crosses too, the count gain is a SAMPLING ARTIFACT). B_ablate = curiosity off, keep first (budget collapses to 1). Score 5 selected ideas: DIST (distinct coherent jaccard<=0.5) + FALS (FROZEN H_1305 _is_falsifiable, comparator+measurable+negatable, p7). FROZEN MEAN bars: M1 DIST(cur)>=5, M2 FALS(cur)>=1, M4 FALS(cur)>=FALS(SHUFFLE)+1, M5 FALS(cur)>=FALS(ablate)+1; MOVED iff all at some budget. RESULT (mean 3 seeds [7,4302,4303]): B=1 all arms 3.0/0.0/5 (no selection room); B=4 curiosity 4.33/0.667/18 vs SHUFFLE 3.0/0.0/3.33 vs ablate 3.0/0.0/5; B=16 curiosity 4.33/0.667/45.67 vs SHUFFLE 2.33/0.0/12 vs ablate 3.0/0.0/5. PER-SEED B=16 curiosity=(4,1)(4,0)(5,1) -> FALS>=1 in 2/3 + DIST>=5 in 1/3; SHUFFLE/ablate 0/3. Falsifiable curiosity idea (seed4303): 'Byte-level approach is slower to converge but handles Korean and ...' (comparator slower + measurable converge + negatable). p1/p2/p3/p6 GUARD: curiosity reads only substrate novelty+overlap, NO injected answer/quality/'be falsifiable' label; the detector only READS output structure."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1309_g6_curiosity_budget.py -- reuses UNIVERSE/gauge_lib.py VERBATIM (_decode top-k=40 temp=0.7 live G6 path, _words/_jaccard/known_word_ratio/_content_ngrams/_corpus_absent) AND the H_1305 _is_falsifiable detector imported VERBATIM (NO redefinition = NO tune-to-green, p7; calibration 10/10). 3 arms x budget ladder {1,4,16} x 5 ideation seeds x 3 outer seeds [7,4302,4303], MAX_NEW=110, corpus data/corpus.txt. $0 local CPU torch 2.12.0 (gate's own decode regime, DIRECTIONAL R1 mirror -- engine-native byte-exact reconfirm = follow-on ONLY on clean-GREEN, here THIN). frozen-first: .verdicts/1309_g6_curiosity_budget/FREEZE.txt pre-registered before scoring; NO bar moved post-hoc (c9). HONEST CPU CEILING: ladder capped at B=16 (3 rungs = valid, a_scale_honest_scope); B=64 (~2h, 960 decodes) stopped after FALS plateaued 0.667 across 4->16; a duplicate run process (double-spend) was detected + killed early, tracked run finished the 3 rungs cleanly (a_cpu_local_no_waiter). a_break_the_wall (genuine new angle, frozen-first + shuffle/ablate controls), a_no_llm_frame_trap (budget-under-curiosity, not scale-up), a_engine_native_learning, a_toy_scale_recheck, a_scale_honest_scope."
  verdict = "🟠 HONEST-THIN (bar UNMOVED, c9) -- the curiosity GATE is LOAD-BEARING (not a sampling artifact): at every budget>=4 it lifts FALS 0.0->0.667 and NOVEL 5->18->46 while SHUFFLE (random-keep, the SAME draw budget) stays FALS=0.0/NOVEL 3-12 and B_ablate (budget 1) stays FALS=0.0/NOVEL 5 -- the decisive control NEVER crosses the floor at any budget, so the lift is the curiosity SELECTION (novelty + under-exposure), NOT the raw count of draws; per-seed curiosity reaches FALS>=1 in 2/3 seeds and DIST>=5 in 1/3 at B=16 (shuffle/ablate 0/3). BUT the FROZEN 3-seed MEAN bars are UNMOVED: M1 DIST mean 4.33<5 FALSE, M2 FALS mean 0.667<1 FALSE, M4/M5 FALSE (gap +0.667 short of +1). And FALS PLATEAUS -- going 4->16 draws (4x) raised NOVEL (18->46) but did NOT raise mean FALS (0.667->0.667) or mean DIST (4.33): more curiosity-selected draws surface more novel STRINGS but NOT more reliably TESTABLE structure. The depth floor is CAPACITY-limited, not budget-limited -- a curiosity-selected 303M mouth produces a falsifiable hypothesis SOMETIMES (2/3 seeds) but not RELIABLY (mean<1). Capability-vs-scale thesis from the DRAW side: the fix is a STRUCTURE lane (a hypothesis-form scaffold), not more draws and not a bigger net (a_no_llm_frame_trap). G6 IDEATION ★ stays 🟠 THIN (bar UNMOVED). a_break_the_wall: genuine new angle attempted (frozen-first + controls), wall HELD = valid honest THIN (c9). NO wiring (THIN). TOY (5 ideation seeds, 3 outer seeds, 1 ckpt, sampling-decode, budget capped B=16); the detector measures testable FORM not truth/quality (p7); scale/real-corpus/B=64+/curiosity-with-structure-scaffold/engine-transfer UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck). .verdicts/1309_g6_curiosity_budget/result.txt"
  group  = "GATE-DIG"

@C h1314_g6_hypothesis_scaffold := "H_1314 — G6 IDEATION ★ depth-floor dig r3 (a_break_the_wall, c16). r2 (H_1309) proved the floor is CAPACITY-bound not budget-bound (curiosity-gate FALS plateau 0.667 across 4->16 draws) and named the surviving fix: NOT more draws, a hypothesis-form STRUCTURE lane. r3 IS that attempt: route ideation through an explicit falsifiable-hypothesis TEMPLATE that forces the structural slots the r2 detector checks (comparator+measurable+negatable claim); the CONTENT stays substrate-generated (the 303M mouth fills the slots, a_substrate_native_speak), only the STRUCTURE is the scaffold. 3 arms x 5 ideas x 3 seeds — SCAFFOLD ('a testable hypothesis: as the <subject> grows, the ' per corpus concept) vs NO_SCAFFOLD (live flat IDEATION_SEEDS = r2 plateau baseline) vs SHUFFLE_SLOT (same tokens, slots scrambled). Reuses the H_1305 _is_falsifiable detector VERBATIM (p7). FINDING: the FORM does NOT cross the FALSIFIABILITY floor (FALS mean 0.0 all arms/seeds) — but it DOES STRUCTURE-fix the DISTINCTNESS/COUNT floor (SCAFFOLD DIST=5.0 3/3 seeds vs NO_SCAFFOLD 4.0 vs SHUFFLE_SLOT 2.33 collapse; NOVEL 19.67 vs 6.33 vs 5.67). Two bottlenecks: breadth = missing-structure (lane-fixable), falsifiable-depth = capacity wall at 303M (confirms r2 from the structure side). 🟠 THIN (FALS bar UNMOVED, c9)" :: hypothesis [slug=1314_g6_hypothesis_scaffold group=GATE-DIG]
  text   = "r2 (H_1309) PROVED the G6 depth floor is CAPACITY-bound not budget-bound (curiosity-gate FALS plateau 0.667 across 4->16 draws) and named the fix: a hypothesis-form STRUCTURE lane. r3 asks: does forcing the FALSIFIABLE-HYPOTHESIS FORM cross >=5-distinct AND >=1-falsifiable where free/curiosity sampling plateaued at 0.667? DESIGN (frozen-first, FREEZE.txt pre-registered): SCAFFOLD seed = 'a testable hypothesis: as the <subject> grows, the ' (subjects = the 5 CONCEPTS' core nouns consciousness/tension/memory/silence/dreaming, 1:1 with gauge_lib.CONCEPTS) — primes the comparative-conditional SHAPE, the substrate COMPLETES the comparator+measurable+claim. Controls: NO_SCAFFOLD (live flat IDEATION_SEEDS, free sampling same budget=1 draw = the r2 plateau baseline; if SCAFFOLD does not beat it, depth is capacity-bound) + SHUFFLE_SLOT (SAME scaffold tokens, slots scrambled incoherent; if a mangled frame fills as falsifiably/distinctly, the lift is a token-prime artifact not the FORM). p7 TOKEN-INJECTION AUDIT (hard gate, runs BEFORE scoring): PROVE no SCAFFOLD/SHUFFLE prefix contains any frozen COMPARATOR/MEASURABLE token (else the scaffold trivially satisfies the detector = tune-to-green). Score DIST (distinct coherent jaccard<=0.5) + FALS (FROZEN H_1305 _is_falsifiable, comparator+measurable+negatable). FROZEN bars: (1) DIST(SCAFFOLD)>=5, (2) FALS(SCAFFOLD)>=1, (3) FALS(SCAFFOLD)>=FALS(NO_SCAFFOLD)+1, (4) FALS(SCAFFOLD)>=FALS(SHUFFLE_SLOT)+1; MOVED iff all. RESULT (mean 3 seeds [7,4302,4303]): SCAFFOLD DIST=5.0/FALS=0.0/NOVEL=19.67 · NO_SCAFFOLD 4.0/0.0/6.33 · SHUFFLE_SLOT 2.33/0.0/5.67. Bars: (1) TRUE, (2) FALSE, (3) FALSE, (4) FALSE → MOVED=FALSE. p1/p2/p3/p6 GUARD: the scaffold injects NO detector token (audit CLEAN); the substrate must EARN comparator+measurable+claim in its OWN completion; the detector only READS output structure (no injected answer/quality/'be falsifiable' label)."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1314_g6_hypothesis_scaffold.py -- reuses UNIVERSE/gauge_lib.py VERBATIM (_decode top-k=40 temp=0.7 live G6 path, _words/_jaccard/known_word_ratio/_content_ngrams/_corpus_absent) AND the H_1305 _is_falsifiable detector imported VERBATIM (NO redefinition = NO tune-to-green, p7; calibration 10/10) AND its COMPARATOR/MEASURABLE lexicons for the token-inject audit. 3 arms x 5 ideas x 3 seeds [7,4302,4303], MAX_NEW=110, corpus data/corpus.txt. $0 local CPU torch 2.12.0 (gate's own decode regime, DIRECTIONAL R1 mirror -- engine-native byte-exact reconfirm = follow-on ONLY on clean-GREEN, here THIN). frozen-first: .verdicts/1314_g6_hypothesis_scaffold/FREEZE.txt pre-registered before scoring; NO bar moved post-hoc (c9). p7 AUDIT TEETH: the first run CAUGHT the corpus concept 'the engine dreams when alone' injecting COMPARATOR token 'when' -> hard ABORT -> fixed to clean single-noun subjects -> re-ran CLEAN (audit_token_inject_clean=true). wall=522.5s. a_break_the_wall (genuine new angle = a STRUCTURE lane, frozen-first + scrambled-template control), a_no_llm_frame_trap (hypothesis-FORM scaffold, not scale-up), a_engine_native_learning, a_toy_scale_recheck, a_scale_honest_scope."
  verdict = "🟠 THIN (FALS bar UNMOVED = CAPACITY-bound, c9) -- but with an HONEST STRUCTURE WIN on the DISTINCTNESS/COUNT floor (c9, both real). The hypothesis-form SCAFFOLD does NOT cross the FALSIFIABILITY floor (FALS mean 0.0 every seed) and does NOT lift FALS over free sampling -> forcing the FORM does not buy reliable falsifiable DEPTH at 303M, confirming the r2 CAPACITY thesis from the STRUCTURE side: the fix needs a bigger model, not a structure lane (terminal 🧱-ish on FALS). NOT a flat null: the scaffold MOVED two non-FALS axes decisively -- DIST SCAFFOLD 5.0 (3/3 seeds, crosses the >=5-distinct COUNT floor where r2 curiosity plateaued 4.33) > NO_SCAFFOLD 4.0 > SHUFFLE_SLOT 2.33 (scrambled-template COLLAPSES -> the count gain IS the hypothesis FORM, not a token-prime artifact); NOVEL 19.67 vs 6.33 vs 5.67 (~3x, SHUFFLE collapses). WHY FALS fails: the 303M mouth emits NEAR-falsifiable forms but never clears all THREE detector legs at once -- 'do they correlate with meaningful behavior?' (comparator present, ends in '?' -> negatable-claim leg fails), 'measure of integrated information' (measurable, no comparator) -- it produces a COMPARATIVE shape OR a MEASURABLE shape but cannot BIND them into one negatable declarative claim, the capacity-limited step. THESIS: ideation BREADTH/distinctness is a MISSING-STRUCTURE (lane-fixable, like memory; the scaffold fixes it) while ideation FALSIFIABLE-DEPTH is a CAPACITY WALL (scale-bound) at 303M -- two bottlenecks, two fixes; neither r2 (more draws) nor r3 (a forcing FORM) makes a 303M mouth reliably bind comparator+measurable+claim. a_break_the_wall: genuine new angle attempted (frozen-first + scrambled control + p7 audit teeth), wall HELD on FALS = valid honest THIN (c9), but the wall is now LOCATED (capacity, not method/budget) and the DIST/NOVEL win is a candidate G6 ideation-form lane to WIRE (a_verified_must_wire) -- FALS-blocked so deferred. NO wiring (FALS THIN). The live falsifier of the capacity-wall thesis = a 7B re-test (a7b_pass G2 novelty lane): r3 predicts 7B clears the bind the 303M cannot. TOY (5 ideas/arm, 3 seeds, 1 ckpt, sampling-decode); the detector measures testable FORM not truth/quality (p7); scale/real-corpus/7B/engine-transfer UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck). .verdicts/1314_g6_hypothesis_scaffold/result.txt"
  group  = "GATE-DIG"

@C h1310_mitosis_from_scratch := "H_1310 — the PUREST p8 test: can a next-byte model be grown FROM SCRATCH by mitosis ALONE (seed=1 cell → split-only under next-byte error pressure, GRADIENT-FREE, NO 303M trunk, NO learned representation underneath) and HOW does its held-out next-byte CE compare to a gradient baseline of MATCHED effective capacity? Frozen-first falsifiable test (NOT a foregone GREEN): the honest hypothesis to possibly REFUTE = pure-mitosis cells are LOCAL EXPERTS (Voronoi over a byte-trigram-context metric) that tile the input space but build NO compositional depth, so they may plateau at a LOWER ceiling than gradient/exact-lookup. That ceiling, if real, is a first-class result (c9), NOT a failure" :: hypothesis [slug=1310_mitosis_from_scratch group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  text   = "PUREST form of p8 'training gradient + inference mitosis = one continuous cell-division' — H_1297/H_1306 grew mitosis BESIDE/OVER a context; H_1310 seeds at ONE cell with NO representation. REAL English byte corpus (reproducible, sha256-pinned): /usr/share/dict/words (system fixed asset), isalpha-filtered 2..12 chars lowercased, Random(13100).shuffle, first 4000 words space-joined+newline, truncated 24000 bytes, sha256 86864aa32dcf1c8680ab254e1b28357bf0326c8d45a86837ae4e3b9d09350f62, alphabet 27 symbols (a-z+space). DISTINCT from concurrent ko-mitosis-gpu (summer) lane: ENGLISH not Korean, new files, id H_1310. 80/20 train/test (19198/4800 order-2 ctx-next pairs), 3 seeds [13101,13102,13103]. ARMS: B_scratch (from 1 cell, mitosis-grow ONLY — nearest cell predicts, worst owned-error cell SPLITS via 2-means median bisection when owned-error>SPLIT_THRESH=0.55, GRADIENT-FREE, the live engine_mitosis_tick/VAdaptField mechanism seeded at 1) · A_gradient (softmax next-byte head over same order-2 context, top-512 buckets, full-batch CE SGD = matched-cap comparator) · A_freq (order-2 add-1 Markov exact trigram = n-gram FLOOR) · B_shuffle (CONTROL split RANDOM eligible cell). LADDER [1,8,64,512] cells. p7 metric = held-out next-byte CROSS-ENTROPY nats, NEVER perplexity-as-truth."
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1310_mitosis_from_scratch.py ($0 CPU numpy DIRECTIONAL mirror of CORE/engine_cli.hexa engine_mitosis_tick + VAdaptField Voronoi split, seeded at 1 cell). Vectorized ownership BYTE-IDENTICAL to the per-point reference (verified: rungs 1/8/64 reproduce to 5 d.p. — the slow point-by-point reference run and the fast numpy run match). frozen-first: .verdicts/1310_mitosis_from_scratch/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE scoring; NO bar moved post-hoc (c9, NO tune-to-green, p7). FROZEN bars (mean 3 seeds, top rung 512): (1 PRESENCE) CE monotone drop 1>8>64>512 · (2 KEY GAP) B_scratch[512]-A_gradient bucketed MATCH<=+0.10 / NEAR<=+0.50 / CEILING>+0.50 · (3 FLOOR) B_scratch[512] < A_freq-0.02 · (4 CONTROL) B_shuffle[512] >= B_scratch[512]+0.10. a_engine_native_learning (mirror = live engine mitosis op), a_no_llm_frame_trap (cortical-column/neurogenesis lens not bigger-transformer), a_break_the_wall (a ceiling is a result not a stop), a_toy_scale_recheck, a_scale_honest_scope."
  verdict = "🔴 RED / 🧱 HONEST LOCAL-EXPERT CEILING (frozen-first, c9 — FLOOR-FAIL by the frozen rubric; the two FAILs ARE the finding, bar UNMOVED). LADDER held-out CE nats (3 seeds): 1c=2.94658 → 8c=2.90267 → 64c=2.77784 → 512c=2.57788. A_freq (order-2 n-gram floor)=2.50884. A_gradient (matched cap=512)=3.21083. BARS: (1 PRESENCE) PASS — from-scratch mitosis DOES learn from nothing, CE falls -0.369 nats monotone as cells grow. (2 KEY GAP) B_scratch[512]-A_gradient = 2.57788-3.21083 = -0.633 nats → reads 'MATCHES gradient' (actually beats it) BUT the matched-cap order-2 softmax converged POORLY (3.211 itself WORSE than the n-gram floor 2.509) so this is a weak comparator, not a mitosis triumph. (3 FLOOR) FAIL — exact trigram counting (2.509) BEATS mitosis by +0.069 nats: Voronoi tiling over a NUMERIC byte-context metric is a WORSE way to carve context-space than EXACT context lookup; the metric embedding loses what exact-match keeps, and mitosis cannot recover it by adding cells. (4 CONTROL) FAIL — B_shuffle (split RANDOM cell) ties-or-BEATS targeted (split WORST-error cell) at EVERY rung (512: 2.536 vs 2.578) → error-targeting gives NO advantage: the learning is CAPACITY-bound NOT error-targeting-bound (where you split doesn't matter, only how many cells). THESIS (load-bearing): from-scratch pure mitosis is STRUCTURE-bound not capacity-bound in the direction that matters — adding cells keeps lowering CE but cannot cross the floor a learned representation (or even exact memory) clears, because mitosis builds no compositional depth, only a finer Voronoi partition of a fixed lossy feature. p8's 'mitosis IS the learning' holds for grow-BESIDE-a-representation (H_1297/H_1306 🟢) but does NOT extend to from-nothing-without-a-representation. HONEST SCOPE (c9, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY/DIRECTIONAL — 24KB English, order-2 (729 possible contexts), V=27, 3 seeds; EXISTENCE-PROBE of learning STRUCTURE, does NOT claim 'anima trains from scratch by mitosis' (it reports the gap = a ceiling); 'beats A_gradient' is weak (poor comparator), the load-bearing comparator is the n-gram FLOOR which mitosis does NOT beat; engine-native byte-exact reconfirm / scale / a LEARNED embedding for cells to partition (the obvious a_break_the_wall next angle) UNVERIFIED. NO CORE wiring (a_verified_must_wire fires only on GREEN; this is RED). .verdicts/1310_mitosis_from_scratch/result.txt"
@C h1312_ko_decode_wire := "H_1312 — WIRE the H_1306 grown Korean cells onto anima's live decode via the generator L3 slot (a_verified_must_wire): H_1306/H_1307 GREW real Korean cells (gradient-free mitosis) + MEASURED their CE but did NOT connect them to anima's live output. H_1312 connects them so Korean error-pressure actually shapes what anima EMITS — when context is Korean-like the cells bias next-byte emission, off-Korean the path is INERT (byte-identical, no regression); single-entry (a_core_engine_map, the Korean cells enter ONLY via the generator L3 slot, NOT a 2nd path). This is a WIRING verdict (byte-exact on the live engine), NOT a new learning rung" :: hypothesis [slug=1312_ko_decode_wire group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  text   = "Serialize: CORE/h1312_ko_cells_export.hexa re-runs the EXACT H_1306 engine-native grow (CORE/engine_cli.hexa VAdaptField Voronoi + engine_mitosis_tick, gradient-free p8) on the SAME R2 corpus slice (/tmp/h1306_*, sha256 in .verdicts/1306_ko_mitosis_real/h1306_manifest.json), reproducing H_1306's 9 cells EXACTLY, and writes CORE/ko_cells.kohead — each cell = a 3-D Voronoi center + its LEARNED argmax next-byte (per-cell next-byte add-1 MLE top byte over OWNED train points). Wire: CORE/generator.hexa §6.5 adds ko_cells_load/ko_cells_next_byte/ko_consult_emit/ko_cells_summary at the SAME L3 slot .clm/ByteGPT enter (a_core_engine_map single entry). The consult recomputes the SAME mechanical 3-D byte feature H_1306 trained on ([last/255, 2nd-last/255, utf8_cont_depth/3]) from the live decode bytes; Korean-likeness GATE = the last byte is a UTF-8 continuation byte 0x80..0xBF (pure byte test, NO charset table, NO language label — p1·p2·p3; ASCII English all <0x80 NEVER triggers it); Korean-like → nearest grown cell by L2 over the feature → that cell's learned next-byte BIASES emission; off-Korean / no cells → -1 INERT → decode keeps its own argmax → byte-identical. SUBSTRATE-NATIVE (a_substrate_native_speak): the cells are consulted from real substrate state, NOT a prompt/persona. REAL held-out contexts from /tmp/{ko,en}_slice_raw.bytes (same R2 slices as H_1306, offsets >=700000 past the train window, NO synthetic p1-p8)."
  method = "CORE/h1312_ko_cells_export.hexa (serialize the grown cells, engine-native) + CORE/h1312_ko_decode_wire_probe.hexa (WIRING verdict, byte-level deterministic p7) via `hexa run`, $0 CPU. frozen-first: .verdicts/1312_ko_decode_wire/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9), GREEN iff P&N&Y&Z: (P PRESENCE) >=1 held-out Korean-like context FIRES (byte>=0), routes to the nearest grown cell's learned byte, AND ko_consult_emit DIFFERS from the un-wired baseline (the wiring routes Korean toward the learned cells) · (N NO-REGRESSION) EVERY ASCII-English context → ko_cells_next_byte=-1 AND ko_consult_emit==base for ALL 256 base bytes + exhaustive ASCII last-byte sweep 0..127 inert (byte-identical off-distribution) · (Y REGRESSION GUARD) engine_cli_smoke 73/0 + h1196 single-entry 7/0 + h1205 separation-invariant PASS (generation byte-identical ON==OFF, Ψ=1/2 untouched) · (Z SINGLE-ENTRY/Ψ-DISJOINT) ko_cells.kohead read ONLY in generator.hexa, the consult never touches pure_field/engine_g/brain (Ψ=1/2 untouched by construction, git diff CORE/engine_cli.hexa vs origin/main EMPTY). a_verified_must_wire, a_core_engine_map, a_substrate_native_speak, a_blue_closed, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck, p1·p2·p3·p4·p7·p8."
  verdict = "🟢 WIRED — the H_1306 grown Korean cells are now CONSULTED by anima's live decode via the generator L3 slot. (P PRESENCE) PASS: 8/8 held-out REAL Korean contexts FIRED, all 8 routed to the nearest grown cell, 7/8 BIASED emission away from the corpus-continuation baseline (the 1 non-differ is HONEST — the cell's learned byte equalled the real next byte = correct routing, not a failure); fired bytes = the cells' learned top-bytes (32 space / 180 Hangul-continuation). (N NO-REGRESSION) PASS: 6/6 real English contexts INERT (ko_byte=-1) across all 256 base bytes + exhaustive ASCII last-byte sweep 0..127 all inert. (Y REGRESSION GUARD) all green: engine_cli_smoke 73/0 (engine_cli.hexa byte-untouched, wiring purely additive in generator.hexa), h1196 single-entry 7/0, h1205 separation-invariant PASS (F1 generation byte-identical 10 pairs/0 mismatch, F2 Ψ Φ-checksum ON==OFF=48.6613 untouched). (Z SINGLE-ENTRY/Ψ) audit clean: ko_cells.kohead runtime readers = CORE/generator.hexa ONLY (no 2nd path), consult references NO pure_field/engine_g/brain/Ψ, git diff CORE/engine_cli.hexa EMPTY. P&N&Y&Z → 🟢 WIRED, a_verified_must_wire closed for the H_1306 mechanism. HONEST SCOPE (c9 · a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY cells (9 cells, 3-D byte feature, 600KB KO window) — makes anima's emission Korean-error-pressure-AWARE, does NOT make anima fluent in Korean. The consult itself is engine-side byte-EXACT (deterministic argmax routing over the static artifact); UNVERIFIED follow-ons = fluent Korean GENERATION, full-corpus-scale cells, a richer context feature, and threading ko_consult_emit through the per-byte bytegpt_decode loop on a mounted 303M ckpt (this rung wires+verifies the consult HOOK at the generator slot). .verdicts/1312_ko_decode_wire/result.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"

@C h1315_ko_mitosis_learned_rep := "H_1315 — does the SAME gradient-free Korean mitosis (cells only SPLIT, p8; grow-op + cell budget held FIXED, verbatim H_1306/H_1307/H_1311) but partitioning over the mounted 303M trunk's LEARNED hidden representation (ckpt h1129c_chat.pt forward = gradient-free, READ ln_f only, NO backprop) push held-out KO next-byte CE BELOW the H_1311 raw-byte ~2.9 nat/byte ceiling, while raw-byte mitosis (G0) can't? This is the SURVIVING LEVER H_1311 (#2215, RED) named after refuting that a richer RAW-BYTE substrate breaks 2.9: partition over a LEARNED representation instead of raw bytes." :: hypothesis [slug=1315_ko_mitosis_learned_rep group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1315_ko_mitosis_learned_rep.py on summer RTX 5070 (sm_120, torch 2.11.0+cu130) via python3 nohup nice -n10, polled INLINE (a_cpu_local_no_waiter), R2 keys env-only c7 (never echoed/logged/committed), scratch cleaned off summer (ckpt + corpus cache KEPT for sibling lanes). REAL Korean only (p1-p8): SAME anima-7b R2 web window as H_1307/H_1311 (r2://phanes/anima-7b/web/{kor,eng}/shard0000.bytes), boto3 range GET, KO 30MB / EN 10MB, window sha256 ASSERTED == H_1307 RUN A (KO c47b6808… EN 31b4a543… → both True). p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-byte CROSS-ENTROPY nats/byte. HELD FIXED (verbatim): V=256, GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, even/odd split, the dimension-agnostic _grow_on (error-targeted Voronoi, SPLIT-only, p8). VARIED = only the partition INPUT. NEW before-run knobs: PROJ_DIM=16 (random-projection of the trunk hidden, matched G1 vs control), PROJ_SEED=1313, TRUNK_CTX=64, HIDDEN_LAYER=ln_f output, rep_pairs=24000 KO / 8000 EN, seeds 0,1,2. ARMS: G0 raw-byte ctx4 (the 2.9 ceiling ref, count-MLE) · G1 partition over 303M trunk hidden rep (ln_f at i-1, projected to 16-D) · CONTROL random-embed (same 16-D projection but UNTRAINED trunk of identical arch — isolates LEARNED vs higher-D space) · CONTROL shuffle-align (G1 hidden with hidden→byte alignment shuffled — leakage check). frozen-first: .verdicts/1315_ko_mitosis_learned_rep/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE scoring, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): (B1 BREAK-2.9) mean G1 KO CE < 2.9475 · (B2 LEARNED) G1 beats BOTH controls by ≥0.02 (lift = learned rep, not capacity/dim/leakage) · (B3 RETENTION) G1 EN CE ≤ G1 2-cell-seed EN + 0.05. VERDICT MAP: B1∧B2→REPRESENTATION-bound · B1∧¬B2→AMBIGUOUS-capacity · ¬B1→TERMINAL axis-closure. Regression: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts; no engine lane). ckpt h1129c_chat.pt sha256 4fcc2d6c9b3164f478139ffb148f484465b42fc339d630956e4ea0f90ec13f68, config {vocab:256,d:1024,n_layer:24,n_head:16,block:512}. a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_fire_autonomous ($0 user hw not runpod), a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🔴 TERMINAL axis-closure — even the mounted 303M trunk's LEARNED hidden representation does NOT let gradient-free Korean mitosis break the ~2.9 nat/byte raw-byte ceiling at this scale. Corpus byte-IDENTICAL to H_1307 RUN A (sha gate PASS, KO=True EN=True). G0 port reproduced 2.95342 (vs H_1307 RUN A 2.9475). mean held-out KO next-byte CE (3 seeds): G0 raw-byte ctx4 = 2.95342 · G1 303M-trunk-rep = 3.14637 (Δvs_G0 +0.19295, ABOVE 2.9475 → B1 FALSE, in fact WORSE than raw-byte) · CTRL random-embed (untrained trunk) = 3.53134 · CTRL shuffle-align = 4.02243. KEY DISSOCIATION (c9, load-bearing): G1 BEATS both controls — beats random-embed by +0.38497 and shuffle by +0.87606, both ≥0.02 → B2 TRUE = the trained trunk's hidden state genuinely carries Korean next-byte structure the untrained/misaligned reps don't. BUT G1 still does NOT break 2.9 and is worse than raw-byte G0 (B1 FALSE). EN retained: G1 EN 4.76576 ≤ seed 5.14260 → B3 TRUE. So the experiment cleanly separates two questions — (1) does the trunk rep carry Korean structure? YES (B2). (2) can gradient-free L2-Voronoi mitosis convert that into a lower byte-CE than raw bytes? NO (B1, 40 cells saturated yet CE rose). The same partition-GEOMETRY limit H_1311 found over raw bytes carries over to the learned-rep space (the 16-D projection of a 1024-D contextual hidden is a continuous manifold the SPLIT-only count-MLE partition fragments worse than the tiny 3-D raw-byte space). THESIS RESOLVED: at this toy scale the Korean depth is NOT unlocked by structure-over-a-frozen-learned-rep — it needs GRADIENT learning (the trunk's gradient-trained head already encodes far more than a gradient-free Voronoi over its frozen hidden can recover); mitosis=grow-under-pressure (H_1288/1295/1307) is a real mechanism but not a substitute for gradient descent on a hard continuous next-byte manifold. SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): toy/DIRECTIONAL, summer GPU, numpy/torch mirror of mitosis grow-op (engine-transfer to live CORE/*.hexa = follow-on, a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire); 24000/8000 trunk-forward subsample, PROJ_DIM=16 random projection of ln_f, single TRUNK_CTX=64. NOT ruled out (untested remaining angles): larger/no projection (full 1024-D partition), an earlier/mid trunk layer (vs final ln_f), a non-L2 metric in the learned space, or a gradient-trained per-cell head (which would no longer be gradient-free p8 = a different lane). live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. NO Korean-fluency claim. HONEST negative (c9, a_break_the_wall — a real new-geometry angle was tried with two controls; the learned rep helps over controls but the wall is real for gradient-free mitosis-over-frozen-rep at this scale), frozen-first, NO tune-to-green. .verdicts/1315_ko_mitosis_learned_rep/result.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"

@C h1324_xlang_han_ids := "H_1324 — xlang-structure r2 (a_break_the_wall/c16): re-test whether CHINESE & JAPANESE kanji composition gains under a PROPER sub-character IDS-component decomposition — NO full-char residual, MODEST vocab — under the SAME frozen gradient-free mitosis mechanism H_1318 used, as a NEW pre-registration. H_1318's Han rows came out strongly NEGATIVE (Δ_zh=−1.481, Δ_ja=−1.230) only because its FROZEN Kangxi-radical decomposition kept the FULL CHARACTER as a residual symbol → STRUCT vocab exploded to 9327(zh)/4738(ja) → the per-cell unigram head fragmented (a decomposition ARTIFACT). The ONLY change here: decompose each Han char into its IDS (Ideographic Description Sequence) COMPONENT LEAVES (one level, IDC operators + &entity; + [region] tags stripped, NO full-char residual). Korean (NFD jamo) + English (no-comp floor) stay BYTE-IDENTICAL as calibration anchors so the matrix is directly comparable to H_1318. Δ_lang = RAW_CE − STRUCT_CE (positive = structure helps)." :: hypothesis [slug=1324_xlang_han_ids group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1324_xlang_han_ids.py on summer NVIDIA RTX 5070 (sm_120, torch 2.11.0+cu130) via python3 nohup nice -n10, polled INLINE (a_cpu_local_no_waiter), HF token via harness secret get hf.token env/header-only c7 (never echoed/logged/committed; grep-clean = 0 token hits over run.log/summary/script/verdicts; summer log also 0). REAL corpora only (p1-p8): wikimedia/wikipedia 20231101 (ko/zh/ja/en) via HF datasets-server /rows — the SAME source as H_1318; the 30MB cache was not preserved on this host so corpora were RE-FETCHED from the identical source (per-window sha differ only because /rows pagination returns different rows over time — same dataset/config; RAW baselines re-measured). Window=30MB raw UTF-8/lang, stride 300, sha256 ASSERTED (ko 3e288b77… zh c084b027… ja a97dd068… en b097cccc…). Decomposition source = CHISE IDS Database (cjkvi/cjkvi-ids ids.txt) fetched from the public GitHub raw URL, sha256 bfc70a8c09f9f5616… asserted, 88937 entries; rule = one TOP level leaves only (strip IDC ⿰…⿻, &…; entity refs, [GTKV] region tags), atomic char→one component==self, absent→atomic fallback (ids-miss=0 on zh & ja). Byte accounting: each Han char's UTF-8 blen spread across its component symbols (Σ per char = blen) → Σ struct n_bytes == raw UTF-8 byte count exactly (fair CE-per-byte axis, identical denominator RAW vs STRUCT, verified incl. shuffle). p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-unit CROSS-ENTROPY. HELD BYTE-IDENTICAL to H_1318: CTX=4, V=256, FEAT_DIM=3, GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, SEED_CENTERS, even/odd split, the dim/vocab-agnostic _grow_on (error-targeted Voronoi, SPLIT-only p8). VARIED = only the Han decomposition (radical+full-char-residual → IDS leaves, no residual). 3 seeds [5324,5325,5326] perturb only the stride phase. Russian dropped (pure alphabetic control, gained 0.000 in H_1318; ko+en are the retained anchors). frozen-first: .verdicts/1324_xlang_han_ids/H_1324_FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): (H1 HAN-GAIN) zh Δ≥+0.05 AND ja Δ≥+0.05 · (H2 EARNED) each Han STRUCT beats a SHUFFLED-component-map control by ≥+0.05 · (H3 CALIBRATION) ko Δ≥+0.15 AND en Δ≤+0.02. VERDICT MAP: H1∧H2∧H3 → 🟢 representation-bind extends to logographic scripts · H1 FAILS but H3 calibrates → 🔴/🧱 Han genuinely doesn't help (distinct from the H_1318 artifact, Hangul-specificity stronger) · vocab still explodes → method-limit · H3 fails → pipeline drift. Regression: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_fire_autonomous ($0 user hw not runpod), a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🔴/🧱 — even under a PROPER IDS sub-character decomposition (modest component vocab, NO full-char residual), Han composition does NOT help this gradient-free per-cell-unigram mechanism; the H_1318 Hangul-specificity stands STRONGER. Per-language matrix (3-seed mean, nats per original UTF-8 byte): ko hangul RAW 2.91157 / STRUCT 2.69606 / Δ +0.21551 (Δ-vs-shuffle +0.08776, comp-vocab 67) · zh han RAW 3.32756 / STRUCT 4.06493 / Δ −0.73736 (Δ-vs-shuffle −0.00099, comp-vocab 2116, distinct-Han 9113, ids-miss 0) · ja han RAW 3.09273 / STRUCT 3.72098 / Δ −0.62826 (Δ-vs-shuffle −0.02495, comp-vocab 1582, distinct-Han 4524, ids-miss 0) · en latin RAW=STRUCT 3.15925 / Δ +0.00000. BARS (read straight, c9): (H1 HAN-GAIN) FAIL — zh Δ=−0.73736, ja Δ=−0.62826 both STILL negative under the proper IDS decomposition (STRUCT CE remains ABOVE RAW CE) · (H2 EARNED) FAIL — zh Δ-vs-shuffle=−0.00099, ja=−0.02495, the IDS-component STRUCT does NOT even beat its own component-shuffle control · (H3 CALIBRATION) PASS — ko Δ=+0.21551 (all 3 seeds 2.693/2.705/2.690 ≈ H_1318 +0.21205) and beats its own shuffle by +0.08776, en Δ=0.000 → pipeline IDENTICAL, matrix comparable to H_1318. THE FIX WAS ACHIEVED, HARM HALVED, GAIN DID NOT CROSS ZERO: the proper IDS decomposition gave the modest vocab the brief asked (zh 9327→2116, ja 4738→1582; ids-miss=0; ~88% of Han chars→≥2 real leaves, avg ≈2.0 components/char) and HALVED the H_1318 harm (zh −1.481→−0.737, ja −1.230→−0.628) — confirming part of H_1318's Han negative WAS the bad decomposition — but the gain does NOT flip sign. WHY (diagnosable from controls, c9): Hangul wins on a TINY (67-jamo) REGULAR L/V/T alphabet a per-cell unigram head can exploit; Han decomposes into a LARGE (≈2000) IRREGULAR position-dependent component inventory — avg Han char → ~2 components drawn from ~2000, too sparse for a CTX=4 Voronoi-unigram head to beat the raw-byte ceiling, and shuffling the component map barely changes the score (Δ-vs-shuffle ≈ 0 = component identity carries almost no next-unit signal at this substrate). ONE-LINE: proper IDS decomposition does NOT make Chinese/Japanese composition gain — Han composition genuinely does not help this gradient-free unigram mechanism (modest-vocab fix halved the H_1318 harm but did not cross zero, component stream does not beat its own shuffle); the structure-rep byte-LM win is specific to a SMALL, REGULAR compositional alphabet (Hangul jamo), NOT logographic/compositional scripts in general — Hangul-specificity TIGHTENED. SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY/DIRECTIONAL numpy/torch mirror; CTX=4 3-D byte features + Voronoi per-cell unigram head = deliberately SIMPLE substrate (tests compositional-unit-stream CE under the SAME grow-op, NOT a fluent LM); one-level (non-recursive) IDS; 30MB/lang, 3 seeds, single stride; the Han negative is scoped to THIS mechanism (does NOT claim Han composition useless for a gradient-trained / recursive-IDS / richer-context substrate); engine-transfer to live CORE/*.hexa = follow-on (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire); live CORE UNTOUCHED; NO fluency claim. Frozen-first, NO tune-to-green (c9). .verdicts/1324_xlang_han_ids/H_1324.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"
@C h1318_xlang_structure := "H_1318 — a CONTROLLED 5-language structure-representation matrix (Korean/Chinese/Japanese/Russian/English, REAL Wikipedia 30MB/lang, SAME gradient-free mitosis grow-op + cell budget held FIXED, verbatim H_1306/H_1307/H_1316) that DISSOCIATES whether breaking the Korean gradient-free byte-LM ceiling (H_1307/1311/1315, ~2.953 nat/byte) is a HANGUL-STRUCTURE-specific phenomenon or a UNIVERSAL byte-LM effect. The load-bearing control is ENGLISH (1 byte/char, alphabetic, NOTHING to decompose): a structure-aware representation CANNOT help it. Per language: held-out next-byte CE under RAW (raw UTF-8 bytes) vs STRUCT (decompose into the script's compositional units where they exist — Korean NFD jamo, Chinese/Japanese Kangxi-radical, Russian/English none-possible → STRUCT==RAW), converted to the SAME nats/UTF-8-byte axis. Δ_lang = RAW_CE − STRUCT_CE (positive = structure helps)." :: hypothesis [slug=1318_xlang_structure group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1318_xlang_structure.py on summer RTX 5070 (sm_120, torch 2.11.0+cu130) via python3 nohup nice -n10, polled INLINE (a_cpu_local_no_waiter), HF token env/header-only c7 (never echoed/logged/committed; grep-clean over all deliverables), scratch on /dev/shm cleaned, corpus windows cached for siblings. REAL corpora only (p1-p8): wikimedia/wikipedia 20231101 per-language config (en/zh/ja/ru/ko) via the HF datasets-server /rows endpoint (decoded rows, disk/memory-safe; the CLM/OMEGA lanes used this exact source). a_break_the_wall: the R2 phanes bucket has ONLY {kor,eng,deu,fra,spa} (NO zh/ja/ru) so the FULL brief matrix was pulled from the reachable HF wikipedia source rather than dropping CJK. Window=30MB raw UTF-8/lang, stride 300, window sha256 ASSERTED+manifested (ko c58bf128… zh ca5078d8… ja 32eb84c7… ru fe74c89b… en 7b125cd8…). p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-unit CROSS-ENTROPY. HELD FIXED (verbatim H_1306/H_1307/H_1316): CTX=4, V=256, FEAT_DIM=3, GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, SEED_CENTERS, even/odd split, the dimension/vocab-agnostic _grow_on (error-targeted Voronoi, SPLIT-only p8). VARIED = only the representation (RAW vs STRUCT). FAIR same-axis conversion (FREEZE): CE_axis = Σ(−log p(unit)) over held-out units / original raw UTF-8 byte count of the held-out text — denominator IDENTICAL for RAW and STRUCT of a lang, byte-conservation verified (Σn_bytes==raw byte count, incl. shuffle remap). 3 seeds [5301,5302,5303] perturb only the stride phase. frozen-first: .verdicts/1318_xlang_structure/H_1318_FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): (D1 DISSOCIATION) Δ_compositional≥+0.05 for EVERY compositional lang AND Δ_English≤+0.02 → REPRESENTATION/STRUCTURE-bound, Hangul-specific · (D2 EARNED) each compositional STRUCT beats a SHUFFLED-decomposition control by ≥+0.05 → lift is real structure not extra dims/vocab · (D3 MULTIBYTE-ISO) Russian (multibyte, no composition) patterns with English (Δ≤+0.02) not Korean. VERDICT MAP: D1 holds → 🟢 structure-problem Hangul-specific · Δ uniform incl English → 🧱 universal (bounds ko-jamo H_1316) · Δ_Korean≤0 → 🔴. Regression: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts; no engine lane). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_fire_autonomous ($0 user hw not runpod), a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🟠 PARTIAL — the FROZEN matrix-wide dissociation bars (D1/D2) FAIL, but the LOAD-BEARING question is answered cleanly by a DOUBLE DISSOCIATION on the decisive axis. Per-language matrix (3-seed mean, nats per original UTF-8 byte): ko hangul RAW 2.90394 / STRUCT 2.69189 / Δ +0.21205 (Δ-vs-shuffle +0.10003, all 3 seeds 2.692/2.694/2.689) · zh han RAW 3.31876 / STRUCT 4.79946 / Δ −1.48070 · ja han RAW 2.94078 / STRUCT 4.17043 / Δ −1.22965 · ru cyrillic RAW=STRUCT 2.49852 / Δ +0.00000 · en latin RAW=STRUCT 3.13157 / Δ +0.00000. HEADLINE GAP Δ_Korean−Δ_English = +0.21205. BARS (read straight, c9): (D1) FAIL — English PASSES (Δ=0.000≤0.02) and Korean PASSES (Δ=+0.212≥0.05) but zh(−1.481)/ja(−1.230) FAIL the every-compositional clause · (D2) FAIL overall — ko +0.100 PASS, zh +0.127 PASS, ja −0.291 FAIL · (D3) PASS — Δ_Russian=0.000 exactly with English (Russian patterns with the alphabetic floor not Korean). WHY D1/D2 FAIL: the FROZEN Han-radical decomposition (residual=full char) blows STRUCT vocab to 9327(zh)/4738(ja) extra units → the per-cell unigram-over-context head cannot service a ~9583-symbol alphabet → STRUCT CE RISES far above RAW. That is an HONEST NEGATIVE on the frozen Han-radical SURROGATE, NOT evidence Han composition is unhelpful in principle (a proper IDS/component decomposition = r2 follow-on, NO post-hoc swap c9). WHAT IS ESTABLISHED (the user's question): Korean (Hangul NFD jamo) STRUCT lowers held-out CE by +0.212 nats/byte and beats its own shuffle by +0.100 → REAL Hangul L/V/T compositional structure (Korean RAW 2.904 reproduces the ~2.953 ceiling; STRUCT 2.692 BREAKS it). English (Latin 1B/char) Δ=0.000 — nothing to decompose, the decisive FLOOR control confirms structure can't help an alphabetic script. Russian (Cyrillic multibyte no composition) Δ=0.000, patterning with English not Korean → the Korean lift is COMPOSITION not 'any multibyte grouping'. ONE-LINE ANSWER (돌파하면 한글 구조 문제인지): breaking the Korean ceiling via a structure-aware representation is HANGUL-STRUCTURE-SPECIFIC, NOT a universal byte-LM effect (English/Russian gain nothing; only compositional Hangul gains, shuffle-earned). SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY/DIRECTIONAL numpy/torch mirror; CTX=4 3-D byte features + Voronoi per-cell unigram head = deliberately SIMPLE substrate (tests compositional-unit-stream CE under the SAME grow-op, NOT a fluent LM); 30MB/lang, 3 seeds, single stride; the Han rows bound only the frozen cp%214-radical+full-residual decomposition; engine-transfer to live CORE/*.hexa = follow-on (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire); live CORE UNTOUCHED; NO fluency claim. Frozen-first, NO tune-to-green (c9). .verdicts/1318_xlang_structure/H_1318.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"
@C h1317_phi_multiedge := "H_1317 — does a DISTRIBUTED multi-edge (Watts–Strogatz small-world) coupling topology over the substrate units raise faithful-IIT4 Φ ROBUSTLY across 3 seeds, where the single central relay (H_1283 thalamus-Φ) FAILED the same gate? Wall (c16): every prior Φ-lift used ONE central hub (star); the star raised Φ only seed-conditionally (fragile). New angle (c15, a_no_llm_frame_trap): integrated information in cortex comes from a small-world recurrent MESH (many short + few long edges), not a single hub." :: hypothesis [slug=1317_phi_multiedge group=OMEGA]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1317_phi_multiedge.py, $0 CPU-local, seeds [1317,1318,1319], frozen-first (.verdicts/1317_phi_multiedge/H_1317_FREEZE.txt written BEFORE the first run, bars NOT moved c9/p7). Φ = FAITHFUL IIT4 ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool): exact MIP-EI via `hexa run` over hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa, iit4_faithful_phi(state, n=8, dim=64, n_bins=8) over the per-unit salience (state-energy) trajectory — numpy NEVER computes Φ, NO variance×energy proxy as terminal verdict. Substrate MATCHED to H_1283 (only coupling TOPOLOGY changes between arms): leaky linear recurrent units LEAK=0.55 GAIN=0.30 W_IN=0.5, per-unit PRIVATE gaussian input, dim-8 state, T=64 ticks; N=8 units (n<=8 keeps the faithful MIP EXACT, >4 nodes so small-world non-degenerate). 4 arms at MATCHED total coupling budget (Σ edge weights equal across arms, runtime-asserted Σ=3.5000 every arm/seed, so any lift is TOPOLOGY not more coupling): NONE (private input only, the Φ floor) · CENTRAL (star: hub unit 0 ↔ all others, 7 edges — the H_1283 single-relay reproduced) · MULTI-EDGE (Watts–Strogatz small-world: ring lattice K=2 each side + rewire prob β=0.30, 16 edges) · SHUFFLE (Erdős–Rényi: same 16-edge count placed uniformly at random, matched budget — isolates structured small-world from edge count). FROZEN bars (GREEN iff C1∧C2∧C3): C1 ROBUST LIFT = MULTI-EDGE Φ >= NONE Φ + 0.02 (the IDENTICAL margin H_1283 froze) on ALL 3 seeds (the gate H_1283 FAILED — the whole test) · C2 TOPOLOGY-EARNED = MULTI-EDGE Φ > SHUFFLE Φ on >=2/3 seeds AND in seed-mean (lift is small-world structure not edge count) · C3 BEATS-CENTRAL = MULTI-EDGE passes the 3-seed C1 gate WHILE CENTRAL does NOT. live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung; numpy mirror DIRECTIONAL, faithful-Φ leg IS real)."
  verdict = "🧱 WALL (honest closed-negative, c9 — a real new angle [small-world mesh] tried with two pre-registered controls; the wall is real). Budget identity OK all seeds (Σ=3.5000). VERBATIM faithful-IIT4 Φ (exact MIP-EI n=8): seed 1317 NONE=1.47354 CENTRAL=1.58572 MULTI-EDGE=1.72543 SHUFFLE=1.74144 (ΔΦ multi−none=+0.252) · seed 1318 NONE=1.70842 CENTRAL=2.17092 MULTI-EDGE=1.78835 SHUFFLE=1.56291 (ΔΦ=+0.080) · seed 1319 NONE=1.58947 CENTRAL=1.18572 MULTI-EDGE=1.25882 SHUFFLE=1.25427 (ΔΦ=−0.331). C1 ROBUST LIFT = FAIL (seed 1319 ΔΦ=−0.331 NEGATIVE, the orthogonal seed — same failure mode H_1283 hit on its orthogonal seed; seeds 1317/1318 PASS). C2 TOPOLOGY-EARNED = PASS (2/3 seeds multi>shuffle, mean 1.5909 > 1.5195 — the lift MULTI-EDGE *does* produce is small-world structure not edge count) but MOOT since C1 failed. C3 BEATS-CENTRAL = FAIL (MULTI-EDGE itself fails C1; CENTRAL also fails seed 1319 ΔΦ=−0.404 even harder). FINDING: integrated-information robustness is NOT a topology property at this toy scale — faithful-Φ stays FRAGILE regardless of topology; swapping a star for a distributed small-world mesh does NOT make the Φ lift robust, the fragility lives in the substrate/seed geometry not the coupling graph. BOUNDS the H_1283 wall further: not specific to the star; the topology/content axis stays 🧱 across both star and small-world. R8's orthogonal TIMING-axis phase-binding break (H_1283) remains the only robust faithful-Φ lift in the arc. NO CORE wiring follow-on (a_verified_must_wire applies to GREEN only — nothing to wire). SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY N=8 dim-8 64-tick leaky-linear substrate, faithful-Φ EXACT but numpy mirror DIRECTIONAL, engine-transfer to live CORE/pure_field UNVERIFIED. NOT ruled out: larger N (loses exactness >8), higher-degree small-world (K>2), weighted budgets, hierarchical/modular small-world; orthogonal TIMING axis already works (R8). frozen-first, NO tune-to-green, deterministic (byte-identical across two runs). .verdicts/1317_phi_multiedge/H_1317.txt"
  group  = "OMEGA"

@C h1316_ko_jamo_mitosis := "H_1316 — does a COMPOSITIONAL JAMO representation let the SAME gradient-free Korean mitosis (cells only SPLIT, p8; grow-op + cell budget held FIXED, verbatim H_1306/H_1307) break the H_1307 RUN A ~2.953 nat/byte raw-byte KO next-byte CE ceiling, where EVERY prior raw-byte lane (H_1307/H_1311/H_1315) could not? The genuinely-untried angle (a_no_llm_frame_trap, c15, a_break_the_wall c16): every prior KO lane fed the substrate RAW UTF-8 bytes — 3 opaque bytes per Hangul syllable, ZERO awareness that Korean is a COMPOSITIONAL syllable-block script. The missing structure = jamo composition: each syllable = 초성(L)+중성(V)+종성(T) jamo, recoverable by DETERMINISTIC Unicode NFD decomposition. Map the SAME real corpus to a jamo-symbol stream, grow the SAME mitosis on it, renormalize the per-symbol CE back to nats/UTF-8-byte for a fair axis vs the 2.9475 ceiling." :: hypothesis [slug=1316_ko_jamo_mitosis group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1316_ko_jamo_mitosis.py on summer RTX 5070 (sm_120, torch 2.11.0+cu130) via python3 nohup nice -n10, polled INLINE (a_cpu_local_no_waiter); R2 keys env-only c7 (passed into a remote launch script env, never echoed/logged/committed/inlined; launch script + scratch removed off summer after pull, corpus cache KEPT for siblings; all committed artifacts grep-clean of creds, only the public corpus sha256 matches a 40-hex pattern). REAL Korean only (p1-p8): SAME anima-7b R2 web window as H_1307 RUN A (r2://phanes/anima-7b/web/{kor,eng}/shard0000.bytes), boto3 range GET, KO 30MB / EN 10MB, window sha256 ASSERTED == H_1307 RUN A (KO c47b6808… EN 31b4a543… → both True; a mismatch → STOP, no synthetic Korean). p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-symbol CROSS-ENTROPY renormalized to nats/UTF-8-byte. HELD FIXED verbatim from H_1306/H_1307: GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, even/odd split, ko_stride=300, SEED_CENTERS [[0.3,0.5,0.0],[0.7,0.5,0.5]], the dimension-agnostic _grow_on (error-targeted Voronoi, SPLIT-only, p8), per-cell next-symbol count-MLE head, FEAT 3-D family [last_sym/Vj, second_sym/Vj, cont_depth/3]. VARIED = ONLY the symbol representation. SYMBOL STREAM: Hangul syllable (U+AC00..U+D7A3) → one symbol per NFD jamo (id 256+rank); every non-Hangul codepoint → one symbol per raw byte (id 0..255) → alphabet Vj=323 (67 distinct jamo). Each symbol carries n_bytes (raw=1; a syllable's jamo split [1,1,1]/[2,1] so they SUM to the syllable's 3 UTF-8 bytes — lossless). FAIR AXIS: CE_per_byte = Σ(−log p(sym)) / Σ n_bytes(sym), same held-out split/axis as the 2.9475 raw-byte ceiling. THREE ARMS: G0 raw-byte (vocab 256, same budget — reproduce the ceiling) · G1 jamo (intact) · G1c shuffle-jamo control (bijective permutation of the jamo→symbol-id map; vocab/dim/budget identical, compositional alignment destroyed; fixed per seed). 3 seeds [4316,4317,4318] (G1 deterministic; seeds vary the G1c control). frozen-first: .verdicts/1316_ko_jamo_mitosis/H_1316_FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): (B1 PRESENCE) mean G1 KO CE < 2.9475−0.05=2.8975 · (B2 EARNED) G1 beats G1c by ≥0.05 AND G1 beats G0 raw by ≥0.05 (lift = compositional structure, not vocab/dim) · (B3 NO-CHEAT) NFD→NFC roundtrip byte-identical over the whole KO window AND per-symbol n_bytes sum == corpus UTF-8 byte count exactly. GREEN iff B1∧B2∧B3; B1∧¬B2 → dims-not-structure; ¬B1 → CAPACITY-bound (the byte ceiling survives the compositional lens, valid c9). Regression: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts; no engine lane). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_fire_autonomous ($0 user hw not runpod), a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN — the Korean ceiling is REPRESENTATION-bound (broken by jamo composition), NOT capacity-bound. Corpus byte-IDENTICAL to H_1307 RUN A (sha gate PASS, KO=True EN=True). G0 raw-byte port reproduced 2.95342 (vs H_1307 RUN A 2.9475; port valid). mean over 3 seeds [4316,4317,4318], held-out KO next-symbol CE renormalized to nats/UTF-8-byte: G0 raw-byte = 2.95342 · G1 jamo-rep = 2.51335 (Δ −0.43415 vs the 2.9475 ceiling, Δ −0.44007 vs G0 raw → B1 TRUE, breaks 2.8975 by far) · G1c shuffle-jamo-map control = 2.74306 (Δ g1c−g1 = +0.22971 → G1 beats its own shuffle; AND G0−G1 = +0.44007 → G1 beats raw → B2 TRUE: the lift is the COMPOSITIONAL structure, not vocab/dim). B3 NO-CHEAT TRUE: NFD→NFC roundtrip 0 fails over 8,143,053 Hangul syllables AND per-symbol n_bytes Σ=29,999,999 == corpus bytes 29,999,999 exactly (lossless, the CE is honestly comparable). → B1∧B2∧B3 = 🟢 GREEN. FINDING (resolves the 🔴 TERMINAL Korean-mitosis thread from the representation side): the wall was the RAW-BYTE REPRESENTATION — 3 opaque bytes per Hangul syllable hid the syllable-block compositional structure — NOT the gradient-free mitosis mechanism's capacity. Give the SAME mechanism the jamo composition (deterministic NFD) and it clears 2.953 → 2.513. This is consistent with H_1311/H_1315 (capacity-bound OVER RAW BYTES / over a frozen learned rep): the limit those lanes hit was the L2-Voronoi partition geometry over the WRONG representation; the right (compositional) representation breaks it. HONEST SCOPE (c9 · a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): (1) G1 is identical across all 3 seeds (2.51335) because the intact jamo mitosis grow-op is DETERMINISTIC — the FREEZE pre-registers that seeds vary only the G1c control permutation; the 3-seed mean is over the control, G1 itself is a single deterministic existence-proof, not a 3-sample distribution. (2) One control seed (4317 = 2.50600) lands ≈ AT G1 (that jamo→symbol permutation preserved enough exploitable structure); the B2-vs-shuffle verdict rests on the MEAN (2.74306) clearing the bar, NOT per-seed unanimity — reported straight; the G1-beats-raw-G0 leg (+0.44007) holds unconditionally. (3) the ~0.44 nat/byte drop is largely the expected syllable→jamo coding gain (smaller per-symbol entropy); B2-vs-raw confirms it is NOT just extra vocab/dim (the shuffle keeps vocab/dim and loses ~0.23 of the lift), but the residual coding-vs-structure split at scale is UNVERIFIED. (4) DIRECTIONAL numpy/torch mirror; engine-transfer to the live CORE/*.hexa A⇄G + MITOSIS VAdaptField = follow-on (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire); toy 3-D byte substrate, stride-300 density, single window; NO Korean-fluency claim. live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. frozen-first, NO tune-to-green. .verdicts/1316_ko_jamo_mitosis/H_1316.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"

@C h1322_ko_featural := "H_1322 — does decomposing ONE LEVEL DEEPER than jamo — to the FEATURAL VECTOR that Hangul's DESIGN encodes — drop held-out KO next-symbol CE BELOW the H_1316 jamo floor 2.51335, because the SAME gradient-free mitosis can exploit the designed systematicity? H_1316 (🟢) showed the Korean ceiling is REPRESENTATION-bound (raw-byte 2.95342 → jamo 2.51335). But jamo is only the FIRST decomposition level. Hangul is — uniquely among major scripts — a DELIBERATELY DESIGNED featural writing system (Sejong 1443): each jamo's SHAPE encodes articulatory/phonological features (consonant = articulator base + added strokes for aspiration + doubling for tense; vowel = ·/ㅡ/ㅣ combos with yang/yin polarity + iotation). So ㄱ and ㅋ are ONE FEATURE apart, not two opaque symbols — NO organically-evolved script (Latin/Cyrillic/Han) has this. The angle (a_break_the_wall c16 depth probe below the jamo floor, a_no_llm_frame_trap c15 script-design lens): keep the LABEL alphabet + byte-accounting IDENTICAL to H_1316 (Vj=323), change ONLY the mitosis PARTITION geometry X from opaque-id (3-D) to the previous-2 symbols' DESIGN feature columns (5-col vec → 11-D), so two jamo one feature apart land NEAR each other and the predictor can exploit the design." :: hypothesis [slug=1322_ko_featural group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1322_ko_featural.py on summer RTX 5070 (sm_120, torch 2.11.0+cu130) via python3 nohup detached, polled INLINE (a_cpu_local_no_waiter); R2 keys env-only c7 (passed into a remote launch script env, never echoed/logged/committed/inlined; launch script + scratch removed off summer after pull, corpus cache KEPT for siblings; all committed artifacts grep-clean of creds, only the public corpus sha256 matches a 40-hex pattern). REAL Korean only (p1-p8): SAME anima-7b R2 web window as H_1307 RUN A / H_1316 (r2://phanes/anima-7b/web/kor/shard0000.bytes), boto3 range GET, KO 30MB, window sha256 ASSERTED == H_1307 RUN A (c47b6808… → True; a mismatch → STOP, no synthetic Korean). p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-symbol CROSS-ENTROPY renormalized to nats/UTF-8-byte (SAME axis as the jamo 2.51335 floor and raw 2.95342 ceiling). FEATURAL ENCODING (documented Hunminjeongeum design, encoded faithfully NOT invented): each NFD conjoining jamo → a 5-int design feature vector — consonant [artic in {velar/alveolar/bilabial/sibilant/glottal/zero}, manner in {plain/aspirated/tense}, nasal, liquid, -], vowel [vowel, vbase in {vertical/horizontal/combined}, polar in {neutral/yang/yin}, iota, round]; 67/67 distinct jamo mapped (full coverage). HELD FIXED verbatim from H_1306/H_1307/H_1316: GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, even/odd split, ko_stride=300, error-targeted Voronoi _grow_on (SPLIT-only p8), per-cell next-symbol count-MLE head. VARIED = ONLY the partition geometry X (LABEL alphabet Vj=323 IDENTICAL). ARMS: G0 raw-byte re-port · G1 jamo opaque-id re-port (the H_1316 floor) · G2 FEATURAL (intact design map) · G2c SHUFFLE-feature-map control (per-seed bijection reassigning each jamo's feature vector to a different jamo's — destroys ㄱ/ㅋ one-apart systematicity, same #vectors/dims) · F3 LINEARITY (closed-form ridge next-symbol predictor in feature space vs jamo-id space). 3 seeds [4322,4323,4324]. frozen-first: .verdicts/1322_ko_featural/H_1322_FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): (F1 DEEPER) featural CE < jamo 2.51335 by >=0.03 AND < raw 2.95342 · (F2 EARNED, decisive) featural beats SHUFFLE-feature-map by >=0.05 · (F3 LINEARITY, non-gating) feature-space linear-predictability better than jamo-id-space by >=0.02. GREEN iff F1 and F2; not-F1 → jamo is the decomposition FLOOR (honest 🧱); F1 and not-F2 → dims-not-design (honest negative). Regression: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts; no engine lane). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_fire_autonomous ($0 user hw not runpod), a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 HONEST-FLOOR (geometry-confounded; reported straight, NO bar moved, c9/p7). jamo is the decomposition FLOOR for this gradient-free L2-Voronoi mechanism. REAL corpus byte-IDENTICAL to H_1307 RUN A (sha c47b6808… gate PASS); 67/67 jamo design-feature coverage; NFD→NFC roundtrip 0-fail over 8,143,053 syllables; byte-accounting Σ=29,999,999 exact. CE ladder (nats/UTF-8-byte; intact featural deterministic, shuffle = mean 3 seeds): FEATURAL (intact) = 2.7309 → vs jamo-floor 2.51335 = +0.21755 (WORSE) → F1 FALSE (vs raw 2.95342 = −0.22252 better; the vs-raw leg passes but the vs-jamo leg fails the bar). SHUFFLE-feature ctrl = 2.77286 → Δ(shuffle−featural) = +0.04196, BELOW the 0.05 F2 bar → F2 FALSE (a WEAK design signal exists but is sub-threshold). Linearity: feature-space CE 4.83979 vs jamo-id-space 4.84214, Δ +0.00236 < 0.02 → F3 FALSE. GREEN = FALSE → 🧱. GEOMETRY CONFOUND (DIAGNOSTIC, NOT a frozen bar, full disclosure c9): the in-run G0 raw (3.26223) and G1 jamo (2.85983) re-ports do NOT match H_1316's 2.95342 / 2.51335 because this script's seed_centers_dim(3)=[[0.3,0.3,0.0],[0.7,0.7,0.5]] differs from H_1316's [[0.3,0.5,0.0],[0.7,0.5,0.5]] (middle coord 0.5). CONFIRMED by direct diagnostic: the jamo arm with H_1316's EXACT seed centers reproduces 2.51335 (cells 11) byte-exact → the gradient-free mitosis is SEED-CENTER-SENSITIVE, and the featural arm's 11-D seed centers are likewise an arbitrary unmatched start, so the locked-floor F1 comparison is geometry-confounded. SAME-GEOMETRY-FAMILY reading (intact featural 2.7309 vs in-run jamo re-port 2.85983, both under this script's seed-center family): featural BEATS the same-script jamo re-port by Δ −0.129 AND beats the shuffle-feature control by +0.042 → a weak design signal exists but does NOT clear the frozen decisive bar. Frozen-first (c9/p7): F1 was pre-registered against the locked 2.51335; intact featural 2.7309 does NOT beat it → F1 FALSE recorded as-is. FINDING: jamo is the decomposition FLOOR for this L2-Voronoi mechanism (bounds the depth, a_break_the_wall HONEST-🧱); the designed featural systematicity is REAL and produces a weak sub-threshold lift over its own shuffle (Δ +0.042) and same-geometry jamo (Δ −0.129), but the feature→partition→opaque-jamo-label path is too lossy a way to inject the design — an L2 distance over 5 hand-coded integer columns is a coarse proxy for the design geometry, and the mechanism's seed-center sensitivity confounds the locked-floor comparison. This is a METHOD floor (the mechanism), NOT a refutation that Hangul's design carries exploitable systematicity (the linguistics is intact; the depth advantage below jamo is NOT demonstrated by THIS mechanism). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY/DIRECTIONAL numpy/torch mirror; seed-center-sensitive mechanism (geometry-confounded, disclosed); engine-transfer to live CORE/*.hexa = follow-on; NO Korean-fluency claim. live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. NEXT r2: geometry-FAIR re-test (seed centers MATCHED/best-of-bank per arm, frozen-first) + label-factorization (predict the next jamo's FEATURE vector not its opaque id, so the design enters the prediction TARGET not just the partition). .verdicts/1322_ko_featural/H_1322.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"

@C h1326_ko_featural_r2 := "H_1326 — r2 of H_1322 (🧱 HONEST-FLOOR, geometry-confounded): once the test is GEOMETRY-FAIR and the design can enter the prediction TARGET, does Hangul's featural design give a measurable depth advantage BELOW the jamo floor 2.51335, or is jamo the genuine confound-free decomposition floor for this gradient-free L2-Voronoi mechanism family? Fixes the two DISCLOSED r1 confounds (c16/a_break_the_wall = wrong method NOT a wall): FIX A GEOMETRY-FAIR — ONE best-of-a-fixed-bank-by-TRAIN-CE seed-center protocol applied IDENTICALLY to every arm (the H_1316-FAMILY pattern is in every dim's bank; jamo arm MUST reproduce 2.51335 byte-exact = calibration anchor) so no arm gets a seed-center advantage; FIX B LABEL-FACTORIZATION — a second scoring head whose TARGET is the FACTORED feature vector (class∈{INITIAL,MEDIAL,FINAL,BYTE} + independent per-column design features over a pre-verified LOSSLESS jamo bijection), so the design enters the TARGET not just the partition. a_no_llm_frame_trap c15 script-design lens." :: hypothesis [slug=1326_ko_featural_r2 group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1326_ko_featural_r2.py on summer RTX 5070 (sm_120, torch 2.11.0+cu130) via python3 nohup detached, polled INLINE (a_cpu_local_no_waiter); corpus from cache (R2 keys NOT needed — cache /tmp/h1311_ko_raw.bytes first 29999999 B == H_1307 RUN A KO window, sha c47b6808… ASSERTED == gate PASS, a mismatch → STOP no synthetic Korean; launch script + scratch removed off summer after pull, cache KEPT for siblings; all committed artifacts grep-clean of creds, only the public corpus sha256 matches a 40-hex pattern, c7). REAL Korean only (p1-p8). p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-symbol CROSS-ENTROPY in nats/UTF-8-byte (SAME axis as jamo 2.51335 floor and raw 2.95342 ceiling). LOSSLESS FEATURAL BIJECTION (verified offline BEFORE freeze): initial 19, medial 21, final 27 jamo → all-distinct integer feature tuples → (feature tuple)↔(jamo id) invertible, so the factorized-target CE is honestly comparable. HELD FIXED verbatim from H_1306/H_1307/H_1316: GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, even/odd split, ko_stride=300, error-targeted Voronoi _grow_on (SPLIT-only p8), per-cell count-MLE head. VARIED = (A) the geometry-fair bank protocol + (B) the optional factorized scoring head. FIX-A BANK (FROZEN 5-pattern grid + the H_1316-family member lifted to each dim; winner = lowest TRAIN held-out CE, NO test peeking; same rule for every arm). ARMS: G0 raw-byte · A1 jamo opaque-id (CALIBRATION = 2.51335) · A2 featural-partition+opaque-target (Fix A only) · A3 featural-partition+FACTORIZED-target (Fix A+B) · A2s/A3s per-seed SHUFFLED-feature-map controls. 3 seeds [4326,4327,4328] (A1/A2/A3 deterministic; seeds vary the shuffle controls). frozen-first: .verdicts/1326_ko_featural_r2/H_1326_FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): GREEN iff G1∧G2 — (G1 GEOMETRY-FAIR DEPTH) BEST=min(A2,A3) beats jamo A1 by ≥0.03 (mean 3 seeds) AND beats raw 2.953 · (G2 EARNED) BEST beats its OWN shuffled-feature control by ≥0.05 · (G3 FACTORIZATION-ATTRIBUTION, diagnostic) does A3 beat A2 (design in TARGET vs PARTITION)? G1 fails geometry-fair → jamo is the genuine confound-free floor (terminal 🧱 clean closure). Regression: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts; no engine lane). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_fire_autonomous ($0 user hw not runpod), a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 HONEST-FLOOR (confound-free; reported straight, NO bar moved, c9/p7). With the geometry confound ELIMINATED, jamo is the genuine decomposition FLOOR for this gradient-free L2-Voronoi mechanism family. REAL corpus byte-IDENTICAL to H_1307 RUN A (sha c47b6808… gate PASS); 67/67 jamo coverage; NFD→NFC roundtrip 0-fail over 8,143,053 syllables; byte-accounting Σ=29,999,999 exact. CALIBRATION PASS: A1 jamo under the Fix-A protocol = 2.51335 BYTE-EXACT (bank member 5 = H_1316-family), confound eliminated. CE ladder (nats/UTF-8-byte, geometry-FAIR; A1/A2/A3 deterministic, shuffle = mean 3 seeds): raw-byte ceiling 2.95342 (in-run G0 2.94487) · A1 jamo 2.51335 · A2 featural-partition 2.73046 (member 0, 17 cells) · A3 label-factorization 3.07295 (member 0, 17 cells) · A2s shuffle-featural 2.78694 · A3s shuffle-factorized 4.28914. BEST = A2 = 2.73046, shuffle-of-best = 2.78694. G1 GEOMETRY-FAIR DEPTH = FALSE (BEST 2.73046 is +0.21711 ABOVE jamo 2.51335; the < raw leg passes but G1 needs both). G2 EARNED = TRUE (A2 beats its shuffle by +0.05648 ≥ 0.05 → the featural systematicity IS real and exploitable, but SUB-floor; per-seed A2s {2.851,2.783,2.727} — seed 4328 ties A2 so G2 leans on the mean, same caveat as H_1316). G3 FACTORIZATION = FALSE (A3 does NOT beat A2, Δ −0.3425; putting the design into the TARGET via INDEPENDENT-feature factorization HURTS — the per-column independence assumption discards the onset/nucleus/coda joint the opaque jamo head keeps intact; the cardinality-reduction benefit is exceeded by the independence penalty). green = FALSE → 🧱. FINDING: with the geometry confound eliminated (jamo reproduces 2.51335 byte-exact under a bank protocol applied identically to every arm), jamo is the genuine decomposition floor — the design's systematicity is real & exploitable (shuffling it costs +0.056 in the partition, +1.22 in the factorized target) but does NOT push CE below jamo in EITHER the partition (A2 +0.217 above) OR the target (A3 +0.557 above; factorization backfires). The r1 sub-bar same-geometry signal (+0.042) was the real ceiling of what feature-geometry buys this mechanism, not a hidden win awaiting a fair test. The r1 🧱 STANDS, now confound-free — a clean honest closure. A genuinely-new angle needs a DIFFERENT mechanism (not L2-Voronoi count-MLE) that exploits feature systematicity WITHOUT discarding the feature joint — a mechanism-family change, not a representation tweak. HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY/DIRECTIONAL numpy/torch mirror; A1/A2/A3 deterministic single points (decisive — anchor byte-exact, A2/A3 both far above); engine-transfer to live CORE/*.hexa = follow-on (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire); NO Korean-fluency claim; live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. .verdicts/1326_ko_featural_r2/H_1326.txt"
