@C h1329_ko_feat_corr := "H_1329 — H_1326's explicitly-named next angle (c16/a_break_the_wall mechanism-FAMILY change, NOT a representation tweak): does a CORRELATION-MODELING / JOINT-PRESERVING featural mechanism break BELOW the jamo 2.51335 floor — where H_1326's A3 independent-factorization BACKFIRED (3.073) and A2 partition-only was sub-floor (2.730)? H_1326's diagnosis: A3 backfires because INDEPENDENT-feature prediction (P(class)·∏ P(f_c|class)) DISCARDS the onset/nucleus/coda + within-jamo feature JOINT the opaque jamo head keeps. THE NEW MECHANISM A4 = a per-cell CONDITIONAL-CHAIN featural head P(jamo)=P(class)·P(f_0|class)·P(f_1|class,f_0)·P(f_2|class,f_0,f_1)… which (a) KEEPS the within-class joint EXACTLY by the chain rule ∏_c P(f_c|class,f_<c)=P(f_0..f_{C-1}|class)=P(jamo|class), and (b) SHARES strength across feature-similar jamo (jamo sharing a feature PREFIX share the conditioning context — ㄱ/ㅋ one feature apart share the articulator-conditioned manner head). The mechanism keeps the joint AND models feature correlations, unlike A3 which threw the joint away. a_no_llm_frame_trap c15 script-design lens." :: hypothesis [slug=1329_ko_feat_corr group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1329_ko_feat_corr.py on summer RTX 5070 (sm_120, torch 2.11.0+cu130) via python3 nohup detached, polled INLINE (a_cpu_local_no_waiter); corpus from cache (R2 keys NOT needed — cache /tmp/h1311_ko_raw.bytes first 29999999 B == H_1307 RUN A KO window, sha c47b6808… ASSERTED == gate PASS, mismatch → STOP no synthetic Korean; launch script + scratch removed off summer after pull, cache KEPT for siblings; all committed artifacts grep-clean of creds, only the public corpus sha256 matches a 40-hex pattern, c7). REAL Korean only (p1-p8). p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-symbol CROSS-ENTROPY in nats/UTF-8-byte (SAME axis as jamo 2.51335 floor and raw 2.95342 ceiling). EVERYTHING verbatim from H_1326 so A1/A2/A3 reproduce byte-exact: GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, even/odd split, ko_stride=300, error-targeted Voronoi _grow_on (SPLIT-only p8), the Fix-A geometry-fair bank protocol (best-of-fixed-bank-by-TRAIN-CE seed centers, identical to every arm; A1 jamo MUST reproduce 2.51335 byte-exact = calibration anchor), the LOSSLESS within-class feature↔jamo bijections. THE ONLY NEW THING = the A4 conditional-chain scoring head (a count-MLE STRUCTURED head: per-(cell,class,feature-prefix) Laplace-smoothed count table over the next feature column, unseen→Laplace-uniform back-off → proper distribution; BYTE class scored identically to A3 so A3-vs-A4 isolates product-vs-chain = the joint). A4 = count-MLE structured head — NOT the gradient-free p8 mitosis (which it RIDES, partition unchanged), NOT gradient-trained either — labeled clearly. ARMS: G0 raw-byte · A1 jamo opaque (CALIB=2.51335) · A2 featural-partition+opaque (reproduced for C3) · A3 featural+INDEPENDENT-factorized (reproduced for C3) · A4 featural+CONDITIONAL-CHAIN (the new mechanism) · A4s per-seed SHUFFLED-feature-map control with the A4 chain head. 3 seeds [4329,4330,4331] (A1/A2/A3/A4 deterministic; seeds vary the shuffle control). frozen-first: .verdicts/1329_ko_feat_corr/H_1329_FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): GREEN iff C1∧C2∧C3 — (C1 BELOW-JAMO) A4 < jamo 2.51335 by ≥0.03 (mean 3 seeds) AND < raw 2.953 · (C2 EARNED) A4 < A4-shuffle by ≥0.05 · (C3 ATTRIBUTION) A4 < A3 AND A4 < A2 (isolates that the gain is the modeled JOINT/correlations, not features per se). C1 fail → jamo is the genuine cross-mechanism floor (deeper 🧱). C1∧¬C3 → features-not-joint (🟠). Regression: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts; no engine lane). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_fire_autonomous ($0 user hw not runpod), a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 HONEST-FLOOR (cross-mechanism; reported straight, NO bar moved, c9/p7). A correlation-modeling / joint-preserving (conditional-chain) mechanism does NOT break the jamo floor → jamo is the genuine decomposition FLOOR ACROSS mechanism families incl. correlation-modeling (a deeper, stronger 🧱 than H_1326). REAL corpus byte-IDENTICAL to H_1307 RUN A (sha c47b6808… gate PASS); 67/67 jamo coverage; NFD→NFC roundtrip 0-fail over 8,143,053 syllables; byte-accounting Σ=29,999,999 exact. CALIBRATION PASS: A1 jamo = 2.51335 BYTE-EXACT (bank member 5 = H_1316-family); A2 2.73046 + A3 3.07295 reproduce H_1326 byte-exact. CE ladder (nats/UTF-8-byte, geometry-FAIR; A1/A2/A3/A4 deterministic, A4-shuffle = mean 3 seeds): raw-byte ceiling 2.95342 (in-run G0 2.94487) · A1 jamo 2.51335 · A2 featural-partition 2.73046 · A3 independent-factorization 3.07295 · A4 conditional-chain (JOINT) 2.75109 (member 0, 17 cells) · A4 shuffle 2.91966 (per-seed {2.86325,3.05597,2.83976}). C1 BELOW-JAMO = FALSE (A4 2.75109 is +0.23774 ABOVE jamo 2.51335; the < raw leg passes but C1 needs both). C2 EARNED = TRUE (A4 beats its shuffle by +0.16857 ≥ 0.05, per-seed UNANIMOUS — 3× A2's +0.056 signal; the chain mechanism DOES exploit Hangul's designed systematicity, but SUB-floor). C3 ATTRIBUTION = FALSE (A4 BEATS A3 by +0.32186 — the chain RECOVERED the joint A3's independence discarded, confirming H_1326's diagnosis byte-exact — but does NOT beat A2: A4 is +0.02063 ABOVE the partition-only A2; C3 needs both). green = FALSE → 🧱. FINDING: a correlation/joint-preserving mechanism does NOT break the jamo floor. The structural reason (decisive): any mechanism that exactly models the within-jamo feature JOINT asymptotes to P(jamo|cell) — exactly what the opaque jamo head already computes — so the featural decomposition buys NO below-jamo depth once the joint is kept; A4 ties the partition-only A2 (both re-express the same joint) and stays +0.238 above jamo. Three independent mechanisms (partition A2 / independent-factorization A3 / correlation-chain A4) now all land above jamo under the geometry-fair protocol → jamo is the cross-mechanism floor. The design's exploitable systematicity (C2 +0.169, the strongest design signal in the arc) lives in count-SHARING across similar jamo, NOT in a sub-jamo prediction gain. HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY/DIRECTIONAL numpy/torch mirror; A4 = count-MLE structured head (NOT gradient-free p8 mitosis, NOT gradient-trained — labeled); A1-A4 deterministic single points (decisive — anchor byte-exact, A4 +0.238 above jamo & +0.021 above A2; C2 per-seed unanimous); engine-transfer to live CORE/*.hexa = follow-on (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire); NO Korean-fluency claim; live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. A new below-jamo angle would need info the opaque jamo head LACKS (cross-syllable phonotactic context, or a learned metric over jamo), NOT a re-factorization of the same featural target. .verdicts/1329_ko_feat_corr/H_1329.txt"
