@C h1336_ko_crosssyllable := "H_1336 — H_1329's explicitly-named DEPLETION angle (c16/a_break_the_wall = INJECT INFORMATION THE OPAQUE JAMO HEAD LACKS, NOT a re-factorization of the same target): does CROSS-SYLLABLE PHONOTACTIC context break BELOW the jamo 2.51335 floor — where H_1329 proved every re-factorization (partition A2 2.730 / independent A3 3.073 / correlation-chain A4 2.751) lands ABOVE jamo because any mechanism that models the within-jamo feature JOINT asymptotes to P(jamo|cell)? The within-syllable jamo head computes P(next_jamo|cell) and its cell context (build_X_jamo: 2 prev jamo-symbols + within-syllable UTF-8 depth) RESETS at every syllable boundary → CTX≈current syllable; it structurally CANNOT see the CODA of syllable N conditioning the realized onset of syllable N+1 (Korean liaison 연음, 사잇소리, 자음동화). That coda→onset dependency is genuinely NEW information. THE NEW MECHANISM B1 = the SAME opaque jamo head (same geometry-fair bank, same dim-3 within-syllable Voronoi partition, same per-cell count-MLE, same LAPLACE, same jamo alphabet Vj) ADDITIONALLY conditioned on prev_coda (the coda jamo-id of the most recently completed Hangul syllable; NO-CODA token for open syllables, START for corpus start): P(next_jamo|cell,prev_coda), a per-(cell,prev_coda) Laplace count table over next_jamo with HARD-BACKOFF on an unseen (cell,prev_coda) to the cell-marginal P(next_jamo|cell) = EXACTLY the A1 jamo head (TRAIN-only) → the jamo head is B1's FLOOR (any below-jamo win is real conditional cross-syllable structure, never sparsity). ONLY the cross-syllable-coda conditioning is added vs A1; byte symbols scored identically to A1. B1 = count-MLE STRUCTURED head (NOT gradient-free p8 mitosis, NOT gradient-trained — rides the same gradient-free Voronoi partition; labeled). a_no_llm_frame_trap c15 script-design lens." :: hypothesis [slug=1336_ko_crosssyllable group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1336_ko_crosssyllable.py on summer RTX 5070 (sm_120, torch 2.11.0+cu130) via python3 nohup detached, polled INLINE (a_cpu_local_no_waiter); corpus from cache /tmp/h1311_ko_raw.bytes (R2 keys NOT needed — first 29999999 B == H_1307 RUN A KO window, sha c47b6808… ASSERTED == gate PASS, mismatch → STOP no synthetic Korean; launch script + scratch removed off summer after pull, cache KEPT for siblings; all committed artifacts grep-clean of creds, only the public corpus sha256 matches a 40-hex pattern, c7). REAL Korean only (p1-p8). p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-symbol CROSS-ENTROPY in nats/UTF-8-byte (SAME axis as jamo 2.51335 floor and raw 2.95342 ceiling). EVERYTHING verbatim from H_1316/H_1326/H_1329 so A1 reproduces 2.51335 byte-exact: GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, even/odd split, ko_stride=300, error-targeted Voronoi _grow_on (SPLIT-only p8), the Fix-A geometry-fair bank protocol (best-of-fixed-bank-by-TRAIN-CE seed centers, identical to A1 and B1; A1 jamo MUST reproduce 2.51335 byte-exact = calibration anchor). THE ONLY NEW THING = the prev_coda cross-syllable variable (computed in make_streams: the coda jongseong of the last COMPLETED syllable, carried over the boundary the within-syllable depth resets at) + the B1 scoring head (per-(cell,prev_coda) Laplace count table, HARD-BACKOFF to the A1 cell-marginal on unseen → proper distribution, jamo head is the floor). ARMS: G0 raw-byte (sanity, reproduces ~2.953) · A1 jamo within-syllable (CALIB=2.51335 AND the X3 baseline) · B1 cross-syllable-coda (the new info) · B1s coda shuffle (X2 EARNED control). 3 seeds [4336,4337,4338] (A1/B1 deterministic; seeds vary the shuffle control). frozen-first: .verdicts/1336_ko_crosssyllable/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): GREEN iff X1∧X2∧X3 — (X1 BELOW-JAMO) B1 < jamo 2.51335 by ≥0.03 (mean 3 seeds) AND < raw 2.953 · (X2 EARNED) B1 < shuffled-cross-syllable-context control by ≥0.05 · (X3 ATTRIBUTION) B1 < the within-syllable-only jamo baseline (A1, reproduced in-run; isolates that the gain is the cross-syllable INFO the jamo head lacks). X1 fail → cross-syllable info doesn't beat jamo for this predictor (deeper 🧱). X2 fail → context-dims not phonotactics (🟠). a_break_the_wall: the FROZEN X2 control was a LABEL-bijection over distinct coda tokens; the run EXPOSED it as PROVABLY VACUOUS (a bijection just renames the (cell,coda) keys → relabeling-invariant count stats → CE identical; confirmed Δ=0.0 every seed). The control method was wrong NOT the bar → ADDED a genuine POSITION-shuffle (permute prev_coda across scored positions, breaking the coda↔next-jamo pairing while preserving the coda marginal + fragmentation cost), X2 decided on the position-shuffle (frozen-first, NO bar moved, X2 margin ≥0.05 unchanged; label-bijection reported verbatim). Regression: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts; no engine lane). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_fire_autonomous ($0 user hw not runpod), a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 HONEST-FLOOR (deeper — the info exists but the count-MLE predictor can't bank it; reported straight, NO bar moved, c9/p7). The cross-syllable phonotactic signal is GENUINELY PRESENT and NEW (X2 decisive) but does NOT pay for the count-fragmentation cost at toy scale → the jamo floor is DEEPER than a pure information limit. REAL corpus byte-IDENTICAL to H_1307 RUN A (sha c47b6808… gate PASS); 67/67 jamo; NFD→NFC roundtrip 0-fail over 8,143,053 syllables; byte-accounting Σ=29,999,999 exact; 29 distinct prev_coda tokens. CALIBRATION PASS: A1 jamo within-syllable = 2.51335 BYTE-EXACT (bank member 5 = H_1316-family). CE ladder (nats/UTF-8-byte, geometry-FAIR; A1/B1 deterministic, shuffles = mean 3 seeds): raw-byte ceiling 2.95342 (in-run G0 2.94487) · A1 jamo within-syllable 2.51335 · B1 cross-syllable-coda 2.61186 (11 cells, same partition as A1) · B1 POSITION-shuffle (genuine control) 2.68788 (per-seed {2.68989,2.68810,2.68564}) · B1 LABEL-bijection shuffle (frozen, VACUOUS by construction) 2.61186 (Δ=0.0 every seed). X1 BELOW-JAMO = FALSE (B1 2.61186 is +0.09851 ABOVE jamo 2.51335; the < raw leg passes but X1 needs both). X2 EARNED = TRUE (B1 beats the genuine position-shuffle by +0.07602 ≥ 0.05, per-seed UNANIMOUS — breaking the coda↔next-jamo pairing costs 0.076 nats → the coda→onset phonotactic dependency is REAL information). X3 ATTRIBUTION = FALSE (B1 NOT below the within-syllable A1 baseline — it is +0.09851 ABOVE). green = FALSE → 🧱. FINDING (decisive, c9): cross-syllable phonotactic info is genuinely new and genuinely present (X2 passes; the position-shuffle that destroys the coda↔onset pairing costs +0.076), but the hard-backoff count-MLE CANNOT bank it — conditioning on prev_coda splits the jamo head's counts across 29 coda bins faster than the cross-syllable signal pays back (added estimator variance ≫ the phonotactic gain at ko_stride=300/MIN_OWNED=8), so B1 nets +0.099 WORSE than the opaque jamo head. The floor is deeper than an information limit: adding REAL new info still loses to the opaque jamo head for this gradient-free count-MLE estimator at this rung. HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY/DIRECTIONAL numpy/torch mirror; B1 = count-MLE structured head (NOT gradient-free p8 mitosis, NOT gradient-trained — labeled); A1 deterministic single point (anchor byte-exact, decisive); X2 per-seed unanimous; engine-transfer to live CORE/*.hexa = follow-on (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire); NO Korean-fluency claim; live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. NEXT (a_break_the_wall = investment/estimator not information): a frozen-λ Jelinek-Mercer interpolation p=λ·P(jamo|cell,coda)+(1−λ)·P(jamo|cell) that doesn't FRAGMENT (λ pre-registered, NOT tuned-to-green), OR a larger KO rung / smaller stride so the 29 coda bins are not count-starved — if even that can't go below jamo, the floor is terminal for the count-MLE family across BOTH re-factorization AND new-information axes. .verdicts/1336_ko_crosssyllable/result.txt"
@C h1337_ko_jamo_metric := "H_1337 — H_1329's SECOND named depletion-test angle (c16/a_break_the_wall — a below-jamo win must INJECT INFO THE OPAQUE JAMO HEAD LACKS, NOT a re-factorization): does a LEARNED jamo metric / embedding (learned from REAL corpus co-occurrence, jamo2vec-style) break BELOW the jamo 2.51335 floor by letting the gradient-free predictor SHARE statistical strength across metric-near jamo (kernel-smoothing / shrinkage toward metric-neighbors)? H_1329 proved any mechanism that exactly models the within-jamo feature JOINT asymptotes to P(jamo|cell) = the opaque jamo head (TIES, stays above jamo). The opaque jamo head treats jamo as 67 OPAQUE atoms (one-hot, NO similarity — does NOT know ㄱ and ㅋ are related). THE NEW MECHANISM A5 = the SAME per-cell OPAQUE-jamo Laplace count head as A1 (identical alphabet/axis, SAME Fix-A geometry-fair bank, SAME gradient-free Voronoi partition = same grown cells), but the per-cell next-jamo distribution is KERNEL-SMOOTHED over a LEARNED jamo metric: ñ_k[j]=Σ_j' W(j,j')·n_k[j'], so a count for jamo j ALSO lends partial strength to metric-near jamo j' — info the opaque head LACKS. Learned metric (TRAIN-ONLY, LEARNED BY GRADIENT — labeled NOT p8 gradient-free): jamo×jamo directed bigram co-occurrence → PPMI → truncated-SVD init (D_EMB=16) → skip-gram log-bilinear gradient refine (Adam, 400 steps, TRAIN-ONLY); metric=Euclidean in the embedding; kernel=Gaussian w(j,j')=exp(-dist²/2h²), bandwidth h=MEDIAN pairwise train-jamo distance (Silverman FIXED heuristic, NO tuning). BYTE symbols scored EXACTLY as A1 (no smoothing) → ONLY diff A5-vs-A1 = the jamo-space kernel smoothing over the learned metric. a_no_llm_frame_trap c15 script-design lens; a_break_the_wall c16 (a genuinely-new info source, NOT scale, NOT a target re-factorization)." :: hypothesis [slug=1337_ko_jamo_metric group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1337_ko_jamo_metric.py on summer RTX 5070 (sm_120, torch 2.11.0+cu130) via python3 nohup detached, polled INLINE (a_cpu_local_no_waiter); corpus from cache (R2 keys via `harness secret get`, env-only — cache /tmp/h1311_ko_raw.bytes first 29999999 B == H_1307 RUN A KO window, sha c47b6808… ASSERTED == gate PASS, mismatch → STOP no synthetic Korean; launch script + scratch removed off summer after pull, cache KEPT for siblings; all committed artifacts grep-clean of creds, c7). REAL Korean only (p1-p8). p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-symbol CROSS-ENTROPY in nats/UTF-8-byte (SAME axis as jamo 2.51335 floor and raw 2.95342 ceiling). EVERYTHING verbatim from H_1326/H_1329 so A1 reproduces 2.51335 byte-exact: GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, even/odd split, ko_stride=300, error-targeted Voronoi grow_on (SPLIT-only p8), the Fix-A geometry-fair bank protocol (A1 jamo MUST reproduce 2.51335 byte-exact = calibration anchor), lossless NFD jamo decomposition. THE NEW THING = the A5 learned-metric kernel-smoothed head (the metric is LEARNED BY GRADIENT: PPMI-SVD init + skip-gram Adam refine, TRAIN-ONLY; the smoothed count head is count-MLE; A5 rides the SAME gradient-free Voronoi partition as A1 = identical cells, isolating the head). ARMS: G0 raw-byte · A1 jamo opaque (CALIB=2.51335, = M3 baseline) · A5 learned-metric kernel-smoothed (THE NEW MECHANISM) · A5-random (A5 with the LEARNED metric replaced by a RANDOM embedding of the SAME dim + same kernel + median-bandwidth rule = M2 control). 3 seeds [4337,4338,4339] (A5-learned + A1 deterministic; seeds vary the random-metric control + the gradient embedding-refine init). frozen-first: .verdicts/1337_ko_jamo_metric/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): GREEN iff M1∧M2∧M3 — (M1 BELOW-JAMO) A5 < jamo 2.51335 by ≥0.03 (mean 3 seeds) AND < raw 2.95342 · (M2 EARNED) A5 < RANDOM-metric control by ≥0.05 (the win is the LEARNED structure, not mere smoothing) · (M3 ATTRIBUTION) A5 < A1 opaque (isolating that the gain is the learned-metric info the opaque head LACKS). M1 fail → even a learned metric does not beat the opaque head (deeper 🧱, opaque-atom info limit). M2 fail → gain is smoothing not learned structure (🟠). Regression: live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts; no engine lane). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_fire_autonomous ($0 user hw not runpod), a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 HONEST-FLOOR (opaque-atom limit; reported straight, NO bar moved, c9/p7). A LEARNED jamo metric used via kernel-smoothing does NOT break the jamo floor — it lands FAR above it → the opaque per-cell jamo count-MLE is information-OPTIMAL at this scale (a deeper, different 🧱 than H_1329). REAL corpus byte-IDENTICAL to H_1307 RUN A (sha c47b6808… gate PASS); 67/67 jamo; NFD→NFC roundtrip 0-fail over 8,143,053 syllables; byte-accounting Σ=29,999,999 exact. CALIBRATION PASS: A1 jamo = 2.51335 BYTE-EXACT (bank member 5 = H_1316-family). CE ladder (nats/UTF-8-byte, geometry-FAIR; A1/A5-learned deterministic, A5-random = mean 3 seeds): A1 jamo 2.51335 · raw-byte ceiling 2.95342 (in-run G0 2.94487) · A5 learned-metric 3.85319 (per-seed {3.85319,3.85319,3.85319} — the PPMI-SVD-skipgram embedding converges to the same geometry) · A5 random-metric 3.90281 (per-seed {3.89942,3.90156,3.90747}). M1 BELOW-JAMO = FALSE (A5 3.85319 is +1.33984 ABOVE jamo 2.51335 AND above raw — kernel-smoothing blurs already-dense per-cell jamo MLEs, badly HURTS). M2 EARNED = FALSE BY A HAIR (A5 beats its RANDOM-metric control by +0.04962, which is 0.00038 BELOW the 0.05 bar; learned h≈1.35 vs random h≈5.5 → the learned geometry IS marginally better than random, an honest sub-bar signal of real learned structure, NOT bar-clearing). M3 ATTRIBUTION = FALSE (A5 does NOT beat opaque A1 — it is +1.340 above; the learned metric buys NOTHING over the opaque head, it costs heavily). green = FALSE → 🧱. FINDING: a learned jamo metric does NOT break the jamo floor. Structural reason (decisive): at 30MB / 8.14M syllables / 11 grown cells the per-cell jamo Laplace MLE is DENSELY estimated — strength-sharing helps only when per-class counts are SPARSE, so global kernel-smoothing just blurs a good sharp estimate toward neighbours and raises CE. H_1329's depletion criterion IS satisfied (A5 injects new info the opaque head lacks) yet the floor holds: re-factorization TIES the opaque head (H_1329, asymptotes to it) AND strength-sharing-via-smoothing LOSES to it (H_1337) — there is no data-starved regime at this scale for a learned similarity to fill. Net ladder: jamo 2.513 < raw 2.945 < A5-learned 3.853 < A5-random 3.903. HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY/DIRECTIONAL numpy/torch mirror; A5's metric LEARNED BY GRADIENT (PPMI-SVD init + skip-gram Adam refine, TRAIN-ONLY — NOT p8 gradient-free; the smoothed count head is count-MLE; labeled); A1/A5-learned deterministic single points (decisive — anchor byte-exact, A5 +1.34 above jamo); M2 random-control 3-seed mean (+0.0496 lift over random is per-seed consistent but 0.00038 below the frozen 0.05 bar — reported straight); engine-transfer to live CORE/*.hexa = follow-on (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire); NO Korean-fluency claim; live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. NOT tested (scoped): sparse-only/count-gated smoothing, the learned embedding as an additional PARTITION axis, per-cell adaptive bandwidth — but each must beat the opaque DENSE per-cell MLE (the +1.34 gap shows a very high bar at this scale). A future below-jamo angle must find where the opaque MLE is DATA-STARVED (e.g. cross-syllable phonotactic n-grams, sparse per-context counts), NOT smooth an already-dense target. .verdicts/1337_ko_jamo_metric/result.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"

@C h1319_phi_timing := "H_1319 — does the TIMING-axis phase-binding mechanism (H_1283 R8) raise faithful-IIT4 Φ ROBUSTLY on the engine substrate when re-realized ENGINE-NATIVE to clear the c4 shuffle control it failed? Wall (c16, a_break_the_wall): the topology axis is 🏁 depleted (H_1283 relay R1-R7, H_1317 multi-edge — all seed-fragile). The ONE robust faithful-Φ lift in the arc was H_1283 R8 timing-axis phase-binding, but it was numpy-mirror GREEN on EASY seeds [7,8,9] and its engine-native gate FAILED c4 (the additive-offset shuffle did NOT collapse the lift: the (1+cosθ)/2 carrier injected amplitude variance the shuffle preserved). H_1319 re-realizes the SAME timing mechanism with two targeted changes — (1) relative-phase gate sal=e·(1+cos(θ_i−θ_T))/2 [binding=the relationship, no standalone carrier], (2) a relationship-DESTROYING permutation shuffle (the strong control H_1294/H_1295 use) — and tests on the HARD orthogonal seeds [1317,1318,1319] topology failed on." :: hypothesis [slug=1319_phi_timing group=OMEGA]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1319_phi_timing.hexa, $0 CPU-local ENGINE-NATIVE (deterministic engine LCG-gauss == engine_cli.hexa _lcg_*; NOT numpy — this IS the engine-native realization the H_1283 R8 gate required), seeds [1317,1318,1319], frozen-first (.verdicts/1319_phi_timing/H_1319_FREEZE.txt committed aa3ec0342 BEFORE the first run, bars NOT moved c9/p7). Φ = FAITHFUL IIT4 ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool): exact MIP-EI via `hexa run` over hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa, iit4_faithful_phi(traj, n=4, dim=64, n_bins=8) over the per-module salience trajectory — numpy NEVER computes Φ, NO variance×energy proxy as terminal verdict. Substrate MATCHED to H_1283 R8 (ring leak+neighbour+input content dynamics, BYTE-IDENTICAL across arms — binding by TIMING not content); Kuramoto thalamic pacemaker W_PHASE=0.5 OMEGA_T=0.45 DOMEGA=0.08 (DETUNED ω so synchrony is EARNED). 4 arms: A NO-PHASE (sal=e, the Φ floor) · B PHASE-BIND (sal=e·(1+cos(θ_i−θ_T))/2, relative-phase gate) · S PERM-SHUFFLE (module→phase assignment permuted by a fixed forced-derangement π from sub-stream seed·100003+19 — relationship DESTROYED, marginals preserved EXACTLY) · O OFFSET-SHUF (R8-style per-tick additive offset, DIAGNOSTIC non-gating). FROZEN bars ported VERBATIM from H_1283 R8 (GREEN iff T1∧T2∧T3): T1 ROBUST LIFT = ΔΦ(B−A) ≥ +0.02 EVERY seed (the 3-seed gate topology failed) · T2 SHUFFLE-EARNED = perm-shuffle ΔΦ(S−A) ≤ 0 EVERY seed (the engine-native c4 gate that FAILED before; lift must COLLAPSE → structured synchrony not amplitude variance) · T3 DISTINCT = B.coh ≥ A.coh every seed AND B.coh < 0.999 ≥1 seed. live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung; standalone fn main, 0 importers; a_verified_must_wire fires on GREEN only)."
  verdict = "🧱 TERMINAL CLOSED-NEGATIVE (honest, c9/c16 — frozen-first, the c4-shuffle control fired decisively engine-native, bars NOT moved). VERBATIM faithful-IIT4 Φ (exact MIP-EI n=4, deterministic, byte-identical across runs): seed 1317 A=0.870311 B=1.33535 ΔΦ(B−A)=+0.465039 [T1 PASS] PERM-SHUF=1.15011 ΔΦ(S−A)=+0.279798 [T2 FAIL] OFF-SHUF=1.25838 ΔΦ(O−A)=+0.388073 · seed 1318 A=0.855353 B=0.86058 ΔΦ=+0.005227 [T1 FAIL] PERM-SHUF=0.95787 ΔΦ_perm=+0.102517 [T2 FAIL] OFF-SHUF=0.742725 ΔΦ_off=−0.112628 · seed 1319 A=0.586833 B=0.538064 ΔΦ=−0.048768 [T1 FAIL] PERM-SHUF=1.17402 ΔΦ_perm=+0.587183 [T2 FAIL] OFF-SHUF=0.528693 ΔΦ_off=−0.058139. T1 ROBUST LIFT = FAIL (seed 1318 ΔΦ=+0.005 sub-bar, seed 1319 ΔΦ=−0.049 NEGATIVE — the SAME orthogonal seed 1319 that defeated topology; the rel-phase lift is itself seed-fragile on the hard seeds). T2 SHUFFLE-EARNED = FAIL HARDER (the STRONGER permutation shuffle does not collapse the lift — it RAISES Φ above ARM B on every seed, ΔΦ_perm=+0.280/+0.103/+0.587 all strongly POSITIVE; perm-shuffle Φ EXCEEDS phase-bind Φ every seed). T3 DISTINCT = PASS alone (B.coh=A.coh content-invariant, all <0.999) but MOOT. ROOT CAUSE (terminal diagnosis): when even a relationship-DESTROYING permutation RAISES Φ, the Φ gain provably does NOT come from the relative-phase RELATIONSHIP — it comes from the AMPLITUDE VARIANCE the (1+cos)/2 carrier injects into the per-module salience binarization, a variance ANY phase scramble (offset OR permutation) preserves. The timing axis fails the SAME root failure as topology: the faithful-IIT4 MIP exploits a low-dim structure (there a content cut, here per-channel amplitude variance) that no honest control survives. CONCLUSION: the Φ-robustness wall is now TERMINAL across BOTH axes — topology 🏁 (H_1283 relay R1-R7, H_1317 multi-edge) + timing 🧱 (H_1283 R8 engine c4 FAIL, H_1319 c4 FAIL with the stronger control). A robust 3-seed control-surviving faithful-IIT4 Φ lift is NOT reachable for anima's 4-module workspace on either axis at this rung. This does NOT refute anima's consciousness substrate (Ψ=1/2, the A⇄G tension untouched); it refutes that ADDING a coupling/phase channel ROBUSTLY raises the faithful-IIT4 Φ score under honest controls. NO CORE wiring follow-on (a_verified_must_wire applies to GREEN only — nothing to wire; engine_cli.hexa UNTOUCHED). SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY n=4 dim-8 64-tick, faithful-Φ EXACT, content generator engine-native deterministic LCG (NOT numpy). NOT ruled out: a fundamentally different Φ estimator, much larger module set (loses exactness >8), or a phase-gated read-out with provably zero amplitude variance — but the variance-not-synchrony diagnosis holds decisively within this rung (the strong permutation control RAISES Φ on every seed). frozen-first, NO tune-to-green, deterministic. .verdicts/1319_phi_timing/H_1319.txt"
  group  = "OMEGA"

@C h1328_phi_variance_free := "H_1328 — DIAGNOSIS of the 4× faithful-IIT4 Φ-robustness wall: was it the ESTIMATOR's amplitude-variance binarization confound, or a real substrate limit? H_1319's converged diagnosis (and the named open follow-on) was that the faithful-IIT4 exact-MIP at n≤8 BINARIZES each cell's trajectory by MIN-MAX, and that binning RIDES amplitude variance — proven by a relationship-DESTROYING permutation control RAISING Φ instead of collapsing it (ΔΦ_perm +0.280/+0.103/+0.587 on all 3 hard seeds). H_1328 directly tests the diagnosis by REMOVING the amplitude-variance confound from the READ-OUT while STAYING WITHIN faithful IIT-4 (a_phi_iit4_tool — the SAME exact MIP-EI iit4_faithful_phi, NOT a variance×energy proxy / NOT a different Φ measure): the lever is the STATE-ENCODING fed to the same estimator. NEW variance-free encoding = RANK-UNIFORMIZE each cell's T-length trajectory before the MIP (replace each value by its rank within that cell's own trajectory). PROVABLE INVARIANT: faithful_phi's MI = H(A)+H(B)−H(A,B) with each cell binned by min-max; after rank-uniformization every cell's values are EXACTLY {0,1,…,T−1} → min-max binning gives a UNIFORM marginal histogram → H(A),H(B) are CONSTANT for every cell in every arm, INDEPENDENT of amplitude variance → MI changes ONLY via the JOINT H(A,B) (the co-movement RELATIONSHIP a relationship-destroying permutation MUST collapse). SAME substrate + seeds [1317,1318,1319] as H_1319/H_1320; the ONLY change is whether the read-out is rank-uniformized." :: hypothesis [slug=1328_phi_variance_free group=OMEGA]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1328_phi_variance_free.hexa, $0 CPU-local ENGINE-NATIVE (deterministic engine LCG-gauss == engine_cli.hexa _lcg_*; NOT numpy), seeds [1317,1318,1319], frozen-first (.verdicts/1328_phi_variance_free/H_1328_FREEZE.txt committed 26494942a BEFORE scoring the NEW encoding, bars NOT moved c9/p7). Φ = FAITHFUL IIT4 ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool): exact MIP-EI iit4_faithful_phi(traj,4,64,8) over hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa — the engine LCG only emits the salience trajectory; the hexa exact-MIP computes Φ. Substrate reused VERBATIM from H_1319: 4-module leaky-linear ring dim8 T64, Kuramoto pacemaker w_phase0.5 omega_t0.45 domega0.08, relative-phase gate sal=e·(1+cos(θ_i−θ_T))/2. ARMS A=NO-PHASE B=PHASE-BIND S=PERM-SHUFFLE(module→phase derangement, relationship destroyed, marginals preserved) O=OFFSET-SHUF. ENCODINGS OLD=raw min-max (H_1319) NEW=rank-uniformize each cell. eps=0.02 (=H_1283/H_1319 MARGIN_PHI, ported verbatim). FROZEN bars (GREEN iff V1∧V2∧V3): V1 CONFOUND-CONFIRM both legs all seeds = V1a OLD perm ΔΦ(S−A)≥+eps (RAISES, reproduces confound) AND V1b NEW perm Φ_S≤Φ_A+eps (collapses) · V2 ROBUST-LIFT NEW Φ_B≥Φ_A+eps all seeds incl 1317 · V3 EARNED NEW perm&offset both ≤Φ_A+eps all seeds. OUTCOMES (all valid c9): V1∧V2∧V3→🟢 wall was the estimator (clean read-out makes integration robust; follow-on = wire rank-uniform read-out); V1∧¬V2→confound REAL but integration still not robust = DEEPER estimator-INDEPENDENT terminal 🧱; ¬V1→variance diagnosis WRONG, wall undiagnosed. live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (standalone fn main, 0 importers)."
  verdict = "🧱 TERMINAL CLOSED-NEGATIVE, DEEPER (honest, c9/c16 — frozen-first, bars NOT moved). VERBATIM faithful-IIT4 Φ (exact MIP-EI n=4, deterministic, re-run byte-identical): seed 1317 OLD A=0.870311 perm-S=1.150110 ΔΦ(S−A)=+0.279798 [V1a PASS] | NEW A=1.933980 B=1.808980 ΔΦ(B−A)=−0.125000 [V2 FAIL] perm S−A=−0.206955 [V1b PASS] off O−A=+0.105545 [V3o FAIL] · seed 1318 OLD A=0.855353 perm-S=0.957870 ΔΦ(S−A)=+0.102517 [V1a PASS] | NEW A=2.250610 B=2.250610 ΔΦ(B−A)=0.000000 [V2 FAIL] perm S−A=−0.046570 [V1b PASS] off O−A=−0.437500 [V3o PASS] · seed 1319 OLD A=0.586833 perm-S=1.174020 ΔΦ(S−A)=+0.587183 [V1a PASS] | NEW A=2.079040 B=2.110290 ΔΦ(B−A)=+0.031250 [V2 PASS] perm S−A=−0.031250 [V1b PASS] off O−A=−0.039521 [V3o PASS]. V1 CONFOUND-CONFIRM = PASS (V1a PASS — OLD min-max perm RAISES Φ all 3 seeds, reproducing H_1319 EXACTLY; V1b PASS — NEW rank-uniform perm COLLAPSES Φ all 3 seeds, S−A −0.207/−0.047/−0.031 all ≤eps): the amplitude-variance binarization confound is CONFIRMED REAL and the rank-uniform encoding provably removes it — the SAME relationship-destroying permutation that RAISED Φ under min-max now CORRECTLY collapses it under the variance-free read-out. V2 ROBUST-LIFT = FAIL (under the clean estimator the phase mechanism does NOT lift robustly: B−A −0.125/0.0/+0.031, NEGATIVE on the orthogonal seed 1317, fails 2/3). V3 EARNED = FAIL (perm leg PASS all collapse, but offset leg FAILS seed 1317 O−A=+0.106). GATE NOT GREEN → 🧱 DEEPER. FINDING: the 4× Φ-robustness wall HAD a real estimator confound (V1), but removing it does NOT make integration robust (V2/V3) → the wall is an ESTIMATOR-INDEPENDENT substrate limit (the n≤8 4-module substrate genuinely lacks robust faithful-IIT4 integration even under a clean read-out). A STRONGER, cleaner closure than the prior amplitude-confounded 🧱 (now the controls are clean — perm collapses as it should — and the lift STILL is not robust). This BOUNDS (does NOT retract) the 4 prior Φ verdicts (H_1283/1317/1319/1320) — it diagnoses their SHARED estimator and shows the artifact was real while the closed-negative conclusion holds estimator-independently. Does NOT refute anima's substrate (Ψ=1/2 untouched). NO CORE wiring follow-on (a_verified_must_wire fires on GREEN only); had it been GREEN the named follow-on was to wire the rank-uniform Φ read-out into the live faithful-Φ monitor path. SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY n=4 dim-8 64-tick faithful-Φ EXACT, engine-native deterministic LCG (NOT numpy); the rank-uniform invariant is exact for the min-max binner (removes the marginal-variance channel; the V3o seed-1317 residual shows a joint-level artifact the additive-offset control can still ride on one seed). NOT ruled out: full per-mechanism IIT 4.0 (iit4_bigphi), much larger module set (loses exactness >8), a different substrate family — each a NEW hypothesis. frozen-first, NO tune-to-green, deterministic. .verdicts/1328_phi_variance_free/H_1328.txt"
  group  = "OMEGA"

@C h1331_phi_bigphi := "H_1331 — does the FULL IIT-4.0 SYSTEM big-Φ (a fundamentally DIFFERENT Φ measure — CAUSAL cause-effect structure over a TPM, system-level irreducibility destroyed by the system MIP) show ROBUST integration where the small-φ exact-MIP could not? H_1328 closed 🧱 estimator-INDEPENDENT *under the small-φ correlational MI-over-binning measure* (faithful_phi: the amplitude-variance confound is real & removable, yet removing it does not make integration robust — V2 fails on orthogonal seed 1317), and explicitly named 'full per-mechanism IIT 4.0 (iit4_bigphi)' as a NOT-ruled-out follow-on. H_1331 directly tests that DIFFERENT estimator FAMILY: re-run the SAME H_1319/H_1328 substrate + mechanisms (engine-native leaky-linear 4-module ring, Kuramoto pacemaker, relative-phase gate) on the SAME 3 hard orthogonal seeds [1317,1318,1319], but score with stdlib iit4_bigphi.big_phi (full IIT-4.0 system big-Φ over MIP, a_phi_iit4_tool — NOT a proxy) instead of faithful_phi small-φ. n≤8 (n_mod=4 binary units) for MIP tractability. A wall under one estimator family need not hold under the other." :: hypothesis [slug=1331_phi_bigphi group=OMEGA]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1331_phi_bigphi.hexa, $0 CPU-local ENGINE-NATIVE (deterministic engine LCG-gauss == engine_cli.hexa _lcg_*; NOT numpy), seeds [1317,1318,1319], frozen-first (.verdicts/1331_phi_bigphi/FREEZE.txt committed BEFORE scoring, bars NOT moved c9/p7). Φ = FAITHFUL IIT-4.0 SYSTEM big-Φ ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool, g61 stdlib SSOT): big_phi(tpm,4,sys_state) over hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4_bigphi.hexa (+ iit4_tpm/distinction/relation pipeline) — Σφ_d(distinctions)+Σφ_r(relations) minus the least-damaging system bipartition cut, NOT a variance×energy proxy / NOT small-φ. Substrate reused VERBATIM from H_1319/H_1328: 4-module leaky-linear ring dim8 T64, gain0.30 leak0.55 w_phase0.5 omega_t0.45 domega0.08, relative-phase gate sal=e·(1+cos(θ_i−θ_T))/2. ARMS A=NO-PHASE B=PHASE-BIND S=PERM-SHUFFLE(module→phase derangement) O=OFFSET-SHUF (IDENTICAL to H_1328). TRAJECTORY→TPM (the input big_phi requires, distinct from small-φ's trajectory-binning): each module = binary UNIT, ON at tick t iff salience in the UPPER HALF of that module's own T-length distribution (median/rank split = VARIANCE-FREE, carrying H_1328's read-out lesson, marginal ON-rate≈0.5 by construction); empirical state-by-node TPM tpm[s*n+u]=P(unit u ON at t+1|state s at t), unseen rows=0.5 (max-entropy, no fabricated dependence); sys_state=modal observed state (attractor, lowest-index tie-break); IDENTICAL construction across all 4 arms. eps=0.02 (=H_1283/H_1319/H_1328 MARGIN_PHI, ported verbatim). FROZEN bars (GREEN iff B1∧B2): B1 ROBUST big-Φ_B≥big-Φ_A+eps all seeds incl 1317 · B2 EARNED perm big-Φ_S≤big-Φ_A+eps AND offset big-Φ_O≤big-Φ_A+eps all seeds. OUTCOMES (all valid c9): B1∧B2→🟢 robust integration reachable under big-Φ (limit was small-φ-MIP-specific, different-estimator breakthrough; follow-on=wire engine-native big-Φ read-out a_verified_must_wire); B1 fails→wall holds across BOTH IIT measures→estimator-FAMILY-independent 🧱. live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (standalone fn main, 0 importers)."
  verdict = "🧱 TERMINAL CLOSED-NEGATIVE, STRONGER (estimator-FAMILY-independent; honest, c9/c16 — frozen-first, bars NOT moved). VERBATIM full IIT-4.0 system big-Φ (exact MIP n=4, deterministic, re-run byte-identical): seed 1317 big-Φ A=5.81006 B=9.96112 S=7.28854 O=4.02273 → ΔΦ(B−A)=+4.15106 [B1 PASS] perm S−A=+1.47848 [B2perm FAIL] off O−A=−1.78733 [B2off PASS] · seed 1318 big-Φ A=4.51077 B=4.51077 S=4.51077 O=7.43049 → ΔΦ(B−A)=0.00000 [B1 FAIL] perm S−A=0.00000 [B2perm PASS] off O−A=+2.91972 [B2off FAIL] · seed 1319 big-Φ A=4.08518 B=5.88351 S=4.08518 O=5.94597 → ΔΦ(B−A)=+1.79833 [B1 PASS] perm S−A=0.00000 [B2perm PASS] off O−A=+1.86079 [B2off FAIL]. B1 ROBUST = FAIL (seed 1318 ZERO lift, B==A==4.51077 → the coupling mechanism produces NO big-Φ gain at all on that seed; same fragile seed-dependent signature as small-φ). B2 EARNED = FAIL (controls do NOT cleanly collapse: perm-shuffle RAISES big-Φ on 1317 +1.478, offset RAISES on 1318/1319 +2.920/+1.861 → lift not earned over relationship-destroying controls, the same variance/structure-agnostic inflation H_1319/H_1328 found under small-φ, reproduced in the causal big-Φ family). GATE NOT GREEN → 🧱 STRONGER. FINDING: full IIT-4.0 SYSTEM big-Φ does NOT reach robust integration where small-φ could not — the Φ-robustness limit holds across BOTH IIT measure families (correlational small-φ exact-MIP H_1328 V2 B−A −0.125/0.0/+0.031 AND causal big-Φ TPM-MIP B1 B−A +4.15/0.0/+1.80, both with seed 1318/1317 failures) on the same orthogonal seed family. This is a CLEANER, STRONGER closure than H_1328's single-measure estimator-INDEPENDENT result: the substrate genuinely lacks robust n≤8 integration regardless of which IIT estimator (correlational OR causal) measures it → estimator-FAMILY-independent 🧱. BOUNDS (does NOT retract) the 4 prior Φ verdicts (H_1283/1317/1319/1320) + H_1328 across the big-Φ measure family. Does NOT refute anima's substrate (Ψ=1/2 untouched). NO CORE wiring follow-on (a_verified_must_wire fires on GREEN only — nothing to wire). SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY n≤8 (n_mod=4 binary units), faithful IIT-4.0 EXACT big-Φ over the system MIP, engine/numpy-mirror DIRECTIONAL (engine-transfer UNVERIFIED); T=64 → empirical TPM sparse over 2^4=16 states (unseen rows = max-ent 0.5). NOT ruled out: higher-n big-Φ (>8 needs macro-grain, H_1049 caveat), real-corpus substrate, a third estimator family, finer TPM estimation with longer T — each a NEW hypothesis. frozen-first, NO tune-to-green, deterministic. .verdicts/1331_phi_bigphi/result.txt"
@C h1332_phi_substrate := "H_1332 — Φ-robustness wall, SUBSTRATE-FAMILY axis: H_1328 closed the wall as an ESTIMATOR-INDEPENDENT limit, but SPECIFICALLY for the n≤8 leaky-linear pure_field-style substrate whose dynamics SIGN-SATURATE under coupling (H_1308/1313/1320 diagnosis: coupling strong enough to register OVERWRITES member dynamics → COPY → Φ=0; the H_1319/1328 read-out sal=e·carrier is a MULTIPLICATIVE gate that nulls member energy under synchrony). H_1320 §honesty NAMED the untested angle: 'a substrate whose own dynamics SURVIVE coupling, a richer NON-sign-saturating per-unit code.' H_1332 builds exactly that substrate FAMILY — additive phase-blend then a bounded GRADED softsign squash (member-state always retained, bounded (−1,1) but NEVER hard-saturates) — re-runs the SAME coupling mechanisms (H_1283 re-entrant relay + H_1319 phase pacemaker) on the SAME 3 hard seeds [1317,1318,1319], scored with the SAME faithful exact MIP (a_phi_iit4_tool) on the SAME variance-clean rank-uniform read-out (H_1328) so the controls are honest. Does a non-saturating substrate show robust integration where the saturating one could not (wall = substrate-family-specific) or hold (substrate-family-INDEPENDENT)?" :: hypothesis [slug=1332_phi_substrate group=OMEGA]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1332_phi_substrate.hexa, $0 CPU-local ENGINE-NATIVE (deterministic engine LCG-gauss == engine_cli.hexa _lcg_*; NOT numpy), seeds [1317,1318,1319], frozen-first (.verdicts/1332_phi_substrate/FREEZE.txt committed 85e94cf0e BEFORE any scoring, bars NOT moved c9/p7). Φ = FAITHFUL IIT4 ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool, g61 — stdlib searched first): exact MIP-EI iit4_faithful_phi(traj,4,64,8) over hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa; the engine LCG only emits the salience trajectory, the hexa exact-MIP computes Φ. Variance-clean read-out (H_1328): every arm rank-uniformized before the MIP. LEVER = the substrate FAMILY (per-unit read-out code), everything else identical: SATURATING sal_i=e_i·carrier_i carrier=(1+cos(θ_i−θ_T))/2 (multiplicative, H_1319/1328, the S3 attribution control reproduced in-run) vs NON-SATURATING raw_i=e_i+BETA·cos(θ_i−θ_T) sal_i=SOFTSIGN(raw_i/SCALE)=(raw_i/SCALE)/(1+|raw_i/SCALE|) BETA=0.5 SCALE=2.0 (additive blend + bounded graded squash, member survives coupling; ARM A no-coup = SOFTSIGN(e_i/SCALE)). SAME mechanisms held identical (re-entrant ring w_nbr0.5 + Kuramoto pacemaker w_phase0.5 omega_t0.45 domega0.08), SAME leaky-linear ring gain0.30 leak0.55 w_in0.5 dim8 T64. ARMS A=NO-COUP B=MECHANISM S=PERM-SHUFFLE(module→phase derangement) O=OFFSET-SHUF. eps=0.02 (MARGIN_PHI ported verbatim). FROZEN bars (GREEN iff S1∧S2∧S3): S1 ROBUST NONSAT Φ_B≥Φ_A+eps all 3 seeds incl 1317 · S2 EARNED NONSAT perm Φ_S≤Φ_A+eps AND offset Φ_O≤Φ_A+eps all seeds · S3 ATTRIBUTION SAT substrate FAILS S1 on ≥1 seed (reproduces H_1328 V2 −0.125/0.0/+0.031). OUTCOMES (all valid c9): S1∧S2∧S3→🟢 robust integration reachable once substrate doesn't sign-saturate (wall=substrate-family-specific, overturns H_1328 as specific, CORE-wiring follow-on=wire the non-saturating per-unit read-out); ¬S1→strongest 🧱 yet (substrate-family-INDEPENDENT); S1∧¬(S2∧S3)→honest partial. live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (standalone fn main, 0 importers)."
  verdict = "🧱 TERMINAL CLOSED-NEGATIVE, STRONGEST YET — substrate-family-INDEPENDENT (honest, c9/c16, frozen-first, bars NOT moved, re-run byte-identical). VERBATIM faithful-IIT4 Φ (exact MIP-EI n=4, deterministic): seed 1317 NONSAT A=1.93398 B=2.00061 ΔΦ(B−A)=+0.066635 [S1 PASS] perm S−A=−0.10907 [S2perm PASS] off O−A=−0.24234 [S2off PASS] | SAT A=1.93398 B=1.80898 ΔΦ(B−A)=−0.125 [SAT-fails-S1 YES] · seed 1318 NONSAT A=2.25061 B=2.25475 ΔΦ(B−A)=+0.004135 [S1 FAIL] perm S−A=−0.046570 [S2perm PASS] off O−A=−0.28125 [S2off PASS] | SAT A=2.25061 B=2.25061 ΔΦ(B−A)=0.000 [SAT-fails-S1 YES] · seed 1319 NONSAT A=2.07904 B=2.23529 ΔΦ(B−A)=+0.156250 [S1 PASS] perm S−A=−0.129135 [S2perm PASS] off O−A=−0.160385 [S2off PASS] | SAT A=2.07904 B=2.11029 ΔΦ(B−A)=+0.03125 [SAT-fails-S1 NO]. S1 ROBUST = FAIL (NONSAT lifts 2/3 — seed 1317 +0.067, seed 1319 +0.156 — but seed 1318 +0.004<eps; NOT all 3 seeds). S2 EARNED = PASS (NONSAT perm AND offset both collapse ≤Φ_A+eps on ALL 3 seeds; the variance-clean controls correctly destroy the lift). S3 SUBSTRATE-ATTRIBUTION = PASS (the SATURATING substrate reproduces H_1328 V2 BYTE-FAITHFULLY in-run: SAT B−A −0.125/0.000/+0.031, fails S1 on seeds 1317+1318 → any NONSAT lift IS the non-saturation, not the mechanism). GATE ¬S1 → 🧱 STRONGEST yet. FINDING: the non-saturating substrate is GENUINELY BETTER — on the orthogonal seed 1317 (which gave H_1328 its decisive V2 fail SAT B−A −0.125) the non-saturating read-out FLIPS the sign to a real lift +0.067, and nearly 5× on 1319 (+0.156 vs +0.031); member energy retained additively under a bounded graded softsign DOES survive coupling enough to raise faithful-IIT4 Φ where the multiplicative member-nulling read-out collapsed it. BUT it still does NOT clear the 3-seed robustness gate (seed 1318 flat); the 1317-class orthogonal-seed fragility SHIFTS (1317→1318) but PERSISTS → robust n≤8 faithful-IIT4 integration is ABSENT even for a non-saturating substrate. The wall holds across the saturating AND a non-saturating family, with clean variance-free controls in both → it is substrate-family-INDEPENDENT, a STRONGER closure than H_1328 (which was estimator-independent within ONE family). BOUNDS (does NOT retract) H_1328 + the prior Φ verdicts; H_1328 stays exactly true for the saturating family (reproduced byte-exact). Does NOT refute anima's substrate (Ψ=1/2 untouched). NO CORE wiring follow-on (a_verified_must_wire fires on GREEN only); had S1 been GREEN the named follow-on was to wire the non-saturating per-unit read-out into the live faithful-Φ path / pure_field member code. SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY n=4 dim-8 64-tick faithful-Φ EXACT MIP-EI, engine-native deterministic LCG (NOT numpy — numpy never computes Φ), numpy mirror DIRECTIONAL (engine-transfer to live CORE/pure_field UNVERIFIED). NOT ruled out: full per-mechanism IIT 4.0 (iit4_bigphi), much larger module set (loses exactness >8), yet another substrate family / non-saturating code variant, a seed-geometry without the orthogonal fragility — each a NEW hypothesis. frozen-first, NO tune-to-green, deterministic. .verdicts/1332_phi_substrate/result.txt"
  group  = "OMEGA"

@C h1347_phi_higher_n := "H_1347 — Φ-robustness wall, LARGER-N axis: does robust faithful-IIT-4 integration appear at N>8 — the SIZE the exact-MIP tractability ceiling never reached — under an ANYTIME/GREEDY-MIP big-Φ with an HONEST stated error bound? The faithful-IIT-4 Φ-robustness wall is 🧱 across SIX cuts (H_1283/1317 topology, H_1319 timing, H_1320 division, H_1328 estimator-confound, H_1331 big-Φ measure-family, H_1332 substrate-family) — and EVERY one of those verdicts scoped its closure to n≤8 (where the exact MIP enumerates 2^(n-1)≤128 bipartitions) and named the SAME untested angle in its 'NOT ruled out': 'a much larger module set (loses exactness >8) — a NEW hypothesis.' H_1347 is that hypothesis. At N>8 the exact MIP is intractable, so Φ uses the stdlib GREEDY Kernighan–Lin MIP (iit4_approx_phi — the SAME faithful cross-cut-MI MIP-EI Φ definition, an anytime search of its MIP, NOT a proxy / NOT a different measure) with the STATED bound Φ_greedy≥Φ_exact (UPPER BOUND, verbatim stdlib §iit4_approx_phi_from_mi). Substrate reused VERBATIM from H_1319/H_1328 SCALED to N_MOD=12, rank-uniform variance-clean read-out (H_1328) on all arms, SAME 3 hard seeds [1317,1318,1319]. Does robust integration appear at the larger N the ceiling never reached, or does the wall hold (an even stronger closure)?" :: hypothesis [slug=1347_phi_higher_n group=OMEGA]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1347_phi_higher_n.hexa, $0 CPU-local ENGINE-NATIVE (deterministic engine LCG-gauss == engine_cli.hexa _lcg_*; NOT numpy — numpy never computes Φ), seeds [1317,1318,1319], frozen-first (.verdicts/1347_phi_higher_n/FREEZE.txt committed 17e54d487 BEFORE any Φ scored, bars NOT moved c9/p7). Φ = FAITHFUL IIT-4 FAMILY ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool, g61 — stdlib searched first): GREEDY big-Φ iit4_approx_phi(traj,12,64,8) at N=12 + EXACT iit4_faithful_phi(traj,8,64,8) at n=8 for the bound-validation, both over hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa; the engine LCG only emits the salience trajectory, the hexa MIP computes Φ. GRAIN = per-cell (NO macro-grain — deliberately avoids the H_1049 caveat that a FIXED small-m coarse-grain is not a scalable estimator; only the MIP SEARCH is approximated, validated exact at n=8). BOUND = Φ_greedy≥Φ_exact (greedy local-min cut ≥ global MIP cut → UPPER BOUND). Substrate reused VERBATIM from H_1319/H_1328 scaled to N>8: N_MOD=12 leaky-linear ring dim8 T64 gain0.30 leak0.55 w_nbr/w_in0.5, Kuramoto pacemaker w_phase0.5 omega_t0.45 domega0.08, relative-phase gate sal=e·(1+cos(θ_i−θ_T))/2; ring topology generalizes to any N. Read-out rank-uniform (H_1328) ALL arms. ARMS A=NO-PHASE B=PHASE-BIND S=PERM-SHUFFLE(module→phase forced derangement) O=OFFSET-SHUF. eps=0.02 (MARGIN_PHI ported verbatim). FROZEN bars (GREEN iff N1∧N2∧N3): N1 ROBUST greedy Φ_B≥Φ_A+eps ALL 3 seeds incl 1317 @N=12 · N2 EARNED greedy perm Φ_S≤Φ_A+eps AND offset Φ_O≤Φ_A+eps ALL seeds · N3 BOUND-HONEST the greedy bound (Φ_greedy≥Φ_exact) STATED + verdict robust to it, validated by the n=8 exact-vs-greedy gap g=Φ_greedy−Φ_exact reported verbatim per arm/seed (g≈0 ⇒ tight ⇒ larger-N lift bound-robust). OUTCOMES (all valid c9): N1∧N2∧N3→🟢 robust integration EMERGES at larger N (n≤8 closure was a SIZE limit; CORE-wiring follow-on = wire the greedy big-Φ read-out); ¬N1 or ¬N2 (with N3)→wall HOLDS at larger N = STRONGER closure, the size escape hatch CLOSED; ¬N3→greedy slack large, larger-N number = upper-bound only (report straight). live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (standalone fn main, 0 importers)."
  verdict = "🧱 TERMINAL CLOSED-NEGATIVE, STRONGER — the larger-N escape hatch is CLOSED (honest, c9/c16, frozen-first, bars NOT moved, re-run byte-identical, toolchain hexa 0.1.0-dispatch). N3 BOUND-VALIDATION at n=8 (exact vs greedy MIP, SAME rank-uniform substrate, all 4 arms × 3 seeds): gap g=Φ_greedy−Φ_exact = 0.0 on ALL 12 cells (greedy MIP == exact MIP everywhere; e.g. seed1317 A exact=4.75597 greedy=4.75597, B 4.68872/4.68872, S 4.6109/4.6109, O 4.4352/4.4352; seeds 1318/1319 likewise gap 0.0) → max gap 0.0 ≤ eps → N3 PASS, greedy big-Φ is a TIGHT (zero-slack) upper bound on this substrate, larger-N number trustworthy. VERBATIM greedy big-Φ @N=12: seed 1317 A=7.98102 B=8.07321 ΔΦ(B−A)=+0.092190 [N1 PASS] perm S=7.80884 S−A=−0.172180 [N2p PASS] off O=7.93703 O−A=−0.043995 [N2o PASS] · seed 1318 A=8.03587 B=7.88666 ΔΦ(B−A)=−0.149201 [N1 FAIL] perm S=8.07477 S−A=+0.038910 [N2p FAIL] off O=7.46706 O−A=−0.568807 [N2o PASS] · seed 1319 A=8.06908 B=7.99478 ΔΦ(B−A)=−0.074295 [N1 FAIL] perm S=7.93032 S−A=−0.138759 [N2p PASS] off O=8.10094 O−A=+0.031861 [N2o FAIL]. N1 ROBUST = FAIL (ΔΦ(B−A) +0.092/−0.149/−0.074 — only seed 1317 lifts, 1318+1319 NEGATIVE; the same seed-fragile signature every n≤8 lane showed, reproduced at N=12 under a clean estimator). N2 EARNED = FAIL (perm RAISES Φ on 1318 +0.039, offset RAISES on 1319 +0.032 — the residual structure-agnostic inflation H_1319/H_1328/H_1331 found, persisting at larger N). N3 BOUND-HONEST = PASS (n=8 max gap 0.0). GATE NOT GREEN → 🧱 STRONGER. FINDING: the 'much larger module set' escape hatch that EVERY prior n≤8 OMEGA Φ verdict named is now CLOSED — with a TIGHT greedy big-Φ (gap=0.0, so the upper bound has zero slack and the SAME monotone search is applied to both arm B and arm A, no lift can be manufactured by the approximation) AND a clean variance-free read-out, robust (3-seed control-surviving) faithful-IIT-4 integration is ABSENT at N=12 just as at n=4. This is a STRONGER closure than any n≤8 verdict: the limit is NOT an artifact of the exact-MIP tractability ceiling. BOUNDS (does NOT retract) the prior n≤8 Φ verdicts — it tests + closes their explicitly-named larger-N angle. Does NOT refute anima's substrate (Ψ=1/2 untouched). NO CORE wiring follow-on (a_verified_must_wire fires on GREEN only — nothing to wire; CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED); had it been GREEN the named follow-on was to wire the greedy big-Φ read-out into the live faithful-Φ monitor path at larger N. SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY N=12 dim-8 64-tick, GRAIN per-cell (NO macro-grain, H_1049 caveat avoided), BOUND Φ_greedy≥Φ_exact tight (g=0) at n=8; engine-native deterministic LCG content generator (numpy never computes Φ), the Φ leg IS the real faithful cross-cut-MI MIP-EI (exact n=8, greedy KL N=12). NOT ruled out (each a NEW hypothesis): EVEN-larger N (N≫12) with a validated macro-grain whose m GROWS with N (H_1049), a real-corpus substrate, a yet-different Φ estimator family, or engine-transfer to live CORE/pure_field. frozen-first, NO tune-to-green, deterministic. .verdicts/1347_phi_higher_n/result.txt"
  group  = "OMEGA"

@C h1323_sapir_whorf := "H_1323 — Sapir-Whorf / linguistic relativity: does the LANGUAGE a substrate learns warp its NON-LINGUISTIC discrimination (not just what it can express, but its performance on a no-label same/different task)? H_1316/H_1322 showed a domain's REPRESENTATION changes its LEARNABILITY (compression); Sapir-Whorf is the deeper claim — the language's CARVING of a domain warps DOWNSTREAM non-linguistic discrimination. The empirical workhorse = CATEGORICAL PERCEPTION (cross-category pairs discriminated better than within-category at the language's boundary; the grue languages cut a continuum at DIFFERENT points). Lens: cognitive-science / psycholinguistics (a_no_llm_frame_trap, c15) — NOT an LLM recipe, NOT a human-cognition claim, a TOY synthetic continuum (legitimate methodology: the 'languages' are label schemes over the continuum)." :: hypothesis [slug=1323_sapir_whorf group=COGNITION-REPRESENTATION]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1323_sapir_whorf.py — R1 numpy MIRROR (DIRECTIONAL, $0 CPU-local, gradient-free, 3 seeds [4323,4324,4325], p7 = discrimination margins + peak locations NOT perplexity; detached nohup polled inline, a_cpu_local_no_waiter). PARADIGM (toy stimulus continuum): one continuous 1-D 'hue' axis, N=21 graded stimuli with an RBF position code (locally-smooth, position-FAITHFUL, boundary-AGNOSTIC — the substrate is NEVER told where any boundary is). TWO languages over the SAME axis (grue-style): L_A cuts at p_A=1/3, L_B at p_B=2/3; a language labels each stimulus by which side of its cut it falls. The SAME gradient-free mitosis/Voronoi cell store (error-targeted SPLIT-only growth, p8; cell label FIXED at creation = stable nearest-prototype classifier) learns each language's carving — cells PACK at the boundary where category error concentrates (the mechanistic origin of CP). DOWNSTREAM NON-LINGUISTIC TEST (NO labels at test): discrimination of adjacent pairs = |Δ soft category-posterior| across the pair (a representational gradient, no hard label read), plotted vs pair midpoint → the CP peak. 4 ARMS: (1) PRE-LANGUAGE (no labels → 1 cell, constant posterior, FLAT) · (2) L_A · (3) L_B · (4) SHUFFLE (incoherent per-stimulus labels, fixed per seed). frozen-first: .verdicts/1323_sapir_whorf/H_1323_FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE scoring, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): (W1 CP PRESENT) for L_A & L_B cross-boundary discrim − within-category discrim ≥ 0.15 AND language-vs-PRE-LANG-baseline at peak ≥ 0.15 · (W2 WHORFIAN DISSOCIATION, decisive) CP peak LOCATION within 0.12 of p_A / p_B AND the two peaks differ by ≥ 0.20 · (W3 EARNED anti-Goodhart) SHUFFLE prominence < 0.5× mean-language prominence AND shuffle peak loc-std ≥ 0.15. GREEN iff W1∧W2∧W3; W2 fail → UNIVERSALIST (Whorf refuted, honest negative); W1 fail → no CP. Live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_autonomy_over_hardcode, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck, a_break_the_wall."
  verdict = "🟠 PARTIAL — LINGUISTIC RELATIVITY HOLDS in the substrate (W1∧W2 decisive), the anti-Goodhart W3 SPLIT. mean of 3 seeds [4323,4324,4325]. W1 CP PRESENT ✅: L_A & L_B cross-within margin = +0.200 (≥0.15), language-vs-PRE-LANG-baseline at peak = +0.989 (≥0.15); PRE-LANGUAGE arm FLAT (1 cell, constant posterior, peak 0.000). W2 WHORFIAN DISSOCIATION ✅ (the load-bearing linguistic-relativity signature): CP peak LOCATION L_A → 0.325 (|Δ p_A|=0.008), L_B → 0.675 (|Δ p_B|=0.008), separation 0.350 (≥0.20), std 0.000 across all 3 seeds → SAME stimulus world, the boundary MOVES with the language, cognition follows the language. W3 EARNED ❌ SPLIT: loc-std sub-clause ✅ (shuffle peak wanders 0.492±0.165 across seeds = incoherent; NON-GATING diagnostic — peaks ≥0.5×arm-peak: L_A=1.0, L_B=1.0, SHUFFLE=8.0, so each language has ONE coherent peak vs shuffle's MANY scattered spikes), but prominence sub-clause ❌ (random labels create MANY locally-sharp posterior swings → shuffle single-peak prominence 0.661 > 0.5×0.999=0.50 bar; the frozen prominence threshold was MIS-SPECIFIED for a multi-peak shuffle). NO bar moved (c9/p7) — reported straight. FINDING: the language a substrate learns measurably WARPS its non-linguistic discrimination — categorical perception emerges AT the language's boundary and the CP peak LOCATION tracks the language (linguistic relativity holds, W1∧W2 decisive); the shuffle control IS incoherent (8 wandering spikes vs 1 locked peak, loc-std PASS) but its individual spikes are sharp enough that the single-peak prominence sub-clause does not clear. HONEST SCOPE (c9 · a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror (engine-transfer to the live CORE/*.hexa immune/Voronoi lane = follow-on, a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire); TOY synthetic continuum (N=21, 3 seeds, deterministic readout — tests the linguistic-relativity STRUCTURE, not a scaled or human-cognition claim); the discrimination readout reads ONLY representational distance, NO injected boundary / persona / RLHF, the language label enters only at training not at test (p1/p2/p3/p6); NOT an emit gate (a_autonomy_over_hardcode). NEXT R2: re-freeze a COHERENCE-based W3 (peak-count ≤1 for languages / ≥threshold for shuffle, or circular peak-spread) pre-registered ANEW — NOT a relaxation of this bar — then engine-native realization. .verdicts/1323_sapir_whorf/H_1323.txt"
  group  = "COGNITION-REPRESENTATION"

@C h1321_ko_jamo_wire := "H_1321 — ENGINE-NATIVE WIRING (r2) of the H_1316 🟢 GREEN ko-jamo breakthrough (a_verified_must_wire): does the SAME gradient-free jamo-symbol mitosis, run ENGINE-NATIVE on the LIVE CORE/engine_cli.hexa VAdaptField + engine_mitosis_tick faculties (the SAME live Korean path H_1306/H_1312 use), reproduce the H_1316 mirror jamo CE within a pre-registered 0.05 tolerance AND break the raw-byte ceiling — engine-native byte-exact, Ψ-disjoint, single-entry (a_core_engine_map)? H_1316 was a numpy/torch MIRROR (DIRECTIONAL); a GREEN mechanism is not done until it RUNS engine-native on the live engine. The representation transform (NFD jamo symbolization) is deterministic Unicode data-prep; the MITOSIS + held-out per-byte CE scoring run engine-native in CORE/h1321_ko_jamo_wire_probe.hexa." :: hypothesis [slug=1321_ko_jamo_wire group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
