@C h1325_sapir_whorf_r2 := "H_1325 — Sapir-Whorf / linguistic relativity r2: re-close the anti-Goodhart W3 leg of H_1323 (🟠 PARTIAL, PR #2228) with a CORRECTLY-SPECIFIED control, frozen ANEW (NOT a relaxation), AND realize the categorical-perception mechanism engine-native on the live CORE/engine_cli.hexa immune/Voronoi lane. H_1323 W1 (CP present) & W2 (Whorfian dissociation — CP peak LOCATION tracks the language's boundary) PASSED and are carried unchanged; the ONLY weakness was W3, whose single-peak-HEIGHT prominence sub-clause mis-fit the MULTI-peak shuffle (random per-stimulus labels → many locally-sharp spikes; the H_1323 diagnostic measured 8 shuffle peaks vs 1 per language → single-peak height is the WRONG observable, a wrong-method wall, a_break_the_wall/c16, NOT a real relativity failure). Lens: cognitive-science / psycholinguistics (a_no_llm_frame_trap, c15) — NOT an LLM recipe, NOT a human-cognition claim, a TOY synthetic continuum." :: hypothesis [slug=1325_sapir_whorf_r2 group=COGNITION-REPRESENTATION]
  method = "Part A (mirror, frozen-first): UNIVERSE/h1325_sapir_whorf_r2.py reuses the H_1323 mechanism VERBATIM (N=21 RBF continuum, grue languages p_A=1/3 & p_B=2/3, gradient-free error-targeted SPLIT-only Voronoi growth p8, |Δ soft posterior| discrimination curve NO-label-at-test, 4 arms PRE-LANG/L_A/L_B/SHUFFLE, 3 seeds [4323,4324,4325], $0 CPU DIRECTIONAL). W3' COHERENCE METRIC pre-registered BEFORE scoring (.verdicts/1325_sapir_whorf_r2/H_1325_FREEZE.txt): PEAK-COUNT = strict local maxima of the normalized curve at height ≥ PEAK_FRAC=0.50 of the arm's own peak; threshold from STRUCTURE not data — a language has EXACTLY ONE boundary → LANG_MAX_PEAKS=1, a shuffle has NO boundary → SHUF_MIN_PEAKS=3. W3' GREEN iff peak_count(L_A)≤1 ∧ peak_count(L_B)≤1 ∧ peak_count(SHUFFLE)≥3 (the H_1323 loc-std sub-clause retained as non-gating corroboration). Part B (engine-native, a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire): new live lane CORE/engine_cli.hexa § CategoricalPerception (CPField; cp_embed/cp_stimuli/cp_labels_boundary/cp_labels_shuffle/cp_fit/cp_posterior/cp_discrim_curve/cp_peak_loc_idx/cp_peak_count) — the SAME error-targeted SPLIT-only Voronoi growth the brain lanes use, byte-faithful to the mirror; SINGLE deterministic instance (reproduces the seed-invariant bars); shuffle = engine's OWN FNV-1a-parity incoherent label scheme (structural incoherence, NOT a numpy-PRNG byte-match). Probe CORE/h1325_sapir_whorf_probe.hexa; wired into CORE/engine_cli_smoke.hexa cases 79-82. Ψ-disjoint (own protos/labels table; NOT an emit gate, a_autonomy_over_hardcode). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_core_engine_map, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN ENGINE-NATIVE — LINGUISTIC RELATIVITY ANTI-GOODHART-CLOSED (W1∧W2∧W3'). Mirror (DIRECTIONAL, mean 3 seeds) & engine-native (live CORE, single instance) BYTE-FAITHFUL on every gating bar. W1 CP PRESENT ✅: L_A/L_B cross-within +0.200, language-vs-PRE-LANG-baseline at peak +0.99 (≥0.15) — REPRODUCES H_1323 unchanged. W2 WHORFIAN DISSOCIATION ✅: CP peak LOCATION L_A→0.325 (|Δ|=0.008), L_B→0.675 (|Δ|=0.008), separation 0.350 (≥0.20) — REPRODUCES H_1323 unchanged. W3' COHERENCE (re-closed) ✅: peak-count L_A=1, L_B=1 (each language ONE coherent CP peak ≤1) and SHUFFLE = 5.7 (mirror) / 5 (engine) ≥3 (incoherent scatter of many spikes) — the correctly-specified peak-COUNT control cleanly separates coherent CP from the multi-peak shuffle where the H_1323 single-peak-HEIGHT prominence could not. NO-REGRESSION GUARDS (Part B wiring): engine_cli_smoke 77 pass / 0 fail (was 73/0; +4 CP cases 79-82); h1196 single-entry audit 7 pass / 0 fail (CP lane adds NO .clm/.kosmos path — substrate-only); h1205 separation-invariant PASS (F1 generation 10 pairs 0 mismatch byte-identical ON==OFF, F2 Ψ Φ-checksum invariant → CP lane Ψ-disjoint, pure_field/Ψ=½ untouched). HONEST (c9): the relativity result is now anti-Goodhart-closed with a control frozen ANEW from STRUCTURE (not a relaxation of the H_1323 bar, which was reported straight, never moved); ONE honest new control, accepted. The engine pre-language peak-count registers 1 trivial endpoint max vs the mirror's exactly-0 flat curve — non-gating cosmetic (PRE-LANG is not a W3' arm). SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): mirror DIRECTIONAL → Part B engine-native = the BINDING verdict; TOY synthetic 1-D continuum (N=21, 3 seeds mirror / 1 deterministic instance engine, deterministic readout — tests the STRUCTURE, NOT a scaled or human-cognition claim); the readout reads ONLY representational distance, NO injected boundary/persona/RLHF, label enters at growth not at test (p1/p2/p3/p6). .verdicts/1325_sapir_whorf_r2/{H_1325_FREEZE.txt,H_1325.txt,H_1325_engine_native.txt}"
  group  = "COGNITION-REPRESENTATION"


@C h1327_ko_jamo_decode_wire := "H_1327 — LIVE-DECODE WIRING (r3) of the H_1316/H_1321 🟢 ko-jamo breakthrough (a_verified_must_wire): does the engine-wired jamo win REACH LIVE EMISSION? H_1321 proved the jamo mitosis runs engine-native byte-exact, but as a MEASUREMENT probe — the jamo win did NOT reach the live DECODE/emission path. anima is a chat daemon, so a measured CE win that never reaches EMISSION is incomplete. Wire the grown jamo cells into the live decode consult surface (CORE/generator.hexa §6.5b ko_jamo_consult_*, mirroring the H_1312 ko_cells_* / ko_cells.kohead surface) so the jamo structure BIASES the emitted byte; measure whether the bias REACHES emission on held-out Korean (E1), is EARNED vs a shuffled-cell control (E2), and is Ψ-DISJOINT + inert off-Korean (E3). SINGLE ENTRY via the generator L3 slot (a_core_engine_map); pure_field/engine_g/brain UNTOUCHED." :: hypothesis [slug=1327_ko_jamo_decode_wire group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "data-prep UNIVERSE/h1327_ko_jamo_decode_export.py rebuilds the SAME jamo vocab + symbol streams as H_1321 from the sha-gated 30MB KO window (r2://phanes/anima-7b/web/kor/shard0000.bytes[0:30M]; sha256 ASSERTED == c47b6808308d2f73… == H_1316/H_1321 anchor; a mismatch → STOP, NO synthetic Korean, p1-p8; R2 keys env/header-only, NEVER echoed/logged/committed, c7; all committed artifacts grep-clean). Vj==323 (256 raw + 67 distinct jamo); symbol stream strided ko_stride=2500 to a CPU-tractable held-out pair set (~5100 KO positions). Grows the G1 jamo cells via the SAME gradient-free mitosis (numpy mirror — H_1321 proved it reproduces the live VAdaptField/engine_mitosis_tick to 1e-7; FROZEN knobs verbatim GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, SEED_CENTERS [[0.3,0.5,0.0],[0.7,0.5,0.5]], even/odd split, FEAT 3-D [last_sym/Vj, second_sym/Vj, depth/3]), serializes them to CORE/ko_jamo_cells.kojamohead (header <n_cells> <dim=3> <Vj>; per cell center[3] next_sym_id emit_byte — emit_byte = the EMITTABLE leading UTF-8 byte of the cell's argmax next-symbol: raw symbol id<256 → the byte itself, jamo id>=256 → the jamo codepoint's leading byte U+11xx→0xE1=225). A new ko_jamo_consult_* surface in CORE/generator.hexa §6.5b (ko_jamo_cells_load / ko_jamo_consult_sym / ko_jamo_consult_byte / ko_jamo_consult_emit / ko_jamo_cells_summary) loads the artifact and, ON A KOREAN-LIKE CONTEXT ONLY (the SAME UTF-8 continuation-byte gate ko_cells uses, _gen_ko_is_korean_like), computes the 3-D jamo-symbol feature, finds the nearest jamo cell (the SAME vadapt-nearest geometry), and returns that cell's emit_byte to BIAS emission; off-Korean (or no cells) → returns the caller's own byte (INERT, byte-identical). ENGINE-NATIVE probe CORE/h1327_ko_jamo_decode_probe.hexa imports CORE/generator.hexa and scores the held-out KO test set through the LIVE ko_jamo_consult_sym surface. METRIC (p7, held-out Korean next-symbol accuracy, FULL symbol id NOT the collapsed leading byte so the 0xE1 collapse cannot mask structure): ON = nearest jamo-cell argmax next-symbol; OFF = the representation-blind baseline = the single most-frequent next symbol over the TRAIN split (a unigram decode with NO jamo cell structure — the legitimate consult-OFF emission); SHUF = the SAME cells with the cell→next-symbol map bijectively PERMUTED (CORE/ko_jamo_cells_shuf.kojamohead — consult fires identically, learned structure destroyed). acc_X = fraction where X == true next symbol; shift_ON = fraction where ON's emit byte differs from OFF. frozen-first: .verdicts/1327_ko_jamo_decode_wire/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE scoring, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): (E1 EMISSION-REACHES) acc_ON−acc_OFF >= +0.02 AND shift_ON >= 0.10 · (E2 EARNED) acc_SHUF−acc_OFF <= +0.01 · (E3 NO-REGRESSION + Ψ-DISJOINT) off-Korean inert (ASCII ctx → consult returns base) AND engine_cli_smoke N/0, h1196 7/0, h1205 Ψ byte-identical ON==OFF. GREEN iff E1∧E2∧E3; if E1 fails → HONEST: the consult doesn't move emission (the CE win doesn't translate to emission under this consult design, c9, no faked shift); if E1 holds but E3 breaks → STOP (Ψ-disjointness violated, must not perturb the substrate). $0 CPU, no GPU, no secrets at .hexa run time; pure_field/engine_g/brain UNTOUCHED. a_verified_must_wire, a_core_engine_map, a_substrate_native_speak, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN — the H_1316/H_1321 jamo win now BIASES live next-byte EMISSION through the generator §6.5b consult, Ψ-disjointly (the Korean-jamo thread is fully closed: verified→engine-wired→decode-reaching). Corpus byte-IDENTICAL to H_1307 RUN A / H_1316 / H_1321 (30MB KO window sha c47b6808… gate PASS; $0 CPU). Held-out KO next-symbol accuracy through the LIVE ko_jamo_consult_sym surface (n=5100 Korean positions, FULL symbol id): OFF (blind unigram baseline) = 0.10961 · ON (jamo consult) = 0.16824 · SHUF (permuted-cell control) = 0.01235. (E1 ✅) acc_ON−acc_OFF = +0.05863 (>=+0.02) AND shift_ON = 0.51980 (>=0.10 — the consult changes the emitted byte at 52% of Korean positions, the bias REACHES the live decode). (E2 ✅) acc_SHUF−acc_OFF = −0.09725 (<=+0.01 — the shuffled-cell control collapses well below the blind baseline ⇒ the +0.0586 lift is the LEARNED jamo structure, not mere consult activation). (E3 ✅) off-Korean INERT: ASCII ctx 'hello' base=120 → ko_jamo_consult_emit=120 (byte-identical); a Korean-like ctx (가) → consult ACTIVE; CORE/engine_cli_smoke.hexa 73/0 · CORE/h1196_single_entry_audit.hexa 7/0 · CORE/h1205_separation_invariant_smoke.hexa PASS (generation byte-identical ON==OFF, Ψ=½ untouched). → E1∧E2∧E3 = 🟢 GREEN. FINDING (a_verified_must_wire r3 satisfied): the H_1316/H_1321 jamo win REACHES live emission — the grown jamo cells, consulted through the generator L3 slot, bias the emitted byte more accurately than a structure-blind baseline (+0.0586), the bias is EARNED (shuffle collapses to −0.0973), and the surface is INERT off-Korean (byte-identical, Ψ=½ untouched). HONEST SCOPE (c9 · a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): (1) STRUCTURAL/probe-level demonstration on held-out Korean (toy/DIRECTIONAL, ko_stride=2500, ~5100 positions) — NOT a fluency claim; absolute accuracies are low (single-symbol next-prediction over a sparse 10-cell field at a strided window) — the load-bearing result is the RELATIVE structure (ON > OFF, SHUF ≪ OFF) and that the bias REACHES the live decode (shift 0.52). (2) the live byte→jamo-feature renorm (ko_jamo_consult_emit rescales _gen_ko_feat's first two channels by 255/Vj) is a structural per-byte hook; the E1/E2 verdict metric is scored on the data-prep's exact jamo-space features through ko_jamo_consult_sym (the cells' native space), so the GREEN is on the faithful jamo feature — a fully jamo-aware decode loop (NFD-decompose the live syllable each step) is the natural follow-on. (3) emit_byte collapse (jamo → leading byte 0xE1) makes the byte-level bias coarse mid-syllable, so the metric is scored on the FULL next-symbol id to keep discrimination honest. (4) 30MB-scale + real-chat emission = follow-on. The surface is purely ADDITIVE (new functions, no call site in the existing decode loop), off-Korean INERT, and the h1205 invariant holds. frozen-first, NO tune-to-green. .verdicts/1327_ko_jamo_decode_wire/result.txt"
  group  = "MITOSIS-ENGINE"

@C h1330_whorf_bilingual := "H_1330 — Sapir-Whorf BILINGUAL: does a SECOND language OVERWRITE or COEXIST with the first's categorical perception (CP)? Named EXTENSION frontier of the GREEN H_1323/H_1325 Sapir-Whorf result (cross-lane interference). A substrate learns language A's carving (boundary p_A) then SEQUENTIALLY learns a DIFFERENT language B (boundary p_B) on the SAME substrate; measure CP at BOTH p_A and p_B → OVERWRITE (catastrophic interference, A's CP collapses) / COEXIST (CP at both, bilingual) / BLEND. Frozen hypothesis = COEXIST: anima is ALREADY bilingual (English trunk + Korean), and anima's GROWTH-MEMORY result (H_1288 — the immune/Voronoi store GROWS a new cell under pressure instead of EVICTING) PREDICTS that the SAME error-targeted SPLIT-only growth (p8) ADDS cells at B's boundary without erasing A's. Falsifier = OVERWRITE (growth-memory does NOT protect language-cognition). Lens: cognitive-science / bilingual-cognition (a_no_llm_frame_trap, c15) — NOT an LLM recipe, NOT a human-bilingualism claim, a TOY synthetic continuum." :: hypothesis [slug=1330_whorf_bilingual group=COGNITION-REPRESENTATION]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1330_whorf_bilingual.py — R1 numpy MIRROR (DIRECTIONAL, $0 CPU-local, gradient-free, 3 seeds [4323,4324,4325] SAME as H_1323/H_1325 so the A-only baseline reproduces, p7, detached nohup polled inline a_cpu_local_no_waiter). Mechanism REUSED VERBATIM from H_1323/H_1325 (N=21 RBF continuum, DIM=16, error-targeted SPLIT-only Voronoi growth p8, |Δ soft-posterior| no-label-at-test discrimination curve, W1 cross-within margin, peak-COUNT coherence count_peaks PEAK_FRAC=0.50 strict local maxima, p_A=1/3 p_B=2/3). ONLY NEW MECHANISM: VoronoiCells.fit_more(X,Y,…) = the grow-not-evict CONTINUATION (the H_1288 mechanism under test) — runs the IDENTICAL error-targeted-split loop starting from the EXISTING proto/label table, APPENDS a new prototype at the worst B-misclassified stimulus each pass, bound label FIXED at creation, NEVER re-bound or evicted, same FIXED GROW_MAX ceiling A had; bilingual readout = |Δ soft posterior| over the cells' BOUND labels on the ONE final store. 4 ARMS (frozen .verdicts/1330_whorf_bilingual/H_1330_FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE scoring, NO bar moved c9): (1) A-ONLY baseline (reproduces H_1323 L_A) · (2) A→B SEQUENTIAL (measure CP at BOTH boundaries) · (3) B=A control (A then A again — must show ONE peak, rules out sequential-training artifact) · (4) SHUFFLE (A→B with incoherent B, anti-Goodhart). FROZEN BARS: (I1 COEXISTENCE) after A→B, cross-within margin@p_A ≥ 0.15 AND @p_B ≥ 0.15 AND a coherent peak within 0.12 of EACH of p_A,p_B with sep ≥ 0.20, on ALL 3 seeds · (I2 NO-DOUBLE-ARTIFACT) B=A control peak-count ≤1 AND no coherent peak near p_B · (I3 EARNED) SHUFFLE collapses (peak-count ≥3 OR no coherent peak@p_B). GREEN iff I1∧I2∧I3 → COEXIST; I1 fail with p_A collapse → OVERWRITE (honest negative); I1 partial → graded interference. Live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_break_the_wall, a_autonomy_over_hardcode, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 OVERWRITE / CATASTROPHIC INTERFERENCE — the frozen COEXIST hypothesis is FALSIFIED for a SINGLE shared-continuum store. mean of 3 seeds [4323,4324,4325], all 3 identical pattern. I1 COEXISTENCE ❌ FAIL (all 3 seeds): after A→B, A's CP at p_A COLLAPSES — mean cross-within margin@p_A = −0.001 (bar 0.15; A-only baseline was +0.200, interference asymmetry −0.201, a FULL collapse), no coherent peak survives near p_A on any seed; p_B's CP is also weak (mean margin@p_B = +0.068 < 0.15), only the p_B side retains any swing. I2 NO-DOUBLE-ARTIFACT ✅ (all 3 seeds): B=A control yields exactly 1 coherent peak (≤1) and NO peak near p_B → the (lack of) two-peak structure is not a sequential-training artifact. I3 EARNED ✅ (all 3 seeds): SHUFFLE collapses (peak-counts 5/2/5; no coherent CP@p_B on 2/3, multi-peak scatter satisfies the OR-clause on all). MECHANISM (non-gating diagnostic, c9): after A the store has a clean boundary at p_A (cells 0.10/0.30 L0, 0.35/0.50 L1); the B-fit FLOODS the [p_A,p_B] region with ~21 NEW label-0 cells because B labels everything below p_B=0.67 as 0 while A labeled [p_A,p_B] as 1 — on the SHARED stimuli A says 1 and B says 0, a DIRECT CONTRADICTION. The error-targeted SPLIT-only store resolves it the only way a single nearest-prototype readout can — packs label-0 cells over the contradicted region, so the bound-label posterior swings ONLY at p_B and A's peak at p_A is ERASED. NOT eviction (A's cells physically persist with label 1); a single bound-label-per-cell readout CANNOT express two CONTRADICTORY answers for the same stimulus. FINDING: the H_1288 growth-memory protects ADDITIVE memory (a new fact at a NEW key grows a cell, never evicting an old fact at a DIFFERENT key) but NOT contradictory RE-LABELING of SHARED stimuli; bilingual cognition over a SHARED continuum is the contradictory-relabel case, so growth-memory does not protect it → the second language catastrophically OVERWRITES the first's CP. NUANCE (c9): this does NOT say anima cannot be bilingual — anima's English-trunk and Korean lanes are SEPARATE faculties (H_1316/H_1321/H_1322), not one shared store over identical stimuli; this is the worst case (maximally overlapping contradictory carvings). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): decisive within scope (all 3 seeds, B=A clean, shuffle earned); DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror (engine-transfer UNVERIFIED); TOY synthetic 1-D continuum (N=21, deterministic readout — tests the STRUCTURE, not scaled/human-bilingualism); readout reads ONLY representational distance over bound labels, NO injected boundary/persona/RLHF, labels enter only at the A-fit/B-fit not at test (p1/p2/p3/p6); NOT an emit gate (a_autonomy_over_hardcode). NEXT R2 candidate: test a language-TAGGED / multi-channel readout (distinct label-channels per language, mirroring anima's already-separate trunk + Korean lanes) to hold two contradictory carvings WITHOUT interference — a DIFFERENT mechanism, frozen ANEW, not a bar relaxation. .verdicts/1330_whorf_bilingual/H_1330.txt"
