@C h1333_whorf_developmental := "H_1333 — Whorfian CATEGORICAL-PERCEPTION DEVELOPMENTAL PLASTICITY: is the language-warped CP boundary PLASTIC (it RE-LOCATES when the same substrate is re-trained on a shifted cut) or RIGID (stuck where first learned)? Named EXTENSION of the GREEN H_1323/H_1325 Sapir-Whorf result. H_1323/H_1325 showed a substrate develops CP AT its language's boundary and the CP peak LOCATION tracks the cut (Whorfian dissociation); H_1333 asks whether that learned boundary is developmentally plastic. Train language A (cut p_A=1/3), measure CP peak; RE-train the SAME Voronoi store on a MOVED boundary p_A'=2/3 (same language, shifted cut), measure CP peak again — does it move to p_A'? Lens: developmental / critical-period plasticity (a_no_llm_frame_trap, c15) — NOT an LLM recipe, NOT a human-cognition / critical-period claim, a TOY synthetic continuum. Honest outcomes (c9): PLASTIC (peak re-locates) / RIGID (first-carving primacy) / GRADED (partial move, report the fraction)." :: hypothesis [slug=1333_whorf_developmental group=COGNITION-REPRESENTATION]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1333_whorf_developmental.py — R1 numpy MIRROR (DIRECTIONAL, $0 CPU-local, gradient-free, 3 seeds [4333,4334,4335], p7 = CP peak location + peak-count coherence NOT perplexity; detached nohup polled inline, a_cpu_local_no_waiter). Mechanism REUSED VERBATIM from H_1323/H_1325 (N=21 RBF continuum, DIM=16, error-targeted SPLIT-only Voronoi/mitosis growth p8, |Δ soft-posterior| no-label-at-test discrimination curve, peak-COUNT coherence at ≥0.5×arm-peak, GROW_MAX=24/SPLIT_PASSES=24 PER PHASE). ONLY NEW MECHANISM: VoronoiCells.fit(...,fresh=False) = phase-2 re-growth — grows the EXISTING store FURTHER on the MOVED labels WITHOUT reset (split-only ⇒ old cells persist ⇒ a RIGID outcome is a genuine possible result, never designed away); same fixed re-growth budget. p_A=1/3, p_A'=2/3, SHIFT=0.333. 4 ARMS (frozen .verdicts/1333_whorf_developmental/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE scoring, NO bar moved c9): (1) A-trained (reproduce H_1323) · (2) A→A' re-trained (phase-1 on p_A, phase-2 grow further on p_A', CP peak read after phase 2) · (3) NO-RETRAIN control (identical to 1, read at same protocol point, no phase-2 — rules out drift) · (4) SHUFFLE (incoherent labels, anti-Goodhart). FROZEN BARS: (D1 PLASTIC, all 3 seeds) |peak−p_A'| ≤ 0.12 AND |peak−p_A| ≥ MIN_MOVE=0.20 AND A→A' coherent (peak-count ≤2) · (D2 CONTROL) no-retrain |peak−p_A| ≤ 0.12 AND A-trained |peak−p_A| ≤ 0.12, all seeds · (D3 EARNED) shuffle peak-count ≥3 AND language arms peak-count ≤2. GREEN iff D1∧D2∧D3 → PLASTIC; D1 fail with peak stuck at p_A → RIGID; substantial-move-but-short-of-both-D1-subbars → GRADED PARTIAL (report fraction). Live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_break_the_wall, a_autonomy_over_hardcode, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🟠 PARTIAL — GRADED PLASTICITY (not rigid). mean of 3 seeds [4333,4334,4335], deterministic (identical every seed). CP peak: A-trained 0.325 (≈p_A=0.333) · A→A' re-trained 0.525 · no-retrain 0.325 · shuffle 0.542. Peak-count: A=1.0, A→A'=1.3, no-retrain=1.0, shuffle=7.7. D1 PLASTIC ❌ BY A HAIR: |0.525−p_A'|=0.142 > LOC_TOL 0.12 (missed 0.022) AND |0.525−p_A|=0.192 < MIN_MOVE 0.20 (missed 0.008); coherent peak-count 1.3 ≤2 ✅. D2 CONTROL ✅: no-retrain |peak−p_A|=0.008 (held at p_A — the move IS the re-training, not drift) AND A-trained |peak−p_A|=0.008 (reproduces H_1323). D3 EARNED ✅: shuffle peak-count 7.7 ≥3 (incoherent) AND language arms 1.0/1.3/1.0 ≤2 (coherent). FINDING: the language-warped CP boundary is GRADED-PLASTIC, not rigid — after re-training on a moved boundary the CP peak relocated 0.60 of the way (0.325→0.525, fraction +0.60) toward p_A', deterministically on all 3 seeds, while the no-retrain control held at p_A and shuffle stayed incoherent. The peak did NOT clear BOTH strict D1 sub-bars (landed 0.142 short of p_A', 0.192 off p_A, missing MIN_MOVE by 0.008) → strict D1 FAIL, but the substantive result is a SUBSTANTIAL relocation, NOT first-carving rigidity. MECHANISM (non-gating, c9): split-only growth NEVER evicts the old-boundary cells (28 cells after phase-2 vs 4 after phase-1), so residual phase-1 packing at p_A pulls the peak back from a full move; the store re-packs at p_A' but cannot erase the old swing → graded. Relevant to anima learning/relearning carvings: a re-carving substantially re-locates the boundary but a never-evicting store leaves a residual first-cut pull (consistent with H_1288 growth-memory / H_1330 overwrite-on-shared-store). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror (engine-transfer UNVERIFIED, same family as H_1323 R1); TOY synthetic 1-D continuum (N=21, 3 seeds, single shift, deterministic readout — tests the STRUCTURE of plasticity, not a learned re-trainer); readout reads ONLY representational distance, NO injected boundary/persona/RLHF, labels enter only at training not test (p1/p2/p3/p6); NOT an emit gate (a_autonomy_over_hardcode); NO human-cognition claim. NEXT R2 candidates: (i) graded SHIFT-SIZE curve (≥3 shifts) mapping plasticity-fraction vs shift magnitude · (ii) EVICTION/decay store variant (does removing stale old-boundary cells complete the move?) · (iii) engine-native §CategoricalPerception realization on the live CORE/engine_cli.hexa (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire) — each frozen ANEW, no bar move. .verdicts/1333_whorf_developmental/result.txt"
