@C h1338_whorf_cp_eviction := "H_1338 — Whorfian CP relocation residual: is the H_1333 GRADED-plastic ~60% move (peak 0.325→0.525, NOT fully to p_A'=0.667) caused by the split-only store's NEVER-EVICTED first-boundary cells, or by a BUDGET/GEOMETRY limit? The LOAD-BEARING follow-on to H_1333 (🟠 GRADED PLASTICITY). H_1333 DIAGNOSED (only hypothesized) its residual pull as the never-evicted phase-1 cells (28 cells after phase-2 vs 4 after phase-1) voting at the old cut. DECISIVE test: add an EVICTION store that removes stale-conflicting cells during the A→A' re-training; if it COMPLETES the move (→~100%), the residual IS the never-evict growth-memory property (a clean dual to H_1288 growth-memory = protect-old-memory); if the move STAYS partial even WITH eviction, the limit is budget/geometry, NOT never-evict. Lens: c15 developmental plasticity + memory-protection-vs-overwrite (a_no_llm_frame_trap) — NOT an LLM recipe, NOT a human-cognition claim, a TOY synthetic continuum." :: hypothesis [slug=1338_whorf_cp_eviction group=COGNITION-REPRESENTATION]
