  verdict = "🧱 RE-DIAGNOSIS — eviction does NOT complete the move; the H_1333 residual pull is BUDGET/GEOMETRY, NOT never-evict. mean of 3 seeds [4333,4334,4335], deterministic (identical every seed). CP peak: A-trained 0.325 · NEVER-EVICT A→A' 0.525 (frac +0.60, reproduces H_1333) · EVICTION A→A' 0.525 (frac +0.60, IDENTICAL) · no-retrain (both stores) 0.325 · shuffle 0.542. Peak-count: A=1.0, never-evict=1.3, eviction=2.0, no-retrain=1.0, shuffle=7.7. cell budget (seed, p1, never-evict-p2, eviction-p2): (4333,4,28,3)(4334,4,28,3)(4335,4,28,3) — the eviction store DID fire hard (28→3 cells, the stale phase-1 packing genuinely removed) yet the CP peak landed at the EXACT same 0.525. V1 COMPLETES ❌: |0.525−p_A'|=0.142 > 0.12 (reaches-new FAIL) AND eviction frac 0.60 < 0.85 (full-move FAIL); coherent peak-count 2.0 ≤2 ✅. V2 CONTRAST ✅: never-evict frac 0.60 ∈ [0.40,0.75] (reproduces H_1333 in-run, so the comparison is NOT a confound) AND |0.525−p_A'|=0.142 > 0.12 (did not complete). V3 EARNED ✅: no-retrain both |peak−p_A|=0.008 (held p_A — move is the re-training, not eviction-drift) AND shuffle peak-count 7.7 ≥3 (incoherent). FINDING (load-bearing answer): the H_1333 residual is NOT the never-evict growth-memory property — it is a BUDGET/GEOMETRY limit. Removing the stale old-boundary cells (28→3) did NOT complete the move; the CP peak stayed at the EXACT same 0.525, frac +0.60, as the never-evict store in the SAME run. The 3 surviving p_A'-aligned cells geometrically place the boundary at ~0.525 not 0.667 — under this RBF geometry + fixed per-phase split budget the discrimination peak cannot be packed all the way to p_A' regardless of whether stale cells linger. So the dual intuition (never-evict ⇒ partial; evict ⇒ full, dual to H_1288) is FALSIFIED for this store: the partial move is a representational/budget-resolution ceiling at the new cut, not old cells voting it back. A non-obvious re-diagnosis (the stale cells exist and were removed but were NOT the cause). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror (engine-transfer UNVERIFIED, same family as H_1333 R1); TOY synthetic 1-D continuum (N=21, 3 seeds, single shift, deterministic readout, HARD eviction — soft decay untested); NO injected boundary/persona/RLHF, labels at training not test (p1/p2/p3/p6); NOT an emit gate (a_autonomy_over_hardcode); NO human-cognition claim. NO bar moved (c9/p7). NEXT R2 (each frozen ANEW): (i) budget / RBF-resolution sweep at the new cut (does raising split budget OR grid density let the peak reach p_A'? = confirms budget/geometry, maps the ceiling) · (ii) graded SHIFT-SIZE curve (≥3 shifts — does the partial fraction track shift magnitude=geometry or stay constant=memory?) · (iii) soft DECAY (down-weight not hard-remove) · (iv) engine-native realization on the live CORE/engine_cli.hexa immune/Voronoi lane (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire). .verdicts/1338_whorf_cp_eviction/result.txt"
