@C h1341_whorf_cp_shift_ladder := "H_1341 — Whorfian CP plasticity SHIFT-SIZE LADDER: does the partial relocation fraction TRACK shift magnitude (=geometry/budget signature) or stay CONSTANT across shift sizes (=memory signature)? The H_1333 load-bearing follow-on (a_scale_honest_scope ladder, ≥3 rungs). H_1333 (🟠 GRADED) showed a re-trained CP boundary relocates ~60% for a SINGLE shift (peak 0.325→0.525); H_1338 (🧱) re-diagnosed that residual as budget/geometry (NOT never-evict) but only at the LARGE shift. H_1341 maps the move-fraction vs SHIFT curve across 3 magnitudes (fixed anchor p_A=1/3; SMALL p_A'=0.467 shift 0.133 / MID 0.600 shift 0.267 / LARGE 0.667 shift 0.333 = the H_1333/H_1338 anchor). Lens: c15 developmental/critical-period plasticity (a_no_llm_frame_trap) — NOT an LLM recipe, NOT a human-cognition claim, a TOY synthetic continuum. CHARACTERIZATION ladder — ALL outcomes valid (c9), report the curve verbatim, NO GREEN/RED to manufacture." :: hypothesis [slug=1341_whorf_cp_shift_ladder group=COGNITION-REPRESENTATION]
