my_over_hardcode, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "📈 CHARACTERIZATION LADDER COMPLETE — the plasticity move-fraction TRACKS shift magnitude ⇒ GEOMETRY/BUDGET-LIMITED (NOT memory). mean of 3 seeds [4333,4334,4335], deterministic (identical every seed). CURVE (mean frac): SMALL (shift 0.133) +1.496 · MID (shift 0.267) +0.750 · LARGE (shift 0.333) +0.599 — monotone-DECREASING in shift, frac range (max−min) = 0.897 ≥ TRACK_TOL 0.15. SMOKING GUN: the ABSOLUTE post-retrain peak is 0.525 at EVERY rung (range 0.000) — the re-trained boundary always lands at the SAME absolute position regardless of how far it was asked to move; the fraction therefore mechanically tracks shift (small move 0.133 → 0.525 OVERSHOOTS the 0.467 target → frac>1; large move 0.333 → 0.525 falls short → frac 0.60). L1 ✅ (curve mapped 3 rungs × 3 seeds). L2 EARNED ✅ (no-retrain held p_A |Δ|=0.008 EVERY rung; shuffle incoherent peak-count 7.7≥3 every rung; lang arms coherent ≤2 every rung — curve valid, unconfounded). L3 = GEOMETRY/BUDGET (range 0.897≥0.15 AND monotone-decreasing). FINDING: a MEMORY mechanism (fixed proportional pull-back) would hold the fraction CONSTANT and move the absolute peak WITH the target — the exact opposite of the measured fixed-absolute-landing 0.525. So the H_1333 ~60% partial is NOT a memory pull-back from the first carving — it is a fixed RBF-resolution + split-budget landing spot the boundary cannot pack past, IDENTICAL for every requested shift. This GENERALIZES the H_1338 budget/geometry finding (established at the LARGE rung only) across the whole shift range, and DECISIVELY REJECTS the constant-fraction MEMORY hypothesis the H_1333 card originally floated. The SMALL-rung overshoot (frac +1.496 > 1) is the cleanest possible evidence for the fixed-landing reading, reported straight (c9). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror (engine-transfer UNVERIFIED, same family as H_1333/H_1338 R1); TOY synthetic 1-D continuum (N=21, 3 seeds, 3 shift rungs, single fixed anchor, rightward shifts only, FIXED split budget, deterministic readout); the fixed landing 0.525 is specific to THIS RBF geometry (DIM=16) + THIS budget; NO injected boundary/persona/RLHF, labels at training not test (p1/p2/p3/p6); NOT an emit gate (a_autonomy_over_hardcode); NO human-cognition claim. NO bar moved (c9/p7). NEXT R2 (each frozen ANEW): (i) budget/RBF-resolution sweep — does the fixed landing move toward p_A' with more cells/finer basis? (separates budget from intrinsic resolution) · (ii) leftward + asymmetric shifts — is 0.525 a continuum-center attractor or a fixed-landing? · (iii) engine-native realization on the live CORE/engine_cli.hexa §CategoricalPerception lane (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire). .verdicts/1341_whorf_cp_shift_ladder/result.txt"
