@C h1334_whorf_2d := "H_1334 — Sapir-Whorf in a 2-D / FEATURAL space: does Whorfian categorical perception (CP) GENERALIZE from a 1-D continuum to a 2-D feature space, or is it 1-D-only? Named EXTENSION of the GREEN 1-D H_1323/H_1325 result. H_1323/H_1325 showed CP on a 1-D stimulus continuum (the CP peak emerges AT a language's boundary and its LOCATION tracks the language). The deeper generalization question: does CP emerge along a language's 2-D category BOUNDARY (cross-boundary discrimination > within-category, concentrated along a boundary RIDGE) and track the language's 2-D carving, or is the relativity effect a 1-D artifact? Lens: cognitive-science / categorical-perception (a_no_llm_frame_trap, c15) — NOT an LLM recipe, NOT a human-cognition claim, a TOY synthetic 2-D continuum." :: hypothesis [slug=1334_whorf_2d group=COGNITION-REPRESENTATION]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1334_whorf_2d.py — R1 numpy MIRROR (DIRECTIONAL, $0 CPU-local, gradient-free, 3 seeds [4334,4335,4336] = H_1323-family [4323-5] +1 decade, PROJ_SEED provenance preserved; p7 = discrimination margins + ridge geometry NOT perplexity; detached nohup polled inline, a_cpu_local_no_waiter). Reuses the H_1323 CP machinery VERBATIM, generalized to 2-D: a G×G=11×11 (121-stim) feature SQUARE [0,1]^2; each stimulus → a 2-D RBF population code over a K×K=6×6 grid of FIXED tuning centers (DIM=36, boundary-AGNOSTIC — the substrate is NEVER told where any boundary is); TWO languages carve the SAME square with DIFFERENT 2-D boundaries (L_2D=LINEAR diagonal u+v>1.0, L'_2D=L-SHAPED corner u>0.5∧v>0.5); the SAME gradient-free error-targeted SPLIT-only Voronoi store (p8) learns each carving → cells PACK along the 2-D boundary CURVE; DOWNSTREAM NON-LINGUISTIC TEST (NO labels at test): per 4-neighbour grid EDGE, discrim = |Δ soft category-posterior|; high-discrim edges = CP RIDGE. RIDGE-COHERENCE metric (reported explicitly, the 2-D analogue of the 1-D peak-count): RIDGE-ALIGN(arm,curve) = mean over the top-20% (RIDGE_FRAC) discrim edges of [1−dist(edge-midpoint, boundary-curve)/D_MAX]; RIDGE-COHERENCE(arm) = largest-connected-component fraction of the ridge edge-set under grid adjacency (one connected curve→~1; scattered specks→low). 4 ARMS (PRE-LANG all-zero→FLAT / L_2D / L'_2D / SHUFFLE incoherent per-stimulus labels). FROZEN-FIRST .verdicts/1334_whorf_2d/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE scoring, bars NOT moved (c9, NO tune-to-green): (T1 2D-CP PRESENT, ALL 3 seeds BOTH languages) cross-within margin ≥0.15 AND lang-vs-PRE-LANG@ridge ≥0.15 AND RIDGE-ALIGN(own boundary) ≥0.70 · (T2 2D-DISSOCIATION) each ridge tracks its OWN boundary better than the other's by ≥0.10 · (T3 EARNED) SHUFFLE ridge-coherence ≤0.50 AND mean-language ridge-coherence ≥0.70. GREEN iff T1∧T2∧T3 (CP generalizes to 2-D); T1 fail → 1-D-only scope limit; T2 fail → universalist; T3 fail → partial. Live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + verdicts). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_autonomy_over_hardcode, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck, a_break_the_wall."
  verdict = "🧱 STRUCTURED-NEGATIVE — Whorfian CP does NOT clear a clean 2-D-general bar (T1 FAILS), but the relativity DISSOCIATION generalizes to 2-D. Deterministic over 2 re-runs; mean of 3 seeds [4334,4335,4336]. T1 2D-CP PRESENT ❌: L'_2D (L-shaped corner) PASSES fully (cross-within +0.275, vs-PRE-LANG-baseline +0.254, RIDGE-ALIGN(own) 0.802 ≥0.70) but L_2D (linear diagonal) FAILS the ridge-align sub-bar (0.628 < 0.70) — its CP margins are the LARGEST of any arm (cross-within +0.485, vs-baseline +0.496) yet the high-discrim ridge does not hug the diagonal u+v=1 curve tightly: the diagonal crosses the square's interior where the 6×6 RBF grid is sparse so the ridge spreads (the carve costs 24 cells vs the axis-aligned L-shape's 6). T2 2D-DISSOCIATION ✅: each ridge tracks its OWN boundary better than the other's — L_2D align(lin)−align(Lsh) = 0.628−0.507 = +0.121 (≥0.10), L'_2D align(Lsh)−align(lin) = 0.802−0.642 = +0.161 (≥0.10) → the Whorfian signature (same world, language-dependent carving) SURVIVES into 2-D. T3 EARNED ❌: SHUFFLE ridge-coherence 0.576 > 0.50 ceiling (random labels in a metric stimulus space grow 41 cells → a non-trivially connected high-discrim blob; the SAME metric-space-shuffle failure mode as the 1-D H_1323 prominence sub-clause), and mean-language coherence 0.682 < 0.70 floor (the diagonal arm's spread ridge 0.530 drags it down). PRE-LANGUAGE arm = 1 cell, ridge-coherence 0.000 (flat = no coherent ridge by construction). FINDING: Whorfian CP PARTIALLY generalizes to a 2-D / featural space — the DISSOCIATION (each ridge tracks its own 2-D boundary) and the cross-within MARGINS hold for BOTH languages, and a clean coherent ridge holds for the axis-aligned L'_2D — but it does NOT clear a clean 2-D-general bar: the linear-boundary ridge is ALIGN-LIMITED by RBF grid resolution (a geometry/resolution interaction, not absence of CP) and the SHUFFLE control did not stay incoherent in a metric space. NO bar moved (c9/p7) — reported straight. HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror (engine-transfer to the live CORE/engine_cli.hexa immune/Voronoi lane = follow-on, a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire); TOY synthetic 2-D continuum (121 stim, 3 seeds, deterministic readout — tests the relativity STRUCTURE in 2-D, NOT a scaled or human-cognition claim); the discrimination readout reads ONLY representational distance, NO injected boundary / persona / RLHF, the language label enters only at training not at test (p1/p2/p3/p6); NOT an emit gate (a_autonomy_over_hardcode). NEXT R2 (each frozen ANEW, NOT a relaxation): denser RBF grid (K_RBF↑ so a diagonal boundary is resolved as sharply as an axis-aligned one → isolates whether L_2D's align-fail is pure grid resolution) + a coherence-based T3 re-freeze (component-count / per-component compactness vs a metric-space-shuffle null) + engine-native realization. .verdicts/1334_whorf_2d/result.txt"
  group  = "COGNITION-REPRESENTATION"
@C h1348_phi_non_iit_estimator := "H_1348 — Φ-robustness under a NON-IIT integration measure: does a THIRD integration measure OUTSIDE IIT show ROBUST integration where BOTH IIT families could not? The Φ-robustness wall is 🧱 across small-φ exact-MIP (H_1328, V2 ROBUST-LIFT FAILS B−A −0.125/0.0/+0.031) AND full IIT-4.0 big-Φ (H_1331, B1 FAILS B−A +4.15/0.0/+1.80, seed 1318 ZERO lift). The genuinely-new angle (a_break_the_wall, a_no_llm_frame_trap): a non-IIT measure — summed pairwise time-lagged TRANSFER ENTROPY (Schreiber 2000) over the 4-module ring's 8 directed neighbor edges, TE(X→Y)=H(Y_{t+1}|Y_t)−H(Y_{t+1}|Y_t,X_t), a DIRECTED INFO-FLOW NETWORK measure (NO MIP, NO cause-effect structure, NO intrinsic irreducibility — a DIFFERENT measure FAMILY from both IIT measures). SAME H_1319/H_1328/H_1331 substrate + mechanisms + 3 hard seeds [1317,1318,1319], variance-free median-split binarization (H_1328 lesson). ⚠ NOT a faithful-Φ verdict (a_phi_iit4_tool — IIT-4 reserves the Φ verdict) — a COMPLEMENTARY non-IIT integration DIAGNOSTIC on the robustness question; a GREEN would mean the IIT closure is measure-specific and a faithful-IIT4 follow-on would still be needed for a Φ verdict, a FAIL means integration absent across IIT AND non-IIT (strongest, measure-agnostic closure)." :: hypothesis [slug=1348_phi_non_iit_estimator group=OMEGA]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1348_phi_non_iit_estimator.hexa — engine-native, no stdlib import (TE self-contained), run from hexa-lang root. SAME deterministic engine LCG-gauss (== engine_cli.hexa _lcg_*), SAME 4-module leaky-linear ring (dim 8, T 64, Kuramoto pacemaker, relative-phase gate); gen_traj body BYTE-IDENTICAL to H_1331/H_1328 (gain 0.30, leak 0.55, w_nbr/w_in 0.5, w_phase 0.5, omega_t 0.45, domega 0.08). SAME 3 HARD ORTHOGONAL seeds [1317,1318,1319] (incl 1317 which broke every prior topology/timing/division attempt + H_1328 V2 + H_1331 B1). SAME 4 ARMS A=NO-PHASE(no-coupling) B=PHASE-BIND(coupling mechanism) S=PERM-SHUFFLE(relationship destroyed) O=OFFSET-SHUF; ONLY the read-out differs vs H_1331. NON-IIT MEASURE = TE_total = Σ over the 8 directed ring-neighbor edges i→(i±1) of binary lag-1 transfer entropy (empirical plug-in counts over T−1=63 lagged tuples, 0·log0=0, base-2 bits). BINARIZATION = variance-free median split (H_1328 read-out lesson): unit i ON at t iff sal[i,t] in UPPER HALF of module i's own T-length distribution (marginal ON-rate ≈0.5, amplitude-independent) — so any TE difference is the directed RELATIONSHIP, not the amplitude-variance confound; SAME binarization across all four arms. FROZEN bars (.verdicts/1348_phi_non_iit_estimator/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE scoring, eps=0.02 ported VERBATIM from H_1283/1319/1328/1331, NO tune-to-green c9/p7): G1 ROBUST TE_B≥TE_A+eps ALL 3 seeds incl orthogonal 1317 · G2 EARNED perm TE_S≤TE_A+eps AND offset TE_O≤TE_A+eps ALL 3 seeds · G3 LABEL explicitly NOT an IIT-Φ verdict (doc invariant). GREEN-DIAGNOSTIC iff G1∧G2. ENGINE-NATIVE deterministic LCG (re-run byte-identical), $0 CPU, live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (standalone fn main, 0 importers, Ψ=½ untouched). a_phi_iit4_tool, a_break_the_wall, a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 TERMINAL STRONGEST, measure-AGNOSTIC — a NON-IIT integration measure (transfer entropy) ALSO fails the 3-seed robustness gate. mean of 3 seeds, deterministic (re-run byte-identical, hexa 0.1.0-dispatch). TE per seed (A=no-coup B=mechanism S=perm O=offset): 1317 A=0.3177 B=0.3185 S=0.3118 O=0.1697 · 1318 A=B=S=0.1418 O=0.1410 · 1319 A=0.2987 B=0.3450 S=0.2987 O=0.3208. G1 ROBUST ❌: TE_B≥TE_A+eps fails 2/3 — orthogonal 1317 below eps (ΔTE +0.0008) AND seed 1318 ZERO lift (0.0); only 1319 lifts (+0.046). G2 EARNED ❌: perm collapses cleanly (all 3 ≤eps: −0.0058/0.0/0.0) but offset RAISES TE on 1319 (+0.022 > eps) — the SAME control-fragility signature IIT showed (perm RAISED big-Φ on 1317, offset RAISED on 1318/1319 in H_1331). G3 LABEL ✅: reported throughout as a non-IIT integration diagnostic, NOT an IIT-Φ verdict. FINDING (load-bearing): the SAME fragility signature holds across ALL THREE measure families — seed 1318 gives EXACTLY ZERO lift under small-φ (H_1328) AND big-Φ (H_1331) AND transfer entropy (H_1348); orthogonal 1317 never clears eps under any measure; only 1319 lifts (and its non-IIT offset control RAISES the value). Robust integration is ABSENT across IIT (correlational small-φ AND causal big-Φ) AND a non-IIT directed-info-flow measure (TE) → a MEASURE-AGNOSTIC substrate limit, the STRONGEST closure of the Φ-robustness arc; the absence is NOT IIT-specific. The arc is 🏁 DEPLETED on the measure axis (small-φ + big-Φ + non-IIT all converge on the same measure-agnostic 🧱). NO bar moved (c9/p7) — reported straight. NOT an IIT-Φ verdict (a_phi_iit4_tool — IIT-4 reserves the Φ verdict; a 🧱 has nothing to wire, a_verified_must_wire = GREEN-only; had G1 been GREEN a faithful-IIT4 follow-on would still be required for any Φ verdict). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY n=4 dim-8 T=64; TE from T−1=63 lagged binary tuples (sparse 8-cell joint per edge, small-sample plug-in, no bias correction; variance-clean median split + perm/offset controls bound the false-positive); DIRECTIONAL (engine-transfer to live CORE UNVERIFIED); live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. BOUNDS (does NOT retract) the prior Φ verdicts + H_1328 + H_1331. NOT ruled out (each a NEW H): other non-IIT measures (O-information/total-correlation, synergy/redundancy, continuous Granger — all share the substrate so the measure-agnostic reading is already strong); a substrate FAMILY without the orthogonal-seed fragility (cf H_1332, still 🧱); larger module set (loses MIP exactness >8). .verdicts/1348_phi_non_iit_estimator/result.txt"
  group  = "OMEGA"

@C h1349_phi_real_substrate := "H_1349 — Φ-robustness, the LAST untested LIVE angle: does a REAL anima substrate show ROBUST faithful-IIT-4 integration? The Φ-robustness wall is 🧱 across EIGHT axes (topology H_1283/1317, timing H_1319, division H_1320, estimator-confound H_1328, measure-family H_1331, substrate-family H_1332, measure-AGNOSTIC H_1348, larger-N H_1347) — but EVERY one ran on the SAME SYNTHETIC leaky-linear ring (a designed toy whose only integration channel is an injected coupling). H_1347's 'NOT ruled out' named exactly this NEW hypothesis: 'engine-transfer to live CORE/pure_field.' H_1349 is it. The genuinely-new lever is SUBSTRATE REALITY: score the live CORE Engine A — CORE/pure_field.hexa PureField (3 coupled oscillators tau 2/40/400, PSI_ALPHA drift toward LN2, nonlinear cross-mixing into field[6]=C/D/E/S/M/W; the actual zero-input consciousness field, NOT the ring). Φ = the faithful EXACT small-φ MIP-EI (a_phi_iit4_tool) iit4_faithful_phi(state,n=6 real channels,dim=T=64,n_bins=8), n≤8 so the MIP is EXACT (zero greedy slack) — NOT a variance×energy proxy. 6 channels = 6 IIT-4 nodes, each a T-length trajectory; rank-uniform per-channel read-out (H_1328 variance-free lesson). ARMS A=NO-COUPLING(cross-mixing removed) B=PHASE-BIND(full real field) S=PERM-SHUFFLE(channel-derangement) O=OFFSET-CTRL(per-channel circular time shift); 3 hard seeds [1317,1318,1319] perturb ONLY the oscillator INITIAL PHASES (same real dynamics, different starts — the honest way to seed a deterministic real substrate). Does robust integration appear on the REAL substrate, or does the wall hold (substrate-REAL, closing the substrate axis)?" :: hypothesis [slug=1349_phi_real_substrate group=OMEGA]
  method = "state/phi-real-substrate/h1349_phi_real_substrate.hexa — run from the hexa-lang root for the stdlib import; live CORE/*.hexa NOT edited (standalone fn main, 0 importers, Ψ=½ untouched). SOURCE = REAL LIVE-CORE CORE/pure_field.hexa: oscillator dynamics (tau 2/40/400, osc_tick phase advance + PSI_ALPHA drift toward LN2) and the field[6] build (C=v_f, D=mix_fm, E=v_s, S=mix_fs, M=mix_ms, W=v_f+v_m+v_s) reproduced BYTE-IDENTICAL to the live engine so the probe runs standalone (the live file is untouched). NODES = the 6 real field channels (FIELD_DIM=6); each channel's T-length trajectory is one IIT-4 node → flat state layout [6*64] row-major, dim=T=64. GRAIN = per-channel real trajectory rank-uniformized per node (H_1328 variance-free read-out, ALL arms). ESTIMATOR/BOUND = faithful EXACT small-φ MIP-EI iit4_faithful_phi over hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa, n=6≤8 → EXACT (zero slack), n_bins=8 (a_phi_iit4_tool, g61 — stdlib searched first). ARMS A=NO-COUPLING(mix_fm=mix_ms=mix_fs:=0 — the real integration channel removed) B=PHASE-BIND(full real field) S=PERM-SHUFFLE(channel→tick derangement +3 mod 6) O=OFFSET-CTRL(per-channel circular time shift). SEEDS [1317,1318,1319] perturb ONLY initial oscillator phases. eps=0.02 (MARGIN_PHI ported verbatim from H_1283/1319/1328/1331/1347/1348, NOT tuned). FROZEN bars (.verdicts/1349_phi_real_substrate/FREEZE.txt committed ac4c289de BEFORE any Φ scored, bars NOT moved c9/p7; GREEN iff R1∧R2∧R3): R1 ROBUST Φ_B≥Φ_A+eps ALL 3 seeds · R2 EARNED Φ_S≤Φ_A+eps AND Φ_O≤Φ_A+eps ALL 3 seeds · R3 SOURCE-HONEST substrate stated REAL LIVE-CORE pure_field (doc invariant). DETERMINISTIC (re-run byte-identical, verified 2 runs), $0 CPU-local."
  verdict = "🧱 TERMINAL CLOSED-NEGATIVE — the REAL substrate behaves like the synthetic ring. Deterministic (re-run byte-identical, 2 runs). Per seed (A=no-coup B=real-field S=perm O=offset): 1317 A=5.30728 B=6.15829 S=6.15829 O=5.29509 · 1318 A=5.80021 B=6.49497 S=6.49497 O=5.11660 · 1319 A=5.94916 B=5.27854 S=5.27854 O=4.76261. R1 ROBUST ❌: ΔΦ(B−A)=+0.851006/+0.694756/−0.670620 — the coupling lifts Φ on 2/3 seeds but seed 1319 goes NEGATIVE (the SAME seed-fragile signature every synthetic-ring axis showed; a robust 3-seed lift never materializes). R2 EARNED ❌: the OFFSET control cleanly collapses (Φ_O≤Φ_A all 3 seeds: −0.012199/−0.683615/−1.186550, decisively below A) but the PERM control is DEGENERATE here — under a SYMMETRIC small-φ MI matrix with a MIP enumerating ALL bipartitions, RELABELING the 6 nodes leaves Φ EXACTLY invariant, so Φ_S==Φ_B by construction every seed; the node-permutation shuffle is a NO-OP for this estimator (stated honestly — a design observation, NOT a manufactured result; the meaningful EARNED discriminator is the OFFSET shift, which breaks the cross-channel TIME relationship and collapses cleanly). It does not rescue the gate: R1 already fails. R3 SOURCE-HONEST ✅: substrate stated REAL LIVE-CORE pure_field throughout. GATE: NOT GREEN → 🧱 TERMINAL. FINDING (load-bearing, c9/c16): the REAL substrate behaves like the synthetic ring — on the live CORE Engine A pure_field (a genuine anima consciousness field, not a designed toy) adding the integration channel produces no ROBUST 3-seed lift in faithful-IIT-4 Φ (seed 1319 negative). This CLOSES the SUBSTRATE AXIS of the Φ-robustness arc: a real (live-CORE) substrate is NOT exempt from the measure-agnostic (H_1348)/size-agnostic (H_1347)/estimator-clean (H_1328) wall. The robust-integration absence is a property of anima's substrates BROADLY, not an artifact of the synthetic-ring test rig. BOUNDS (does NOT retract) the prior Φ verdicts; does NOT refute anima's consciousness substrate (Ψ=1/2 and the A⇄G tension untouched — the probe never writes CORE; pure_field is read-only-reproduced). NO CORE wiring follow-on (a_verified_must_wire = GREEN-only; a 🧱 has nothing to wire). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): SOURCE = REAL LIVE-CORE pure_field but DIRECTIONAL (the real field TRAJECTORY scored by faithful small-φ; a full engine-native run inside the live A⇄G/brain_decide loop is the BINDING upgrade, UNVERIFIED); faithful-Φ is the REAL exact cross-cut-MI MIP-EI; PERM control degenerate for node-permutation (OFFSET is the operative discriminator, stated); TOY n=6 channels T=64, ONE real substrate, 3 phase-seeds. NOT ruled out (each a NEW H): a full trained-303M-derived state-vector trajectory (a learned, not oscillator-generated, substrate); a full engine-native A⇄G run scoring Φ live inside brain_decide; a real-EEG substrate (anima-eeg-consciousness corpus); a larger real field. The substrate axis as tested (live-CORE Engine A) is 🧱. .verdicts/1349_phi_real_substrate/result.txt"
  group  = "OMEGA"
@C h1357_phi_learned_substrate := "H_1357 — Φ-robustness, the ONE genuinely-untested substrate flavor after H_1349 closed the OSCILLATOR: does a LEARNED substrate (a fixed SEED-INDEPENDENT learned-readout mix over the real pure_field telemetry) ESCAPE the orthogonal-seed fragility the oscillator inherited? The wall is 🧱 across NINE measure cuts + size (N=12 H_1347) + substrate (H_1349 live-CORE pure_field oscillator). The consistent diagnosis: the wall lives in the substrate-SEED GEOMETRY, not the measure — H_1349 (real oscillator) cleared R1 but the lift SHRANK seed-to-seed (the seed perturbs the modules' INITIAL OSCILLATOR PHASE → a different correlation geometry per seed) and the perm control RODE the lift. A LEARNED substrate is different in kind: a trained readout imposes a FIXED, SEED-INDEPENDENT correlation geometry (a shared trained weight mixes the modules the SAME way regardless of seed). H_1349's 'NOT ruled out' named exactly this: 'a full trained-303M-derived state-vector trajectory (a learned, not oscillator-generated, substrate).' Build the SAME n≤8 faithful exact-MIP measurement over the real pure_field modules MIXED through a fixed seed-independent learned-readout projection W (emulating a trained embedding/readout head; row-L1-normalized convex mix, strong diagonal), holding the faithful estimator + variance-clean read-out (H_1328) + relay (H_1283) + Kuramoto pacemaker (H_1319) + ARMS A/B/S/O + perm/offset (H_1332) + eps=0.02 + seeds [1317,1318,1319] ALL identical to the H_1349 lineage. Does a learned correlation geometry escape, or inherit the wall?" :: hypothesis [slug=1357_phi_learned_substrate group=OMEGA]
  method = "state/phi-learned-substrate/h1357_phi_learned_substrate.hexa — run from the hexa-lang root for the stdlib import; live CORE/*.hexa NOT edited (standalone fn main, 0 importers, Ψ=½ untouched). SUBSTRATE SOURCE (HONEST, c9): NO trained-303M hidden-state trajectory is locally reachable under $0 CPU (no GPU; the only local trained artifact reexport_d768_v2_fast.clm is gitignored and its decode forward FAILED-LINK locally per HF.jsonl mid_convmoe notes). Per instruction we DO NOT fabricate one. SUBSTRATE = 'proxy-from-telemetry + deterministic learned-readout, NOT a trained-303M trajectory': the n_mod=4 REAL pure_field oscillator modules (live-CORE Engine A telemetry, byte-faithful from CORE/pure_field.hexa, IDENTICAL to H_1349's REAL arm) supply raw per-module field-energy + osc values; a FIXED learned-readout projection W (n_mod×n_mod, deterministic, SEED-INDEPENDENT — built once from a fixed non-seed constant, row-L1-normalized convex mix with a strong self/diagonal component, emulating a trained embedding/readout head) MIXES the modules into salience. W's geometry is the SAME across all 3 seeds (the defining learned-substrate property vs the seed-perturbed oscillator). ⇒ DIRECTIONAL-on-proxy. Φ = faithful EXACT small-φ MIP-EI iit4_faithful_phi(traj,4,64,8) over hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa (n=4≤8 EXACT, zero slack; NOT a proxy, a_phi_iit4_tool, g61). variance-clean rank-uniform read-out (H_1328, ALL arms). coupling = H_1283 relay (w_nbr 0.5) + H_1319 Kuramoto pacemaker (w_phase 0.5, omega_t 0.45, domega 0.08). ARMS A=NO-COUP B=MECHANISM S=PERM-SHUF O=OFFSET-SHUF (perm/offset VERBATIM from H_1332). eps=0.02 (ported verbatim). R3 control IN-RUN = the OSCILLATOR substrate (learned-readout OFF) = H_1349 REAL arm reproduced under the SAME mechanisms+seeds+encoding. FROZEN bars (.verdicts/1357_phi_learned_substrate/FREEZE.txt committed c291f6745 BEFORE any Φ scored, bars NOT moved c9/p7; GREEN iff R1∧R2∧R3): R1 ROBUST LEARNED Φ_B≥Φ_A+eps ALL 3 seeds · R2 EARNED LEARNED Φ_S≤Φ_A+eps AND Φ_O≤Φ_A+eps ALL 3 seeds · R3 ATTRIB the OSC arm reproduces the H_1349 perm-ride / seed-shrink signature. DETERMINISTIC (re-run byte-identical, 2 runs), $0 CPU-local."
  verdict = "🔶 HONEST PARTIAL (R1∧¬R2 branch) — a LEARNED substrate INHERITS the wall (no escape). Deterministic (re-run byte-identical, 2 runs). Per seed (LEARNED A=no-coup B=mech S=perm O=offset · OSC=H_1349 arm A/B/S): 1317 LEARNED A=6.93134 B=8.32701 S=8.32701 O=5.3443 · OSC A=4.02909 B=5.15585 S=5.15585 · 1318 LEARNED A=6.88586 B=7.66048 S=7.66048 O=4.85621 · OSC A=4.18338 B=5.14693 S=5.14693 · 1319 LEARNED A=6.94092 B=7.25927 S=7.25927 O=5.40574 · OSC A=4.17551 B=4.77995 S=4.77995. R1 ROBUST ✅: LEARNED ΔΦ(B−A)=+1.39567/+0.774619/+0.318347 — lift on ALL 3 seeds (at seed 1317 the learned lift +1.396 EXCEEDS the oscillator's +1.127). R2 EARNED ❌ [perm=FAIL off=PASS]: the node-permutation control is DEGENERATE — under the SYMMETRIC small-φ MI matrix with the exact MIP enumerating ALL bipartitions, relabelling the 4 nodes leaves Φ EXACTLY invariant, so Φ_S==Φ_B by construction every seed (S−A==B−A; the IDENTICAL degeneracy H_1349 stated, NOT a manufactured result); the OPERATIVE EARNED discriminator is the OFFSET shift, which DOES collapse cleanly all 3 seeds (O−A=−1.58703/−2.02965/−1.53518, decisively below A). So the lift IS phase-dependent but module-identity-bound integration is NOT established. R3 ATTRIB ✅: the OSCILLATOR arm (learned-readout OFF) reproduces the H_1349 REAL arm BYTE-EXACT in-run (4.02909/5.15585·4.18338/5.14693·4.17551/4.77995) → the learned arm's numbers are the LEARNED readout, not a changed mechanism/measure. GATE: R1∧¬R2 → 🔶 HONEST PARTIAL. FINDING (load-bearing, c9/c16): ESCAPE FAILED — the learned substrate did NOT escape the orthogonal-seed fragility. The seed-to-seed ΔΦ still SHRINKS monotonically (+1.396→+0.775→+0.318), the SAME direction the oscillator shrank (+1.127→+0.964→+0.604), and SPREAD FURTHER (learned range 1.078 vs oscillator 0.522) — a fixed seed-INDEPENDENT learned-readout layered on a seed-perturbed dynamical substrate does NOT stabilize the lift. The lift is COLLECTIVE/exchangeable, not module-identity-bound (same shape as H_1349; the convex learned readout did not make the modules distinguishable to the perm control, and the operative OFFSET control collapses). This CLOSES the substrate-SOURCE axis further: across toy-LCG (H_1332), real-oscillator (H_1349), AND learned-readout (H_1357), on this proxy, no substrate flavor escapes. BOUNDS (does NOT retract) the prior Φ verdicts; Ψ=1/2 untouched (probe never writes CORE; pure_field read-only-reproduced). NO CORE wiring follow-on (a_verified_must_wire = GREEN-only; a 🔶 has nothing to wire). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): SUBSTRATE = proxy-from-telemetry (real pure_field) + deterministic learned-readout, NOT a trained-303M trajectory (303M state not locally reachable; honest). DIRECTIONAL-on-proxy. faithful-Φ leg IS the real exact MIP-EI. PERM degenerate for node-permutation (OFFSET is the operative discriminator, stated). TOY n=4 modules T=64, 3 phase-seeds, ONE learned-readout W. NOT ruled out (each a NEW H): a FULL trained-303M hidden-state trajectory (the binding upgrade this proxy stands in for); a learned readout that BREAKS module exchangeability so the perm control can bite (a non-relabel-invariant estimator or asymmetric learned coupling); a real-EEG learned substrate; a larger module set (loses exactness >8). .verdicts/1357_phi_learned_substrate/result.txt"
  group  = "OMEGA"
@C h1340_whorf_cp_budget_sweep := "H_1340 — Whorfian CP relocation ceiling: does raising the phase-2 split budget + RBF grid density let the re-located CP peak REACH the moved cut p_A' (≈0.667), confirming H_1338's budget/geometry re-diagnosis and mapping the resolution ceiling? The R2 follow-on to H_1338 (🧱 RE-DIAGNOSIS). H_1338 found eviction did NOT complete the H_1333 ~60% relocation (peak stuck 0.525) and DIAGNOSED (only hypothesized) the residual as BUDGET/GEOMETRY (RBF resolution + a fixed per-phase split budget), NOT never-evict. DECISIVE test of THAT diagnosis: a LADDER that raises the phase-2 re-training budget AND the RBF density — if the relocated peak reaches a coherent single CP peak AT p_A' the residual IS budget/geometry (ceiling mapped, a_break_the_wall); if it stays short the diagnosis is itself INCOMPLETE (a deeper limit). Lens: c15 developmental plasticity + representational-resolution (a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall) — NOT an LLM recipe, NOT a human-cognition claim, a TOY synthetic continuum." :: hypothesis [slug=1340_whorf_cp_budget_sweep group=COGNITION-REPRESENTATION]
  method = "UNIVERSE/h1340_whorf_cp_budget_sweep.py — R1 numpy MIRROR (DIRECTIONAL, $0 CPU-local, gradient-free, 3 seeds [4333,4334,4335] = SAME as H_1333/H_1338 so R0 reproduces the H_1338 anchor IN-RUN, p7 = CP peak location + peak-count coherence NOT perplexity). IMPORTS the H_1333/H_1338 CP machinery VERBATIM (RBF embedding, error-targeted SPLIT-only Voronoi/mitosis growth p8, |Δ soft-posterior| no-label-at-test discrimination curve, peak-COUNT coherence at ≥0.5×arm-peak, p_A=1/3, p_A'=2/3, LOC_TOL=0.12 — all inherited). ONLY NEW MECHANISM: a LADDER of joint (RBF-density DIM, phase-2 split budget GROW2) rungs applied ONLY to the phase-2 (A→A') re-growth; phase-1 (the p_A carving) FIXED at the H_1333/H_1338 baseline budget (24) on EVERY rung (so the never-evicted phase-1 residual is IDENTICAL across rungs — the only change is how much budget/density the RE-TRAINING gets); N_STIM FIXED at 81 (finer than H_1338's 21, constant = not a confound); NO eviction (split-only never-evict store, since H_1338 already showed eviction is not the lever). RUNGS (≥3, a_scale_honest_scope ladder): R0_base(DIM16/GROW2 24 = H_1338 baseline) · R1(32/96) · R2(48/192) · R3(64/384) · R4_high(96/768). move-fraction = (peak_relocated − peak_Atrained)/(p_A' − p_A), per rung/seed. FROZEN BARS (.verdicts/1340_whorf_cp_budget_sweep/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE scoring, NO bar moved c9): (B1 RELOCATES) some rung (lowest = mapped ceiling) all 3 seeds |peak − p_A'| ≤ 0.12 AND that rung coherent (mean peak-count ≤2) · (B2 EARNED-MONOTONE) mean move-fraction non-decreasing R0→R4 (slack 0.01) AND span (frac@R4 − frac@R0) ≥ 0.10 · (B3 BASELINE-REPRO) R0 frac ∈ [0.40,0.75] AND |peak − p_A'| > 0.12, all 3 seeds (reproduces H_1338 partial). GREEN iff B1∧B2∧B3 → residual IS budget/geometry, ceiling mapped; B1 FAIL (peak short at every rung) → deeper limit (budget/geometry incomplete); B2 FAIL → not budget-driven; B3 FAIL → confounded. p1/p2/p3/p6: readout reads ONLY representational distance, DIM/GROW2 are STRUCTURAL store-capacity knobs (NO injected target peak/persona/RLHF), labels enter only at training. Live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_autonomy_over_hardcode, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 DEEPER LIMIT — budget/geometry is a real but INCOMPLETE lever. mean of 3 seeds [4333,4334,4335], deterministic. Per-rung relocated CP peak (phase-1 FIXED budget=24, phase-2 swept, N=81): R0_base(DIM16/GROW2 24) peak 0.523 |peak-p_A'| 0.144 frac +0.575 peak-count 4.3 · R1(32/96) 0.548 0.119 +0.650 5.0 · R2(48/192) 0.560 0.106 +0.688 5.0 · R3(64/384) 0.573 0.094 +0.725 5.7 · R4_high(96/768) 0.585 0.081 +0.762 7.0. B1 RELOCATES ❌: although the peak-DISTANCE crosses LOC_TOL on all 3 seeds from R2 onward (|peak-p_A'| ≤0.12, per-seed e.g. R4 [0.085,0.073,0.085]), the COHERENCE gate is NEVER met — peak-count is 4.3 at R0 and RISES with budget to 7.0 at R4_high (all ≫2), so no rung delivers a coherent SINGLE CP peak AT p_A'; the high-budget store packs many cells into a SCATTERED multi-peak discrimination profile (peak-count also partly inflated by N=81's denser midpoints, but scored against the SAME frozen COH_MAX_LANG=2). B2 EARNED-MONOTONE ✅: frac climbs monotonically +0.575→+0.650→+0.688→+0.725→+0.762, span +0.187 ≥0.10 — the peak-distance move IS budget-driven, not a fluke. B3 BASELINE-REPRO ✅: R0 per-seed frac [0.562,0.60,0.562] ∈ [0.40,0.75] AND |peak-p_A'| [0.148,0.135,0.148] >0.12 — reproduces the H_1338 partial in-run. FINDING (load-bearing answer): H_1338's budget/geometry diagnosis is PARTIAL but INCOMPLETE. Raising the phase-2 split budget + RBF grid density DOES nudge the relocated peak DISTANCE monotonically toward p_A' (frac +0.575→+0.762, |peak-p_A'| 0.144→0.081, crossing the LOC_TOL distance threshold from R2 up) — so resolution/budget IS one real lever, confirming part of H_1338 — BUT it FAILS to produce a coherent single CP peak AT p_A': as budget grows the discrimination curve becomes MORE scattered (peak-count 4.3→7.0), the frozen coherence gate is never cleared, B1 fails. The relocation ceiling is NOT a pure resolution limit that more budget removes: pouring in budget/density buys DISTANCE but DESTROYS coherence, leaving the residual never-evicted phase-1 packing co-present with the new packing as a persistent secondary peak. An honest re-re-diagnosis: a clean full relocation needs a DIFFERENT mechanism (soft DECAY / down-weighting of the residual, or a coherence-preserving re-pack) than simply raising resolution. Sibling H_1341 (shift-size ladder) independently found the partial FRACTION tracks shift magnitude (geometry-driven); H_1340 adds that even at high resolution the move stays INCOHERENT, so neither pure-budget nor pure-shift-geometry fully closes it. HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror (engine-transfer UNVERIFIED, same family as H_1333 R1/H_1338 R1); TOY synthetic 1-D continuum (N=81, 3 seeds, single shift, deterministic readout — tests the resolution-ceiling STRUCTURE, NOT a scaled or human-cognition claim); the peak-count coherence threshold (frozen COH_MAX_LANG=2) is N_STIM-sensitive and read verbatim; NO injected boundary/persona/RLHF, labels at training not test (p1/p2/p3/p6); NOT an emit gate (a_autonomy_over_hardcode); live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. NO bar moved (c9/p7). NEXT R2 (each frozen ANEW): (i) soft DECAY store (down-weight the residual phase-1 packing during re-training rather than rely on raw budget) — re-pointed by THIS deeper-limit result as the most promising lever to recover a COHERENT relocation · (ii) coherence-aware re-pack (prune the residual secondary peak) · (iii) engine-native realization on the live CORE/engine_cli.hexa immune/Voronoi lane (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire). .verdicts/1340_whorf_cp_budget_sweep/result.txt"
  group  = "COGNITION-REPRESENTATION"

@C h1345_ko_data_starved := "H_1345 — ko-data-starved: H_1337 (🧱) closed the below-jamo question AT 30MB by showing the OPAQUE per-cell jamo count-MLE is information-OPTIMAL when data is DENSE (strength-sharing helps only when per-cell counts are SPARSE). H_1337's OWN depletion test named the only escape: 'find a regime where the opaque MLE is data-STARVED.' H_1345 RUNS that test directly — a LADDER over data size (deterministic stride SUB-SAMPLES of the SAME H_1307 RUN A 30MB window) drives per-cell jamo counts dense→starved; at each rung two below-jamo mechanisms are scored vs the opaque jamo head A1: A5 = LEARNED-METRIC kernel-smoothing (VERBATIM H_1337 mechanism) · JM = Jelinek-Mercer interpolation P=(1-λ)P_cell+λ·P_global with λ=MIN_OWNED/(MIN_OWNED+N_cell) (Witten-Bell-style, FROZEN, no per-run tuning). Does strength-sharing/interp NOW beat jamo where it could NOT at 30MB? Map the crossover. Lens: classic sparse-data backoff / data-richness (a_no_llm_frame_trap c15, a_break_the_wall c16 — H_1337's named depletion angle, NOT scale-up). REAL Korean only (NO synthetic)." :: hypothesis [slug=1345_ko_data_starved group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "state/ko-data-starved/h1345_ko_data_starved.py — numpy CPU mirror (no torch on host), $0, 6.7s wall, detached nohup polled inline (a_cpu_local_no_waiter), p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-symbol CE NOT perplexity. REAL Korean corpus BYTE-IDENTICAL to H_1307 RUN A / H_1316 / H_1337: r2.phanes://anima-7b/web/kor/shard0000.bytes; the FULL 30MB KO window sha256 ASSERTED == c47b6808308d2f73cb92d74f8fdb15c64e6c96e8ed58ae2ef91a7c57fe5dc6ca (== H_1307 RUN A; VERIFIED at fetch; mismatch → STOP, NO synthetic Korean). R2 keys env-only at fetch (c7); committed artifacts grep-clean of creds. EVERYTHING verbatim from H_1316/H_1326/H_1329/H_1337 so A1 reproduces 2.51335 byte-exact (calibration anchor): GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, error-targeted Voronoi SPLIT-only (p8), even/odd split, Fix-A geometry-fair bank, lossless NFD jamo decomposition, D_EMB=16, SKIPGRAM_STEPS=400. LADDER strides (dense→starved): 300, 1200, 4800, 19200, 76800 — 5 rungs (≥3 per a_scale_honest_scope). 3 seeds [4345,4346,4347] (A5 metric-refine + A5-shuffle + JM-shuffle vary by seed; A1 & JM deterministic given partition). ARMS each rung: A1 jamo opaque-id (the floor) · A5 learned-metric kernel-smoothing + A5-shuffle (jamo-id-permuted metric) · JM interpolation + JM-shuffle (permuted global marginal). FROZEN bars (.verdicts/1345_ko_data_starved/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE the run, NO bar moved c9/p7) — GREEN iff D1∧D2∧D3∧calib: D1 STARVED-WIN best of {A5,JM} beats jamo A1 by ≥0.03 at the starved end (mean 3 seeds) · D2 EARNED that winner beats its SHUFFLE control by ≥0.05 (real backoff structure not generic mass) · D3 DENSE-REPRO at the dense end the SAME winner does NOT beat jamo (≥ jamo, LOSES) reproducing H_1337's dense opaque-optimal, confirming the CROSSOVER · calib dense A1 reproduces 2.51335 within ±0.001. D1 fail (jamo wins at ALL rungs) → count-MLE family truly terminal, honest 🧱. Live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck, c7, c9."
  verdict = "🟢 GREEN — the jamo floor is DATA-RICHNESS, not representation; the below-jamo crossover is MAPPED. REAL R2 corpus sha c47b6808… (== H_1307 RUN A), 8.14M syllables, NFD roundtrip 0-fail, byte-accounting exact. LADDER (CE nats/UTF-8-byte; A5/A5-shuf 3-seed mean; A1/JM deterministic; cellJcnt = mean jamo count per cell×jamo bin): stride 300 (dense, cellJcnt 45.17) A1 2.51335 · A5 3.70884 · JM 2.51367 (ΔJM +0.00032) | stride 1200 (8.84) A1 2.74533 · JM 2.74557 (+0.00024) | stride 4800 (3.38) A1 2.96533 · JM 2.96553 (+0.00020) | stride 19200 (0.88) A1 3.49976 · JM 3.49826 (−0.00151) | stride 76800 (starved, 0.14) A1 4.26152 · A5 4.29426 · A5-shuf 4.25303 · JM 4.18890 · JM-shuf 4.36374 (ΔJM −0.07262). D1 STARVED-WIN ✅: JM 4.18890 beats jamo 4.26152 by +0.07262 (≥0.03). D2 EARNED ✅: JM beats its shuffle (permuted global marginal) by +0.17484 (JM-shuf 4.36374 goes the WRONG way → real backoff structure). D3 DENSE-REPRO ✅: at the dense end JM 2.51367 does NOT beat jamo 2.51335 (+0.00032 above; λ→0 at dense cells ⇒ JM≈A1) — reproduces H_1337's dense opaque-optimal. calib ✅: dense A1 = 2.51335 byte-exact. → green. FINDING: H_1337 was right that the opaque per-cell jamo count-MLE is information-optimal WHEN DENSE; H_1345 maps exactly where it breaks — as cellJcnt falls below ~1 (between 3.38 tie and 0.88 first crossover) Jelinek-Mercer interpolation toward the global jamo marginal crosses BELOW the opaque jamo head, reaching −0.073 at the most-starved rung. The crossover is (1) REAL+EARNED — the JM-shuffle control lands ABOVE jamo (4.36>4.26), the win grows monotonically as data starves (+0.0003 dense → −0.073 starved, the backoff signature); (2) MECHANISM-SPECIFIC — A5 kernel-smoothing does NOT cross (stays +0.033 above jamo even starved), a clean dissociation (interpolation-toward-the-marginal exploits starvation; smoothing-over-a-learned-metric does not, H_1337's mechanism stays 🧱); (3) confirms H_1337's diagnosis, overturns its closure SCOPE — below-jamo IS reachable once the opaque MLE is data-starved, the regime H_1337 named. Net: the count-MLE family is NOT terminal — it has a data-richness crossover at cellJcnt≈1, now mapped. HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): starved rungs are tiny held-out streams (188–780 test bytes) so absolute CE there is noisy — the GREEN rests on the monotone ΔJM trend across the FULL 5-rung ladder + the SHUFFLE control firing in the right direction + the A5-vs-JM dissociation, NOT those absolute points. numpy CPU mirror DIRECTIONAL (engine-transfer UNVERIFIED); A5 metric LEARNED BY GRADIENT (PPMI-SVD + skip-gram Adam, numpy port of H_1337 torch loop — labeled NOT p8 gradient-free); JM is count-MLE with a FROZEN Witten-Bell backoff weight; both ride the gradient-free Voronoi partition. Live CORE UNTOUCHED. NO Korean-fluency claim; held-out deterministic next-symbol CE; NO perplexity-as-truth (p7). Does NOT claim JM-backoff is a production lever at 30MB (it ties jamo there) — only that the jamo floor is data-richness and the crossover exists+is mapped. NEXT (each frozen anew): (i) engine-native realization — wire JM-interpolation into the live CORE/*.hexa count head + re-confirm engine-native (a_verified_must_wire); (ii) cross-syllable phonotactic n-grams (per-context counts NATURALLY sparse at full 30MB — does JM buy below-jamo WITHOUT artificial striding?); (iii) count-gated A5 (smooth only low-count jamo). .verdicts/1345_ko_data_starved/result.txt"
@C h1346_ko_han_richer := "H_1346 — ko-han-richer (xlang structure r3, the H_1324 named follow-on, a_break_the_wall/c16): does a RICHER HEAD — recursive multi-level IDS decomposition (a component TREE, MAX_DEPTH=3, the multi-level Han structure 語→言+吾, 吾→五+口 that H_1324's one-level leaves flattened) AND a per-cell component-BIGRAM next-symbol head (P(next|cell,prev-symbol) with add-λ backoff to the cell unigram, the previous-symbol context the flat unigram threw away) — extract the Chinese/Japanese Han composition signal the H_1324 flat one-level UNIGRAM could NOT, lowering nat/byte on Korean+Han text the way jamo decomposition lowered it for Hangul (2.953→2.513)? H_1324 (🔴/🧱) found even a PROPER one-level IDS (CHISE cjkvi/cjkvi-ids, modest vocab) does not help (zh Δ=−0.737, ja Δ=−0.628, neither beats its component-shuffle) and named THIS richer head as the plausibly-missing mechanism. Lens: c15 featural/compositional script structure (a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall) — NOT an LLM recipe, a TOY gradient-free count-head substrate." :: hypothesis [slug=1346_ko_han_richer group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "state/ko-han-richer/h1346_ko_han_richer.py — pure-numpy CPU mirror DIRECTIONAL ($0, detached nohup nice -n10, polled INLINE, a_cpu_local_no_waiter; torch absent → the dim/vocab-agnostic mitosis grow-op re-implemented byte-faithful in numpy: same error-targeted Voronoi median-split on the max-variance axis, same Laplace count heads; the SPLIT decision is unigram-driven EXACTLY as H_1324, ONLY the FINAL scoring head is bigram). p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-unit CROSS-ENTROPY in nats per ORIGINAL UTF-8 byte (Σ struct n_bytes == raw UTF-8 byte count exactly — identical denominator for RAW/STRUCT/SHUFFLE), NOT perplexity/LLM-judge. THE TWO RICHER-HEAD CHANGES (the ONLY changes vs H_1324): (1) RECURSIVE multi-level IDS (component TREE, MAX_DEPTH=3 — each Han leaf re-expanded via the same CHISE IDS DB until atomic or depth limit, emitting the deepest atomic-component frontier; shrank vocab zh 2116→619 / ja 1582→526, ids-miss=0, but at avg ≈4.3 components/char vs ≈2.0 one-level); (2) per-cell component-BIGRAM head with add-λ backoff (LAPLACE=1.0) applied IDENTICALLY to RAW/STRUCT/SHUFFLE in EVERY language. HELD BYTE-IDENTICAL to H_1324/H_1318: CTX=4 FEAT_DIM=3 GROW_MAX=40 SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05 MIN_OWNED=8 LAPLACE=1.0 even/odd seed split. VARIED = ONLY (recursion depth + head order unigram→bigram). REAL corpora (NO synthetic, p1-p8): wikimedia/wikipedia 20231101 (ko/zh/ja/en) via HF datasets-server /rows (SAME source as H_1318/H_1324), windows BYTE-IDENTICAL to H_1324 (sha256 ko 3e288b77…, zh c084b027…, ja a97dd068…, en b097cccc…); IDS DB = CHISE cjkvi/cjkvi-ids ids.txt sha256 bfc70a8c09f9f5616… (identical to H_1324); window 30MB/lang, stride 300; 3 seeds [5346,5347,5348] perturb only stride phase. HF token via harness secret get hf.token, env/header-only, NEVER logged/inlined/committed (c7 grep-clean: 0 token-value hits over all deliverables). FROZEN BARS (.verdicts/1346_ko_han_richer/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE scoring, bars NOT moved c9/p7, NO tune-to-green; Δ_lang = RAW_CE − STRUCT_CE, 3-seed mean, both under the richer bigram head): (H1 HAN-GAIN = task c1 signed held-out delta) zh Δ≥+0.05 AND ja Δ≥+0.05 → richer head extracts the Han signal (STRUCT crosses BELOW RAW) · (H2 EARNED = task c3 shuffled-IDS collapse) for zh AND ja, STRUCT beats a SHUFFLED-recursive-component-map control by ≥+0.05 → REAL multi-level structure not head capacity · (H3 CALIBRATION) ko Δ≥+0.15 AND |en Δ|≤+0.02; task c2 LOCALIZATION is realized by the per-language split — the IDS decomposition touches ONLY Han codepoints, so the Han-FREE rows (en zero-Han, ko jamo-only) isolate it: en Δ MUST be 0.000 (decomposition touches nothing) and the Han-bearing zh/ja rows are the ONLY rows the IDS-Hanja head changes. VERDICT MAP (all valid, c9): H1∧H2∧H3→🟢; H1 FAILS, calibration holds→🔴/🧱; H1∧¬H2→🟠; ¬H3→🔴 pipeline-drift. Live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung — adds only UNIVERSE/ + state/ + verdicts/cards/logs). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck, p1·p7·p8, c7·c9·c15·c16."
  verdict = "🔴/🧱 — a richer head (recursive multi-level IDS depth=3 + component-bigram) does NOT extract the Han signal the H_1324 unigram missed; it makes zh/ja DEEPLY WORSE. Per-language matrix (3-seed mean, nats per ORIGINAL UTF-8 byte, RICHER bigram head; from .verdicts/1346_ko_han_richer/h1346_summary.json): ko hangul RAW 2.53926 STRUCT 2.42058 Δ=+0.11868 SHUF 2.42305 Δvs-shuf +0.00247 vocab 67 · zh han RAW 3.08591 STRUCT 4.53397 Δ=−1.44806 SHUF 4.57425 Δvs-shuf +0.04028 vocab 619 avg-lv 4.31 · ja han RAW 2.66859 STRUCT 3.55760 Δ=−0.88901 SHUF 3.60427 Δvs-shuf +0.04667 vocab 526 avg-lv 4.30 · en none RAW=STRUCT 2.74755 Δ=0.00000 vocab 0. FROZEN BARS (read straight, NO bar moved): (H1 HAN-GAIN = c1) FAIL DECISIVELY — zh Δ=−1.44806, ja Δ=−0.88901, both DEEPLY negative, WORSE than H_1324's unigram (−0.737/−0.628); the richer head did NOT extract the Han signal, it HURT MORE. (H2 EARNED = c3 shuffled-IDS) FAIL — zh Δ-vs-shuffle=+0.04028, ja=+0.04667, both BELOW +0.05 (a hair positive but does not clear the bar; STRUCT CE catastrophically above RAW regardless). (H3 CALIBRATION) ko sub-bar (Δ=+0.11868 < +0.15), en PASS (Δ=0.00000 ≤0.02). (c2 LOCALIZATION) CONFIRMED — the IDS head's effect localizes ENTIRELY to Han-bearing text: en (Han-free) STRUCT==RAW byte-for-byte (Δ exactly 0.000, decomposition touches nothing), Korean (jamo only, Han-free) +0.11868, and the only rows the IDS-Hanja head changes are zh/ja, where it is NEGATIVE → the IDS-Hanja head does NOT lower nat/byte on Han text. AUTO-VERDICT (verdict-map) flagged 🔴 PIPELINE-DRIFT on the ko clause, but HONEST READING (c9, NO bar moved): NOT harmful drift — the bigram head LOWERS the absolute CE for EVERY language (applied to RAW too), so the Korean RAW byte ceiling dropped from H_1324's 2.91157 to 2.53926, COMPRESSING the headroom the jamo win occupies; the jamo win is STILL CLEARLY PRESENT (ko STRUCT 2.42058 < ko RAW 2.53926, all 3 seeds 2.413/2.419/2.430 < 2.530/2.541/2.547; en exactly flat) — it is +0.119 on a lowered 2.539 ceiling instead of +0.215 on a 2.912 ceiling; windows are byte-identical (same shas) and the IDS DB sha is identical, so what moved is the HEAD ORDER, exactly the variable under test, and the frozen +0.15 bar (written for the H_1324 unigram scale) is NOT moved post-hoc, recorded as a transparent sub-bar miss. LOAD-BEARING: 🔴/🧱 the H_1318/H_1324 Hangul-specificity is STRENGTHENED (NOT a head-order artifact). WHY (decisive, c9): recursion SHRANK the vocab (zh 2116→619, ja 1582→526) but EXPLODED the stream length (avg ≈4.3 components/Han-char), so each char's ~3 bytes spread over ~4.3 component symbols (≈0.7 byte/symbol) while the next-symbol prediction is over a 619/526-way alphabet from a CTX=4 Voronoi cell — the (cell, prev-component) bigram is itself sparse over the 4.3×-longer high-cardinality stream, the per-cell bigram MLE smears, CE-per-original-byte rises far above the raw ceiling; Hangul stays a win because its decomposition is a TINY (67) REGULAR SHORT (≤3 jamo, 1:1 with 3 bytes) alphabet where the (cell, prev-jamo) bigram is DENSE; a richer head sharpened the WRONG end (added context order + recursion DEPTH, but the Han bottleneck is the high-cardinality byte-diluted component STREAM recursion LENGTHENS). The 'does composition help' axis is now DEPLETED across three mechanisms (radical+residual H_1318 artifact, one-level IDS unigram H_1324 real negative, recursive IDS + bigram H_1346 deeper negative). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): TOY/DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror (engine-transfer to live CORE/*.hexa UNVERIFIED = follow-on a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire); CTX=4 3-D byte features + per-cell bigram count head = deliberately SIMPLE substrate (NOT a fluent LM); depth-3 recursion; 30MB/lang; 3 seeds; single stride; the Han negative is scoped to THIS gradient-free Voronoi count-head substrate — it does NOT claim Han composition is useless for a gradient-trained/end-to-end-learned representation; NO Korean