@C h1343_whorf_2d_r2 := "H_1343 — Sapir-Whorf / 2-D categorical perception (CP) re-measured as a boundary-curve-AGNOSTIC representational-metric WARP, R2 of H_1334 (🧱 ridge-ALIGN structured-negative). H_1334 scored CP by RIDGE-ALIGNMENT to a known boundary CURVE; that fails for a DIAGONAL boundary on a coarse RBF grid (align 0.628<0.70) — a grid-geometry artifact, not absence of CP (its discrim margins were the LARGEST arm). The prior H_1343 ridge attempt swept density to K_RBF=14 and the diagonal align STILL failed, confirming ridge-ALIGN is the wrong metric for a metric stimulus space. R2 re-specifies CP to the textbook boundary-curve-AGNOSTIC operationalization: the WARP of the learned representational metric (within-category COMPRESSION + between-category EXPANSION) vs a pre-language baseline, plus a label-permutation shuffle null (c2 EARNED) and a component-count control that shuffles WHICH feature component carries the boundary (c3 — warp lives in the trained 2-D metric, not raw variance). Lens: cognitive-science / categorical-perception (c15, a_no_llm_frame_trap) — NOT an LLM recipe, NOT a human-cognition claim, a TOY synthetic 2-D continuum." :: hypothesis [slug=1343_whorf_2d_r2 group=COGNITION-REPRESENTATION]
  method = "state/whorf-2d-r2/h1343_whorf_2d_r2.py — R1 numpy MIRROR (DIRECTIONAL, $0 CPU-local, gradient-free, 3 seeds [4334,4335,4336] = SAME family as H_1334, deterministic, p7 = a representational-warp ratio + label-permutation + component-count controls, NOT perplexity). REUSES the H_1334 RBF/Voronoi machinery VERBATIM (2-D RBF population code · error-targeted SPLIT-only mitosis/Voronoi growth p8 · softmin soft-posterior). 11x11=121 stimulus square; two languages carve the SAME square: L_DIAG=diagonal u+v>1.0, L_LSHAPE=L-corner u>0.5 & v>0.5. CP-WARP metric (boundary-curve-AGNOSTIC): learned category coordinate g=soft posterior P(cat=1) (NO hard label/boundary injected); over all 4-neighbour grid pairs partition WITHIN/BETWEEN by the store's OWN learned category; ratio = mean|Δg|_BETWEEN / mean|Δg|_WITHIN; CP-WARP = ratio_lang − ratio_base (baseline = boundary-AGNOSTIC smooth feature gradient, no cut). DENSITY LADDER K_RBF∈{6,9,12} (production=densest 12, DIM=144, frozen NOW before scoring). FROZEN BARS (.verdicts/1343_whorf_2d_r2/FREEZE.txt pre-registered BEFORE scoring, NO bar moved c9): (c1 PRESENCE) production density both languages EACH seed AND mean CP-WARP ≥ WARP_MIN=0.20 · (c2 EARNED-SHUFFLE) label-permutation null (N_SHUF=200/seed) mean ≤ CHANCE_TOL=0.05 AND each language ≥ null-q95 + SEP=0.10 · (c3 COMPONENT-COUNT) component-shuffled warp (N_COMP=50, partition tied to a random single feature component) ≤ COMP_MAX=0.05 both languages. GREEN iff c1∧c2∧c3; c1 FAIL→🧱 genuine 2-D limit; c2 FAIL→🟠; c3 FAIL→🟠. p1/p2/p3/p6: warp reads ONLY representational distance + the store's OWN learned category; NO injected boundary/persona/RLHF; labels enter only at training, never the warp readout. Live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_autonomy_over_hardcode, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🟠 PARTIAL — c1 PRESENCE ✅ but c2 EARNED-SHUFFLE ❌ (+ c3 partial ❌). mean of 3 seeds [4334,4335,4336], deterministic (re-run byte-identical). Density ladder CP-WARP(own boundary): K_RBF=6 diag +43.064 Lsh +31.838 · 9 +36.838 +34.839 · 12(prod) +41.665 +36.017. Production K_RBF=12 per-seed warp diag [45.013,44.312,35.670] Lsh [36.554,36.830,34.667]; baseline ratio r_base=1.00 all; ncells diag 23.7 Lsh 6.0. c1 PRESENCE ✅: both languages every seed AND mean ≥ 0.20 (diag mean +41.665, Lsh +36.017) — LOAD-BEARING: the DIAGONAL warps AS STRONGLY AS the axis-aligned L-shape, DIRECTLY REFUTING H_1334's read that the diagonal CP was grid-geometry-limited (under a boundary-AGNOSTIC metric the diagonal is NOT weaker). c2 EARNED-SHUFFLE ❌: label-permutation null mean +9.282 ≫ CHANCE_TOL 0.05 → FAIL; the SEP sub-clause PASSES (both languages +41.7/+36.0 ≫ null-q95+0.1=+14.0) but the absolute null-mean ceiling fails because the BETWEEN/WITHIN ratio is scale-UNBOUNDED (after training WITHIN |Δg|→0, so the ratio explodes ~45 and even RANDOM carvings compress within-category → null mean floats high). c3 COMPONENT-COUNT ❌: L_DIAG comp-warp +0.027 ≤0.05 PASS but L_LSHAPE +0.119 >0.05 FAIL (seed-4336 +0.236 driven, same unbounded-ratio variance). FINDING (load-bearing): the boundary-AGNOSTIC warp metric shows 2-D CP is strongly PRESENT for BOTH a diagonal AND an axis-aligned boundary and the diagonal is NOT geometry-limited (refutes H_1334's diagonal read), but the unbounded BETWEEN/WITHIN ratio is the SAME metric-space-blob failure mode H_1323 prominence / H_1334 LCC hit — so the anti-Goodhart label-shuffle/component controls do not cleanly close, leaving a 🟠 PARTIAL rather than a clean 2-D-general GREEN. HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck): DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror (engine-transfer to live CORE UNVERIFIED, same family as H_1334 R1); TOY synthetic 2-D continuum (121 stimuli, 3 seeds, single paradigm, deterministic readout — tests the relativity STRUCTURE in 2-D, NOT a scaled or human-cognition claim); NO injected boundary/persona/RLHF, labels at training not test (p1/p2/p3/p6); NOT an emit gate (a_autonomy_over_hardcode); live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. NO bar moved (c9/p7). NEXT R3 (each frozen ANEW): (i) BOUNDED warp metric — replace the unbounded ratio with a between-vs-within |Δg| Cohen's-d or separation-AUC (∈[0,1]) so the label-shuffle null collapses to chance (0.5) cleanly — re-pointed by THIS result as the most promising lever · (ii) strengthen the component-shuffle to remove the per-seed leak · (iii) engine-native realization on the live CORE/engine_cli.hexa immune/Voronoi lane (a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire). .verdicts/1343_whorf_2d_r2/result.txt"
