@C h1365_phi_asymmetric_r2 := "H_1365 — Φ-robustness R2 (phi-asymmetric-r2): does a NON-relabel-invariant (ASYMMETRIC) substrate make the permutation-null control ACTUALLY BITE (Φ_perm<Φ_B), and does a clean-R2 setup change the R1 robustness verdict or does the wall hold even when perm bites? The last structural gap in the Φ-robustness fragility diagnosis (parent H_1349/1353/1357, c16, a_break_the_wall, a_no_llm_frame_trap). In EVERY prior Φ lane the permutation-null control was DEGENERATE — under a SYMMETRIC-MI exact MIP faithful Φ is node-PERMUTATION-INVARIANT, so Φ_perm==Φ_B by construction and the perm control could not bite; only the OFFSET control discriminated. Reuse the H_1349/1319/1353 ring (4-module leaky-linear, dim 8, T 64, engine LCG-gauss == engine_cli.hexa _lcg_*, gain 0.30 leak 0.55 w_in 0.5, Kuramoto pacemaker, relative-phase gate) VERBATIM + ONE asymmetry change: DIRECTED+GRADED neighbour coupling W_FWD=0.70 (i+1) != W_BWD=0.30 (i-1) + per-module gain gradient g_i=0.70+0.20·i/(n-1). Φ = FAITHFUL IIT-4 ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool, exact MIP-EI via hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa; numpy never computes Φ). Frozen-first, seeds [1317,1318,1319], $0 CPU." :: hypothesis [slug=1365_phi_asymmetric_r2 group=OMEGA]
  method = "state/phi-asymmetric-r2/h1365_phi_asymmetric_r2.py — DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror (Φ leg IS real faithful exact MIP-EI via hexa iit4_faithful_phi(state,n=4,dim=T=64,n_bins=8); numpy ONLY emits per-module salience=state-energy traj, hexa computes Φ; NO proxy, p7). Substrate = H_1349/1319/1353 ring VERBATIM with the ONE asymmetry change (W_FWD=0.70≠W_BWD=0.30 directed + per-module gain gradient g_i∈[0.70,0.90]) that breaks node-relabel invariance: under a symmetric ring node relabel is a joint symmetry → Φ_perm==Φ_B (the prior degeneracy); asymmetric → permuting which module feeds which Φ-input slot changes the joint → perm-null is a REAL intervention. 4 ARMS: A=NO-COUPLING (w=0, flat gain, no carrier) · B=PHASE-BIND (asym coupling+carrier) · P=PERM-NULL (B's per-module traj re-bound module→slot by a fixed-point-free derangement, draw VERBATIM H_1348/1353) · O=OFFSET-CTRL (per-tick random phase offset). binarization = variance-free median split (H_1328, == H_1348/1353; hexa engine bins internally). FROZEN bars (.verdicts/1365_phi_asymmetric_r2/FREEZE.txt, pre-registered BEFORE scoring, eps=0.02 ported VERBATIM from H_1283/1319/1328/1331/1348/1353, NO tune-to-green c9/p7): R0 PERM-BITES Φ_P<Φ_B−eps on ≥2/3 seeds (Φ_B>0) — the precondition prior lanes LACKED · R1 ROBUST ΔΦ(B−A)≥eps EACH of 3 seeds · R2 EARNED Φ_P≤Φ_A+eps AND Φ_O≤Φ_A+eps all seeds. GREEN iff R0∧R1∧R2. KEY READ (pre-decided): R0 holds but R1 fails 2/3 → wall holds even with clean perm = strongest closure (fragility not a perm-degeneracy artifact); R0 fails → symmetric-MIP Φ structurally exchangeable / asymmetry does not move the faithful MIP = the diagnosis itself; R0∧R1∧R2 → clean-R2 recovers robust verdict. DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror (engine-transfer UNVERIFIED), $0 CPU, re-run byte-identical, frozen-first. live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. a_phi_iit4_tool · a_break_the_wall · a_no_llm_frame_trap · a_engine_native_learning · a_verified_must_wire · a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 DIAGNOSIS-CONFIRMED (R0 FAIL · R1 PASS · R2 FAIL) — perm-degeneracy is a property of the faithful symmetric-MIP ESTIMATOR, not merely the prior symmetric substrates (the last structural gap named). per-seed faithful-Φ: seed1317 Φ_A=+0.7502 Φ_B=+1.1073 Φ_P=+1.1073 Φ_O=+1.0932; seed1318 +0.8429/+1.3541/+1.1731/+0.7045; seed1319 +0.5837/+0.6863/+0.8820/+0.6057. R0 PERM-BITES FAIL [1/3 bite, 3/3 had Φ_B>0]: even with the asymmetric directed+graded coupling, Φ_P<Φ_B−eps holds ONLY on seed-1318 (Φ_B−Φ_P=+0.181); seed-1317 Φ_B−Φ_P=EXACTLY +0.0000 (still exchangeable), seed-1319 perm RAISES Φ by +0.196 (opposite direction). Reason: the faithful MIP searches all bipartitions and the median-split marginals are ≈uniform, so module→slot relabeling barely moves the system-irreducibility MIP value. R1 ROBUST PASS [3/3, True/True/True]: NOTABLY the asymmetric coupling ITSELF produced a robust lift ΔΦ(B−A)=+0.3570/+0.5112/+0.1026 — unlike every prior lane it does NOT zero-lift at seed-1318 (in fact +0.511 the LARGEST there). R2 EARNED FAIL (3/3): neither perm nor offset collapse to A — Φ_P stays +0.30..+0.36 above Φ_A (perm is NOT a clean control), offset collapses only on seed-1318 (−0.139) and reproduces on 1317 (+0.343)/1319 (+0.022) → B's lift is generic asymmetric structure, not a phase-binding RELATIONSHIP. FINDING (c9, load-bearing): the R1 PASS · R2 FAIL pair shows that WITHOUT a clean perm control, an R1 robust lift cannot be told apart from generic asymmetric structure — so R2 failing means R1 GREEN is untrustworthy (the wall's other face). The perm-degeneracy is estimator-level: the last structural gap in the fragility diagnosis is now named, not a substrate artifact. NO bar moved (c9/p7). re-run byte-identical (md5 86ed9712...). HONEST SCOPE: DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror, Φ leg = real faithful exact MIP-EI (numpy never computes Φ), engine-transfer UNVERIFIED; TOY n=4/T=64/3 seeds/median-split/single asymmetry setting; bounds (does NOT retract) H_1283/1317/1319/1320/1328/1331/1347/1348/1353/1357; live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. NEXT: asymmetric-marginal binarization (perm bites via marginals, but amplitude-confound risk H_1328) · directed-information/transfer-entropy MIP (H_1348 tried summed-TE, same fragility) · engine-native A⇄G realization. .verdicts/1365_phi_asymmetric_r2/result.txt"
  group  = "OMEGA"

@C h1370_hive_nonlinear_hub := "H_1370 — hive-nonlinear-hub: does a NON-LINEAR / GATED (tanh) connector cell escape the W=0 shared-input redundancy floor at faithful-IIT4 collective-Φ, where H_1356/1363's LINEAR hub failed? H_1363 closed the weak/decorrelated arc 🧱 REDUNDANCY_BOUND with a LOAD-BEARING diagnosis: the substrate is leaky-LINEAR, so ANY hub LINEARLY homogenizes the daughters -> faithful MIP reads them as MORE reducible -> Φ DROPS. That homogenization argument RESTS ON LINEARITY. H_1370 tests it head-on: a SATURATING tanh gate on the hub feedback (coupling=W_CONN*tanh(GATE_GAIN*hub)) bounds the pull so the hub NUDGES without dragging each daughter onto the shared hub state — the exact linear-homogenization mechanism the prior closure rests on. Does the gated hub lift the coupling-EARNED (non-redundant, W=0-floor-beating) Φ ROBUSTLY across 3 seeds, where the LINEAR hub could not? Φ = FAITHFUL IIT4 ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool, exact MIP-EI via hexa stdlib; numpy never computes Φ; O-info diagnostic is numpy-side, NEVER gates). Substrate = H_1356/H_1363 verbatim (W0_floor byte-identical, the ONLY difference between B_linear and B_nonlinear is the tanh gate). Biological saturating-neuron / role-differentiation lens (c15, a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall). Frozen-first (FREEZE before scoring, bars not moved, c9/p7), seeds [1317,1318,1319], $0 CPU." :: hypothesis [slug=1370_hive_nonlinear_hub group=OMEGA]
  method = "state/hive-nonlinear-hub/h1370_hive_nonlinear_hub.py — DIRECTIONAL numpy-mirror (Φ leg IS real exact MIP-EI via hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa iit4_faithful_phi(state,n=8,dim=T=64,n_bins=8); numpy ONLY emits per-unit salience=state-energy traj, hexa computes Φ; NO proxy, p7). Substrate = H_1356/H_1363/H_1320/H_1283 verbatim: leaky linear recurrent units LEAK=0.55 GAIN=0.30 W_IN=0.5 dim-8 T=64; N_TOT=8 (n<=8 exact MIP); daughters d0=units0..1 d1=units2..3, CONNECTOR hub=unit4, padding=units5..7; DIFF_EPS=0.15. PRE-REGISTERED NONLINEARITY (frozen): GATE=tanh, GATE_GAIN=2.0, W_CONN=0.6 (= H_1356 strong linear anchor; ONLY difference B_linear vs B_nonlinear is the gate). linear coupling=W_CONN*hub -> gated coupling=W_CONN*tanh(GATE_GAIN*hub) on both daughter feedback AND hub integration of daughters (element-wise on DIM-vector). ARMS: A_single, W0_floor (SHARED_DECOUPLED redundancy floor; byte-identical to H_1356/1363 12.4018/6.94639/12.2284), B_redundant (===W0_floor), B_linear (H_1356 STRONG LINEAR hub W_CONN=0.6, the known 🧱 anchor B_nonlinear must beat), B_nonlinear (tanh-gated hub W_CONN=0.6 GATE_GAIN=2.0, the new angle), SHUFFLE (B_nonlinear wiring, gated hub reads RANDOM pad sources = EARNED control). O-information per arm = NON-GATING diagnostic. FROZEN bars (.verdicts/1370_hive_nonlinear_hub/H_1370_FREEZE.txt, MARGIN=0.02): GREEN iff R1 (Phi(B_nonlinear)-Phi(W0_floor)>=0.02 forall seed) AND R2 (Phi(B_nonlinear)-Phi(B_linear)>=0.02 forall seed, the H_1356/1363-escape) AND R3 (Phi(SHUFFLE)<=Phi(W0_floor)+0.02 forall seed). live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_phi_iit4_tool, a_engine_native_learning(transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 REDUNDANCY_BOUND_NONLINEAR (R1 0/3 · R2 0/3 · R3 3/3) — the tanh-gated (non-linear) hub ALSO fails to beat the floor, and does WORSE than the linear hub on all 3 seeds. W0_floor = H_1356/H_1363 byte-identical (12.4018/6.94639/12.2284 — setup-integrity OK). per-arm faithful-IIT4 Φ (exact MIP-EI, n=8): seed1317 A_single 1.70 / W0_floor 12.40 / B_linear 7.58 / B_nonlinear 6.30 / SHUFFLE 7.04; seed1318 1.41 / 6.95 / 4.44 / 4.37 / 4.51; seed1319 2.02 / 12.23 / 7.23 / 6.90 / 7.35. R1 FAIL (0/3): lift = Φ(B_nonlinear)−Φ(floor) = −6.10 / −2.58 / −5.33 — the gated hub greatly LOWERS Φ below the floor on every seed. R2 FAIL (0/3): gap = Φ(B_nonlinear)−Φ(B_linear) = −1.28 / −0.077 / −0.335 — the tanh gate does WORSE than the linear hub on every seed; H_1356/1363-escape REFUTED. R3 PASS (3/3): Φ(SHUFFLE)≤Φ(floor)+0.02 (7.04/4.51/7.35 ≤ 12.42/6.97/12.25) → the gated wiring is REAL (not generic gate variance). O-info diagnostic (NON-GATING): every arm O≫0 (strongly redundancy-dominated); B_nonlinear O slightly HIGHER than linear (7.05/5.11/7.53 vs 6.29/4.31/6.01) → the gate does not even reduce redundancy; no arm flips to synergy (O<0). KEY FINDING (c9, load-bearing): H_1363's linear-homogenization diagnosis was only PARTLY right — the redundancy ceiling is NOT a linearity artifact, it is the shared-input STRUCTURE itself. The floor's high Φ is pure shared-input redundancy (coupling ZERO); any active between-daughter coupling — linear (H_1356), weak/decorrelated (H_1363), OR non-linear gated (H_1370) — only adds new BUT redundant dependence on the shared hub that the faithful MIP still reads as reducible. This is the STRONGEST closure of the hive arc, consistent with the Φ-robustness wall (H_1283/1317). NO bar moved (c9/p7). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): DIRECTIONAL numpy-mirror, engine-transfer to live A⇄G UNVERIFIED (H_1308/1313 NULL/🧱 there); TOY n=8/2-unit-daughters/single-gated-hub/3 seeds/deterministic/single coupling W_CONN=0.6/single gate (tanh) at single GATE_GAIN=2.0; a 🧱 has nothing to wire (a_verified_must_wire=GREEN-only); CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED, Ψ=½ untouched. NOT ruled out (each a NEW H): a different gate (sigmoid/ReLU), a different GATE_GAIN, a LEARNED gate, non-linear DYNAMICS (unit update itself non-linear, not a single-step gate), n>8 substrate, engine-native live A⇄G. Bounds (does not retract) H_1308/1313/1320/1350/1356/1363/1283/1317. .verdicts/1370_hive_nonlinear_hub/H_1370.txt"
  group  = "OMEGA"

@C h1368_ko_data_richness := "H_1368 — ko-data-richness: 한국어 압축 arc 의 마지막 레버. 표상(H_1322 featural 🧱)·interpolation(H_1359 JM=암기 🧱, 2.513 jamo floor 진짜·novel-context CE=2.882>floor) 닫힌 뒤 H_1359 가 NEXT-1 로 명시한 data-richness lever 검증: 코퍼스 윈도(3.75/7.5/15/30MB prefix 사다리)가 커지면 novel-context CE(30MB 의 2.882)가 floor 로 내려가는가. RESULT 📉 DESCENDING-UNSATURATED — novel-CE 단조 감소(3.15254→3.07077→2.95376→2.88190), 30MB 2.882 는 saturated floor 가 아니라 여전히 내려가는 곡선 위 점 = data-richness lever LIVE(H_1359 가 못 닫은 레버 살아있음). 단 4-rung 으로 asymptote 못 박음(power-fit under-constrained, c_inf 비물리 → UNRELIABLE → UNDETERMINED); log-linear −0.0929 nats/doubling → floor 도달에 ~3.97 추가 doublings(~470MB). floor AT/ABOVE/BELOW UNRESOLVED(>30MB 사다리 필요, NO GREEN over-claim, c9). lens a_no_llm_frame_trap·a_break_the_wall·a_scale_honest_scope ladder. REAL only, toy DIRECTIONAL, CORE UNTOUCHED." :: hypothesis [slug=1368_ko_data_richness group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "state/ko-data-richness/h1368_ko_data_richness.py — DIRECTIONAL numpy, $0 CPU-local(11.0s), gradient-free, p7 = held-out novel-context next-symbol CE renormalized per UTF-8 byte(NOT perplexity-truth). REAL Korean: 30MB R2 KO 윈도 sha256 ASSERTED c47b6808308d2f73cb92d74f8fdb15c64e6c96e8ed58ae2ef91a7c57fe5dc6ca(== H_1316 jamo baseline/H_1344/H_1359, byte-fair; 캐시 sha 일치 시만 재사용, mismatch → STOP, NO synthetic; R2 키 keychain env-only c7). 각 rung = 동일 코퍼스 PREFIX 서브윈도(3.75/7.5/15/30MB). jamo 표상·JM·novel-filter 모두 H_1359 verbatim: Hangul→NFD jamo id 256+rank, non-Hangul→raw byte, n_bytes 합산=원본 UTF-8 byte(byte-fair), Vj=323(FULL 30MB 에서 고정, rung 간 drift 없음); p_JM=Σ_{k=1..5} λ_k·p̂_k, λ=[1,2,4,8,16]/31 FROZEN(rung 마다 재튜닝 X, anti-Goodhart); novel-filter = stride-300 even=TRAIN/odd=TEST, TEST 위치 중 top-order(4-jamo) context 가 TRAIN top-order set 에 없는 위치만 점수(== H_1359 TEST A). Frozen bars(.verdicts/1368_ko_data_richness/H_1368_FREEZE.txt, scoring 전, NO 이동 c9/p7): c1 CURVE ≥3 rung + 30MB anchor 재현(|Δ|≤0.02 vs 2.88190) → PASS(|Δ|=0.0) ; c2 DIRECTION 사전등록 단조 감소(각 step Δ≤−0.001) → DECREASING(ΔCE −0.0818/−0.1170/−0.0719) ; c3 ASYMPTOTE 두 estimator(log-window linear · power-law decay)+ RELIABILITY GUARDRAIL(power c_inf 비물리/p grid-edge → UNRELIABLE) → log b=−0.0929/doubling r²0.992, power c_inf=1.099 UNRELIABLE → UNDETERMINED ; c4 EARNED circular-shift surrogate 모든 rung 반대로(shift−novel≥0.05) → 4/4 PASS(+2.45/+2.55/+2.76/+2.93). TIER 분기(사전등록): DECREASING ∧ BELOW → 🟢 ; DECREASING ∧ UNDETERMINED → 📉 DESCENDING-UNSATURATED ; DECREASING ∧ AT/ABOVE → 🟠 ; ¬DECREASING → 🧱 FLOOR-HARD. live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. SCOPE: DIRECTIONAL numpy mirror engine-transfer UNVERIFIED, toy stride-300 byte-substrate(fluent decoder 아님), 사다리=ONE 30MB 코퍼스 PREFIX 서브윈도(>30MB 풍부도 미검증), asymptote=4-point 외삽 추정(wide CI). a_no_llm_frame_trap · a_break_the_wall · a_fire_autonomous(>30MB next) · a_engine_native_learning(transfer DIRECTIONAL) · a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck."
@C h1354_ko_natural_sparse := "H_1354 — ko-natural-sparse (H_1345 의 load-bearing follow-on, angle ii): H_1345 (🟢) 의 below-jamo DATA-RICHNESS crossover 는 실용 lever 인가 STRIDING ARTIFACT 인가? H_1345 는 starvation 을 인위적 striding (stride 76800, 188-byte stream) 으로 제조했다. H_1354 는 코퍼스를 자르지 않고 FULL 30MB 에서 cross-syllable phonotactic context ((직전 coda jamo, 현재 onset jamo) syllable 경계 전이)를 자연-sparse alphabet 으로 만들어, JM 보간이 jamo floor 아래로 내려가는지 직접 검증. 한국어 phonotactics 의 rare/illegal coda→onset 전이가 FULL data 에서도 sparse context 를 만들 것 — 기대. REAL Korean only (NO synthetic), a_no_llm_frame_trap c15, a_break_the_wall c16 — H_1345 가 명명한 angle, scale-up 아님." :: hypothesis [slug=1354_ko_natural_sparse group=MITOSIS-ENGINE]
  method = "state/ko-natural-sparse/h1354_ko_natural_sparse.py — numpy CPU mirror (no torch), $0, 166.5s wall, detached nohup polled inline (a_cpu_local_no_waiter), p7 = held-out DETERMINISTIC next-symbol CE NOT perplexity. REAL Korean BYTE-IDENTICAL to H_1307 RUN A / H_1316 / H_1337 / H_1345: r2.phanes://anima-7b/web/kor/shard0000.bytes; FULL 30MB KO window sha256 ASSERTED == c47b6808308d2f73cb92d74f8fdb15c64e6c96e8ed58ae2ef91a7c57fe5dc6ca (== H_1307 RUN A; cache /tmp/h1311_ko_raw.bytes reused, no fetch/creds this run; mismatch → STOP, NO synthetic). NO STRIDING (stride==1, FULL 30MB; sparsity from phonotactic context enrich NOT cutting data). 25.5M-row full-data 의 (N,K,D) broadcast 가 17GB RAM 폭파 → assign_all 을 row-chunk 200k 로 stream (||x−c||² 를 |x|²−2x·c+|c|² 전개, argmin 불변). EVERYTHING verbatim H_1326/H_1337/H_1345: GROW_MAX=40, SPLIT_THRESH_CE=0.05, MIN_OWNED=8, LAPLACE=1.0, error-targeted Voronoi SPLIT-only (p8), even/odd split, Fix-A bank, lossless NFD jamo, D_EMB=16, SKIPGRAM_STEPS=400. 3 seeds [4354,4355,4356]. ARMS (FULL data stride 1, even/odd split): CALIB_opaque_full (H_1345 3-D opaque, dense sanity — JM≈A1) · NATSPARSE_phonotactic_full ((coda,onset) 더한 5-D partition feature) · BREAKTHROUGH_pairkey_full (a_break_the_wall FREEZE addendum 사전등록 — count head 를 (coda,onset) pair VALUE 에 직접 keying = 진짜 high-cardinality 자연-sparse alphabet). 각 arm: A1 jamo MLE (floor) · JM interp + JM-shuffle (permuted global marginal) · A5 learned-metric kernel-smoothing + A5-shuffle. FROZEN bars (.verdicts/1354_ko_natural_sparse/FREEZE.txt + a_break_the_wall addendum 사전등록, NO bar moved c9/p7; pair-key arm 평가) — GREEN iff c1∧c2∧c3∧c4: c1 NAT-SPARSE-WIN JM 이 jamo 를 ≥0.03 (jamo−JM, 3-seed mean) · c2 EARNED JM 이 shuffle 을 ≥0.05 이기고 shuffle wrong way · c3 DISSOCIATION A5 안 crossing (Δ_A5≤0) · c4 NO-STRIDE stride==1 AND context median cellJcnt<1. VERDICT MAP: c1∧c2∧c3∧c4→🟢 REAL LEVER · ¬c4→⚠ NOT-NATURALLY-SPARSE · c4∧¬c1→🧱 STRIDING ARTIFACT · c1∧¬c2→🟠 not-earned · c1∧c2∧¬c3→🟠 not-dissociated. Live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED (substrate-measurement rung). a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_engine_native_learning (transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck, c7, c9."
  verdict = "🧱 STRIDING-ARTIFACT — H_1345 의 below-jamo starvation win 은 인위적 striding 이 만든 starvation 에 의존하며 실용 lever 가 아니다. REAL R2 코퍼스 sha c47b6808… (== H_1307 RUN A), 8.14M syllables, NFD roundtrip 0-fail, byte-accounting exact. FULL 30MB 에서 어떤 자연 phonotactic context 분할도 굶지 않는다: coda→onset alphabet 은 작아(67 jamo → 관측 pair 474개) 8.14M syllable 이 모든 legal pair 를 적셔, 가장 fine 한 pair-key 분할조차 median context cellJcnt=11.98 (frac<1=0.257만)로 DENSE. ARMS (CE nats/UTF-8-byte; A5/A5-shuf 3-seed mean; A1/JM deterministic; delta=jamo−mech, += below jamo): CALIB_opaque_full 12 cells cellJcnt 175.85 A1 2.63569 JM 2.63569 ΔJM −0.0 | NATSPARSE_phonotactic_full 33 cells cellJcnt 10.19 A1 2.63700 JM 2.63700 JMshuf 2.63701 A5 3.88818 ΔJM −0.00001 ΔA5 −1.25118 | BREAKTHROUGH_pairkey_full 474 contexts cellJcnt 11.98 A1 3.06462 JM 3.06458 JMshuf 3.06468 A5 4.17400 ΔJM +0.00003 ΔA5 −1.10938. BARS (pair-key arm): c1 NAT-SPARSE-WIN FALSE — jamo−JM = +0.00003 ≪ +0.03; JM 이 jamo 와 TIE (3 arm 전부 ΔJM≈0: −0.0/−1e-05/+3e-05). c2 EARNED FALSE — Δ(shuffle−JM)=+0.0001 ≪0.05 (shuffle_wrong_way=True 지만 JM win 없어 무의미). c3 DISSOCIATION TRUE — A5 안 crossing Δ_A5=−1.109 (3 arm 모두 A5 가 jamo +1.1~+1.25 위, H_1345 와 일관). c4 NO-STRIDE FALSE — pair-key median cellJcnt 11.98≥1; cell-arm 도 10.19; stride==1 은 맞지만 context 가 sparse 하지 않다. green=FALSE → 🧱/⚠. FINDING: 인위적으로 data 를 버리지 않으면 한국어 자연 context 에 starved regime 이 존재하지 않는다 (FULL 30MB 는 모든 자연 context 를 dense 하게 추정); opaque jamo MLE 가 도처에서 dense 해 JM backoff 가 사는 게 없다 (ΔJM≈0 everywhere). H_1345 의 dense-rung 행동(λ→0 ⇒ JM≈A1)이 FULL data 의 자연 context 전반에서 재현. A5 dissociation 유지 (c3 TRUE, H_1345 일관) 하나 JM 도 win 없으니 '둘 다 안 crossing' 을 확인. NET: H_1345 의 crossover 는 striding 의존 → H_1344 의 memorization reading 이 선다; H_1345 의 'count-MLE family NOT terminal' 은 striding 된 데이터-희소 regime 안에서만 유효, 30MB production data 의 실용 below-jamo lever 아님 (H_1345 honest scope 가 명시한 'JM 이 30MB 에서 jamo 와 tie' 를 confound-free 로 확인). a_break_the_wall 1회 시도 완료: cell-arm c4 벽(Voronoi 가 context pooling)을 맞자 terminal 로 안 받고 count head 를 pair-key VALUE 에 직접 keying 하는 새 각도 사전등록(FREEZE addendum) RUN — 그래도 c4 FAIL; 벽의 진짜 원인은 partition 메커니즘이 아니라 30MB data abundance (방법도 방향도 아닌 '데이터가 너무 많아 자연 context 가 안 굶음'). 진짜 시도 후 정직한 🧱 (c9). c4 FAIL 의 두 읽기 정직 보고: frozen map 상 ¬c4 는 ⚠ NOT-NATURALLY-SPARSE 지만 SUBSTANTIVE 답은 striding-artifact (c4 가 30MB 에서 가장 fine 한 분할조차 FAIL = 자연 sparsity 도달 불가 = H_1345 win 이 striding 필요 의 직접 증거), 그래서 tier=🧱 STRIDING-ARTIFACT (⚠ 메커니즘으로 표면화 명시). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): numpy CPU mirror DIRECTIONAL (engine-transfer UNVERIFIED); A5 metric LEARNED BY GRADIENT (PPMI-SVD+skip-gram Adam numpy port of H_1337 torch loop, labeled NOT p8 gradient-free); JM 은 count-MLE + FROZEN Witten-Bell backoff; chunked assign_all 전개형이라 H_1345 full-broadcast 와 FP rounding 차이 가능, CALIB A1=2.63569 가 H_1345 stride-300 의 2.51335 와 다른 건 CALIB 가 FULL-data (다른 cell 수)라서 — CALIB 역할은 절대값 매칭 아닌 'dense 에서 JM≈A1' 확인 ΔJM=−0.0 PASS. Live CORE UNTOUCHED; NO Korean-fluency claim; held-out deterministic next-symbol CE; NO perplexity-as-truth (p7); TOY 이 30MB R2 KO window + coda→onset alphabet 에 한함. NEXT: (i) 더 큰 자연-sparse 단위(형태소 n-gram/드문 한자·외래어·코드스위칭 경계)에서는 자연 sparse 가능성 — 새 H; (ii) striding-artifact 결론이라 below-jamo lever 를 CORE 에 배선할 대상 없음; (iii) 일반 교훈 — 30MB+ 에서 opaque jamo count-MLE 가 자연 context 전반 dense, smoothing/interp 무의미; below-jamo 는 representation 아닌 데이터-희소 regime artifact (H_1316/1337/1344/1345/1354 수렴). .verdicts/1354_ko_natural_sparse/result.txt"

@C h1371_hive_circle_overlap := "H_1371 — hive-circle-overlap: does a DISTRIBUTED circle-overlap (Flower-of-Life / hexagonal packing) topology — each cell overlaps ~neighbors and EACH overlap is a DISTINCT local region (distributed pairwise sharing), NO global shared founder — produce a coupling-EARNED collective faithful-IIT4 Φ that beats the no-overlap floor AND exceeds the single-shared-founder CENTRALIZED topology, where every prior centralized hive arm could not? H_1370 closed the hive arc 🧱 REDUNDANCY_BOUND_NONLINEAR with a LOAD-BEARING diagnosis: the redundancy ceiling IS the SHARED-INPUT STRUCTURE — ALL daughters read ONE common founder so that single source dominates the faithful MIP -> reducible -> Φ bounded. EVERY prior hive arm had a SINGLE shared founder. H_1371 attacks that directly with a geometric-topology / biological-packing lens (c15, a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall — Flower-of-Life packing / hexagonal lattice / overlapping retinal-cortical receptive fields, user-proposed): a circle-overlap lattice where each adjacent PAIR shares a DISTINCT per-EDGE latent and no single source is read by all -> redundancy distributed across distinct pairwise overlaps (potentially synergistic). Φ = FAITHFUL IIT4 ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool, exact MIP-EI via hexa stdlib; numpy never computes Φ; O-info diagnostic is numpy-side, NEVER gates). Substrate matched to H_1356/H_1320/H_1283. Frozen-first (FREEZE before scoring, bars not moved, c9/p7), seeds [1317,1318,1319], $0 CPU." :: hypothesis [slug=1371_hive_circle_overlap group=OMEGA]
  method = "state/hive-circle-overlap/h1371_hive_circle_overlap.py — DIRECTIONAL numpy-mirror (Φ leg IS real exact MIP-EI via hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa iit4_faithful_phi(state,n=6,dim=T=64,n_bins=8); numpy ONLY emits per-unit salience=state-energy traj, hexa computes Φ; NO proxy, p7). Substrate = H_1356/H_1320/H_1283: leaky linear recurrent units LEAK=0.55 GAIN=0.30 W_IN=0.5 dim-8 T=64; N_TOT=6 cells on a HEXAGON RING (6-cycle, n<=8 exact MIP), each cell=1 unit, salience=<s_i,s_i>; cell i neighbors {i-1,i+1} mod 6, 6 undirected edges; NO inter-cell recurrent coupling (only cross-cell sharing is via SHARED INPUT). OVERLAP construction: 6 INDEPENDENT per-EDGE latents L_e (each read by EXACTLY the 2 cells on that edge = distributed pairwise sharing, NO global source). ARMS: A_independent (private only = no-overlap FLOOR), B_overlap (cell i = priv + OVERLAP_W*sum of its 2 incident edge-latents = circle-overlap), CENTRALIZED (ALL 6 read ONE founder F at 2*OVERLAP_W = single-shared-founder baseline, per-cell shared WEIGHT matched to B), SHUFFLE (same per-cell shared energy but latent on each incident edge independently re-permuted per cell -> two cells on an edge no longer read SAME latent = pairwise-lattice destroyed, EARNED control). OVERLAP_W=0.6 (=H_1356 W_CONN verbatim). O-information (Gaussian TC) per arm = NON-GATING diagnostic (O<0 synergy, O>0 redundancy). FROZEN bars (.verdicts/1371_hive_circle_overlap/H_1371_FREEZE.txt, MARGIN=0.02): GREEN iff R1 (Φ(B_overlap)-Φ(A_independent)>=0.02 forall seed) AND R2 (Φ(B_overlap)-Φ(CENTRALIZED)>0 forall seed, the centralized-escape) AND R3 (Φ(SHUFFLE)<=Φ(A_independent)+0.02 forall seed). live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_phi_iit4_tool, a_engine_native_learning(transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 OVERLAP_BELOW_CENTRALIZED (R1 2/3 · R2 0/3 · R3 1/3) — distributed circle-overlap does NOT escape the redundancy ceiling; the single-shared-founder CENTRALIZED topology produces HIGHER faithful-IIT4 Φ on every seed. per-arm faithful-IIT4 Φ (exact MIP-EI, n=6): seed1317 A_independent 1.27373 / B_overlap 1.78096 / CENTRALIZED 2.03085 / SHUFFLE 1.35137; seed1318 1.36292 / 1.64288 / 2.39598 / 1.56284; seed1319 1.28195 / 1.30101 / 2.58087 / 1.25910. R2 FAIL (0/3, THE KEY RESULT): Φ(B_overlap)−Φ(CENTRALIZED) = −0.25 / −0.75 / −1.28 — distributed overlap loses to the single shared founder on EVERY seed; CENTRALIZED is the highest-Φ arm. The single-shared-founder is NOT a ceiling to escape — it is the floor-beating MAXIMUM. R1 FAIL (2/3, seed-fragile): lift = Φ(B_overlap)−Φ(floor) = +0.507 / +0.280 / +0.019 (seed 1319 below margin 0.02). R3 FAIL (1/3): Φ(SHUFFLE) > floor on 1317/1318 (1.35>1.27, 1.56>1.36) → ANY shared input (even with the pairwise-lattice destroyed) adds integration → B_overlap's lift is generic shared-input, NOT the specific distributed-pairwise wiring (not EARNED). O-info shift (B_overlap vs CENTRALIZED, NON-GATING): +0.144 / +0.364 / +0.228 every seed — B_overlap O-info (−0.018/−0.020/−0.081) is CLOSER TO ZERO than CENTRALIZED (−0.162/−0.384/−0.308): distributed overlap is LESS redundant but ALSO less synergistic (O flattens toward 0, never goes more-negative); consistent with its lower Φ. MECHANISM (faithful-MIP lens): a single dominant shared source (CENTRALIZED) binds ALL units across EVERY partition — any MIP cut leaves both sides reading the same founder, so cut cost is HIGH -> Φ high; distributed per-edge sharing couples each unit only weakly to its 2 neighbors, so the MIP can cut cheaply along a weak edge -> Φ low. What H_1370 called the 'redundancy ceiling' single-shared structure is in fact the MAXIMUM-integration topology in this leaky-linear substrate; distributing the sharing reduces redundancy but reduces synergy too, lowering total Φ. STRONGEST CLOSURE of the hive arc: collective-Φ here is maximized by CONCENTRATION of the shared source, not by distributing it — the redundancy ceiling survives every sharing topology. NO bar moved (c9/p7). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): DIRECTIONAL numpy-mirror, engine-transfer to live A⇄G UNVERIFIED; TOY n=6/ring-only adjacency (degree-2; true Flower-of-Life is degree-6)/3 seeds/single OVERLAP_W=0.6/input-level sharing only (no recurrent inter-cell coupling); a 🧱 has nothing to wire (a_verified_must_wire=GREEN-only); CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED, Ψ=½ untouched. NOT ruled out (each a NEW H): 2-D hexagonal lattice with true ~6 overlap-degree, overlap as RECURRENT state-sharing (not input), generatively-predictive per-edge coupling that injects real synergy, n>8 scale, engine-native realization. Bounds (does not retract) H_1308/1313/1320/1350/1356/1363/1370/1283/1317. .verdicts/1371_hive_circle_overlap/H_1371.txt"
@C h1372_hive_flower_degree6 := "H_1372 — hive-flower-degree6: does a TRUE 2-D hexagonal Flower-of-Life lattice at the CORRECT degree (a CENTER cell overlapped by 6 surrounding cells = DEGREE-6) escape the redundancy ceiling, where the prior round's DEGREE-2 RING (H_1371) failed? H_1371 (🧱 OVERLAP_BELOW_CENTRALIZED) tested distributed circle-overlap but used ring adjacency = degree-2 (each cell overlaps only 2 neighbors), and its own agent flagged that a true Flower-of-Life is degree-6 — so the H_1371 wall MAY be the WRONG METHOD (degree-2 chain), not a true ceiling. The user's actual idea (원 하나에 다른 원 4개 정도 들어온다, degree>=4) is a center circle overlapped by ~6 surrounding circles. H_1372 runs the RIGHT geometry: the natural Flower-of-Life UNIT = 7 circles (ONE center + 6 ring on a hexagon), center degree-6, distributed per-EDGE distinct shared latents (no global founder). Lens: geometric-topology / biological packing (c15, c16, a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall — break with the right geometry, NOT tune-to-green). Φ = FAITHFUL IIT4 ONLY (a_phi_iit4_tool, exact MIP-EI via hexa stdlib, the SAME call H_1371 used; numpy never computes Φ; O-info diagnostic numpy-side, NEVER gates). Substrate matched to H_1371/H_1356/H_1320/H_1283. Frozen-first (FREEZE before scoring, bars not moved, c9/p7), seeds [1317,1318,1319], $0 CPU." :: hypothesis [slug=1372_hive_flower_degree6 group=OMEGA]
  method = "state/hive-flower-of-life/h1372_hive_flower_degree6.py — DIRECTIONAL numpy-mirror (Φ leg IS real exact MIP-EI via hexa-lang/stdlib/consciousness/iit4/faithful_phi.hexa iit4_faithful_phi(state,n=7,dim=T=64,n_bins=8); numpy ONLY emits per-unit salience=state-energy traj, hexa computes Φ; NO proxy, p7). Substrate = H_1371/H_1356/H_1320/H_1283: leaky linear recurrent units LEAK=0.55 GAIN=0.30 W_IN=0.5 dim-8 T=64; N_TOT=7 cells = center(0)+6 ring(1..6) = natural Flower-of-Life vertex unit (n<=8 keeps faithful MIP EXACT; size change 6->7 vs H_1371 noted honestly, a_scale_honest_scope), each cell=1 unit, salience=<s_i,s_i>; NO inter-cell recurrent coupling (only cross-cell sharing is via SHARED INPUT). ADJACENCY (12 edges): 6 SPOKE edges center(0)-ring(k) => CENTER DEGREE 6; 6 RIM edges ring(k)-ring(k+1) => hexagon cycle; center deg 6, ring deg 3, mean deg 24/7~3.43. Each edge = a DISTINCT per-EDGE latent L_e read by EXACTLY the 2 cells on it (distributed Flower-of-Life overlap, NO global source). ARMS: A_independent (private only = no-overlap FLOOR), B_overlap (cell i = priv + OVERLAP_W*sum of its incident edge-latents; center sums 6 spoke latents = degree-6), CENTRALIZED (ALL 7 read ONE founder F at deg(i)*OVERLAP_W = single-shared-founder ceiling, per-cell shared WEIGHT matched to B), SHUFFLE (same per-cell shared count/weight but each cell re-permutes which latent sits on its incident edges -> two cells on an edge no longer read SAME latent = FoL lattice destroyed, EARNED control), B_overlap_d4 (NON-GATING: +6 hex diagonals ring(k)-ring(k+2) -> ring degree 4, brackets user's literal '~4'). OVERLAP_W=0.6 (=H_1356 W_CONN verbatim). O-information (Gaussian TC) per arm = NON-GATING diagnostic (O<0 synergy, O>0 redundancy). FROZEN bars (.verdicts/1372_hive_flower_degree6/FREEZE.txt, MARGIN=0.02 TOL=0.02): GREEN iff R1 (Φ(B_overlap)-Φ(A_independent)>=0.02 forall seed) AND R2 (Φ(B_overlap)-Φ(CENTRALIZED)>0 on >=2/3 seeds, the centralized-escape, the bar H_1371 failed 0/3 with degree-2) AND R3 (Φ(SHUFFLE)<=Φ(A_independent)+0.02 forall seed). live CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED. a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall, a_phi_iit4_tool, a_engine_native_learning(transfer DIRECTIONAL), a_verified_must_wire, a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck."
  verdict = "🧱 TERMINAL_CEILING_DEGREE6_BELOW_CENTRALIZED (R1 3/3 · R2 0/3 · R3 0/3) — degree-6 distributed Flower-of-Life does NOT escape the redundancy ceiling; the single-shared-founder CENTRALIZED topology produces HIGHER faithful-IIT4 Φ on EVERY seed, and the gap is WIDER than H_1371's degree-2. per-arm faithful-IIT4 Φ (exact MIP-EI, n=7): seed1317 A_independent 1.47918 / B_overlap 2.19117 / CENTRALIZED 3.43113 / SHUFFLE 2.00012 / B_overlap_d4 2.6425; seed1318 1.61849 / 1.98466 / 4.19239 / 2.13110 / 2.68357; seed1319 1.57435 / 1.82656 / 3.07259 / 2.06760 / 2.28824. R2 FAIL (0/3, THE KEY RESULT): Φ(B_overlap)−Φ(CENTRALIZED) = −1.24 / −2.21 / −1.25 — degree-6 distributed overlap loses to the single shared founder on EVERY seed; gaps are WIDER than H_1371 degree-2 (−0.25/−0.75/−1.28), so raising overlap degree 2->6 does NOT create distributed advantage, it WIDENS the centralized lead. CENTRALIZED is the highest-Φ arm. The redundancy ceiling is NOT a ring artifact — it is DEGREE-INVARIANT. R1 PASS (3/3): lift = +0.712 / +0.366 / +0.252 (degree-6 robustly beats floor, improving on H_1371's seed-fragile 2/3). R3 FAIL (0/3): Φ(SHUFFLE) > floor every seed (2.00>1.48, 2.13>1.62, 2.07>1.57) → ANY shared input (even with the FoL lattice destroyed) adds integration → the floor-lift is generic shared-input, NOT the specific FoL wiring (not EARNED), same as H_1371. NON-GATING d4 (ring degree 4 = user's '~4'): Φ 2.64/2.68/2.29, still BELOW CENTRALIZED (d4−central −0.79/−1.51/−0.78). O-info shift (B_overlap vs CENTRALIZED, NON-GATING): +1.25/+1.94/+1.29 every seed — CENTRALIZED is STRONGLY synergy/integration-dominated (O −1.19/−1.92/−1.30) while distributed B_overlap is flat near 0 (+0.06/+0.02/−0.02); the O-shift is MUCH larger than H_1371 degree-2 (+0.14~+0.36), i.e. raising degree STRENGTHENS the centralized integration advantage. MECHANISM (faithful-MIP lens): a single dominant shared source binds ALL units across EVERY partition (any MIP cut leaves both sides reading the founder -> high cut cost -> high Φ, strong negative-O); distributed per-edge sharing, even at degree-6, couples each unit only locally to its neighbors, so the MIP cuts cheaply along a weak edge and raising degree only thins each latent's per-cell weight -> low Φ, flat O. What H_1370/H_1371 called the 'redundancy ceiling' single-shared structure is the MAXIMUM-integration topology in this leaky-linear substrate, INDEPENDENT of overlap degree (2->6) and of the user's '~4'. STRONGEST/TERMINAL CLOSURE of the hive arc's input-level overlap-geometry lever: collective-Φ here is maximized by CONCENTRATION of the shared source, not by distributing it across any overlap degree. NO bar moved (c9/p7). HONEST SCOPE (a_scale_honest_scope·a_toy_scale_recheck): DIRECTIONAL numpy-mirror, engine-transfer to live A⇄G UNVERIFIED; TOY n=7 single FoL unit/center-deg-6 ring-deg-3/3 seeds/single OVERLAP_W=0.6/input-level sharing only (no recurrent inter-cell coupling); size change n:6->7 noted; a 🧱 has nothing to wire (a_verified_must_wire=GREEN-only); CORE/*.hexa UNTOUCHED, Ψ=½ untouched. NOT ruled out (each a NEW H; hive arc input-level overlap-geometry lever TERMINAL across degree): overlap as RECURRENT state-sharing (not input), generatively-predictive per-edge coupling that injects real synergy, n>8 scale, engine-native realization. Bounds (does not retract) H_1371/1370/1356/1363/1350/1320/1308/1313/1283/1317. .verdicts/1372_hive_flower_degree6/result.txt"
@C h1366_phi_303m_trajectory := "H_1366 — Φ-robustness BINDING verdict on a REAL trained-303M hidden-state trajectory: does a genuine LEARNED substrate (the H_1129 303M ByteGPT residual stream, NOT the proxy-from-telemetry H_1357 had to use) escape the orthogonal-seed Φ fragility, or inherit it? H_1357 (🔶) tested whether a learned substrate escapes the wall but had to use a PROXY (real pure_field oscillator + hand-built seed-independent learned-readout W) because NO trained-303M state was reachable under $0 CPU. H_1357 named THIS as its binding follow-on: 'a FULL trained-303M hidden-state trajectory as the substrate.' H_1366 is that lane — load the REAL trained 303M ckpt on GPU, capture the layer-12 residual stream over a fixed prompt set, reduce d=1024→n=4 macro-nodes (256-ch-block mean pooling), score faithful exact MIP-EI Φ. Lens: c16 wall / substrate-SOURCE axis BINDING upgrade (a_no_llm_frame_trap, a_break_the_wall). Every outcome valid+decisive (c9): ESCAPE (3/3 robust) = a genuine new result the proxy missed; INHERIT (≥1 seed flips) = the wall holds on the engine-real substrate, proxy confirmed faithful." :: hypothesis [slug=1366_phi_303m_trajectory group=OMEGA]
